&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T12:37:53-07:00","id":1148655,"title":"","content":"What level would a working that would create an image in the sky, visible for many hundreds of miles, that would send a message from the sorcerer be?<br /> <br /> I am also a bit unsure on how the exp cost would be for something that is a one time effect... Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4567-volivat","name":"Volivat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T12:59:08-07:00","id":1148658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volivat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1148655#post1148655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What level would a working that would create an image in the sky, visible for many hundreds of miles, that would send a message from the sorcerer be?<br /> <br /> I am also a bit unsure on how the exp cost would be for something that is a one time effect... Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would suggest that if the effect is supposed to be one-time-only, then it's better modelled as a spell, rather than a working. That's one of the big differences, in my opinion, between spells and workings: spells are typically temporary (with some exceptions like Benediction of Archgenesis, of course), while a sorcerous working, once created, is basically permanent - at most, another working can warp it, or other circumstances render it useless. But the working itself will still be there.<br /> <br /> So, I'd peg a spell to create a giant image visible for hundreds of miles, that can convey a message, a Celestial Circle spell. As a working, creating a <i>permanent</i> image visible for hundreds of miles would be a Celestial circle working, Ambition 1 if it was stuck with one image (and thus message) eternally, Ambition 2 if it could be changed, within certain parameters (so, for example, a giant image of the sorcerer, who could gesture to ward off intruders, make signs with their hands to communicate in sign language, and so on, but was still limited to being an image of the sorcerer), and Ambition 3 if the image could be literally anything the sorcerer wanted, changed on the fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T13:31:14-07:00","id":1148665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1148658#post1148658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would suggest that if the effect is supposed to be one-time-only, then it's better modelled as a spell, rather than a working. That's one of the big differences, in my opinion, between spells and workings: spells are typically temporary (with some exceptions like Benediction of Archgenesis, of course), while a sorcerous working, once created, is basically permanent - at most, another working can warp it, or other circumstances render it useless. But the working itself will still be there.<br /> <br /> So, I'd peg a spell to create a giant image visible for hundreds of miles, that can convey a message, a Celestial Circle spell. As a working, creating a <i>permanent</i> image visible for hundreds of miles would be a Celestial circle working, Ambition 1 if it was stuck with one image (and thus message) eternally, Ambition 2 if it could be changed, within certain parameters (so, for example, a giant image of the sorcerer, who could gesture to ward off intruders, make signs with their hands to communicate in sign language, and so on, but was still limited to being an image of the sorcerer), and Ambition 3 if the image could be literally anything the sorcerer wanted, changed on the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I disagree with this reasoning. At least in a broad sense. Certainly, if this is an effect that the player intends to repeat or re-use whenever they need, this would be best modeled as a spell. however if the player wants to do this as a one-off (and is okay with permanently losing the xp spent the working since once your sign has been see then it cannot be neutralized afterwards), it would likely work better as a working. <br /> <br /> I could see it as enacting a working that re-shapes the clouds into your message but not specifying what happens to the clouds afterwards. IE, <i>those </i>clouds are forever transformed into the message, but then they dissipate and shift as clouds do and then the message is gone forever.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's worth forcing the player to create a brand new sorcerous spell just ot perform something like this, but if they're planning on doing it again, then yeah this fits better as a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T07:46:14-07:00","id":1148817,"title":"","content":"If I were to make a music box that healed and regenerated and relaxed all who heard it, what working would it be? Celestial 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T08:48:29-07:00","id":1148833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1148817#post1148817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to make a music box that healed and regenerated and relaxed all who heard it, what working would it be? Celestial 1?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on the exact level of healing, I think. I'd probably peg it as always Celestial-tier in general, but something like just granting mortals Exalted-level healing rates would be Ambition 1, while stepping up even exalted to something like healing lethal levels in the time it normally takes to heal bashing would be Ambition 2, and straight up &quot;listen to this for a few minutes, be completely healed of all wounds&quot; would be Ambition 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T10:57:25-07:00","id":1148864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1147565#post1147565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. I wish for a mortal clan to be born with the innate power of terrestrial circle sorcery. What level is this? Celestial 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>The city of Ysyr shows that such a mutation can and does exist, so I'd call it Terrestrial 2 to apply to a single person. Applying it to an entire clan would be Celestial level, probably Ambition 2 or 3, unless you're willing to apply it to one person at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T11:20:09-07:00","id":1148866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1148864#post1148864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The city of Ysyr shows that such a mutation can and does exist, so I'd call it Terrestrial 2 to apply to a single person. Applying it to an entire clan would be Celestial level, probably Ambition 2 or 3, unless you're willing to apply it to one person at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The potential for TCS exists certainly, but they'd still have to initiate into the circle like everybody else. If Accelerator is talking about <i>automatic </i>initiation that might even be a solar circle working","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T15:52:41-07:00","id":1148921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1148833#post1148833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Depends on the exact level of healing, I think. I'd probably peg it as always Celestial-tier in general, but something like just granting mortals Exalted-level healing rates would be Ambition 1, while stepping up even exalted to something like healing lethal levels in the time it normally takes to heal bashing would be Ambition 2, and straight up &amp;quot;listen to this for a few minutes, be completely healed of all wounds&amp;quot; would be Ambition 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted level healing rates","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T04:45:17-07:00","id":1149051,"title":"","content":"How about linking two places with a portal/door that would allow people stepping throught to be transported from one to the other? <br /> <br /> Both places being in Creation, I'm not talking about portals to other realms.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Celestial 2, but I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T05:13:55-07:00","id":1149058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1149051#post1149051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about linking two places with a portal/door that would allow people stepping throught to be transported from one to the other?<br /> <br /> Both places being in Creation, I'm not talking about portals to other realms.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Celestial 2, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, most likely celestial 3 or solar 1<br /> <br /> Given that these are similar to those first age teleport gates. Also, what's the size. Instant transportation is very useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T07:31:43-07:00","id":1149091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1148866#post1148866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The potential for TCS exists certainly, but they'd still have to initiate into the circle like everybody else. If Accelerator is talking about <i>automatic </i>initiation that might even be a solar circle working</div> </div> </div> </div>Automatic initiation. <br /> <br /> I was thinking of people like the Crimson magic clan from konosuba.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T09:13:41-07:00","id":1149137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1149091#post1149091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Automatic initiation.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of people like the Crimson magic clan from konosuba.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah as automatic initiation that everybody in the clan gets and it's hereditary? Either Solar Circle 2 or just straight up impossible. You're talking something that would seriously break the setting to have access to. An army of sorcerers that you just have to breed is a seriously big deal. <br /> <br /> It would involve impressing the members of the tribe with the right amount of occult to be able to cast spells and meet the initiation requirements. My ST and I were talking about this actually. We figured that since a solar (and potentially other exalts) get access to TCS at occult 3, it makes sense for mortals to need occult 4-5 to get there. You're also talking about bypassing initiation requirements so I'd guess they'd all be getting a custom initiation (not gonna be born with a pact with an ifreet lord after all).<br /> <br /> If it was my game I wouldn't allow it, but if you've gotta choose a circle and ambition, I'd say Solar Ambition 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T09:33:09-07:00","id":1149145,"title":"","content":"What about just giving the capacity to become a sorcerer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T14:58:11-07:00","id":1149243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1149051#post1149051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about linking two places with a portal/door that would allow people stepping throught to be transported from one to the other?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd peg that at Celestial 3. I think the utility and power of moving instantly between two points in the same realm is about equal to that of opening a portal between realms, and the latter is canonically Celestial 3. I might call it Celestial 2 if the distance was relatively short - no more than a couple days' journey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T15:03:25-07:00","id":1149244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1149145#post1149145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about just giving the capacity to become a sorcerer?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd call that Solar Ambition 2, myself. I agree with armyofwhispers about not allowing a working of &quot;you automatically initiate as a sorcerer&quot; at all, but if I <i>were</i> to allow it, I'd put it at Solar 3 myself, so Solar 2 for giving everyone the <i>potential</i> to initiate seems right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T16:22:06-07:00","id":1149265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1149244#post1149244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd call that Solar Ambition 2, myself. I agree with armyofwhispers about not allowing a working of &amp;quot;you automatically initiate as a sorcerer&amp;quot; at all, but if I <i>were</i> to allow it, I'd put it at Solar 3 myself, so Solar 2 for giving everyone the <i>potential</i> to initiate seems right.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about just 1 person?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T16:39:40-07:00","id":1149266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1149265#post1149265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about just 1 person?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar 1 sounds right for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T13:39:52-07:00","id":1149517,"title":"","content":"As indicated by my previous post, I disagree. An inheritable mutation that basically allows you to become a sorceror with Occult 3 but without needing to buy a shaping ritual is a big deal, but it's not a game breaker. Occult 3 is a considerable accomplishment, it's well above &quot;regular professional&quot; skill level, and the mutation itself is established in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T14:55:11-07:00","id":1149546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1149517#post1149517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An inheritable mutation that basically allows you to become a sorceror with Occult 3 but without needing to buy a shaping ritual is a big deal, but it's not a game breaker. Occult 3 is a considerable accomplishment, it's well above &quot;regular professional&quot; skill level, and the mutation itself is established in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. I suppose (assuming that you're referring to Ysyr as the mutation granting sorcery) that the Solar-scale effect in that is really granting everybody in a wide area the sorcery mutation, rather than the fact that it's granting it at all. I could see pulling it down a bit. I still wouldn't use Terrestrial 2, though, even if that's the normal level to grant mutations, and Ysyr-style sorcery is eventually modeled as a mutation, because sorcery really isn't comparable, power-wise, to the majority of mutations. If Terrestrial-level sorcerers could do so, I think they would be going out and granting sorcerery to lots of people. Another sorcerer is potentially much more capable as an ally or a servant than someone with claws. I think it does undesirable things to the setting to make sorcery so easy to give to people. I'd put it at Celestial 2, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T15:08:05-07:00","id":1149549,"title":"","content":"I think the gameline's general take is that being able to grant people sorcerous potential on demand is a no-no. En masse and individually. If you want an individual character to have that potential, simply ask your ST and they can decide they can, even if they've not had the chance to act on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T20:47:58-07:00","id":1149593,"title":"","content":"You're both assuming that any noticeable number of sorcerors would be willing to perform such a ritual. Also, if you do some arithmetic you'll find that 10 threshold successes in 5 rolls with a difficulty above 1 is fairly difficult to get, virtually requiring various means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T20:49:46-07:00","id":1149594,"title":"","content":"Oh well. <br /> <br /> Maybe i should make a shard where Salina's last act was make a working where every mortal in creation got sorcery","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T08:14:51-07:00","id":1149686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1149593#post1149593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're both assuming that any noticeable number of sorcerors would be willing to perform such a ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, I am, given that there exist whole organizations dedicated to creating more sorcerers (the schools like the Heptagram or Valkhawsen). I can't see why such organizations wouldn't want to use a working like this to grant sorcerous potential to worthy candidates. No matter how rare Occult 3 or higher is, it's got to be less rare than the potential for sorcery!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you do some arithmetic you'll find that 10 threshold successes in 5 rolls with a difficulty above 1 is fairly difficult to get, virtually requiring various means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but means aren't that hard to get, at least for the sort of sorcerer likely to do this. An institution like the Heptagram can muster Complementary Skills, Complementary Spells, Cooperation, Sorcerous Infrastructure, and almost certainly a demesne, without particularly straining its resources. Throw in Exotic Components and Extra Time if some Great House is willing to foot the bill to have a scion of theirs made into a sorcerer, and will pay for the weird magical stuff and extra time spent by the sorcerers doing the working, and you've got so many means. Plus, this is all being done by Dragonblooded sorcerers, who (almost certainly) have dice adders and other tricks, and a Terrestrial-level working becomes almost trivial for them. <br /> <br /> All of this is why I really don't believe that granting sorcerous potential, if it's possible at all, should be allowed at Terrestrial level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T09:57:06-07:00","id":1149716,"title":"","content":"Can you, say, trigger when a sorcerous working takes effect? <br /> <br /> I wish to write a shard where Salina took one more step, but i'm not sure on how to start it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T10:10:28-07:00","id":1149720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1149716#post1149716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you, say, trigger when a sorcerous working takes effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see doing a sorcerous working that would have some effect after a certain event. The idea of a sorcerer who lets it be known that a terrible curse lies in wait for anyone who slays them sounds like a triggered working, for example.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb, I'd say that putting a simple trigger (&quot;when x event happens, do y&quot;) would be the same circle and ambition as the basic effect it produces, while more complicated triggers (&quot;when x event occurs, do y, unless events a, b, or c have already occured&quot;) or trigger delays notably longer than a reasonable mortal lifetime (&quot;A century hence, unleash this effect&quot;) would bump up the Ambition by 1 stage, as would having a trigger that's completely under the sorcerer's control (&quot;when I speak the magic word, unleash this effect on the person I speak to&quot;).<br /> <br /> Your finesse on such workings would generally determine how easy it would be to &quot;fake&quot; the trigger. With Finesse 5, it's basically only going to go off exactly when the sorcerer wants it to, whereas down at Finesse 1, accidentally setting it off is a real issue. (&quot;Your death curse triggered because someone accidentally published your obituary?!&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T10:53:21-07:00","id":1149733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1149720#post1149720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see doing a sorcerous working that would have some effect after a certain event. The idea of a sorcerer who lets it be known that a terrible curse lies in wait for anyone who slays them sounds like a triggered working, for example.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb, I'd say that putting a simple trigger (&quot;when x event happens, do y&quot;) would be the same circle and ambition as the basic effect it produces, while more complicated triggers (&quot;when x event occurs, do y, unless events a, b, or c have already occured&quot;) or trigger delays notably longer than a reasonable mortal lifetime (&quot;A century hence, unleash this effect&quot;) would bump up the Ambition by 1 stage, as would having a trigger that's completely under the sorcerer's control (&quot;when I speak the magic word, unleash this effect on the person I speak to&quot;).<br /> <br /> Your finesse on such workings would generally determine how easy it would be to &quot;fake&quot; the trigger. With Finesse 5, it's basically only going to go off exactly when the sorcerer wants it to, whereas down at Finesse 1, accidentally setting it off is a real issue. (&quot;Your death curse triggered because someone accidentally published your obituary?!&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn. <br /> <br /> What working would it be, to: <br /> <br /> Enable Dragonblooded to initiate into celestial sorcery. <br /> <br /> give every mortal sorcerous potential<br /> <br /> Make every mortal a sorcerer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T11:40:37-07:00","id":1149751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1149733#post1149733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What working would it be, to:<br /> <br /> Enable Dragonblooded to initiate into celestial sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd call that Solar 1 for a single person. If it was lower than Solar-tier, I imagine a Dragonblood or mortal sorcerer would have done it. Probably Solar 3 to upgrade a Celestial-tier sorcerer to Solar-tier (so Raksi has a hope, but it's very hard, basically). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">give every mortal sorcerous potential</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar 3, if I allowed it all. Salinea's working to give everyone in Creation <i>with pre-existing potential</i> the ability to self-initiate was already presented as pretty much the peak of sorcerous working, so Solar 3. Giving everybody potential is stronger than that, so it should be more difficult. If I allowed it at all, I might actually treat it as a higher-than-Solar tier of working, with the attendant penalties for even Solar-level sorcerers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make every mortal a sorcerer</div> </div> </div> </div>As I already stated in this thread, I wouldn't allow this. Flat out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T00:16:30-07:00","id":1149867,"title":"","content":"Perhaps this is the wrong thread, but what defines sorcerous potential?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T02:52:28-07:00","id":1149886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1149867#post1149867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps this is the wrong thread, but what defines sorcerous potential?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no detailed explanation for that intangible quality that allows Alice to become a sorcerer where Bob can't, probably because if there was, forumites would try and game the system to break the setting by cranking out a bajillion sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T13:25:35-07:00","id":1150196,"title":"","content":"Actually, there's nothing to suggest that there is any specific quality needed to initiate into sorcery beyond a great deal of learning and a mind both strong and flexible. It does seem to be difficult, and for most people it's not worth it; things like keeping up the farm or getting the trees chopped tend to take priority over reading ancient, dusty tomes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T15:00:55-07:00","id":1150216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1150196#post1150196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, there's nothing to suggest that there is any specific quality needed to initiate into sorcery beyond a great deal of learning and a mind both strong and flexible. It does seem to be difficult, and for most people it's not worth it; things like keeping up the farm or getting the trees chopped tend to take priority over reading ancient, dusty tomes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, y'know, Ysyr.<br /> <br /> If sorcery was something any dedicated mortal could do, then Ysyr's entire caste system would be crap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T16:56:05-07:00","id":1150235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1150216#post1150216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, y'know, Ysyr.<br /> <br /> If sorcery was something any dedicated mortal could do, then Ysyr's entire caste system would be crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the mutation is some kind that reduces xp cost and training times? Or some kind of favoured ability","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T22:16:04-07:00","id":1150270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1150196#post1150196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, there's nothing to suggest that there is any specific quality needed to initiate into sorcery beyond a great deal of learning and a mind both strong and flexible.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the writeup for Ysyr, it specifies that &quot;Essence emanations warped the Ys, twisting their bodies and minds\u2014and, through chance, <i>attuning them to the power of sorcery. </i>But only a handful of Ysyr\u2019s people can master the sorcerous arts.&quot; (emphasis mine).<br /> <br /> To me, that reads that it takes special conditions to &quot;attune&quot; you to sorcery, and then <i>more</i> work and effort and probably certain talents to actually put that power to use. <br /> <br /> Also, Holden has stated, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page115\">Robert confirmed</a>, since he became a dev, that sorcery requires a certain &quot;ineffable something&quot; - it's not <i>just</i> hard work and learning. If you don't have the Right Stuff, all your education and dead goats will be in vain. It's just that we pretty much always assume that PCs who choose to learn sorcery <i>do</i> happen to have what it takes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T05:26:24-07:00","id":1150305,"title":"","content":"A question on artifacts made by sorcery. Is it possible to put passive effects on it? I.e. no need for attunement or essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T08:04:44-07:00","id":1150356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1150305#post1150305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question on artifacts made by sorcery. Is it possible to put passive effects on it? I.e. no need for attunement or essence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We know regular artifacts don't always require attunement or essence commitment, so I don't see why sorcery couldn't produce them as well. In fact, the one artifact we know is produced by sorcery, the Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes, doesn't require attunement, so that's one example. Basically, I'd treat artifacts created by sorcery the same as other artifacts - if I feel they need an attunement cost to be balanced, I'll give them one, otherwise not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T21:54:12-07:00","id":1150543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1150356#post1150356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We know regular artifacts don't always require attunement or essence commitment, so I don't see why sorcery couldn't produce them as well. In fact, the one artifact we know is produced by sorcery, the Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes, doesn't require attunement, so that's one example. Basically, I'd treat artifacts created by sorcery the same as other artifacts - if I feel they need an attunement cost to be balanced, I'll give them one, otherwise not.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok! now, second question. <br /> <br /> Let's say I wish to make a crown, produced by a sorcerer. Perhaps lunar, perhaps sidereal, perhaps solar. <br /> <br /> The Exalted, wishing to help the king of a certain country, produced this crown for him. The crown, when put upon his head, assists him in ruling the country. Basically, it does stuff like speed the wheels/ bureauracy and social excellency/ bureau rectifyin method. Thing is, how much is too much? Its from a terrestrial circle sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T23:10:04-07:00","id":1150548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1150543#post1150543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say I wish to make a crown, produced by a sorcerer. Perhaps lunar, perhaps sidereal, perhaps solar. <br /> <br /> The Exalted, wishing to help the king of a certain country, produced this crown for him. The crown, when put upon his head, assists him in ruling the country. Basically, it does stuff like speed the wheels/ bureauracy and social excellency/ bureau rectifyin method. Thing is, how much is too much? Its from a terrestrial circle sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having it directly mimic Solar Charms should <i>definitely</i> put it out of the realm of mere sorcerous workings altogether, let alone Terrestrial. Probably outside the range of Craft (Artifacts) as well; at my table, I'd declare it a work of First Age Artifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T23:22:35-07:00","id":1150549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1150548#post1150548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having it directly mimic Solar Charms should <i>definitely</i> put it out of the realm of mere sorcerous workings altogether, let alone Terrestrial. Probably outside the range of Craft (Artifacts) as well; at my table, I'd declare it a work of First Age Artifice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... true. <br /> <br /> So basically just bonuses to bureaucracy and running of the state?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T05:24:03-07:00","id":1150611,"title":"","content":"One of my players wants to lift a Corrupted Words. Is a terrestrial working ambition 2 ok ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>French Exalt &amp; ST &amp; ToolMaker [<a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/\" target=\"_blank\">Website</a>]<br /> Advanced Character Generator <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1087290-advanced-character-generator#post1087290\" target=\"_blank\">Thread, </a><a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Fiche%20perso%20colab.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Excel Version</a> &amp; <a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Fiche%20perso%20colab.ods\" target=\"_blank\">LibreOffice Version</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141199-exalted-3-familiar-generator\" target=\"_blank\">Familiar Generator Thread</a> &amp; <a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Familiar%20Generator.ods\" target=\"_blank\">Libreoffice Version</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13355-refhi","name":"Refhi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13355_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T07:27:09-07:00","id":1154703,"title":"","content":"What sort of working could make it impossible for Exalts to use Charms or spells in a defined time and place (say, at night in a specific valley)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T08:02:13-07:00","id":1154715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1154703#post1154703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of working could make it impossible for Exalts to use Charms or spells in a defined time and place (say, at night in a specific valley)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would not allow this as a working period. As far as we know there is no power anyway that can prevent a Solar from using their charms. <br /> <br /> At most I'd allow a working that deadened an area to essence and restricted mote respiration during specified times. That'd be a Solar circle ambition 1 at the least though. You're changing a fundamental aspect of creation in a small area. <br /> <br /> Maybe a separate working that kinda automatically distorts sorcery cast within it at night, but again, I'd never allow for a complete blanket 'no spells zone' The distortion working would once again be at least solar 1 or maybe solar 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T08:25:06-07:00","id":1154719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1154703#post1154703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of working could make it impossible for Exalts to use Charms or spells in a defined time and place (say, at night in a specific valley)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar 3, sounds like fundamentally changing the supernatural indvidual or a city wide change to metaphysics. I'm guessing the intent is some sort of neutral ground, so I might just make it a surcharge of motes instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T09:46:38-07:00","id":1154749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1154703#post1154703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of working could make it impossible for Exalts to use Charms or spells in a defined time and place (say, at night in a specific valley)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Impossible. <br /> <br /> Charms, by definition, come from the exalted himself. You cannot interfere with it unless you can bypass their defeses first","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T10:08:29-07:00","id":1154754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1154703#post1154703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of working could make it impossible for Exalts to use Charms or spells in a defined time and place (say, at night in a specific valley)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is there anything in specific you want to block?<br /> Its a big gap, but i think a &quot;no sorcery area could be between Celestial 3 to Solar 2. With a working that mess up the gathering of sorcerous motes.<br /> For charms, you can do it by negating the action that a charm enhances. If you make a an area with magically enforced non-violence rules, the solar wont be able to use melee, because his ability to swing a sword is impaired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T07:22:01-07:00","id":1155048,"title":"","content":"Actually, the intent is a booby trap. I had an idea for a plot wherein a mortal sorcerer lures Exalts to his valley, uses this working to inhibit their powers, and captures them for sacrifice to the Yozis. His motivation is that he's been promised Infernal Exaltation if he can sacrifice a certain number of Exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T07:26:21-07:00","id":1155050,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that you're seeing Charms as &quot;powers,&quot; which is not the intended paradigm. The Solar athlete isn't using a modular superpower when he lifts an elephant overhead; rather, he is <i>strong</i>, and his Charms represent his learned ability to apply that amazing strength.<br /> <br /> Let me put it another way: what level Working would it be to create a zone where people's ability to punch one another, <i>but nothing else</i>, is turned off?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T07:40:22-07:00","id":1155053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155048#post1155048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the intent is a booby trap. I had an idea for a plot wherein a mortal sorcerer lures Exalts to his valley, uses this working to inhibit their powers, and captures them for sacrifice to the Yozis. His motivation is that he's been promised Infernal Exaltation if he can sacrifice a certain number of Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahahaha. <br /> <br /> No. <br /> <br /> Impossible. Any storyteller that allows that should be shot. <br /> <br /> What about one that transforms it into a shadowland, then then motetap them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T07:59:28-07:00","id":1155062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155053#post1155053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about one that transforms it into a shadowland, then then motetap them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Underworld doesn't stop you respiring motes in Ex3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T08:46:08-07:00","id":1155080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155048#post1155048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the intent is a booby trap. I had an idea for a plot wherein a mortal sorcerer lures Exalts to his valley, uses this working to inhibit their powers, and captures them for sacrifice to the Yozis. His motivation is that he's been promised Infernal Exaltation if he can sacrifice a certain number of Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>His best bet is to lure them into a valley and then collapse the side of the valley on them and hope they don't have charms that allow them to survive.<br /> <br /> As a sorcerous working a solar exalt at Essence 5 wouldn't be able to pull off what you're suggesting. A mortal doing it is ludicrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T09:15:57-07:00","id":1155088,"title":"","content":"There was a manacle artifact in previous editions that siphoned essence form the captured exalt. It could be a working that replicates this effect in an area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12483-ale137","name":"ale137","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T09:54:16-07:00","id":1155101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ale137</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155088#post1155088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a manacle artifact in previous editions that siphoned essence form the captured exalt. It could be a working that replicates this effect in an area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerous workings don't just get to mimic the powers of artifacts, though. Also those manacles were horseshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T10:58:42-07:00","id":1155132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155101#post1155101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerous workings don't just get to mimic the powers of artifacts, though. Also those manacles were horseshit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There was a post in the ask the devs, where Vance said that, because of how broad workings are, it cant be helped if there is some overlap with other things. So it is possible for a working to emulate the effect of an artifact.<br /> How bad is the effects is another thing, and should be discussed with the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12483-ale137","name":"ale137","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T11:17:11-07:00","id":1155137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155048#post1155048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the intent is a booby trap. I had an idea for a plot wherein a mortal sorcerer lures Exalts to his valley, uses this working to inhibit their powers, and captures them for sacrifice to the Yozis. His motivation is that he's been promised Infernal Exaltation if he can sacrifice a certain number of Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd mess with mote regeneration in someway instead, yeah. I had a few arrows that were able to delay mote regeneration some until removed from the body. Good for hunting gods as well as Exalts. <br /> <br /> In general, however, it might be better to attack from other angles. Sleeping gas, for instance, or knock out fruits or the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T20:21:42-07:00","id":1155269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155050#post1155050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is that you're seeing Charms as &quot;powers,&quot; which is not the intended paradigm. The Solar athlete isn't using a modular superpower when he lifts an elephant overhead; rather, he is <i>strong</i>, and his Charms represent his learned ability to apply that amazing strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with that at all. A mortal with Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 cannot learn to replicate the feats of a Solar with Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, no matter how he trains. The Solar is channelling and shaping Essence - effectively modifying reality - in order to perform acts that are impossible for mortals.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T20:48:25-07:00","id":1155274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155269#post1155269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree with that at all. A mortal with Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 cannot learn to replicate the feats of a Solar with Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, no matter how he trains. The Solar is channelling and shaping Essence - effectively modifying reality - in order to perform acts that are impossible for mortals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What Alucard means is, you cannot seperate a solar from his powers the way you can say...superman. It'd be like taking away heracles' strength.<br /> Superman's powers have an external source (the sun) and he can lose them to external events (blocked sun+Kyrpto-how-is-this-so-common-nite).<br /> Heracles is strong. He just <i>is</i>. We can model that strength with discrete charms, and with motes, but if you asked heracles how he did somehting, Increasing Strenth Exervcise as a phrase isn't gonna get referenced. He just exerted more effort in that task (motes here).<br /> a valley that makes Superman lose powers makes sense. There's an external that's being inhibited.<br /> a valley that reduced heracles to normal strength is trickier. A valley that generally made people less strong would do that...but that's not what &quot;they can't use charms&quot; means. Can't use charms means the super-strong are just...strong. <br /> It'd be like if Batman had all his intellect and stealth and gadgets...but not to the comic book extreme. Or if Oddesseyeus was <i>just</i> normal smart, with his extra special smart removed. Or Elijah was <i>just </i> convincing, lakcing the power his rhetoric normally had. The magic of solars builds on and is an intrinsic part of who they are. It's also why &quot;no backsies on exaltations&quot; is a rule of sorcery that can't be broken.<br /> I'd argue it's removing the genre of their abillities, which is why it's kinda a no-no (Personally? I'd allow a personal scale interference. Like the shackles or something that overcame their personal defenses. An <i>entire valley</i> doing it passively though? Seems a bit much). <br /> <br /> For the booby trap, however, somehting that sapped your strength (meaning you had charms, but their effectiveness was diminished bc A) your dice pool might be diminished, and b) your starting at a lower number)? Sounds good. Hell, just inflict tons of penalites with it, via painwracking poisons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T21:42:27-07:00","id":1155286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155269#post1155269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mortal with Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 cannot learn to replicate the feats of a Solar with Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, no matter how he trains.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about when he trains so hard that he <i>does</i> replicate the Solar's results, and the Sun himself recognizes his devotion to excellence, and places a mark upon his brow?<br /> <br /> (I also dispute the notion that a Solar <i>simply spending Essence</i> is &quot;modifying reality.&quot; It's flexing your muscles, not Wyld-Shaping Technique.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-03-2017, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T06:46:55-07:00","id":1155371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155286#post1155286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about when he trains so hard that he <i>does</i> replicate the Solar's results, and the Sun himself recognizes his devotion to excellence, and places a mark upon his brow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then he's no longer a mortal, and my point stands. Please don't be disingenuous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (I also dispute the notion that a Solar <i>simply spending Essence</i> is &quot;modifying reality.&quot; It's flexing your muscles, not Wyld-Shaping Technique.) </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what spending Essence does, and Wyld-Shaping Technique is a great example. The Solar shapes Essence to congeal a new pocket of reality out of the infinite possibility of the Wyld. Increasing Strength Exercise shapes Essence to make the Solar stronger than she normally is: reality is changing, even if the only part of it that changes is the Solar herself.<br /> <br /> We see the same phenomenon in sorcery. What does a sorcerer gather in order to change reality? Sorcerous motes of Essence. Essence is what Creation is made of. Modifying the flow of Essence is, by definition, modifying reality.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T06:51:33-07:00","id":1155372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155371#post1155371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly what spending Essence does, and Wyld-Shaping Technique is a great example. The Solar shapes Essence to congeal a new pocket of reality out of the infinite possibility of the Wyld. Increasing Strength Exercise shapes Essence to make the Solar stronger than she normally is: reality is changing, even if the only part of it that changes is the Solar herself.<br /> <br /> We see the same phenomenon in sorcery. What does a sorcerer gather in order to change reality? Sorcerous motes of Essence. Essence is what Creation is made of. Modifying the flow of Essence is, by definition, modifying reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting aside my opinions on solars being mortal, it is worth noting that sorcerous motes are not normal motes. You can't cast obsidian butterflies with Solar motes this go around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T22:24:23-07:00","id":1155648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155372#post1155372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Putting aside my opinions on solars being mortal</div> </div> </div> </div>The game itself uses &quot;mortal&quot; as shorthand for &quot;non-Exalted humans,&quot; and I believe it is perfectly clear that I'm using it the same way. Again: please don't be disingenuous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it is worth noting that sorcerous motes are not normal motes. You can't cast obsidian butterflies with Solar motes this go around. </div> </div> </div>Misleading. Solars may no longer draw on their own internal reserves of Essence for sorcery, but they're still shaping Essence.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T22:49:41-07:00","id":1155652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155648#post1155648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game itself uses &quot;mortal&quot; as shorthand for &quot;non-Exalted humans,&quot; and I believe it is perfectly clear that I'm using it the same way. Again: please don't be disingenuous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't mean to be. It's a nitpick I have w/the book as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155648#post1155648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Misleading. Solars may no longer draw on their own internal reserves of Essence for sorcery, but they're still shaping Essence.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Alright then, straight to the point:<br /> I disagree that Sorcerous Motes=Solar Motes, based on that factor that Sorcerous is external and does wildly different themes. However this is all mostly irrelevant to your question regarding a working. This is best for another thread.<br /> THat being said, I'd say no. You can't stop people from using their charms. This discussion regarding whether or not Exalts are mortal or whether charms are powers is mostly irrelevant. Straight to the point: It's interfering with an exaltation. THe working closes to this is Solar Ambition 2 (Equivalent of making a demon a god).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T23:34:32-07:00","id":1155656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1155269#post1155269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree with that at all. A mortal with Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 cannot learn to replicate the feats of a Solar with Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, no matter how he trains. The Solar is channelling and shaping Essence - effectively modifying reality - in order to perform acts that are impossible for mortals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We can all argue about what is and isn't a 'power' but how about I simply refer you to the exalted core book? Read the intro to the charms chapter. Especially the bit about 'depicting charms'. It's on page 250 of the 3E core.<br /> <br /> In short what you're saying is that the guys in wuxia movies are casting spells when they leap from the tops of trees and bound accross the water. Your argument implies that batman is a wizard because he's casting spells when he analyses a crime scene. Or the bride is using a magical power when she causes Bill's heart to explode in Kill Bill. None of this is true, and it's not true of the solar exalted either. The solars are not Shazam in other words.<br /> <br /> Charms are not something that can be switched off. There is nothing that can cut off access to his powers because they're not some place else that he's getting access to. Charms are the solar and the solar is the charms. It's like you're asking how to stop someone from accessing their brain. It's a meaningless sentence. You want to stop someone from thinking? You kill them. You want to stop a Solar from using her charms? You gotta kill her first.<br /> <br /> The external magical powers you're talking about? That's sorcery. You know how you stop sorcery? Countermagic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T19:19:02-08:00","id":1157677,"title":"","content":"Hello all, I was wondering what circle and ambition would you think is appropriate to transform an NPC's Volcano Cutter into an arm for an NPC? One of my players just assisted one of my NPC's, saving his life but the npc was nearly killed and still lost his right arm, but has Volcano Cutter so one of the players wanted to transform it into a new arm, ala Wormtail from Harry Potter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T19:52:53-08:00","id":1157682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1157677#post1157677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all, I was wondering what circle and ambition would you think is appropriate to transform an NPC's Volcano Cutter into an arm for an NPC? One of my players just assisted one of my NPC's, saving his life but the npc was nearly killed and still lost his right arm, but has Volcano Cutter so one of the players wanted to transform it into a new arm, ala Wormtail from Harry Potter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Huh. Intreasting. Keeping Evocations and everything?<br /> ...I'm stealing at least part of that idea. Anyway, I'd say Celestial, between ambition 2-3, depending on the nature of the arm (Can it use evocations? What level artifact weapon is it? Is it inert if motes aren't committed? Etc). I'd lean towards 3, since the power set of an artifact is comparable to a full charmset more than a one off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T00:13:08-08:00","id":1158103,"title":"","content":"A question on finesse. <br /> <br /> Congrats, you can now inflict mutations on your mortal warrior bodyguard. <br /> <br /> You wish to make him the fightiest fighter, ever. So you give him stuff like enhanced healing, sleeplessness, and natural armour and bladeproof skin. And you make it all internal. Cause you don't want him to stand out too much. <br /> <br /> So if you make it Finesse 1, how would it be like? His wounds glow as they knit together, showing his supernatural healing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T12:54:24-08:00","id":1158257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1158103#post1158103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You wish to make him the fightiest fighter, ever. So you give him stuff like enhanced healing, sleeplessness, and natural armour and bladeproof skin. And you make it all internal. Cause you don't want him to stand out too much.<br /> <br /> So if you make it Finesse 1, how would it be like? His wounds glow as they knit together, showing his supernatural healing?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the working was designed to make the abilities it granted non-obvious (which would raise the Ambition of the working, above the default for &quot;add mutations to somebody&quot;), then I'd treat them being non-obvious as part of the point, so low-finesse complications shouldn't subvert that. Glowing when they heal does that, I'd say, so I'd look for other things for low-finesse to do. Some suggestions:<ul><li>Using the mutations involves burning a lot of energy, so whenever they get used, the person has to eat a huge meal and take a long nap afterwards.</li> <li>The mutations aren't actually added to the character's body inherently. Instead, they're tied to an amulet or other piece of jewelry. If someone can get that item off them, the mutations would slowly fade from the servant, while the other person developed them.</li> <li>The life of your servant is now tied to you. If they get too far from you (say, over 20 yards), they start to weaken and lose the mutations, and will eventually die. They've now got to be around you all the time, even in intimate moments.</li> <li>The mutations draw from the sorcerer's life-force to power things, particularly the regeneration. For every, say, 4 health levels the bodyguard heals, the sorcerer suffers one.</li> <li>The mutations channel some kind of martial arts prowess. The servant has to assume an appropriate martial arts form to gain the benefit, and if they assume another form, the benefits end.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T22:55:45-08:00","id":1158782,"title":"","content":"Let's say, using the mutations system and sorcerous workings, i get a bat and lizard hybrid, which is the size of a yeddim, with extra soak and armour, plus the ability to fly. <br /> <br /> Now, the only thing left is the breathe attack. Is this terrestrial circle or celestial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T23:38:10-08:00","id":1158786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1158782#post1158782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say, using the mutations system and sorcerous workings, i get a bat and lizard hybrid, which is the size of a yeddim, with extra soak and armour, plus the ability to fly. <br /> <br /> Now, the only thing left is the breathe attack. Is this terrestrial circle or celestial?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue it depends on the nature of the breath attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T00:37:03-08:00","id":1158798,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Alucard is right. The sorcerer in my game made Dragons, and their breath weapon counted as a heavy ranged non-magical attack with the Flame quality. I think that's just Terrestrial 2 level, max. It's just the same as a firewand, after all.<br /> <br /> If the breath weapon was much better than a regular weapon, it might be Celestial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T01:11:11-08:00","id":1158811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1158798#post1158798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Alucard is right. The sorcerer in my game made Dragons, and their breath weapon counted as a heavy ranged non-magical attack with the Flame quality. I think that's just Terrestrial 2 level, max. It's just the same as a firewand, after all.<br /> <br /> If the breath weapon was much better than a regular weapon, it might be Celestial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa. Really. The idea i had had the dragon being used like in asoiaf, i.e. flying artillery. Able to fly over the enemy army and decimate it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T09:13:24-08:00","id":1158976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1158811#post1158811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoa. Really. The idea i had had the dragon being used like in asoiaf, i.e. flying artillery. Able to fly over the enemy army and decimate it</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that unless the dragon has, like, a huge passive Hardness, flying by with the intent of raining down fire from above will <i>probably</i> result in it being brought down by a legion of soldiers firing arrows into its belly. <br /> <br /> Getting hit by a battle group's attack is no joke.<br /> <br /> (Also, the sort of devastation you're suggesting, assuming you intend the more modern use of &quot;decimate&quot; as opposed to its historical meaning, is probably higher-caliber than a firewand, so I'd rank that as Celestial.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-15-2017, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T09:21:26-08:00","id":1158986,"title":"","content":"That's truly unfortunate. <br /> <br /> What about giving sorcerers the ability to shoot lightning from their eyes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T09:57:33-08:00","id":1159009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1158986#post1158986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's truly unfortunate.<br /> <br /> What about giving sorcerers the ability to shoot lightning from their eyes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Celestial 2. It's literally one of the examples: &quot;Grant a supernatural power to one\u2019s self or to a willing subject, such as a burning gaze...&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T10:05:34-08:00","id":1159020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1159009#post1159009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Celestial 2. It's literally one of the examples: &amp;quot;Grant a supernatural power to one\u2019s self or to a willing subject, such as a burning gaze...&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats the problem. <br /> <br /> There is a mutation called natural missile. <br /> <br /> Natural Missile: One of the mutant\u2019s non-clinching <br /> natural attacks can be used at range, gaining Range 10. He might fire regenerating bone claws from his fist, shoot beams of Essence from his palms, or launch missile pods from ports built into his legs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T10:51:46-08:00","id":1159061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1159020#post1159020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats the problem.<br /> <br /> There is a mutation called natural missile.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a 2nd Edition thing, not 3rd edition. I would be extremely cautious in assuming you can just port them over. If a &quot;natural weapon&quot; mutation merit appears in 3rd ed, I'd expect it to not involve shooting lightning at all. It will probably be more &quot;I have a natural spike/dart/poison jet that I can fire once, then has to regrow&quot;. Duplicating a bolt of elemental energy is a bit too openly supernatural compared to most example mutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T12:21:55-08:00","id":1159118,"title":"","content":"I dunno, having your flesh turned into stone or other weird stuff seems pretty common for wyld mutations. At least, the supernatural merits are pretty overt. The Subtlety mutation even specifies that the wyld usually doesn't grant it on its own. <br /> <br /> I don't think that the aesthetics of a mutation effect much the mechanics of it. For instance you could take the &quot;throws lightning from eyes&quot; mutation and treat it like a capacitor that needs to be recharged instead of spines that need to be regrown. <br /> <br /> Your point stands on it being a 2E thing and not automatically translatable into 3E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T12:43:16-08:00","id":1159124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1157682#post1157682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...Huh. Intreasting. Keeping Evocations and everything?<br /> ...I'm stealing at least part of that idea. Anyway, I'd say Celestial, between ambition 2-3, depending on the nature of the arm (Can it use evocations? What level artifact weapon is it? Is it inert if motes aren't committed? Etc). I'd lean towards 3, since the power set of an artifact is comparable to a full charmset more than a one off.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea is that the new arm would be keeping similar evocations, but would require in character adjustments over time and likely doing entirely new trials to open up the evocations, with the character getting their evocation experience back, so they can rebuy them over time. Thank you for the advice on the circle and ambition level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T18:43:27-08:00","id":1159289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1159118#post1159118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, having your flesh turned into stone or other weird stuff seems pretty common for wyld mutations. At least, the supernatural merits are pretty overt. The Subtlety mutation even specifies that the wyld usually doesn't grant it on its own.<br /> <br /> I don't think that the aesthetics of a mutation effect much the mechanics of it. For instance you could take the &quot;throws lightning from eyes&quot; mutation and treat it like a capacitor that needs to be recharged instead of spines that need to be regrown.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book's pretty clear, though, that supernatural powers are a Celestial-tier thing, not Terrestrial. I think I'd guess that there's basically an unspoken caveat of &quot;<i>natural</i>&quot; on the mutations that Terrestrial-tier can give you - that is, they have to represent abilities or traits that some natural creature could have in Creation, without being empowered by essence or something. That's going to limit your lightning-bolt-shooting, for sure - since electric eels exist, you probably can use Terrestrial to give yourself <i>some</i> electrical generating capability, but it should be within natural bounds, so it would recharge on a timescale of minutes, at least, not combat turns, and there'd be some biological organs or something behind it, it wouldn't just be &quot;channelling Air essence&quot; or something to produce lightning on demand. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T15:49:01-08:00","id":1159601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1158976#post1158976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that unless the dragon has, like, a huge passive Hardness, flying by with the intent of raining down fire from above will <i>probably</i> result in it being brought down by a legion of soldiers firing arrows into its belly.<br /> <br /> Getting hit by a battle group's attack is no joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make it a hive dragon of deadly flesh eating bombardier beetles, it can deploy swarms of them as battle groups. The more it deploys the more it shrinks. On the other side if they destroy enemy battle group they can increase their number and when they return to the dragon to be reabsorbed it will grow bigger.<br /> <br /> Make is so bombardier beetles can start fires and with the Ifrit initiation you are all set <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T20:13:52-08:00","id":1159688,"title":"","content":"Oh hey. Thats interesting. <br /> <br /> I remember a species of ants capable of overloading glands to explode. Maybe give the hive mutation, then basically have a walkif nest of flying grenades?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T01:03:57-08:00","id":1159743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1158811#post1158811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whoa. Really. The idea i had had the dragon being used like in asoiaf, i.e. flying artillery. Able to fly over the enemy army and decimate it</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am the player from that game and the dragons I designed are more like what happens if a dragon is just a large reptile that exists with a couple of extras. Rather than being a high fantasy Dragon like Elric or GoT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T10:25:19-07:00","id":1195779,"title":"","content":"Reviving this thread because it seems pretty variable in purpose. If that's a faux pas I'm sorry. <br /> <br /> I have the idea of someone taking a hearthstone and permanently copying it's power within themselves. It's effect becoming a supernatural merit or mutation at that point, that I'd prefer to be able to be inheritable.<br /> <br /> The hearthstone I had in mind for this ritual was The Chameleon Stone. A Standard Lunar Hearthstone that was detailed in 611 of the 3E core, which has the effect of allowing one to transform their features to blend in the natives of the local region for a point of willpower. <br /> <br /> My estimate is that effect would count as 4 dot supernatural Merit considering the Chameleon merit that allows one to simply change their colour to match their surroundings is 3 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T15:02:30-07:00","id":1195859,"title":"","content":"Havent read the whole and i am lazy. Was alchemy ever discussed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:43:11-07:00","id":1195897,"title":"","content":"A transmogrifier, a machine that can turn a person or an animal into another creature until changed back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11692-amseriah","name":"Amseriah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T19:23:11-07:00","id":1195929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments#post733522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Say I wanted to give myself an eternal lifespan with a sorcerous working. What Circle do you believe would be required for that, and at what level of Ambition? Obviously there would be caveats to the lifespan due to the limitations of sorcery, but how do I get there in the first place? Or what if I merely wanted to use it to double my lifespan with a one-time working?<br /> <br /> Assume I'm not a Sidereal; we know it probably won't work there.</div> </div> </div> </div> If I was your ST I would most likely put it at a Celestial 2 with finesse 3 or Celestial one for Finesse 5. Would depend on what you put forward as ingredients to make the effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T20:17:34-07:00","id":1195937,"title":"","content":"I have a few workings ideas. I will list the idea below.<br /> <br /> Creating as big a field as the constraints of Terrestrial or Celestial or Solar working would allow. The field will be vineyard and the grapes either are modified to collect ambient essence in them or the plants pull it in from the soil. The grapes are then turned into wine and stored. after 3 years they mature into exceptional tasting wine to mortals. To spirits this essence wine is exceptionally tasty and can help them respire motes faster for up to one hour after they finish drinking a bottle.<br /> <br /> To geomantically sculpt an area to cause the formation of a manse in either 1 season or one year. Minor/Major/Legendary whichever on or ones would be considered allowed.<br /> <br /> To create an air ward over a city 50K or less people to prevent aerial enemies from dropping things on the city or dive bombing inhabitants. Like an essence net or field that only becomes visible when struck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T13:14:57-07:00","id":1196196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>drakor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1195937#post1195937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few workings ideas. I will list the idea below.<br /> <br /> Creating as big a field as the constraints of Terrestrial or Celestial or Solar working would allow. The field will be vineyard and the grapes either are modified to collect ambient essence in them or the plants pull it in from the soil. The grapes are then turned into wine and stored. after 3 years they mature into exceptional tasting wine to mortals. To spirits this essence wine is exceptionally tasty and can help them respire motes faster for up to one hour after they finish drinking a bottle.<br /> <br /> To geomantically sculpt an area to cause the formation of a manse in either 1 season or one year. Minor/Major/Legendary whichever on or ones would be considered allowed.<br /> <br /> To create an air ward over a city 50K or less people to prevent aerial enemies from dropping things on the city or dive bombing inhabitants. Like an essence net or field that only becomes visible when struck.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Yeah, this depends on the field size<br /> 2. Celestial, depending on how manse construction works (I legitmately have 0 idea, but making a magic place sounds like Celesital 3's make a gate to another world)<br /> 3. scale indicates solar to me.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T13:17:36-07:00","id":1196197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1195859#post1195859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Havent read the whole and i am lazy. Was alchemy ever discussed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at length, in part because alchemy might be a thautmurgy instead or a normal skill. I'd say most is probably terrestrial, because...well, Terrestrial moves natural to natural. The magical metals are probably different, but otherwise, lead to gold seems like a Terrestrial working.<br /> Now, the philospher stone/pancea/etc? Probably Celestial 2, depending on the substance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T02:33:51-07:00","id":1196753,"title":"","content":"What do folks think a working to trap an enemy (previously knocked out and bound) within a mirror where he could be tormented by the reflections of people standing in front of it would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T03:18:22-07:00","id":1196757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1196753#post1196753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do folks think a working to trap an enemy (previously knocked out and bound) within a mirror where he could be tormented by the reflections of people standing in front of it would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is he trapped forever? Will a year of torment occur inside, only for him to come out and realize only a minute has passed outside? <br /> <br /> I'd say Celestial, probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T05:45:29-07:00","id":1196768,"title":"","content":"Remove the need for breathing, sleep, drinking and eating. Or just breathing and sleeping. What kind of working?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4567-volivat","name":"Volivat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T18:55:07-07:00","id":1196999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1196757#post1196757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is he trapped forever? Will a year of torment occur inside, only for him to come out and realize only a minute has passed outside?<br /> <br /> I'd say Celestial, probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trapped indefinitely until someone frees him via sorcerous working or a Charm/anima effect that can force a spirit to materialize. (I'm envisioning it as effectively dematerializing him and trapping him in a custom sanctum.) Time passes at the same rate for him as everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T19:16:41-07:00","id":1197003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1157677#post1157677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all, I was wondering what circle and ambition would you think is appropriate to transform an NPC's Volcano Cutter into an arm for an NPC? One of my players just assisted one of my NPC's, saving his life but the npc was nearly killed and still lost his right arm, but has Volcano Cutter so one of the players wanted to transform it into a new arm, ala Wormtail from Harry Potter.</div> </div> </div> </div> From just a personal perspective I would have someone do a craft: Artifacts roll to remodel the volcano cutter for this. But to stay on theme of the discussion for workings I would have to ask how the player would go about it. I found with the game I play in my ST has regularly told me workings have two components. The idea of the working, and how is it carried out. So you have the idea together but how would your character or the party carry out changing a powerful artifact 5 sword into a PC's arm ? With no additional information I would say low end would be Celestial 1 and high end would be Solar 1. Also I would set the finesse at 5 for anything under solar 1 on this one.<br /> <br /> The things that affect what I would ultimately peg the level at would be:<br /> 1. How much of the Volcano Cutters abilities would the arm retain? From a scale of all to none. At none I would let it go at a celestial one.<br /> 2. How is the weapon getting reforged into an arm?<br /> 3. How will the player equip and use the arm? Detachable? Permanent?<br /> 4. What materials or items will they be using to do this?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T19:29:53-07:00","id":1197008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1150543#post1150543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok! now, second question.<br /> <br /> Let's say I wish to make a crown, produced by a sorcerer. Perhaps lunar, perhaps sidereal, perhaps solar.<br /> <br /> The Exalted, wishing to help the king of a certain country, produced this crown for him. The crown, when put upon his head, assists him in ruling the country. Basically, it does stuff like speed the wheels/ bureaucracy and social excellency/ bureau rectifying method. Thing is, how much is too much? Its from a terrestrial circle sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wanted to chime in on this one as I was reading through the posts. I like the idea of this and the idea is solid but the effect the player wants to try to do is really nebulous. I thought I would offer a few ideas I would try to guide them on to help narrow down what it can do.<br /> <br /> * Allow the King to guess an intimacy of anyone who comes to petition him in court.<br /> * Anyone who fails a resolve role against the king when he makes a decree gains the minor intimacy Respect: King<br /> * Allow the king to make a roll against a targets resolve to levy a minor curse or geas that makes the target do something beneficial for the kingdom.<br /> * Any decree the king personally puts into effect make a roll. Multiply the speed at which it would be implemented by the number of successes.<br /> * As long as the king wheres the crown he is immune to mundane poisons and diseases.<br /> * As long as the crown is worn while having private time with his Queen / Consort / Concubine if a pregnancy occurs he can choose for it to be a boy or girl.<br /> <br /> There are a ton of ways a crown could support or help a ruler the effects above are just a few. I would put it from terrestrial 3 to celestial 2 for pretty much any of the effects above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T06:51:59-07:00","id":1197581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>drakor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197008#post1197008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wanted to chime in on this one as I was reading through the posts. I like the idea of this and the idea is solid but the effect the player wants to try to do is really nebulous. I thought I would offer a few ideas I would try to guide them on to help narrow down what it can do.<br /> <br /> * Anyone who fails a resolve role against the king when he makes a decree gains the minor intimacy Respect: King<br /> * Allow the king to make a roll against a targets resolve to levy a minor curse or geas that makes the target do something beneficial for the kingdom.<br /> * Any decree the king personally puts into effect make a roll. Multiply the speed at which it would be implemented by the number of successes.<br /> <br /> There are a ton of ways a crown could support or help a ruler the effects above are just a few. I would put it from terrestrial 3 to celestial 2 for pretty much any of the effects above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but...<br /> <br /> One. What if I want stuff like 2 or 3 from that list?<br /> <br /> Ok, I have an idea. A plant/ vine/ kudzu. Incredibly hard to kill via natural sources. But incredibly easy to burn. Let's say that it can easily survive in stony ground or barren wastelands. Its roots burrow into the earth and brea it to pieces. It produces chemicals and drugs and things that speed up the development and fertility and richness of the soil around it.<br /> <br /> Basically, a hard to kill vine that can easily be disposed of via fire, that terraforms barrne earth into fertile soil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 03-20-2018, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T12:29:50-07:00","id":1197708,"title":"","content":"That sounds like one of those things that could reshape the entire setting. I don't know that I'd permit it at my table, but if I did, it'd be a Solar working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T13:19:49-07:00","id":1197722,"title":"","content":"Limiting it to only within the same sort of area that Benediction of Archgenesis has with the plant/vine/kudzu unable to thrive outside that area seems like it would be doable for a Solar working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T19:45:16-07:00","id":1197844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197581#post1197581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but...<br /> <br /> One. What if I want stuff like 2 or 3 from that list?<br /> <br /> Ok, I have an idea. A plant/ vine/ kudzu. Incredibly hard to kill via natural sources. But incredibly easy to burn. Let's say that it can easily survive in stony ground or barren wastelands. Its roots burrow into the earth and brea it to pieces. It produces chemicals and drugs and things that speed up the development and fertility and richness of the soil around it.<br /> <br /> Basically, a hard to kill vine that can easily be disposed of via fire, that terraforms barrne earth into fertile soil.</div> </div> </div> </div> For making the vine that can break up the soil over time I would put it on Terrestrial 3 since it really is just magnifying natural ability of the vine a bit. If you add in that it causes the rocks or barren soil to breakup and makes it fertile I would put it at Celestial 2 area. I would use Ambition levels to denote how quickly it would make the soil more fertile and how much or quickly it could spread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T20:09:51-07:00","id":1197856,"title":"","content":"What would you do for a lake who's fish turn those that eat them into deep ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T21:26:13-07:00","id":1197885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197856#post1197856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you do for a lake who's fish turn those that eat them into deep ones?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd put that at Solar Ambition 2 - it sounds comparable to me to &quot;Enchant a city-sized region or a group to change the nature of the afterlife for those who die within it...&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T05:53:31-07:00","id":1197948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197885#post1197885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd put that at Solar Ambition 2 - it sounds comparable to me to &quot;Enchant a city-sized region or a group to change the nature of the afterlife for those who die within it...&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I think he meant a physical transformation upon eating. <br /> <br /> I mean, to boil it down, it pretty much.... <br /> <br /> Wait. <br /> <br /> What exactly are deep ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T05:57:36-07:00","id":1197950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>drakor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197844#post1197844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For making the vine that can break up the soil over time I would put it on Terrestrial 3 since it really is just magnifying natural ability of the vine a bit. If you add in that it causes the rocks or barren soil to breakup and makes it fertile I would put it at Celestial 2 area. I would use Ambition levels to denote how quickly it would make the soil more fertile and how much or quickly it could spread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial 2? <br /> <br /> Have you heard of the three sisters? <br /> <br /> I think the 'making the soil fertile' thing should be perfectly attainable by terrestrial level. Its what beans and legumes do naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T06:10:51-07:00","id":1197952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197950#post1197950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you heard of the three sisters?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do maize, winter squash, and beans have to do with your magical drug-producing kudzu?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197950#post1197950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the 'making the soil fertile' thing should be perfectly attainable by terrestrial level.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, if it's something that's almost certain to sweep over the entire setting and change the dynamics of Creation, <i>I disagree</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197950#post1197950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its what beans and legumes do naturally.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a drastically lesser extent than the plant you suggested. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197948#post1197948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What exactly are deep ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're an immortal, aquatic species of fish-frog-men who worship and serve Dagon, Mother Hydra, and Cthulhu and his loathsome ilk, presented in the fiction of H.P. Lovecraft. They do not die except by accident or violence; the offspring they sire on humans <i>will</i> eventually become Deep Ones themselves, barring that they don't die prior to that.<br /> <br /> Depending on <i>how</i> faithfully one wants to adhere to Lovecraft's details, the suitability of this as a sorcerous working would also be suspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-21-2018, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.t