b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197959#post1197959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they got superpowers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking mutations like hideous, gills, unusual hide, maybe natural weapon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T08:56:35-07:00","id":1197990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197961#post1197961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking mutations like hideous, gills, unusual hide, maybe natural weapon</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah. Celestial 2 or 3. It's just mutations. Terrestrial enables mutations for a single being. This is just for a... small lake. <br /> <br /> It's small, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T10:09:48-07:00","id":1198019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197990#post1197990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial 2 or 3. It's just mutations. Terrestrial enables mutations for a single being. This is just for a... small lake.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I'm recommending Solar is because of its ongoing nature, affecting <i>everyone</i> who eats the fish, and this effect would persist forever, or at least until the lake was destroyed or something. Affecting one creature with mutations is Terrestrial, affecting a &quot;whole ecosystem&quot; with mutations is Celestial, but by my reading, both of those are one-off things - you hit the creature or creatures with mutations, they go their way, and while they might pass the mutations on if they reproduce, other creatures aren't getting mutated with the same working. I think &quot;constantly afflicting mutations on anyone who comes in an area&quot; (which this basically is) is enough of a jump in capability that it justifies the higher Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T11:39:56-07:00","id":1198049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1198019#post1198019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason I'm recommending Solar is because of its ongoing nature, affecting <i>everyone</i> who eats the fish, and this effect would persist forever, or at least until the lake was destroyed or something. Affecting one creature with mutations is Terrestrial, affecting a &amp;quot;whole ecosystem&amp;quot; with mutations is Celestial, but by my reading, both of those are one-off things - you hit the creature or creatures with mutations, they go their way, and while they might pass the mutations on if they reproduce, other creatures aren't getting mutated with the same working. I think &amp;quot;constantly afflicting mutations on anyone who comes in an area&amp;quot; (which this basically is) is enough of a jump in capability that it justifies the higher Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my concern yeah. A mutated fish is easy. Solar sounds rifht for a constant mutagenic fish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T11:42:18-07:00","id":1198051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197950#post1197950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial 2? <br /> <br /> Have you heard of the three sisters? <br /> <br /> I think the 'making the soil fertile' thing should be perfectly attainable by terrestrial level. Its what beans and legumes do naturally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Refertlozing one area by kudzu means is fine, but this sounds like \u201cterraform the deserts in a few days\u201d level. Which is solar. Terrestrial might modify a normal kudzu plant to decay more slowly(creating a layer of nutrient soil) but growing at a regular rate and having trouble in deserts at first at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T06:22:48-07:00","id":1198306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1198051#post1198051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Refertlozing one area by kudzu means is fine, but this sounds like \u201cterraform the deserts in a few days\u201d level. Which is solar. Terrestrial might modify a normal kudzu plant to decay more slowly(creating a layer of nutrient soil) but growing at a regular rate and having trouble in deserts at first at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That's it. It's supposed to take decades to have any visible effect. A small, long term plan by a lunar planning to make more usable land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T01:46:25-07:00","id":1198979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1198049#post1198049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was my concern yeah. A mutated fish is easy. Solar sounds rifht for a constant mutagenic fish.</div> </div> </div> </div>But still, by eating the fish, the fishermen have made themselves part of the ecosystem. So the mutations pass to them. <br /> <br /> Doesn't this mean this falls under celestial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:52:25-07:00","id":1199055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1198979#post1198979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But still, by eating the fish, the fishermen have made themselves part of the ecosystem. So the mutations pass to them.<br /> <br /> Doesn't this mean this falls under celestial?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think celestial would be a wave of mutations. If you came into the ecosystem after the wave of mutations, you'd be fine.<br /> The distinction here is that things that come into the ecosystem after the wave would still get mutated by the gurgling fish.<br /> <br /> What would be the working for making a simulacra of myself, that I can control with my mind from a distnace?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:59:52-07:00","id":1199059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1199055#post1199055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think celestial would be a wave of mutations. If you came into the ecosystem after the wave of mutations, you'd be fine.<br /> The distinction here is that things that come into the ecosystem after the wave would still get mutated by the gurgling fish.<br /> <br /> What would be the working for making a simulacra of myself, that I can control with my mind from a distnace?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.... its also a boost up from the 'give a person mutations'. Creating a source to give multiple people mutations should be celestial. <br /> <br /> Anyway, probably either Terrestrial 3 or Celestial 1. <br /> <br /> Depends on how powerful is the simulacra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T22:11:28-07:00","id":1199944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1199055#post1199055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would be the working for making a simulacra of myself, that I can control with my mind from a distance?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a craft charm lets lets you make a clone the is essence 4. Due to that I would say what all can the simulacra do? Just looking like you could be in the terrestrial range. anything more and it will prolly go in to celestial range depending on the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T05:34:30-07:00","id":1199991,"title":"","content":"This is possibly not even a working - maybe just 2 dot thaumaturgy - but I want a character to be able to make walk-away talismans, with a twist.<br /> <br /> Basically whenever she kills an enemy in single combat, she stains one of her inch thick dreadlocks with its hearts-blood and it becomes a walkaway talisman against that particular type of foe (DB, solar, demon, spirit, whatever). When one of those types of being would kill her, the red dreadlock flares back to blonde again and she avoids the damage taken from that specific attack completely (aside from aesthetically split lip, cut eyebrow, etc)<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13646,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","user":"realitycheque","date":". 03-27-2018, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T06:35:53-07:00","id":1200011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>realitycheque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1199991#post1199991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is possibly not even a working - maybe just 2 dot thaumaturgy - but I want a character to be able to make walk-away talismans, with a twist.<br /> <br /> Basically whenever she kills an enemy in single combat, she stains one of her inch thick dreadlocks with its hearts-blood and it becomes a walkaway talisman against that particular type of foe (DB, solar, demon, spirit, whatever). When one of those types of being would kill her, the red dreadlock flares back to blonde again and she avoids the damage taken from that specific attack completely (aside from aesthetically split lip, cut eyebrow, etc)<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking... celestial? <br /> <br /> Any kind of attack? Even attacks that would blow up a mountain? Even a strike from an Essence 5 solar? <br /> <br /> That's kinda... the problem. This is a stackable perfect defense that comes with a heavy cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T07:06:06-07:00","id":1200019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1200011#post1200011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking... celestial?<br /> <br /> Any kind of attack? Even attacks that would blow up a mountain? Even a strike from an Essence 5 solar?<br /> <br /> That's kinda... the problem. This is a stackable perfect defense that comes with a heavy cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>In previous editions walkaway talismans weren't particularly rare (at least as far as artifacts go - only level 1), and worked against *anything*.<br /> <br /> This is a lot more focused, and yet technically stackable... although it would be fairly trivial to put a time limit on them, or a restriction of one per type. You're also not going to get one that works against a Deathlord, unless you're already powerful enough to kill one in single combat...<br /> <br /> You can see why I'm having trouble placing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T09:05:37-07:00","id":1200060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>realitycheque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1200019#post1200019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In previous editions walkaway talismans weren't particularly rare (at least as far as artifacts go - only level 1), and worked against *anything*.</div> </div> </div> </div>Source?<br /> <br /> Also, would a talisman that you got when you killed a freshly exalted dragonblooded defend you against a blow from an essence 7 dragonblooded general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T01:18:26-07:00","id":1200367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1200060#post1200060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Source?<br /> <br /> Also, would a talisman that you got when you killed a freshly exalted dragonblooded defend you against a blow from an essence 7 dragonblooded general?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have the books to reference now (all my EX1 and 2 books are in storage) but I checked the artifact level yesterday on a fan site (which I now can't find, but I seem to remember they were in the main 2E book)<br /> <br /> And yes, that would be the case (if such a dragon blooded existed, which I don't think can any more?). If you start taking potency into account, that starts getting a little complex when it comes to book-keeping so I'd ideally prefer to avoid it!<br /> <br /> I was debating having the attack leave me on -4, rather that ignoring all damage, mostly because of watching too much DbZ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T08:15:47-07:00","id":1200436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>realitycheque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1199991#post1199991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is possibly not even a working - maybe just 2 dot thaumaturgy - but I want a character to be able to make walk-away talismans, with a twist.<br /> <br /> Basically whenever she kills an enemy in single combat, she stains one of her inch thick dreadlocks with its hearts-blood and it becomes a walkaway talisman against that particular type of foe (DB, solar, demon, spirit, whatever). When one of those types of being would kill her, the red dreadlock flares back to blonde again and she avoids the damage taken from that specific attack completely (aside from aesthetically split lip, cut eyebrow, etc)<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>realitycheque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1200367#post1200367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the books to reference now (all my EX1 and 2 books are in storage) but I checked the artifact level yesterday on a fan site (which I now can't find, but I seem to remember they were in the main 2E book)<br /> [snip]<br /> <br /> I was debating having the attack leave me on -4, rather that ignoring all damage,</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing to note is that in 2e, a walkaway talisman didn't absolutely guarantee survival - it simply removed one success on a potentially-lethal damage roll (or 2 or 3 successes for a particularly strong talisman). So completely negating, or even guaranteeing you your last -4 HL, is definitely more powerful.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that this power level is definitely working-level, not just thaumaturgy. In fact, I'd peg this at Celestial. It's really a form of immortality, just with some pretty sharp limits. I'd put this at Celestial Ambition 2, because it sounds like it's granting a useful supernatural power to yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T08:48:46-07:00","id":1200450,"title":"","content":"Immortality?<br /> <br /> More like 'barebones perfect defense'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T07:33:58-07:00","id":1200797,"title":"","content":"Perfect defenses should never be free. I'm not talking the set up cost here, but the activation cost you suggest is free. Honestly, given the movement away from hyper lethal combat and perfect defenses in general I would say that walkaway talisman as a concept is no longer valid. Certainly not as an artifact 1.<br /> <br /> This idea might make sense as an artifact evocation. Probably artifact 3 (maybe artifact 4 depending on what all it does) and costing motes and a willpower to shrug off the blow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 03-29-2018, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:50:40-07:00","id":1201449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197952#post1197952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're an immortal, aquatic species of fish-frog-men who worship and serve Dagon, Mother Hydra, and Cthulhu and his loathsome ilk, presented in the fiction of H.P. Lovecraft. They do not die except by accident or violence; the offspring they sire on humans <i>will</i> eventually become Deep Ones themselves, barring that they don't die prior to that.<br /> <br /> Depending on <i>how</i> faithfully one wants to adhere to Lovecraft's details, the suitability of this as a sorcerous working would also be suspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, what part of Lovecraft's details make them unsuitable to a working? The ineheritabillity?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T17:19:18-07:00","id":1201478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1201449#post1201449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, what part of Lovecraft's details make them unsuitable to a working? The ineheritabillity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect immortality is something the sorcerous working rules explicitly forbid, let alone <i>mass</i> perfect immortality that might affect millions of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T18:36:31-07:00","id":1201498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1201478#post1201478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect immortality is something the sorcerous working rules explicitly forbid, let alone <i>mass</i> perfect immortality that might affect millions of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, gotcha, thanks!<br /> What about a talisman to communicate and control a specific type of animal? Like, krakens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T00:35:40-07:00","id":1201553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1201498#post1201498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, gotcha, thanks!<br /> What about a talisman to communicate and control a specific type of animal? Like, krakens?</div> </div> </div> </div>Communicate? That should be terrestrial. <br /> <br /> Now.... control? Probably celestial 1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T05:24:32-07:00","id":1201587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1201478#post1201478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect immortality is something the sorcerous working rules explicitly forbid, let alone <i>mass</i> perfect immortality that might affect millions of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deep One immortality is hardly perfect. It's more like agelessness; they only die of injury or disease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T05:44:35-07:00","id":1201588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1201587#post1201587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deep One immortality is hardly perfect. It's more like agelessness; they only die of injury or disease.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agelessness is <i>a kind</i> of immortality.<br /> <br /> Greek gods were immortal, and also <i>couldn't die</i> (even when their jackass dad ate them alive, or when Typhon yanked every sinew out of their bodies!).<br /> <br /> Norse gods <i>were also immortal</i>. They stayed young as long as they ate the golden apples, but could die by violence or even grief (and indeed, their ends were prophesied).<br /> <br /> There is no contradiction in the above.<br /> <br /> Immortality is <i>the ability</i> to live forever, not the guarantee.<br /> <br /> (Also the Deep Ones were immune to earthly diseases.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-31-2018, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T06:28:51-07:00","id":1201596,"title":"","content":"At this point, I am forced to conclude that you are being deliberately dense to avoid the conclusion that you could be in error. Perfect immortality means that you can't die, period. By any means, in any circumstances, no matter what. Deep One agelessness is not perfect. It has flaws, quite large, and thus is eminently permissible. Such a working would be extremely difficult, but entirely possible. I'd be inclined to call it Celestial at the least, possibly Solar. Lower if the working isn't intended to mutate the eaters of the fish into unaging creatures, but simply into creatures similar to the Gill-Man with normal lifespans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 03-31-2018, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T06:47:21-07:00","id":1201600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1201596#post1201596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point, I am forced to conclude that you are being deliberately dense to avoid the conclusion that you could be in error.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't. I'm not a psychic; I possess no ability to read the dictionary that exists inside your head. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1201596#post1201596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect immortality means that you can't die, period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that's how you define it; how was I supposed to know that?<br /> <br /> Once again, though, immortality is not the same thing as the inability to die (though it can include it), so to me, &quot;perfect immortality&quot; would be any form of immortality that doesn't require upkeep. Besides, if giving yourself the ageless kind of immortality the in-game gods possess* was supposed to be doable with sorcery, why is it treated like a mystery that Rakan Thulio hasn't aged?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ____________<br /> *At least, absent turning yourself into a spirit; I'd permit a character to attain that kind of immortality by turning himself into a god, but at that point, he'd stop being human, so the touch of the Unconquered Sun/Luna/whatever would ebb from him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-31-2018, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T07:06:05-07:00","id":1201603,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I always thought perfect immortality means that you can\u2019t die of old age/stop aging with no catches like having to bath in virgin blood every years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T07:14:02-07:00","id":1201605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1201603#post1201603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I always thought perfect immortality means that you can\u2019t die of old age/stop aging with no catches like having to bath in virgin blood every years?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I had guessed as well. So it looks like there's no consensus on it as of yet.<br /> <br /> That said, my apologies to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1184\" data-vbnamecard=\"1184\">LadyLens</a> - earlier posts of mine (since edited) suggested that she should already know there's many kinds of immortality, but in fact it wasn't in this t