l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1209073#post1209073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Okay, so here's my reasonings.<br /> <br /> 1.Evil eye effects are not just &amp;quot;oh, your dead&amp;quot;, their &amp;quot;you keep having bad things happen&amp;quot;. To me, a penalty makes sense to emulate the misfortune side of it.<br /> 2.On the other end, the wasting away do to the evil eye is gradual, so the damage aspect comes in there. Its slow, relatively speaking, and allows for characters of different constitutions to resist.<br /> 3. Poisons are also a place where the system gives Exalted an advantage already: with a good enough roll they can completely ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Ok then. <br /> <br /> I'm just stuck between setting people on fire, and a ranged non contact required curse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:06:26-07:00","id":1209439,"title":"","content":"I feel as if for a Celestial Ambition 2 working, the power granted ought to be a little more impressive than a two dot merit that goes with one of the shaping rituals. I'd say at a minimum something whose mechanics are equal to Flight of the Brilliant Raptor or Dancing Devil Trigger Finger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:26:25-07:00","id":1209448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1209439#post1209439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as if for a Celestial Ambition 2 working, the power granted ought to be a little more impressive than a two dot merit that goes with one of the shaping rituals. I'd say at a minimum something whose mechanics are equal to Flight of the Brilliant Raptor or Dancing Devil Trigger Finger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My push back is that Burnt Name is a model that doesn't need motes (and I wouldn't go straight to motes for a Celestial working). Personally, I set Celestial 2 as &quot;supernatural merits&quot; whil celestial 3 starts getting into &quot;Okay, maybe a charm&quot; effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T00:11:21-07:00","id":1210850,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this isn't the right thread for this, but it seems about right. <br /> <br /> So let's say you wanted to create a working to replicate something like the dart trap from Indiana Jones. With the working being that the dart trap is self repairing and reloading. So someone breaks the pressure plate a day or two later the springs and such will reset, darts fired will be broken down after a fashion and used to create new darts for the next time the trap is sprung. With the limitation that there aren't a limitless supply of darts, and refilling the system takes at least 24 hours assuming all it needs to do is create more darts.<br /> <br /> Would this be a terrestrial or celestial class working if you wanted to apply this to a tomb?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T05:24:22-07:00","id":1210909,"title":"","content":"Something ordinary as that?<br /> <br /> Terrestrial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T19:47:22-07:00","id":1211268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1197581#post1197581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but...<br /> <br /> One. What if I want stuff like 2 or 3 from that list?<br /> <br /> Ok, I have an idea. A plant/ vine/ kudzu. Incredibly hard to kill via natural sources. But incredibly easy to burn. Let's say that it can easily survive in stony ground or barren wastelands. Its roots burrow into the earth and brea it to pieces. It produces chemicals and drugs and things that speed up the development and fertility and richness of the soil around it.<br /> <br /> Basically, a hard to kill vine that can easily be disposed of via fire, that terraforms barren earth into fertile soil.</div> </div> </div> </div>For multiple abilities on the crown ideas i mentioned I would happily work it out with you. I would allow additional workings to the crown to add abilities. Maybe when you first made it it had ability x and after you added more runes of rulership and a gem representing each of the elemental poles it gains an additional power or two. It may be broken up into several different level workings for certain effects depending on what you wanted.<br /> <br /> For you vine I would break it down like this.<br /> <br /> Vine itself Terrestrial ambition 2 finesse 5 for it to be able to survive in poor/stony soil and be able to slowly break up rocks etc. Being hardy except against fire is doable all within this.<br /> Adding - secretions or ability to return nutrients to the soil at an unnatural rate would bump you to the Celestial 1 finesse 3 area or you could do a second terrestrial working ambition 2 finesse 5 to add this to your existing plant you made.<br /> Adding - grows really fast plops all of it to a Celestial 2 working all together finesse 5 or terrestrial 2 finesse 3 to add one more working to the vine you are making<br /> <br /> this is just solely my opinion on it. I like the idea and would encourage ideas like this in the game if I was an ST but the full combination all at once pushes it to a celestial level working if done at once or multiple terrestrial ones in my opinion to complete it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T04:46:30-07:00","id":1211361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>drakor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1211268#post1211268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For multiple abilities on the crown ideas i mentioned I would happily work it out with you. I would allow additional workings to the crown to add abilities. Maybe when you first made it it had ability x and after you added more runes of rulership and a gem representing each of the elemental poles it gains an additional power or two. It may be broken up into several different level workings for certain effects depending on what you wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. thank you. <br /> <br /> But it's only a terrestrial circle working. What are the upper limits of the evocations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:00:16-07:00","id":1212860,"title":"","content":"What would a working to give a women thaumaturgy and have it be guaranteed that her first daughter, and her first daughter's first daughter, and so on indefinitely would be born thaumaturges be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:14:19-07:00","id":1212863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1212860#post1212860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would a working to give a women thaumaturgy and have it be guaranteed that her first daughter, and her first daughter's first daughter, and so on indefinitely would be born thaumaturges be?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hm. I think it depends on where you place thautmurgy on the power scale? I'd say a solar 1 working(with Celestial 2 for granting Thaumaturgy at all). I'd also say it depends on the thaumaturgy in question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:20:08-07:00","id":1212866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1212863#post1212863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hm. I think it depends on where you place thautmurgy on the power scale? I'd say a solar 1 working(with Celestial 2 for granting Thaumaturgy at all). I'd also say it depends on the thaumaturgy in question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever the people develop.<br /> This wouldn't be a finesse 5 working where the sorcerer decided what everyone's natural thaumaturgies would be (and really, you wouldn't want to, because it'd mean they couldn't learn thaumaturgies from across the generations). Finesse 3 at most, just to guarantee that the inheritance pattern is as desired. Finesse 5 would only be worth it if, instead, it let 'em set up rules for the working to compensate for the loss of a childless firstborn and keep the thaumaturgic line going, in lieu of dictating the thaumaturgies people are born with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:22:34-07:00","id":1212867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1212866#post1212866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whatever the people develop.<br /> This wouldn't be a finesse 5 working where the sorcerer decided what everyone's natural thaumaturgies would be (and really, you wouldn't want to, because it'd mean they couldn't learn thaumaturgies from across the generations). Finesse 3 at most, just to guarantee that the inheritance pattern is as desired. Finesse 5 would only be worth it if, instead, it let 'em set up rules for the working to compensate for the loss of a childless firstborn and keep the thaumaturgic line going, in lieu of dictating the thaumaturgies people are born with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! So kinda like having the merit, but not having the rituals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:29:12-07:00","id":1212870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1212867#post1212867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! So kinda like having the merit, but not having the rituals?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no.<br /> Like, in your original post you said &quot;the thaumaturgy in question&quot; which made me think you were assuming they would all be born with a particular ritual.<br /> Not giving them a ritual would lower the ambition if anything.<br /> <br /> I was just saying &quot;I doubt any sorcerer thinking matters through would spring for 5 dots of finesse and then dictate a particular ritual for the line to carry if they were thinking in practical terms, because if the line produces a variety of rituals like natural thaumaturges do, that means there's an opportunity to pick and choose the best ones to pass down via training&quot;.<br /> <br /> You /might/ go finesse 5 just to define what happens if the lineage is severed by the childless death of a firstborn child, but even then I imagine you'd neglect to specify a particular thaumaturgy to be inherited. Plus, you'd have to be very confident in your odds of success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:35:05-07:00","id":1212875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1212870#post1212870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, no.<br /> Like, in your original post you said &quot;the thaumaturgy in question&quot; which made me think you were assuming they would all be born with a particular ritual.<br /> Not giving them a ritual would lower the ambition if anything.<br /> <br /> I was just saying &quot;I doubt any sorcerer thinking matters through would spring for 5 dots of finesse and then dictate a particular ritual for the line to carry if they were thinking in practical terms, because if the line produces a variety of rituals like natural thaumaturges do, that means there's an opportunity to pick and choose the best ones to pass down via training&quot;.<br /> <br /> You /might/ go finesse 5 just to define what happens if the lineage is severed by the childless death of a firstborn child, but even then I imagine you'd neglect to specify a particular thaumaturgy to be inherited. Plus, you'd have to be very confident in your odds of success.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ooooh. See, I'd make it a lower ambition(maybe?) if like. It was explicity exorcists or talisman makers. I assumed it was a specific ritual line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T23:18:25-07:00","id":1212954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1207473#post1207473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extracting a willing soul into a new vessel is Solar 1, so\u2026 Solar 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>This was a few pages back, but is that not how it worked for Alchemicals and everyone in Autocthonia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T05:08:04-07:00","id":1213011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1212954#post1212954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was a few pages back, but is that not how it worked for Alchemicals and everyone in Autocthonia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very different thing, that just has some superficial similarities. <br /> <br /> When Autochthonian Alice dies, and her soulgem is pried loose and its contents emptied into the Radiant Amphora, and the soul finds its way into a new gem to be implanted into a newborn\u2026 it's not Alice anymore, it's Bob.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-29-2018, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T14:57:01-07:00","id":1213190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1213011#post1213011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a very different thing, that just has some superficial similarities.<br /> <br /> When Autochthonian Alice dies, and her soulgem is pried loose and its contents emptied into the Radiant Amphora, and the soul finds its way into a new gem to be implanted into a newborn\u2026 it's not Alice anymore, it's Bob.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but it gives us the baseline. Retaining memories is a step up.<br /> Mind you the Forest Witches had an Artifact in first edition that did something similar. I'd need to read Outcasts again to get the details, but there does seem to be historical support for this kind of working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T18:31:25-07:00","id":1213255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1213190#post1213190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but it gives us the baseline. Retaining memories is a step up.<br /> Mind you the Forest Witches had an Artifact in first edition that did something similar. I'd need to read Outcasts again to get the details, but there does seem to be historical support for this kind of working.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it was impossible; I said it would be of the Solar circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T18:57:52-07:00","id":1213262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1213255#post1213255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say it was impossible; I said it would be of the Solar circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even saying that is inaccurate; just that further down the line, we will have more resources to check on identifing the level of Ambition + the Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T07:51:43-07:00","id":1213428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1213011#post1213011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a very different thing, that just has some superficial similarities.<br /> <br /> When Autochthonian Alice dies, and her soulgem is pried loose and its contents emptied into the Radiant Amphora<b>, and the soul finds its way into a new gem to be implanted into a newborn\u2026 it's not Alice anymore, it's Bob.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how Autochthonian soul gem works at all.<br /> <br /> When a person with a soulgem dies the soul is trapped in the soul gem, yes, but it leaves a mark on the soul that's identifiable in the next incarnation. Then whenever a baby is born (the normal way with a normal soul), the Luminors check the mark and look up the soul's record to see which of the Autochthonian castes they should belong to.<br /> <br /> Only after this is the soulgem of the appropriate shape implanted in the newborn's head.<br /> <br /> It has no control over the actual cycle of reincarnation other than to push pause at the time of death. The only time a soul is implanted into a body in the manner you suggest is during the creation of an Alchemical exalt. Though it's worth pointing out that the Alchemical somehow remembers a lot from their past lives despite purges between lives and yet they're <i>still</i> completely different people when reborn as an alchemical. IE, even with all the memories of Alice, it's still not gonna be Alice who comes out of the vat.<br /> <br /> Edit: Bolded the text I was specifically refuting for clarity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 04-30-2018, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T09:32:19-07:00","id":1213463,"title":"","content":"ah. Can I post links from other threads of sorcerous workings. They all have very interesting ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T10:33:06-07:00","id":1213481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1213428#post1213428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not how Autochthonian soul gem works at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies for forgetting to include the word &quot;Alchemical&quot; after &quot;newborn.&quot; Yes, a soul going into a newborn mortal does not need to be implanted into a soulgem first; my larger point still stands, <b>which is</b> that regardless of whether it's a mortal or an Alchemical, the continuity-of-personhood is not maintained in the default setup of Autochthonia, making them drastically different from the suggested Working.<br /> <br /> <i>Also</i>, even back in previous editions, the creation of soulgems was a significant mystical undertaking, hence why they used Artifact dots then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T15:00:05-07:00","id":1213538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1213481#post1213481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My apologies for forgetting to include the word &quot;Alchemical&quot; after &quot;newborn.&quot; Yes, a soul going into a newborn mortal does not need to be implanted into a soulgem first; my larger point still stands, <b>which is</b> that regardless of whether it's a mortal or an Alchemical, the continuity-of-personhood is not maintained in the default setup of Autochthonia, making them drastically different from the suggested Working.<br /> <br /> <i>Also</i>, even back in previous editions, the creation of soulgems was a significant mystical undertaking, hence why they used Artifact dots then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do wonder how soul gems will be created this edition. <br /> <br /> I think I'd actually do it by creating an artifact that with the appropriate reagents added, it can create new soulgems/recycle old ones. Otherwise I think they make more sense as workings than artifacts this time around since most artifacts are supposed to be singular wonders. Though if anywhere has the facilities for mass producing copies of low-dot artifacts it'd be Autochthon. Tough call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T15:43:02-07:00","id":1213549,"title":"","content":"I don't see why it can't just be a Craft (or possibly Occult) roll. Duplicating a soulgem's functionality in <i>Creation</i> would be an incredible feat, but in Autochthon, it's perfectly natural. I assume that Authochthon expressly designed his metaphysical infrastructure to support it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T18:44:19-07:00","id":1213627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1211361#post1211361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. thank you.<br /> <br /> But it's only a terrestrial circle working. What are the upper limits of the evocations?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would most likely cap it at 5. Now if as a player you came up with a really great idea on how to increase the power of the crown or asked if there was a way to make it able to get more evocations or powers I would work that out with you. a lot of it would depend on what the crown could already do and what you were wanting it to do that was new or upgraded to an existing power it has. I would definitely work with you on it though to make a narratively flavorful and useful item that was meaningful in use and accomplishment.<br /> <br /> For example in increasing the crowns power to be able to hold or unlock more evocations. Maybe having several powerful gods each bless that crown with a powerful blessing. Finding a reclusive sage that has a craft skill or knowledge that they work upon the crown to increase its power things like that. I wont ever try to stifle a players enthusiasm for an item but I would make it suitably challenging as it means it is the equivalent to doing a working outside the power of the workings level. Another idea would be to do a working on the king or ruler to let them develop the thaumaturgy merit and maybe open up some creative space in that realm as the crown becomes Thaumaturgically linked to the bloodline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T20:19:39-07:00","id":1213641,"title":"","content":"so was going to pitch this to my ST but I thought why not ask all you wonderful peoples here first instead.<br /> <br /> Background: I have a Twilight Solar who is mentored by and believes in a god of Lightning and Storms. I was allowed to purchase a variant of the burning name and my char can shoot lightning bolts instead of flames. so currently it is the damage of a light mortal thrown weapon to short range. what I am wanting to do is up the ability a bit. Details below.<br /> <br /> Upgrade the Burning Name Variant to do the following.<br /> Use Artifact Light Weapon Stats for damage<br /> Range extends to Medium<br /> Possibly spend motes to use it to Long range.<br /> <br /> I was looking over everything in the book and I was tending to peg this as Celestial 3 Finesse 5 for the first two items. not sure if this would allow the range extension though. Could I get some thoughts on what everyone thinks of this to help make sure this is balanced and not OP but can still get the little bit more oomph i was looking for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T20:30:00-07:00","id":1213643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>drakor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1213641#post1213641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Upgrade the Burning Name Variant to do the following.<br /> Use Artifact Light Weapon Stats for damage<br /> Range extends to Medium<br /> Possibly spend motes to use it to Long range.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd put this at Celestial 2. It seems comparable to &quot;Grant a supernatural power to oneself&quot;, particularly if you've already paid merit dots for the base effect. Finesse shouldn't change the stats, in my opinion - the working's ambition should be evaluated based on what you want, and Finesse would then adjust how that's accomplished. Everything you're asking for qualifies for Ambition 2, so you'd get it whether you had Finesse 1 or 5.<br /> <br /> What Finesse <i>might </i>affect is other elements, like what you have to do to maintain the working (with lower Finesse, perhaps you have to stand out in a lightning storm at least once a month to build up a charge) or whether it can be potentially be taken from you (maybe it's tied to that rod of amber with rabbit-fur trimming you have to wear, and if someone grabbed it, you'd lose it), or whether using the power attracted significant attention (at Finesse 1, the lightning bolt might always come down from the sky, through you, and <i>then </i>strike your target, incidentally making you <i>really obvious</i> every time you used it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T04:15:49-07:00","id":1217326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>drakor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1211268#post1211268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For multiple abilities on the crown ideas i mentioned I would happily work it out with you. I would allow additional workings to the crown to add abilities. Maybe when you first made it it had ability x and after you added more runes of rulership and a gem representing each of the elemental poles it gains an additional power or two. It may be broken up into several different level workings for certain effects depending on what you wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh oh oh. New ideas. <br /> <br /> How about this<br /> <br /> Bountiful nation: <br /> <br /> This working means that whomever wears this crown, his group, his organization, or his nation state will gain the most in whatever resources they produce. The country's primary export is food? The fields are fertile. The plants are well grown and verdant. The country is primarily mining? The mines are literally dripping with gold and silver. The end effect is not supernatural. There are no magical materials. No artifact plants. No sudden bursts of sorcerers amongst you. What it does, is that it takes what makes your nation strong, and crank it up several notches. <br /> <br /> Keen eye for talent: <br /> <br /> I got this idea while reading Iris Zero. And a homebrewed demon called Vicero, the wasteland Khan. Iris Zero: Sasamori, a girl, has the power to literally think of a job, and use signs above a person's head to determine if this person is the best suited for the job or no, denoted by a cross or a tick. Vicero has a talent for picking the best servants and those with talent. <br /> <br /> So let's say that the crown lets the king make a roll. Maybe Bureaucracy, social, or perception, or awareness. But he rolls. He botches? He gets wrong information. Maybe a alcoholic gets appointed to protect the wine cellar. He rolls ok? He manages to pick out, amongst a gathering of people, the best person for, say, leading his army. He rolls really well? He says a name, along with immediate family and appearance and circumstances, of a person that either is in his country or works under him by any means no matter how small, and that person is literally the best guy for the job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T02:13:30-07:00","id":1218835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1217326#post1217326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh oh oh. New ideas.<br /> <br /> How about this<br /> <br /> Bountiful nation:<br /> <br /> This working means that whomever wears this crown, his group, his organization, or his nation state will gain the most in whatever resources they produce. The country's primary export is food? The fields are fertile. The plants are well grown and verdant. The country is primarily mining? The mines are literally dripping with gold and silver. The end effect is not supernatural. There are no magical materials. No artifact plants. No sudden bursts of sorcerers amongst you. What it does, is that it takes what makes your nation strong, and crank it up several notches.<br /> <br /> Keen eye for talent:<br /> <br /> I got this idea while reading Iris Zero. And a homebrewed demon called Vicero, the wasteland Khan. Iris Zero: Sasamori, a girl, has the power to literally think of a job, and use signs above a person's head to determine if this person is the best suited for the job or no, denoted by a cross or a tick. Vicero has a talent for picking the best servants and those with talent.<br /> <br /> So let's say that the crown lets the king make a roll. Maybe Bureaucracy, social, or perception, or awareness. But he rolls. He botches? He gets wrong information. Maybe a alcoholic gets appointed to protect the wine cellar. He rolls ok? He manages to pick out, amongst a gathering of people, the best person for, say, leading his army. He rolls really well? He says a name, along with immediate family and appearance and circumstances, of a person that either is in his country or works under him by any means no matter how small, and that person is literally the best guy for the job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Iris:Zero! This is a really cool way to adapt an anime idea to exalted. On the idea of fields being more fertile and mines being overflowing with materials. For a crown for a power like that I would modify the description like food harvest are done so timely and well that waste that traditionally happens doesn't. Or the ores get smelted better or the veins of ore are purer yield higher quality or more quantity of the material. To theme/tie the idea of a good ruler more. As the crown leads to better policies that result in less wastes etc.<br /> <br /> The Iris: Zero idea would be a really cool add on power. Have the ability to make a roll and find a person perfectly suited to a task. I love it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T03:12:01-07:00","id":1218846,"title":"","content":"As come on, man. Why not retroactively make the resources better?<br /> <br /> Remember, we aren't solars. The crown's power doesnt need to manifest as superhuman excellence in ruling. It can also be a shaping effect, retroactively shifting the past and the surroundings. <br /> <br /> Also, you're a fan too?<br /> <br /> Yippeeee\ud83d\ude00\ud83d\ude00\ud83d\ude00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T14:40:33-07:00","id":1225730,"title":"","content":"Say I want to curse a tribe of people in such a way that people from that tribe cannot be the subject of feelings of love, not even by themselves. The mothers won't feel love for their children, the wives won't feel love for their husbands, and so on. Other emotions are unaffected; only that band we call love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T15:22:35-07:00","id":1225746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1225730#post1225730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say I want to curse a tribe of people in such a way that people from that tribe cannot be the subject of feelings of love, not even by themselves. The mothers won't feel love for their children, the wives won't feel love for their husbands, and so on. Other emotions are unaffected; only that band we call love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial circle, ambition 2. One can argue that the lack of love is a mental mutation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T15:22:44-07:00","id":1225747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1225730#post1225730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say I want to curse a tribe of people in such a way that people from that tribe cannot be the subject of feelings of love, not even by themselves. The mothers won't feel love for their children, the wives won't feel love for their husbands, and so on. Other emotions are unaffected; only that band we call love.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd peg this at terrestrial 3. &quot;Place a curse on a small region in a way that diminishes, warps, or blights its mundane aspects [...] making it all but impossible to make a livelihood off the cursed land&quot;<br /> Sounds like what you propose might not even make it impossible to work the land, but much harder.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'd say that the exact mechanism would be at least finesse 3 to pull off though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 06-07-2018, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T15:28:44-07:00","id":1225750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1225746#post1225746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One can argue that the lack of love is a mental mutation.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not that they lack the capacity <i>to</i> love - they lack the capacity to <i>be</i> loved. I am not mutating anybody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-07-2018, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T05:37:12-07:00","id":1226437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1225750#post1225750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's not that they lack the capacity <i>to</i> love - they lack the capacity to <i>be</i> loved. I am not mutating anybody.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a curse? Sounds supernatural. I think... celestial 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T17:26:28-07:00","id":1226613,"title":"","content":"Question. How about a school? A school which teaches extra well. Its like every single teacher inside got those lore training charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T17:46:26-07:00","id":1226618,"title":"","content":"Once again that's too powerful, enough such to be outside the scope of sorcerous workings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T18:01:17-07:00","id":1226622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1226618#post1226618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again that's too powerful, enough such to be outside the scope of sorcerous workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Come on, how is &quot;A Good School&quot; too hard? The charms, yeah, but school that supplement the abillity for its teachers to teach is certainly within range of workings. The fluff needs work, but some of the mechancis are viable (bonus die, instilling an intimacy with the lessons, etc.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1226613#post1226613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question. How about a school? A school which teaches extra well. Its like every single teacher inside got those lore training charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Celestial something or other. Id say 3, since it sounds more magical than resilence, but might be on the scale of human intellect. Depends on the fluff or effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T18:27:29-07:00","id":1226629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1226622#post1226622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come on, how is &quot;A Good School&quot; too hard?</div> </div> </div> </div>When it's done through the Solar Lore tree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1226622#post1226622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the fluff or effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that he specified &quot;those Lore training Charms,&quot; my guess is he wants to duplicate the effects of those Lore training Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T18:32:09-07:00","id":1226631,"title":"","content":"Nah. Just... it's effects. Basically, super university. That memetic school where everyone that comes out is a super genius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T19:30:13-07:00","id":1226641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1226629#post1226629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it's done through the Solar Lore tree.<br /> <br /> Given that he specified &quot;those Lore training Charms,&quot; my guess is he wants to duplicate the effects of those Lore training Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I read like far less narrowly.<br /> <br /> For a university that gives bonus die to teaching, a Celestial 3 seems fine. For permanently/automatically giving every student who attends bonus dots, I don't know. Seems between solar and celestial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T21:12:52-07:00","id":1226672,"title":"","content":"How about treating whatever they learn as a favoured ability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T07:31:28-07:00","id":1227647,"title":"","content":"Found some things: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/912982-sorcerous-workings-and-xp?p=913035#post913035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two are direct buffs to me and are always applicable. One is a horse sized dragon that is an in character development thing, character comes from a place where they had full sized dragons and was working back up to those, I have now done that and so I don't use that mount at all anymore, I haven't used it in over a story, I am considering killing it to release the xp. One was to create a cave which spawns a dragon each month that you someone can then spend three months to try and bond to, the dragon needs to go back to the cave system for 2 week every season, the Djala ride them and while the character is the commander at a local level for them they are the Djala states resource. The most recent one was to create one Griffions out of 100 lions and 100 eagles and then spend the time to bond them to 100 riders, these are ridden by people in her kingdom.<br /> <br /> The Eye of Adramelch which is a big flame sitting atop a tower which mortals step into to help them initiate into sorcery and can get badly burnt by if they fail, honestly on this one I am not sure how well it works as the ST has never really told me what the gubbins are. And the last one so far was a dress and tiara for another PC that glows with the light of the moon after dark.<br /> <br /> Other workings I want to do going forward are about turning humans into Melniboneans, enchanting walls, making palantir, creating Elric like things for the kingdom and so on, so from here on out there is less direct benifit to me.<br /> <br /> While I will benifit from most of them probably, none of them will stop me getting stabbed in a fight or interact with things on a personal scale, the way charms do. So in the last game I didn't do a working to enchant a cities walls that is about to be besiged because the xp will be tied up in it forever. If it was Solar xp I wouldn't be quite as worried because my charm progression would still be the same. And while the ability spread wouldn't be as good as other character eventually I could live with that because my core abilities are covered and workings can be used to fix some problems and be that characters thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T08:45:48-07:00","id":1228866,"title":"","content":"A question. If you were to make a bargain basement Solar exalted, one that could only go up to essence 3 or 4 or 5, what would be the sorcerous working level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T08:53:29-07:00","id":1228869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1228866#post1228866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question. If you were to make a bargain basement Solar exalted, one that could only go up to essence 3 or 4 or 5, what would be the sorcerous working level?</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition anything you created would not be a solar exalt. You're not the unconquered sun<br /> <br /> If you're talking a being of such power that they're comparable to a low-essence solar exalt then a) If that\\s possible at all then it's a Solar Ambition 3 working (with a very generous Storyteller honestly), and b) I'll remind you that the vast majority of the solar charmset is in the Essence 1-3 range so that doesn't exactly imply &quot;bargain basement&quot; in any sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T09:41:47-07:00","id":1228877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1228869#post1228869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By definition anything you created would not be a solar exalt. You're not the unconquered sun<br /> <br /> If you're talking a being of such power that they're comparable to a low-essence solar exalt then a) If that\\s possible at all then it's a Solar Ambition 3 working (with a very generous Storyteller honestly), and b) I'll remind you that the vast majority of the solar charmset is in the Essence 1-3 range so that doesn't exactly imply &quot;bargain basement&quot; in any sense</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was thinking of the Lintha. I'm trying to think of a being that can develop his/ her own charms. Not as powerful as a solar exalt. Not as mighty. But still flexible and way above any mortal. Somewhere between first circle and second circle demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T10:23:37-07:00","id":1228888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1228877#post1228877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I was thinking of the Lintha. I'm trying to think of a being that can develop his/ her own charms. Not as powerful as a solar exalt. Not as mighty. But still flexible and way above any mortal. Somewhere between first circle and second circle demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... about celestial Ambition 2-3 then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T12:27:31-07:00","id":1228935,"title":"","content":"So, if I wanted to create a working that enhanced a control spell that doesn't normally allow evocations to be unlocked (like Unslakable Thirst of the Devil Maw) so that it can now awaken evocations, would that work? If so what would it be, Celestial 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T13:39:25-07:00","id":1228950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1228935#post1228935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if I wanted to create a working that enhanced a control spell that doesn't normally allow evocations to be unlocked (like Unslakable Thirst of the Devil Maw) so that it can now awaken evocations, would that work? If so what would it be, Celestial 2?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say so, yeah. Celestial 3 at most. I'd specify, it's altering your devil maw, not the spell itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T16:13:02-07:00","id":1229000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1228888#post1228888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... about celestial Ambition 2-3 then?</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's for demons. <br /> <br /> This can grow and develop and make it's own charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T17:12:07-07:00","id":1229022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229000#post1229000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's for demons. <br /> <br /> This can grow and develop and make it's own charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>And demons can't?<br /> <br /> Remind me, what's the story of Stanewald, again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T17:18:39-07:00","id":1229023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229000#post1229000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's for demons.<br /> <br /> This can grow and develop and make it's own charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>so can demons. they're not locked into their charms, just their themes<br /> <br /> Plus celestial ambition three specifically says &quot;Create a loyal minion with supernatural powers <b>comparable </b>to a Second Circle demon or notable god&quot;<br /> bolding mine. I don't think it's actually possible to create a 'demon' as a working any more than your can create a solar. By definition second circle demons are beings that are part of the soul heirarchy of a yozi( at least I assume that hasn't changed. I don't think it's explicitly called out in 3E yet). You can't just create one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T17:28:32-07:00","id":1229025,"title":"","content":"Oh. I apologize. Really? They can develop their own charms?<br /> <br /> I thought demons can only have charms they are made with. Like gods and elementals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T17:31:52-07:00","id":1229026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's actually possible to create a 'demon' as a working any more than your can create a solar. By definition second circle demons are beings that are part of the soul heirarchy of a yozi( at least I assume that hasn't changed. I don't think it's explicitly called out in 3E yet). You can't just create one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a sorcerous working isn't just a matter of flexing your willpower until magic happens; you <i>could</i> use some means to coax a new soul into being from a Third Circle. In which case you would indeed be making a Second Circle Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-20-2018, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T19:34:33-07:00","id":1229043,"title":"","content":"This is extremely embarassing. <br /> <br /> What about something that can reliably transform people into first circle demon level beings?<br /> <br /> Cause I got an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T19:44:34-07:00","id":1229045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229025#post1229025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought demons can only have charms they are made with. Like gods and elementals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods and elementals can grow, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T19:48:06-07:00","id":1229046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229045#post1229045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods and elementals can grow, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>But slowly. And hardly. And I know they can learn martial arts and sorcery. But I thought their charms were static.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T19:50:40-07:00","id":1229047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229043#post1229043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is extremely embarassing.<br /> <br /> What about something that can reliably transform people into first circle demon level beings?<br /> <br /> Cause I got an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar 3--sounds like a 3rd circle demon (the Ebon Shadow has one that does that)<br /> And if it makes you feel better, I have assumed that spirit charms are basically static and developing your own charms being a unique thing to Exalted as well (in addition to Excellencies).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T19:59:09-07:00","id":1229052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229047#post1229047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if it makes you feel better, I have assumed that spirit charms are basically static and developing your own charms being a unique thing to Exalted as well (in addition to Excellencies).</div> </div> </div> </div>That only fits 2e's model, where all gods, demons, and elementals share the exact same set of Charms, the only difference being the different flavors and power levels through which they express them. <br /> <br /> And even then, spirits were still able to learn spirit Charms, and powerful spirits developed Panoply Charms.<br /> <br /> Remember that spirits in Ex3 don't have a single uniform Charmset to share, so there's no sense explicating an inability to innovate new Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-21-2018, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T20:02:00-07:00","id":1229053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229047#post1229047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Solar 3--sounds like a 3rd circle demon (the Ebon Shadow has one that does that)<br /> And if it makes you feel better, I have assumed that spirit charms are basically static and developing your own charms being a unique thing to Exalted as well (in addition to Excellencies).</div> </div> </div> </div>I got an idea. There's one thing that this setting needs. Space marines. <br /> <br /> Solar esque charms, 1 to 3. Gives several mutations like large, acute senses, healing and regeneration, and a bunch more. <br /> <br /> Massively enhances speed, strength, durability, and other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T20:06:00-07:00","id":1229055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229053#post1229053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got an idea. There's one thing that this setting needs. Space marines.<br /> <br /> Solar esque charms, 1 to 3. Gives several mutations like large, acute senses, healing and regeneration, and a bunch more.<br /> <br /> Massively enhances speed, strength, durability, and other things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, if your looking to convert Space Marines to Exalted...it has those? Dragonblooded in Power Armor, or enhancements via Tiger Warrior charms? Oh! The Yennin kinda. So yeah. Sounds good and possible and fitting of setting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> I mean, I just assume all Blood Apes will have the same charms and can't expand them--Elementals can grow into dragons, gods can gain higher station, but like. Every Garda bird is the same set of charms as the other. I concede that I was misunderstanding perhaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T20:23:18-07:00","id":1229057,"title":"","content":"Apologies. But.... well, the space marines... I like how they came from mortal stock, then were enhanced and transmuted into something beyond human. The best of the best, enhanced even further by geneseed. <br /> <br /> Besides, I want them as really strong elite looks. Dragonblooded aren't mooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T20:30:29-07:00","id":1229058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229057#post1229057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies. But.... well, the space marines... I like how they came from mortal stock, then were enhanced and transmuted into something beyond human. The best of the best, enhanced even further by geneseed.<br /> <br /> Besides, I want them as really strong elite looks. Dragonblooded aren't mooks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No need! Adding a new source of supernatural weirdness is always good, and your right, Dragonblooded aren't mooks. I just often think of Sorcerous workings as the last resort, which might be just a me thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T20:43:46-07:00","id":1229060,"title":"","content":"Where so people get the idea that gods and elementals can't grow or get new charms? In 2E we know for sure that elementals developed into lesser elemental dragons when they reached a certain essence and then if they developed to a certain point they became greater elemental dragons and immediately went crazy and started laying waste. Gods can swap purviews, add to their purviews or simply refine themselves. In 2E this gave them unique panolopy charms based on what their job was, but in 3E I suspect that this will be reflected in their charmset as well.<br /> <br /> Even with demons we have examples of growth and expansion. Octavian conquered a large portion of Malfeas. He can never become a third circle demon but he can push his own limits and flex and grow within his sphere of influence. His bane of the earth power is a direct result of actions he's taken/actions taken against him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T20:51:44-07:00","id":1229061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229058#post1229058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No need! Adding a new source of supernatural weirdness is always good, and your right, Dragonblooded aren't mooks. I just often think of Sorcerous workings as the last resort, which might be just a me thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit, I did it partially for the giant pauldrons. Those giant shoulder guards need big shoulders to rest on. <br /> <br /> But is it.... too powerful? I mean, these are solar charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T20:53:51-07:00","id":1229062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229058#post1229058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I just often think of Sorcerous workings as the last resort, which might be just a me thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, for me, personally I think sorcerous workings left over from sorcerers are a good way to add in weird things from left over eras and deceased sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T22:10:16-07:00","id":1229082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229060#post1229060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where so people get the idea that gods and elementals can't grow or get new charms? In 2E we know for sure that elementals developed into lesser elemental dragons when they reached a certain essence and then if they developed to a certain point they became greater elemental dragons and immediately went crazy and started laying waste. Gods can swap purviews, add to their purviews or simply refine themselves. In 2E this gave them unique panolopy charms based on what their job was, but in 3E I suspect that this will be reflected in their charmset as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both examples require external stimuli or changing into something else though, I don't think that the Neomah just can't one day decide to learn new charms without doing something like bathing themselves in Szoreny's quicksilver lake or changing into one of Erembour's night creature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T22:59:04-07:00","id":1229088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229082#post1229082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both examples require external stimuli or changing into something else though\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Change and growth in <i>humans </i>requires external stimuli.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229082#post1229082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that the Neomah just can't one day decide to learn new charms without doing something like bathing themselves in Szoreny's quicksilver lake or changing into one of Erembour's night creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that your typical neomah isn't prone to up and learning a new Charm, as well; but to me, it's less about demonic capability and more about &quot;meaningfully grows and changes more than a handful of times in their lives&quot; being something of a rare character trait (for <i>most</i> things). Nor would I just up and permit a Charm that would represent a <i>drastic</i> alteration of their nature without something to justify it, such as your example exposure to the music of Erembour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-21-2018, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T08:14:53-07:00","id":1229158,"title":"","content":"Well, in that case, since I've already got my questions answered...<br /> <br /> How about this? Remember the river where the dude went to wash, and got his leprosy cured? <br /> <br /> How about a lake that makes it that everyone who washes in it get cured of any injury or disease?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T08:45:52-07:00","id":1229163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229158#post1229158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in that case, since I've already got my questions answered...<br /> <br /> How about this? Remember the river where the dude went to wash, and got his leprosy cured?<br /> <br /> How about a lake that makes it that everyone who washes in it get cured of any injury or disease?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably Celestial 2 if it takes time to cure them and doesn't work on the Great Contagion or do anything about aggravated damage. Probably Solar 2 if the healing happens instantaneously, or if it can cure the Great Contagion or downgrade aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T23:20:22-07:00","id":1229529,"title":"","content":"A question. What do you think of a working that makes an ability favoured?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T01:23:32-07:00","id":1229544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229529#post1229529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question. What do you think of a working that makes an ability favoured?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Favored Abilities aren't a thing in-universe, and only works as an out-of-character function to save players XP, I wouldn't allow it at my table. If a player of mine wants to change his character's Favored Abilities, he can discuss it with me; I'm not just gonna let him dump XP into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T01:40:20-07:00","id":1229548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229544#post1229544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that Favored Abilities aren't a thing in-universe, and only works as an out-of-character function to save players XP, I wouldn't allow it at my table. If a player of mine wants to change his character's Favored Abilities, he can discuss it with me; I'm not just gonna let him dump XP into it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Favoured abilities don't just save XP, they also save a significant amount of training time. Which could preset itself as something that someone just naturally learns a lot faster. Considering that I would consider a favoured ability just as in universe as a dot of strength.<br /> <br /> That said, workings that go in the direction of altering how XP is spent by a character is certainly an area that requires caution. I would agree that it is best to go for the option of changing a favoured ability, not adding a new one. With serious consideration given to how invested they already are in the current ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T03:16:41-07:00","id":1229556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229548#post1229548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Favoured abilities don't just save XP, they also save a significant amount of training time. Which could preset itself as something that someone just naturally learns a lot faster. Considering that I would consider a favoured ability just as in universe as a dot of strength.<br /> <br /> That said, workings that go in the direction of altering how XP is spent by a character is certainly an area that requires caution. I would agree that it is best to go for the option of changing a favoured ability, not adding a new one. With serious consideration given to how invested they already are in the current ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... actually this is for that school idea. <br /> <br /> I was thinking of either a manse or a celestial working that makes it so that when people learn in a certain school, they treat whatever they learn as if it was in a favoured ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T05:02:41-07:00","id":1229563,"title":"","content":"So, I've got a few ideas for workings I'm wondering about.<br /> <br /> First of, what would it take to make a world inside a gem like Asphodel (or Pendurant Vault, I guess)? What if that internal 'world' was just the size of a house instead?<br /> <br /> Second, how about raising an island from the sea? Or raising a hill/small mountain on land?<br /> <br /> Third, how about building a palace on a cloud (or enchanting an existing palace to float on a cloud)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Let us take men and give them the favor of the gods and use them as our champions against the Primordials, that we might overthrow them and play for ourselves the Games of Divinity.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2272-senresk","name":"senresk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T06:04:54-07:00","id":1229574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>senresk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229563#post1229563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've got a few ideas for workings I'm wondering about.<br /> <br /> First of, what would it take to make a world inside a gem like Asphodel (or Pendurant Vault, I guess)? What if that internal 'world' was just the size of a house instead?<br /> <br /> Second, how about raising an island from the sea? Or raising a hill/small mountain on land?<br /> <br /> Third, how about building a palace on a cloud (or enchanting an existing palace to float on a cloud)?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of them celestial circle workings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T06:49:29-07:00","id":1229582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229574#post1229574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of them celestial circle workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhm. I'd hoped raising a hill would be terrestrial, considering flattening one is.<br /> <br /> But alright, any idea what Ambitions those would be?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Let us take men and give them the favor of the gods and use them as our champions against the Primordials, that we might overthrow them and play for ourselves the Games of Divinity.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2272-senresk","name":"senresk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T07:12:11-07:00","id":1229591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>senresk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229582#post1229582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mhm. I'd hoped raising a hill would be terrestrial, considering flattening one is.<br /> <br /> But alright, any idea what Ambitions those would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem. <br /> <br /> You said raising an island from the sea. What's the depth of the water? <br /> <br /> You also said raise a hill/ small mountain. A small mountain is quite different. <br /> <br /> You know what you should do for projects like this? Summon a bunch of elementals and demons, then task bind them. Its easier. <br /> <br /> As for the other projects, for me, I usually put things that are blatantly supernatural and widescale as celestial. <br /> <br /> Internal world? Celestial...2 <br /> <br /> Palace to float on a cloud? How large? Smallish? Celestial 3. Largish? Solar 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T07:52:17-07:00","id":1229598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229591#post1229591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem.<br /> <br /> You said raising an island from the sea. What's the depth of the water?<br /> <br /> You also said raise a hill/ small mountain. A small mountain is quite different.<br /> <br /> You know what you should do for projects like this? Summon a bunch of elementals and demons, then task bind them. Its easier.<br /> <br /> As for the other projects, for me, I usually put things that are blatantly supernatural and widescale as celestial.<br /> <br /> Internal world? Celestial...2<br /> <br /> Palace to float on a cloud? How large? Smallish? Celestial 3. Largish? Solar 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite sure how deep the water would be, to be honest... Not too far off the coast?<br /> <br /> And probably should just be a hill then (I'm absolutely terrible at considering any kind of scale). But fair enough on the demons/elementals, just hauling a ton of rock and dirt likely works fine-ish.<br /> <br /> But anyway, thanks. Would the size of the internal world matter there at all, or not really?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Let us take men and give them the favor of the gods and use them as our champions against the Primordials, that we might overthrow them and play for ourselves the Games of Divinity.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2272-senresk","name":"senresk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T08:40:32-07:00","id":1229603,"title":"","content":"Small house?<br /> <br /> Celestial. .<br /> <br /> City? Solar. <br /> <br /> Dude. It's literally a pocket universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T06:18:45-07:00","id":1229794,"title":"","content":"/Question. What about a working so that a mortal can use essence, and has access to worker and enlightened pattern charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T07:29:37-07:00","id":1229799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229794#post1229794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">/Question. What about a working so that a mortal can use essence, and has access to worker and enlightened pattern charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Making them some sorta spirit/mountain folk thing it sounds like. Celestial 3 at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T08:45:58-07:00","id":1229802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229799#post1229799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Making them some sorta spirit/mountain folk thing it sounds like. Celestial 3 at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. <br /> <br /> But a mountain folk isn't on the level of a second circle demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T09:07:11-07:00","id":1229806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229802#post1229802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah.<br /> <br /> But a mountain folk isn't on the level of a second circle demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but granting someone an entire charm tree seems substantially above the one abillity mark of Celestial 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T09:36:28-07:00","id":1229810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229806#post1229806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but granting someone an entire charm tree seems substantially above the one abillity mark of Celestial 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Celestial 2 means second circle demon. And, well, Worker castes are basically on the level of first circles. Barely. <br /> <br /> I mean, if I was to do something like Celestial 3, it would be on the level of making someone like the Artisan. <br /> <br /> And demons can develop their own charms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T10:00:15-07:00","id":1229814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229810#post1229810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Celestial 2 means second circle demon. And, well, Worker castes are basically on the level of first circles. Barely.<br /> <br /> I mean, if I was to do something like Celestial 3, it would be on the level of making someone like the Artisan.<br /> <br /> And demons can develop their own charms</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Celestial 3 means second circle demon, yeah. I'd say giving people charms, the abillity to use artifacts, and martial arts charms is on the level Celestial 3. Celestial 2 is &quot;one magic power&quot;. Giving a ton of magic powers seems Celestial 3--I'll note I think &quot;Adding powers&quot; is higher on the scale then &quot;making new thing whole cloth&quot;, given that making a first circle demon is Celestial 1 according to the devs (or celestial 2), while &quot;give someone a hypnotic tongue&quot; is Celestial 2 as well. <br /> <br /> as for demons learning their own charms: While I respect Alucard, their means of developing charms seems substantially more difficult then Exalted, and maybe Mountain Folk/Lintha/DragonKings. In the past, I've required characters to get more workings for more charms, which seems fair to me. I admit, I don't know the Mountain Folk's whole trees, but giving anyone a charm <i>tree</i> sounds like the edge of celestial power (also, are enlightend pattern charms also that weak? If so, man they need a buffing up.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T10:14:39-07:00","id":1229816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229814#post1229814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as for demons learning their own charms: While I respect Alucard, their means of developing charms seems substantially more difficult then Exalted, and maybe Mountain Folk/Lintha/DragonKings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not disagreeing with you on any of those (except insofar as to note that Lintha are human). The life of a spirit is substantially different than that of a fleshy being, often in a way that leaves one relatively set in one's ways. Still, if a player wanted to play a demonic character in one of my games, I wouldn't require him to have to undergo a working each game session before he could spend his XP.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, are enlightend pattern charms also that weak?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not; he seems to be downplaying their significance, as if he specifically wants your answer to not be Celestial 3.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-24-2018, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T10:33:22-07:00","id":1229820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229816#post1229816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not disagreeing with you on any of those (except insofar as to note that Lintha are human). The life of a spirit is substantially different than that of a fleshy being, often in a way that leaves one relatively set in one's ways. Still, if a player wanted to play a demonic character in one of my games, I wouldn't require him to have to undergo a working each game session before he could spend his XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. In my case, it was the child of an Exalt endowed with magic powers, and the Exalt had to do a new working for new batches of powers. <br /> And fair on the Lintha, I meant more their demonblooded powers/potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T11:06:38-07:00","id":1229829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229820#post1229820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. In my case, it was the child of an Exalt endowed with magic powers, and the Exalt had to do a new working for new batches of powers.<br /> And fair on the Lintha, I meant more their demonblooded powers/potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Demon-Blooded aren't assumed to have Charms as the default anymore, and that even Demon-Blooded who <i>do</i> get the use of Charms from their magical heritage don't tend to be better at it than their demonic parent, I don't see reason to think a bog standard Lintha would pick up particularly more Charms than a bog standard demon.<br /> <br /> (And of course, once we're into the territory of exceptions, well, that's kinda what I've been on about all along.)<br /> <br /> \u200bNow, for another sorcerous working question. Let's say I wanted to remake the flying carpet from Disney's <i>Aladdin</i>. Should it be a working, or an artifact, and which level of such?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T12:00:35-07:00","id":1229837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229829#post1229829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Demon-Blooded aren't assumed to have Charms as the default anymore, and that even Demon-Blooded who <i>do</i> get the use of Charms from their magical heritage don't tend to be better at it than their demonic parent, I don't see reason to think a bog standard Lintha would pick up particularly more Charms than a bog standard demon.<br /> <br /> (And of course, once we're into the territory of exceptions, well, that's kinda what I've been on about all along.)<br /> <br /> \u200bNow, for another sorcerous working question. Let's say I wanted to remake the flying carpet from Disney's <i>Aladdin</i>. Should it be a working, or an artifact, and which level of such?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. I'd say it's fine for a sorcerous working, as an intellegient flying carpet(I would allow a craft roll to, but this is a border case). I'd say celestial 1, since it's not building on the innate qualities of a rug to give it flight. Fits the &quot;supernatural but minor&quot; requirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T12:17:14-07:00","id":1229839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1229829#post1229829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say I wanted to remake the flying carpet from Disney's <i>Aladdin</i>. Should it be a working, or an artifact, and which level of such?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to say &quot;artifact&quot; because, despite it being a sentient being, it still feels like a made thing to me. I realize there isn't any evidence for this (I suppose the cartoon might have gone into Carpet's backstory, but I don't recall that), but I believe that a) Carpet was crafted in a way that carpets generally are (i.e. woven), just with extra magic, and b) I don't really picture the process as involving first creating it, then enchanting it separately. Note that when Jafar destroys Carpet in the movie, he <i>unravels</i> it - I think that, if the creation of Carpet had involved weaving a mundane carpet then enchanting it, the process of destroying it would resemble classic D&amp;D Dispel Magic - just point the staff, puff of magic pixie dust, and the carpet is now just an inanimate rug. Whereas the actual process reverses the creation process, which implies to me that the creation process was inherent to the magic.<br /> <br /> Anyway, all that said, as an Artifact, I'd probably rate it at Artifact 5, and probably First Age Artifice. Compare it to Wings of the Raptor (Arms of the Chosen, p. 126) - at 4 dots, it's a mobility artifact, but only capable of carrying one person (the user) plus whatever weight they can lift, and it <i>isn't</i> capable of independent, intelligent thought.<br /> <br /> If you were taking something like Carpet at character creation, though, I'd probably allow you to purchase it as Ally merit (probably 3-dot), rather than as an Artifact - Carpet is really an independent character, capable of being offended or choosing their own path, and doesn't quite have the level of total loyalty I'd expect from an artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T13:12:52-07:00","id":1229847,"title":"","content":"I don't think that the carpet is such a powerful thing that it would be artifact 5 let alone FAA. I'd actually rate the carpet as a celestial 3 project. Similar to the creation of a notable god. Remember that flight is powerful but not game breaking. You can always summon an Agata and they'd be able to catch you and fly you around as well (though maybe not hit all the major landmarks across creation in one night).<br /> <br /> As for Jafar destroying the carpet, remember first that artifacts cannot be destroyed in that manner. There is no 'dispel magic' in Exalted. However, a sorcerer could attempt a working to distort the working that created the carper. For instance rendering a thinking, carpet inert by unraveling it? Remember also that Jafar wished to become the world's most powerful &quot;sorcerer&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T13:26:54-07:00","id":1231434,"title":"","content":"Necromantic, but same jist: I have a player who wants to unleash a horde of ghosts at his party, guised as a seance. The ghosts will reveal all the deepest and darkest secrets of guests in the room for all to hear. Since it's a one off use, I feel like this is more a working than a spell. Any ideas for what circle? Auto-reveal vs a roll against Resolve/Guile is still in the air<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T16:51:19-07:00","id":1231475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1231434#post1231434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ghosts will reveal all the deepest and darkest secrets of guests in the room for all to hear. Since it's a one off use, I feel like this is more a working than a spell. Any ideas for what circle? Auto-reveal vs a roll against Resolve/Guile is still in the air</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's really <i>all</i> the secrets, I'd call it at least Celestial 3, if not Solar 1. That's pretty strong. If it's something a bit more limited, like &quot;all the secrets that a reasonable Read Intentions pool could reveal&quot;, then that's a bit more limited, and I could see it as being low Celestial or even high Terrestrial, depending on how large an area was covered and how fast the ghosts could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T21:52:47-07:00","id":1232306,"title":"","content":"A working to cure a highly virulent, but non-magical (ie black plague, ebola, small pox, etc), disease over a 1) city, 2) continent, 3) whole world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24362-fredo","name":"Fredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T22:54:04-07:00","id":1232316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fredo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232306#post1232306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A working to cure a highly virulent, but non-magical (ie black plague, ebola, small pox, etc), disease over a 1) city, 2) continent, 3) whole world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> These are all going to be Solar Circle, just based on scale. Start at Solar 1 for the city, and go up one Ambition level for each step.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T23:33:01-07:00","id":1232319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fredo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232306#post1232306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A working to cure a highly virulent, but non-magical (ie black plague, ebola, small pox, etc), disease over a 1) city, 2) continent, 3) whole world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Linking to this, how about a disease which causes you to gain resistance to Ebola? It's not deadly or even dangerous at all. But gives resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T05:36:40-07:00","id":1232349,"title":"","content":"My Zenith Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Stylist's Kimono keeps getting destroyed, so she's going to imbue her next one with a sorcerous working.<br /> Making a garment self-repair or not get torn/stained seems very low-end for a working, so what do you guys think could be tagged onto it while keeping it Ambition 1 Terrestrial (she is Essence 1)? Or do you think that's enough of a feature for the 2xp?<br /> Bonus: what could you do with an ambition 2 Terrestrial working slapped onto a garment? Make the wearer immune to extreme heat or cold (as in not getting weary while travelling through tropical rainforests, or nordic blizzards, not being immune to being dropped into a volcano, or frozen by the wicked magics of the Fair Folk of the north)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T08:05:19-07:00","id":1232380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232319#post1232319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Linking to this, how about a disease which causes you to gain resistance to Ebola? It's not deadly or even dangerous at all. But gives resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically an infectious vaccination? Since many disease symptoms are really the results of viruses reproducing in the host and incidentally destroying a bunch of cells, I'd say that you effectively have to create a form of life with supernatural abilities here, the magical power to reproduce <i>without</i> harming the host. I'd peg this at Celestial 1, if &quot;reproduces magically&quot; was the only supernatural trait you gave it. If you wanted to add some safety factors like &quot;will never mutate into a more-lethal variant&quot;, I'd bump it up to Celestial 2. And, note, it would spread like a normal disease too, so it might take a long time to immunize everyone in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T09:32:04-07:00","id":1232405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232380#post1232380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically an infectious vaccination? Since many disease symptoms are really the results of viruses reproducing in the host and incidentally destroying a bunch of cells, I'd say that you effectively have to create a form of life with supernatural abilities here, the magical power to reproduce <i>without</i> harming the host. I'd peg this at Celestial 1, if &quot;reproduces magically&quot; was the only supernatural trait you gave it. If you wanted to add some safety factors like &quot;will never mutate into a more-lethal variant&quot;, I'd bump it up to Celestial 2. And, note, it would spread like a normal disease too, so it might take a long time to immunize everyone in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>But.... this is creation. <br /> <br /> I'm hoping to create a infectious bacteria with the same glycoprpotein as the one on the Ebola Virus's surface, so that the presence of the Ebola virus would provoke an immune response, and thus allow the body itself to fight it off. The presence of a protein on both the bacteria and the virus, means that once the body has gained immunity to the virus, it gains one to Ebola as well. <br /> <br /> Also, this is, at most, Terrestrial 3. Adding in an extra protein on the bacterial surface is a mutation. Additional adaptations to ensure it is able to survive in a wide variety of environments is a mutation. And setting in extra structure to make sure that all DNA replication is done perfectly is also more mutations. <br /> <br /> The terrestrial 3 is to make sure that no matter what, no one dies from this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T09:33:39-07:00","id":1232406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232349#post1232349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Zenith Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Stylist's Kimono keeps getting destroyed, so she's going to imbue her next one with a sorcerous working.<br /> Making a garment self-repair or not get torn/stained seems very low-end for a working, so what do you guys think could be tagged onto it while keeping it Ambition 1 Terrestrial (she is Essence 1)? Or do you think that's enough of a feature for the 2xp?<br /> Bonus: what could you do with an ambition 2 Terrestrial working slapped onto a garment? Make the wearer immune to extreme heat or cold (as in not getting weary while travelling through tropical rainforests, or nordic blizzards, not being immune to being dropped into a volcano, or frozen by the wicked magics of the Fair Folk of the north)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Self-repair? Hah! Why a sorcerous working at all? Why not simply use the spell, elemental empowerment of wood? <br /> <br /> Bonus: resistance against environmental effects, but not magical ones nor ones that are sent as attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T09:41:27-07:00","id":1232408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232405#post1232405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, this is, at most, Terrestrial 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you seem to know the answer you want already (it's always &quot;Oh c'mon, it's Terrestrial at most&quot;), why are you asking the questions? I'm no longer going to bother answering you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T09:44:12-07:00","id":1232411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232405#post1232405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But.... this is creation.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping to create a infectious bacteria with the same glycoprpotein as the one on the Ebola Virus's surface, so that the presence of the Ebola virus would provoke an immune response, and thus allow the body itself to fight it off. The presence of a protein on both the bacteria and the virus, means that once the body has gained immunity to the virus, it gains one to Ebola as well.<br /> <br /> Also, this is, at most, Terrestrial 3. Adding in an extra protein on the bacterial surface is a mutation. Additional adaptations to ensure it is able to survive in a wide variety of environments is a mutation. And setting in extra structure to make sure that all DNA replication is done perfectly is also more mutations.<br /> <br /> The terrestrial 3 is to make sure that no matter what, no one dies from this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd model this more as a working specifically to grant immunity to ebola to a region. Terrestrial 3 definitely, but the actual vector it takes would be a finesse thing. If you absolutely want to use a virus to help protect against a virus then that'd be finesse 5. All the stuff about modifying the bateria surface to have a specific protein? That's all how stuff works on Earth in the real world but as you say, this is creation<br /> <br /> This sounds like something that a DB sorcerer should be able to do. <br /> <br /> If you're talking a self-perpetuating thing that will eventually immunize the entirety of creation then that's simply out of the scope of a terrestrial working. That's high end solar working for sure. Otherwise the DB would have simply wiped out all disease forever already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:00:34-07:00","id":1232416,"title":"","content":"Hm, that does lead to a more general question of mine: if a creation/working is self perpetuating/growing with input, does that increase it's circle?<br /> For an example, an early working I had an NPC do that I at the time thought was celestial level was create a large creature that, when fed stone or jade, produce animated statues. Because it has no cap, is this more a Solar range in people's opinion, or is the need for more materials make it Celestial? <br /> Or, in my current game, I have a character who's working was to create a species of semi-material jellyfish spies (They're immaterial, floating jellyfish covered in eyes). Is there a distinction in working level if:<br /> 1-the species is self reproducing and starts with an intimacy towards the maker<br /> 2-the species isn't self reproducing, but rather the working creates the device that makes more of them (similair to my stone monster above. Say, a tree that when watered certain chemcials, makes the spy fish. The species of jellyfish thus require constant effort by the sorcerer after the working to reproduce)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:20:05-07:00","id":1232424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232416#post1232416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, that does lead to a more general question of mine: if a creation/working is self perpetuating/growing with input, does that increase it's circle?</div> </div> </div> </div>How much it increases would vary, but in general, yes, I would say an automatically-growing effect will be a higher ambition than one that isn't. How much it increases depends on the nature of the working, and its general ability to expand. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232416#post1232416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an example, an early working I had an NPC do that I at the time thought was celestial level was create a large creature that, when fed stone or jade, produce animated statues. Because it has no cap, is this more a Solar range in people's opinion, or is the need for more materials make it Celestial?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is going to depend on the base power of the statues produced, I think. If they're basically &quot;mundane creature&quot; level, with maybe one supernatural power, then they're base Celestial 1, and I'd peg the multiplication aspect as bumping it up to Celestial 3. If, on the other hand, the statues are significantly stronger than that, or if the &quot;reproduction&quot; rate is seriously fast (like, faster than &quot;once a season&quot;, then Solar 1 or higher definitely seems more appropriate.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't reduce the ambition level for the materials cost if it's &quot;stone or jade&quot;, because stone is <i>much</i> too common to be a significant limitation. If it was &quot;stone, and small quantities of jade&quot;, always requiring a magical material, that might pull it down one level. It's never going to be as low as just making a single, once-off statue, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232416#post1232416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, in my current game, I have a character who's working was to create a species of semi-material jellyfish spies (They're immaterial, floating jellyfish covered in eyes). Is there a distinction in working level if:<br /> 1-the species is self reproducing and starts with an intimacy towards the maker<br /> 2-the species isn't self reproducing, but rather the working creates the device that makes more of them (similair to my stone monster above. Say, a tree that when watered certain chemcials, makes the spy fish. The species of jellyfish thus require constant effort by the sorcerer after the working to reproduce)</div> </div> </div> </div>Either way, I'd definitely bump the ambition level up at <i>least</i> one level compared to the level required to make just a single jellyfish spy with an (I assume, positive) intimacy towards you. I'd peg the basic level of that at Celestial 2, and put the self-reproduction with a built-in positive intimacy at Solar 1. Depending on how difficult the machine to produce more jellyfish was to operate, you <i>might</i> convince me to call that version Celestial 3. But I'd be more inclined towards Solar 1 for that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:30:02-07:00","id":1232428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232406#post1232406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Self-repair? Hah! Why a sorcerous working at all? Why not simply use the spell, elemental empowerment of wood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because my Essence 1 Zenith with ~30ish XP doesn't know that spell, and doesn't know anybody who could teach her that spell, and we didn't convert that spell to 3rd Edition yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bonus: resistance against environmental effects, but not magical ones nor ones that are sent as attacks. </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought along the lines of as well, thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:32:27-07:00","id":1232433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232424#post1232424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How much it increases would vary, but in general, yes, I would say an automatically-growing effect will be a higher ambition than one that isn't. How much it increases depends on the nature of the working, and its general ability to expand.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is going to depend on the base power of the statues produced, I think. If they're basically &quot;mundane creature&quot; level, with maybe one supernatural power, then they're base Celestial 1, and I'd peg the multiplication aspect as bumping it up to Celestial 3. If, on the other hand, the statues are significantly stronger than that, or if the &quot;reproduction&quot; rate is seriously fast (like, faster than &quot;once a season&quot;, then Solar 1 or higher definitely seems more appropriate.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't reduce the ambition level for the materials cost if it's &quot;stone or jade&quot;, because stone is <i>much</i> too common to be a significant limitation. If it was &quot;stone, and small quantities of jade&quot;, always requiring a magical material, that might pull it down one level. It's never going to be as low as just making a single, once-off statue, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, for completion sake: The statues were the automata one in the core if given stone. If given jade it made better automata (I think they had a few charms? and raised harndess? It's been about a year since that creature was around.). I pegged it as Celestial because making an automata with materials supplied seemd second circle range of abillities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232424#post1232424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, I'd definitely bump the ambition level up at <i>least</i> one level compared to the level required to make just a single jellyfish spy with an (I assume, positive) intimacy towards you. I'd peg the basic level of that at Celestial 2, and put the self-reproduction with a built-in positive intimacy at Solar 1. Depending on how difficult the machine to produce more jellyfish was to operate, you <i>might</i> convince me to call that version Celestial 3. But I'd be more inclined towards Solar 1 for that too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intreasting. I agree that making one jellyfish&lt;making many jellyfish, but I'd have lowered it to Celestial. It helps that the jellyfish spy for me is Celestial 1--it's a jellyfish that can float and see things(which is terrestrial mutations) but is permanently immaterial and can communciate (which makes it 1 or 2 depending on power value).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":".  Clarification 07-04-2018, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:37:26-07:00","id":1232434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232433#post1232433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, for completion sake: The statues were the automata one in the core if given stone. If given jade it made better automata (I think they had a few charms? and raised harndess? It's been about a year since that creature was around.).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the automata from the Core book would rate Celestial 1 to create individually, so I'd stick with my above estimates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intreasting. I agree that making one jellyfish&lt;making many jellyfish, but I'd have lowered it to Celestial. It helps that the jellyfish spy for me is Celestial 1--it's a jellyfish that can float and see things(which is terrestrial mutations) but is permanently immaterial and can communciate (which makes it 1 or 2 depending on power value).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the immateriality that's kicking it up to Celestial 2 for me - to me, that's a very good example of a supernatural power, which requires Celestial 2 to give out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T07:56:13-07:00","id":1232625,"title":"","content":"Question. Grant someone the thaumaturgy merit. Celestial or terrestrial working?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T06:11:02-07:00","id":1232844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1232625#post1232625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question. Grant someone the thaumaturgy merit. Celestial or terrestrial working?</div> </div> </div> </div>Granting supernatural powers, minimum Celestial 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T09:30:38-07:00","id":1233447,"title":"","content":"Question. I've been reading guyver. <br /> <br /> A suit that can bind to the person and give him mild, first circle demon level powers. Heck, Peronnelle do that already. <br /> <br /> So?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T09:59:39-07:00","id":1233453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1233447#post1233447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question. I've been reading guyver.<br /> <br /> A suit that can bind to the person and give him mild, first circle demon level powers. Heck, Peronnelle do that already.<br /> <br /> So?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Terrestrial 3/Celestial 1. Vance said making a first circle was 1-2, I've been house ruling it as T. 3<br /> <br /> EDIT: With the Caveat that your making the suit, and the symbiot can leave/die etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T10:29:42-07:00","id":1233462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1233453#post1233453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I've been house ruling it as T. 3</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Me too. <br /> <br /> *high fives*<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T06:02:19-07:00","id":1234608,"title":"","content":"I got an idea. <br /> <br /> A doorframe with water flowing from the upper section to the lower section, forming a sheet of water flowing downwards. The water disappears when it hits the ground. <br /> <br /> Whoever passes through this doorway, is 'cleansed' of all forms of servitude, unnatural mental influence, emotional, and illusionary effects. <br /> <br /> What level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T06:46:54-07:00","id":1234616,"title":"","content":"Oh my.. All forms of servitude? Like, including the binding of demons? All emotional influences including the ones Black Claw Stylists have to internalize? And it's not a one-time thing, but a permanent un-mindfucking feature anyone can walk through? I'm gonna peg that at Solar Circle.<br /> <br /> If it only undoes effects that are normally <b>possible </b>to undo, I might be talked down to the higher end of Celestial. Maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T06:51:42-07:00","id":1234620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1234616#post1234616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my.. All forms of servitude? Like, including the binding of demons? All emotional influences including the ones Black Claw Stylists have to internalize? And it's not a one-time thing, but a permanent un-mindfucking feature anyone can walk through? I'm gonna peg that at Solar Circle.<br /> <br /> If it only undoes effects that are normally <b>possible </b>to undo, I might be talked down to the higher end of Celestial. Maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only for humans. <br /> <br /> Question. What are the effects that are impossible to undo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T07:05:21-07:00","id":1234622,"title":"","content":"Oh, only for mortals? That'd bump it down a fair bit, yeah.<br /> <br /> Those were the only two I could think of off the top of my head - there might be a few more somewhere. You can't unbind a bound demon - they develop a magically impervious drive to serve their summoner to the letter and their understanding of the spirit (here's where shenanigans might come in, but even then, only out of ignorance). and you can't make a Black Claw Stylist stop loving their teacher. Black Claw Style is rather fucked up like that.<br /> <br /> If those things were possible, they'd be Solar workings, 'cause that's where &quot;turn somebody into a completely different sort of being&quot; is. I imagine a demon wouldn't be bound if it weren't a demon anymore, hm? Expect the demon to resist if it realizes what you're doing, though - because it has a Defining Principle to accomplish its mission, which it can't do if you unbind it.<br /> <br /> You..Actually might be able to un-mindfuck a Black Claw Stylist at Celestial - by erasing their memory of ever having learned the style in the first place, but that's probably not the point here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","user":"Amayad","date":". 07-13-2018, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T00:37:09-07:00","id":1234882,"title":"","content":"Darned black claw stylists. So darned creepy. <br /> <br /> They remind me of abusive relationships.....<br /> <br /> Anyway, another idea. <br /> <br /> In the woods, there is a pool. Formed by a sorcerer seeking for rent. The local lord uses this pool for his troops and knights, when they are injured. The pool's perimeter has a fence upon it, and there is always a guard posted around, to block interlopers and intruders. <br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle, ambition 3. <br /> <br /> The pool grants temporary mutations to anyone who drinks from it. The mutations exist, only for one month before fading away. All mutations are internal, and do not show up. <br /> <br /> Mutations include: <br /> <br /> Superior healing - body becomes like an exalt. <br /> Accelerated healing - healing rate doubles<br /> Limb regeneration - amputated limbs can be repaired, with each amputated limb working like a single -4 health level filled in with missing damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T08:16:40-07:00","id":1234961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1234882#post1234882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Darned black claw stylists. So darned creepy.<br /> <br /> They remind me of abusive relationships.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Only because your eyes are working!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, another idea.<br /> <br /> In the woods, there is a pool. Formed by a sorcerer seeking for rent. The local lord uses this pool for his troops and knights, when they are injured. The pool's perimeter has a fence upon it, and there is always a guard posted around, to block interlopers and intruders.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle, ambition 3.<br /> <br /> The pool grants temporary mutations to anyone who drinks from it. The mutations exist, only for one month before fading away. All mutations are internal, and do not show up.<br /> <br /> Mutations include:<br /> <br /> Superior healing - body becomes like an exalt.<br /> Accelerated healing - healing rate doubles<br /> Limb regeneration - amputated limbs can be repaired, with each amputated limb working like a single -4 health level filled in with missing damage </div> </div> </div>That sorcerer went a long way for free room and board - I'm pretty sure, for that kind've effort, he could've just commanded the trees to bend themselves into a house and warded it against tax collectors. Even so, I'm not sure which Circle it's at, but I can tell you that you couldn't pay me to keep this thing in my minor kingdom.<br /> <br /> A mortal takes 52 days to get from mangled (6L damage) to full health. assuming they do nothing but rest and have decent medical care keeping things from going pear-shaped, as they do for mortals. <br /> <br /> An exalt takes 16 days., which is still a bit over half a month, but at least they don't need a doctor to stave off infection.<br /> <br /> You have a magical pool that cuts this down to 8 days, for everybody, and the effects last for a month after, plus it regrows limbs in five days (which you'd normally need Essence 3 Solar Medicine for, and even then, not nearly as quickly).<br /> <br /> This thing's going to cause more suffering than it eases, because the minute people find out where it is, wars will be waged over it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T09:00:25-07:00","id":1234974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1234882#post1234882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyway, another idea.<br /> <br /> In the woods, there is a pool. Formed by a sorcerer seeking for rent. The local lord uses this pool for his troops and knights, when they are injured. The pool's perimeter has a fence upon it, and there is always a guard posted around, to block interlopers and intruders.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle, ambition 3.<br /> <br /> The pool grants temporary mutations to anyone who drinks from it. The mutations exist, only for one month before fading away. All mutations are internal, and do not show up.<br /> <br /> Mutations include:<br /> <br /> Superior healing - body becomes like an exalt.<br /> Accelerated healing - healing rate doubles<br /> Limb regeneration - amputated limbs can be repaired, with each amputated limb working like a single -4 health level filled in with missing damage</div> </div> </div> </div>Heal like an exalt for a month---sure, sounds within terrestrial to me<br /> Accelerated healing---mmmm. mmm..This I think moves you into celestial. This is healing, as Amayad said, exceptionally fast.<br /> Limb Regeneration--If this was longer, I could by it by itself for a terresterial 1 off (give people lizard powers! Woo!). However, given its speed, I'd peg this as a Celestial power to start with.<br /> <br /> Individually, each of these is a low Celestial, high Terrestrial. Stacking so many, however, moves it to high celestial low Solar--I'm inclined to Celestial 3. An army of temporary Toffee's is kinda amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T09:08:17-07:00","id":1234979,"title":"","content":"You need 8 days? Damn. Well, I'll change it later. <br /> <br /> The sorcerer didn't do it just because of rent. It was also for support. Backing. Resources. Allies. Talking. A place to stay. <br /> <br /> A sorcerer alone is good. A sorcerer with the backing of a kingdom, with his own pick for apprentices? With an army of guards, and increased resources from having a sorcerer cast summon the harvest? That kingdom is going to become a juggernaut. And he'll be right beside it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T09:31:23-07:00","id":1234984,"title":"","content":"Question. Exalted healing and limb regeneration. <br /> <br /> How fast to go from a 'charred, limbless husk' to 'perfectly healthy'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T10:00:22-07:00","id":1234991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1234984#post1234984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question. Exalted healing and limb regeneration.<br /> <br /> How fast to go from a 'charred, limbless husk' to 'perfectly healthy'?</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring Lunars, you can't heal crippling wounds(including amputation) without ST intervention/decision making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T10:30:48-07:00","id":1234999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1234991#post1234991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Barring Lunars, you can't heal crippling wounds(including amputation) without ST intervention/decision making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. 2e or 3e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T10:35:08-07:00","id":1235002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1234961#post1234961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sorcerer went a long way for free room and board - I'm pretty sure, for that kind've effort, he could've just commanded the trees to bend themselves into a house and warded it against tax collectors.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of a pattern of his.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1234999#post1234999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait. 2e or 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div>All three editions did not just let Exalts regenerate from having their leg amputated just by dint of being Exalted. They needed to employ <i>some</i> kind of magic to restore the limb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T10:47:59-07:00","id":1235006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1234999#post1234999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait. 2e or 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 3e, I have no memory of 2e beyond infernals. I know it's been commented by Devs that Lunars can recover limbs with charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/2