e-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T09:37:17-08:00","id":1266219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1266162#post1266162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh...not the Brazen Bull?<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazen_bull\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazen_bull</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> Not at all. From 40k.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T05:42:17-08:00","id":1266927,"title":"","content":"So... I was performing a working to create a portal to the deep wyld, so that I could shape wyld from the safety of home, but my GM nixed every idea I had, so I want to check some mechanics of wyld for later (perhaps). Do wyld things made with WST disappear when they leave the wyld, do demesnes depower if they enter Creation, and do powersources made in the wyld stop working outside of it? Could a sorcerous working that transforms wyld power into creation-surviving power be a thing? I just wanted to use the wyld to generate sorcerous power for further, grander workings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":11875,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","user":"Rowanas","date":". 11-13-2018, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T07:08:37-08:00","id":1266941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1266927#post1266927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do wyld things made with WST disappear when they leave the wyld,</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's the whole point of WST - you're turning the Wyld into real stuff you can use in Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">do demesnes depower if they enter Creation,</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite sure what you mean here? Demesnes normally don't move. But if you're creating a demesne with WST, you're changing the Wyld into Creation in that location anyway, and the demesne wouldn't disappear at that point, or it wouldn't be very useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and do powersources made in the wyld stop working outside of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean by &quot;powersource&quot;. If you're talking about making a demesne or manse with a hearthstone, then no, the hearthstone wouldn't stop functioning, since the demesne/manse is now real, and would continue to power it. On the other hand, if you mean something else, well, it's going to depend on what you're talking about. I could picture an artifact, for instance, that drew in chaotic energy to turn into power, functioning like a hearthstone linked to a manse, but without any building to worry about, but only while in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a sorcerous working that transforms wyld power into creation-surviving power be a thing? I just wanted to use the wyld to generate sorcerous power for further, grander workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;creation-surviving power&quot;? In general, though, I think it's reasonable for workings to affect the Wyld, yes. I'd allow a working that counts as a means for further workings at level 3 ambition for the circle one below the one you want to boost. So, to act as a means for Celestial-circle workings, you'd need to do a Terrestrial 3 working, while one to boost Solar-Circle would be a Celestial 3 working. And if you had a nice large patch of Wyld, I'd let <i>that</i> count as a means for the boosting working. Having Wyld Shaping Technique would count as having the two-means level of Complementary Abilities as well, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T08:23:15-08:00","id":1266960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1266941#post1266941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that's the whole point of WST - you're turning the Wyld into real stuff you can use in Creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not quite sure what you mean here? Demesnes normally don't move. But if you're creating a demesne with WST, you're changing the Wyld into Creation in that location anyway, and the demesne wouldn't disappear at that point, or it wouldn't be very useful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Depends on what you mean by &quot;powersource&quot;. If you're talking about making a demesne or manse with a hearthstone, then no, the hearthstone wouldn't stop functioning, since the demesne/manse is now real, and would continue to power it. On the other hand, if you mean something else, well, it's going to depend on what you're talking about. I could picture an artifact, for instance, that drew in chaotic energy to turn into power, functioning like a hearthstone linked to a manse, but without any building to worry about, but only while in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Define &quot;creation-surviving power&quot;? In general, though, I think it's reasonable for workings to affect the Wyld, yes. I'd allow a working that counts as a means for further workings at level 3 ambition for the circle one below the one you want to boost. So, to act as a means for Celestial-circle workings, you'd need to do a Terrestrial 3 working, while one to boost Solar-Circle would be a Celestial 3 working. And if you had a nice large patch of Wyld, I'd let <i>that</i> count as a means for the boosting working. Having Wyld Shaping Technique would count as having the two-means level of Complementary Abilities as well, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, sorry, to be clear - I wanted to make things and then drop them out of a portal into creation, to create demesnes where no demesnes were. Essentially, I was going to cap an ordinary hill with magic wyld shaped demesne, to power further workings.<br /> <br /> Your other answers are quite helpful, cheers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T08:44:16-08:00","id":1266970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1266960#post1266960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to make things and then drop them out of a portal into creation, to create demesnes where no demesnes were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that a demesne is a piece of land, not just an object, so dropping it out of a portal is going to be tricky. The working to move such a piece of land will be its own thing - you couldn't just create a portal to the Wyld and shove a whole bunch of things through it, including the demesne. I'd peg the difficulty of moving a demesne at Solar Circle ambition 2 (&quot;Alter major metaphysical properties of a city-sized region&quot;). For a slightly easier, but more involved, process, you could use a Solar Ambition 1 working to make the place you wanted the demesne to basically <i>be</i> the Wyld (&quot;Enchant a village or small city-sized region to emulate the nature of another realm of existence&quot;), and then use WST there to make it into the demesne you wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T09:11:05-08:00","id":1266978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1266970#post1266970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that a demesne is a piece of land, not just an object, so dropping it out of a portal is going to be tricky. The working to move such a piece of land will be its own thing - you couldn't just create a portal to the Wyld and shove a whole bunch of things through it, including the demesne. I'd peg the difficulty of moving a demesne at Solar Circle ambition 2 (&quot;Alter major metaphysical properties of a city-sized region&quot;). For a slightly easier, but more involved, process, you could use a Solar Ambition 1 working to make the place you wanted the demesne to basically <i>be</i> the Wyld (&quot;Enchant a village or small city-sized region to emulate the nature of another realm of existence&quot;), and then use WST there to make it into the demesne you wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd point out that turning a chunk of creation big enough to support a demesne into pure chaos would probably set off all of the alarms on the Loom of Fate.<br /> <br /> It's not enough to turn the area of <i>just</i> the demesne into chaos either. You'd need to go big enough so that when you're standing in the middle of it, your wyld shaping has enough room to be able to expand and make the appropriate rolls to create the demesne. You're not guaranteed to get one until phase 3 which requires a minimum of 930 square miles of chaos to be converted. Now I'm assuming if you're not working with bare minimum successes on each phase you'd probably be getting enough threshold sux to make an attempt at demesne on each phase, but you've still got a better-than-even chance of getting nothing from those rolls and even worse chance of getting a demesne you actually <i>want</i>.<br /> <br /> I think if you're able to throw around solar circle workings you should probably just focus on geomantically crafting a demesne directly, which would probably be easier than this whole mess.<br /> <br /> Edit: I should note that even at the bare minimum, when spending successes to create a demesne on phase one, you'd need 50 square miles of pure chaos in which to do this, and you'd need a minimum of 7 threshold successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 11-13-2018, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T17:47:43-08:00","id":1267146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1266970#post1266970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that a demesne is a piece of land, not just an object, so dropping it out of a portal is going to be tricky. The working to move such a piece of land will be its own thing - you couldn't just create a portal to the Wyld and shove a whole bunch of things through it, including the demesne. I'd peg the difficulty of moving a demesne at Solar Circle ambition 2 (&amp;quot;Alter major metaphysical properties of a city-sized region&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. For a slightly easier, but more involved, process, you could use a Solar Ambition 1 working to make the place you wanted the demesne to basically <i>be</i> the Wyld (&amp;quot;Enchant a village or small city-sized region to emulate the nature of another realm of existence&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, and then use WST there to make it into the demesne you wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. City sized?<br /> <br /> I thought demense set basically the size of a few acres?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T07:48:07-08:00","id":1267285,"title":"","content":"It's probably easier just to use sorcery to directly reshape the landscape to be a demesne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T09:36:09-08:00","id":1267329,"title":"","content":"If I want to resurrect a lost prehuman race\u2014I found their bodies or writing or the memory of them in a dream of yogi\u2014is that a Solar or Terrestrial working? I can think of reasons for both","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T09:53:30-08:00","id":1267334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1266978#post1266978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if you're able to throw around solar circle workings you should probably just focus on geomantically crafting a demesne directly, which would probably be easier than this whole mess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1267285#post1267285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably easier just to use sorcery to directly reshape the landscape to be a demesne.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are both true, yeah. Creating a new demesne geomantically is probably the most subtle, but might take longer than any other method. Using a working to just create a demesne might cause a bit more of a metaphysical stir, but will probably be quicker, at least if you're of the right circle to accomplish the working. I'd put &quot;create a demesne of your chosen aspect but the ST picks everything else about it&quot; at Celestial 1, while &quot;create a custom demesne that you pick everything about&quot; at Celestial 3. Creating a <i>greater</i> demesne with similar parameters would be Solar 1 and 3 respectively. <br /> <br /> Note, I wouldn't let a working alone create a <i>manse</i> on a demesne - I think that's a thing for Craft, not sorcery. So there could be some benefit in the &quot;spill a bunch of Pure Chaos into Creation&quot; method, if you've got Manse-Raising Method, which allows you to shape manses with WST. Still a convoluted and dangerous prospect, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd point out that turning a chunk of creation big enough to support a demesne into pure chaos would probably set off all of the alarms on the Loom of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, yes. I'd probably have anything sorcerous that involved creating a demesne also have a chance to trigger alarm bells for Sidereals, but &quot;just dump a bunch of pure Chaos into Creation&quot; would be the most certain, and loudest, since that's pretty much exactly what the Sidereals and the Maidens don't ever want to happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not enough to turn the area of <i>just</i> the demesne into chaos either. You'd need to go big enough so that when you're standing in the middle of it, your wyld shaping has enough room to be able to expand and make the appropriate rolls to create the demesne.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably relax this requirement if you used a working to pour chaos out into Creation. I think if you're going to the effort to do a Solar-Circle working, you probably deserve a bit of a break. I'd still require you to do the phases of WST required to get to the level where you can convert to a demesne, but I wouldn't require the land to actually occupy the space that would suggest.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T10:07:20-08:00","id":1267339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1267329#post1267329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want to resurrect a lost prehuman race\u2014I found their bodies or writing or the memory of them in a dream of yogi\u2014is that a Solar or Terrestrial working? I can think of reasons for both</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If they have no supernatural powers, and you have an actual sample to work from (a corpse, a living example preserved in a magical crystal, their &quot;genetic blueprint&quot; stored by a mad First Age Twilight scholar, etc.), I'd call this Celestial 1. I know Terrestrial 3 is supposed to be able to produce a new mundane form of life, but I assume that has an unspoken &quot;non-sapient&quot; rider on it. I think creating (or, in this case, resurrecting) an <i>intelligent</i> species should be harder, if only to make sure mortal and Dragonblooded sorcerers aren't going about creating new intelligent species willy-nilly. <br /> <br /> For each of the following conditions that apply, I'd raise the required Ambition by 1: <br /> 1) The race has supernatural abilities (+2 if they're significant or have the potential to become so, like the Dragon King's Paths).<br /> 2) You don't have a good sample of the race, just descriptions.<br /> 3) The race has significantly faster reproductive speed than humans, or otherwise has the ability to quickly increase its population.<br /> 4) The race has a mentality that's extremely alien to humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T09:22:13-08:00","id":1267592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1267339#post1267339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If they have no supernatural powers, and you have an actual sample to work from (a corpse, a living example preserved in a magical crystal, their &quot;genetic blueprint&quot; stored by a mad First Age Twilight scholar, etc.), I'd call this Celestial 1. I know Terrestrial 3 is supposed to be able to produce a new mundane form of life, but I assume that has an unspoken &quot;non-sapient&quot; rider on it. I think creating (or, in this case, resurrecting) an <i>intelligent</i> species should be harder, if only to make sure mortal and Dragonblooded sorcerers aren't going about creating new intelligent species willy-nilly.<br /> <br /> For each of the following conditions that apply, I'd raise the required Ambition by 1:<br /> 1) The race has supernatural abilities (+2 if they're significant or have the potential to become so, like the Dragon King's Paths).<br /> 2) You don't have a good sample of the race, just descriptions.<br /> 3) The race has significantly faster reproductive speed than humans, or otherwise has the ability to quickly increase its population.<br /> 4) The race has a mentality that's extremely alien to humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree with point two. Such things should be means. I also disagree with 4, it having a completely different mentality seem irrelevant. Human-like elementals and bat-shit wierd elementals are both as easy to create after all (assuming similar power levels). I would also add that some minor supernatural abilities are fine for Ambition 1 witch mostly make the race more interesting and maybe some minor bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T10:10:59-08:00","id":1267605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1267592#post1267592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with point two. Such things should be means.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point, actually. I could see having &quot;create a new life form from scratch&quot; be the base Celestial 1 ambition, while having a good description counts as 1 means, while having an actual sample counts as 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also disagree with 4, it having a completely different mentality seem irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thought with that one was less about game balance and more that I think creating something with a distinctly alien mentality should simply be harder from a setting perspective. I just feel that creating a new species with a mind totally divergent from humanity should be harder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also add that some minor supernatural abilities are fine for Ambition 1 witch mostly make the race more interesting and maybe some minor bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be careful about adding supernatural powers to Celestial Ambition 1 races, as opposed to individuals, because I think a race, that is, a breeding population that can pass on gifts to their offspring, is inherently a larger scope than simply giving supernatural powers to an individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T10:41:15-08:00","id":1267615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1267605#post1267605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My thought with that one was less about game balance and more that I think creating something with a distinctly alien mentality should simply be harder from a setting perspective. I just feel that creating a new species with a mind totally divergent from humanity should be harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can create flora and fauna and everything inbetween and none have the same mentality as humans, sorcerers clearly have no trouble with it. Of course, such is prime real estate for the storyteller to move in if the finesse is lower than 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1267605#post1267605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would be careful about adding supernatural powers to Celestial Ambition 1 races, as opposed to individuals, because I think a race, that is, a breeding population that can pass on gifts to their offspring, is inherently a larger scope than simply giving supernatural powers to an individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed in the case where it might have a significant mechanical benefit. But say the circle come across a ruin where everything is goddamn blue. Turns out the inhabitants were a race that turned everything their skin touched blue, so they were subject to genocide by their neighbours who were tired of this race making everything blue all the damn time. The circle sorcerer rather like the color blue, in fact, it is their favorite color. So they restore the race. I would hardly call for an increased ambition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T05:08:11-08:00","id":1267808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1267605#post1267605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thought with that one was less about game balance and more that I think creating something with a distinctly alien mentality should simply be harder from a setting perspective. I just feel that creating a new species with a mind totally divergent from humanity should be harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of mixed mind here. I can see how drastically divergent minds would be hard to model conceptually, which is crucial to the creation process. On the other hand, simply crafting people presents this very issue as opinions between two people, of the same culture even, can be so drastically divergent that they would be hard-pressed to model each other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T09:10:28-08:00","id":1267867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ajsjududnsw</div> </div> </div> </div>I know there's a 10 char limit that doesn't include quoted text but providing context is appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T22:16:11-08:00","id":1268168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1267867#post1267867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there's a 10 char limit that doesn't include quoted text but providing context is appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies. There's a thread on the main, that's talking about fighting slavery with words. <br /> <br /> So they're thinking of ways to peacefully force away the city to move away from slavery. The sorcerous workings were an incentive. Do you want slaves, or working plumbing? Do you want slaves, or do you want an endless supply of food?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think a cow that can be slaughtered each day to provide a feast for the village, and then resurrect each morning to be on the level of Terrestrial 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T23:36:17-08:00","id":1268186,"title":"","content":"I don't think immortality should be Terrestrial 3. It should probably be Celestial 2 <i>at minimum</i>, considering that you're bestowing a supernatural power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T00:51:19-08:00","id":1268200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1268186#post1268186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think immortality should be Terrestrial 3. It should probably be Celestial 2 <i>at minimum</i>, considering that you're bestowing a supernatural power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah. But it's not immortality. <br /> <br /> At least, I don't think it's like what the book means. Functionally, this just means that there's a permanent supply of meat. <br /> <br /> Like... dunno? A tree that bears fruits of meat each day, is the same. But different aesthetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T03:00:07-08:00","id":1268213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1268200#post1268200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Woah. But it's not immortality.<br /> <br /> At least, I don't think it's like what the book means. Functionally, this just means that there's a permanent supply of meat.<br /> <br /> Like... dunno? A tree that bears fruits of meat each day, is the same. But different aesthetics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An immortal cow is not immortality? The main benefit of an immortal animal is not that you can repeatedly slaugther it... <br /> A possible but sadistic thing you can do is combine a cow with a lizards ability to regenerate limbs....<br /> A beef tree is terrestrial 2 (cow+fruit tree) but for it to bear fruit each day is an additional T3 working. &quot;an existing species with a minor supernatural<br /> power that augments its strongest traits.&quot; Would probably allow a single celestial 2 working, does not match any of the listed examples but seems a fitting level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T03:20:02-08:00","id":1268778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1268213#post1268213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> An immortal cow is not immortality? The main benefit of an immortal animal is not that you can repeatedly slaugther it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait... then what is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T08:52:08-08:00","id":1268873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1268200#post1268200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woah. But it's not immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <i>a</i> form of it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1268200#post1268200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least, I don't think it's like what the book means.</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs have already addressed what the books meant by immortality, but I'd argue that being unable to permanently die is a kind of immortality that shouldn't be easy, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1268200#post1268200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Functionally, this just means that there's a permanent supply of meat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Function isn't the only concern in sorcerous workings, the how of it is also worth considering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1268200#post1268200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A tree that bears fruits of meat each day, is the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I beg to differ. Changing the fruit a tree bears and how often it bears it, is an altogether more acceptable level of alteration than making an animal that can come back across the chasm of death daily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T11:59:15-08:00","id":1271817,"title":"","content":"Oh... alright. Alright.<br /> <br /> How about this? Maybe some kind of enhancer, that can be put inside stuff? <br /> <br /> Let's say that there's some kind of plant. That creates some kind of juice or some kind of thaumaturgical ingredient. When used during the crafting process, they enhance the end result. Normal becomes exceptional. Exceptional becomes perfect. Perfect becomes a 1-dot artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T18:01:33-08:00","id":1271889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1271817#post1271817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about this? Maybe some kind of enhancer, that can be put inside stuff? <br /> <br /> Let's say that there's some kind of plant. That creates some kind of juice or some kind of thaumaturgical ingredient. When used during the crafting process, they enhance the end result. Normal becomes exceptional. Exceptional becomes perfect. Perfect becomes a 1-dot artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect equipment and one-dot artifacts aren't things anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T06:19:05-08:00","id":1271964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1271889#post1271889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect equipment and one-dot artifacts aren't things anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Graaaggghh!!!<br /> <br /> Have I ever mentioned how I really hate 3e's crafting system? <br /> <br /> How about this? An automated factory. Meant to build anything and everything a city needs. Meant for sieges and support a desert town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T06:31:27-08:00","id":1271965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1271964#post1271964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have I ever mentioned how I really hate 3e's crafting system?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have anything to do with the crafting system, dude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1271964#post1271964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about this? An automated factory. Meant to build anything and everything a city needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is this a Working?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T06:50:33-08:00","id":1271968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-wher