ass=\"message\">Also\u2026<br /> <br /> You might want to calm down a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright fine. I'll calm down. <br /> <br /> Ok. Question. Because I don't have 3e handy. Is there still the cult merit and background?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T08:52:53-08:00","id":1271985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1271984#post1271984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. Question. Because I don't have 3e handy. Is there still the cult merit and background?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Merit still exists, but works differently. It only gives Willpower now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T09:07:30-08:00","id":1271992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1271985#post1271985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Merit still exists, but works differently. It only gives Willpower now.</div> </div> </div> </div>mm... I was thinking of an alter or a temple. Something which allows for sacrifices and prayers and rituals to have great fireworks and give actual flashy powers. But is that better for manses or artifacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T11:24:19-08:00","id":1272017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1271992#post1271992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mm... I was thinking of an alter or a temple. Something which allows for sacrifices and prayers and rituals to have great fireworks and give actual flashy powers. But is that better for manses or artifacts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like the sacrifices and infrastructure are means and the flashy powers are the workings themselves. If you are after &quot;If x people are slain here, grant y power&quot; then it COULD be a working (high celestial at least depending on the details) but is way more fitting as first age artifice.<br /> <br /> Something that could work would be something like &quot;A beliver in the sorcerer may perform a sacrifice at the altar, granting them a number of dice equal to the resource value of the sacrifice x2. These dice can be spent on actions made to fulfill the purpose of the sacrifice. A practitioner can only benefit from one sacrifice per month and once a new sacrifice is made, unspent dice are lost. Human sacrifices count as resource 3 if they are taken from enemies and outsiders and 5 if they are a fellow beliver.&quot; The human sacrifice part could be taken out if the solar is not a cruel bastard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":15748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","user":"Carrot Crusader","date":". 11-30-2018, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T16:25:16-08:00","id":1272072,"title":"","content":"What would be required to break a Monstrance of Celestial Portion and free the exaltation linked to it? Or even cleanse the exaltation allowing it to enter the normal reincarnation cycle?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing certainly solar circle. We know that the Monstrances were made with very high level necromancy, makes sense they might be unmade with high level sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T06:04:35-08:00","id":1272162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1272072#post1272072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be required to break a Monstrance of Celestial Portion and free the exaltation linked to it? Or even cleanse the exaltation allowing it to enter the normal reincarnation cycle?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing certainly solar circle. We know that the Monstrances were made with very high level necromancy, makes sense they might be unmade with high level sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Breaking the monstrance is like breaking any other artifact I imagine, tricky but possible with physical violence. The hard part is actually gaining access to it. A ST is of course free to add any complications they deem fitting if any to the breaking of the monstrance.<br /> <br /> Cleansing an abyssal... If the ST want to allow it at all under the workings rule system, I would say Solar 2. &quot;Utterly transform the nature of a supernatural being&quot;. I would probably place a requirement to break the monstrance before it may be attempted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T20:14:30-08:00","id":1272521,"title":"","content":"Last I checked, we don't really know jack about Abyssals in 3e. Do they even have Monstrances? Is deconversion even possible?<br /> <br /> I'd kinda prefer it if nothing was ever said about it, In 2e, &quot;redemption&quot; was a thing nobody in-setting even knew was theoretically possible, but so much ink was poured into this clearly impossible thing that there was a step-by-step guide for doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T01:53:43-08:00","id":1273688,"title":"","content":"We were looking at cleaning shadowlands last night - which is an Ambition 1 Solar working. I couldn't think of any reason to do it above a Finesse of 1, because cleansed is cleansed. Am I missing something? Seems pretty easy for a pair of Celestial Sorcerers to do, assuming they have friends around to kick the crap out of anyone who comes to interfere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T02:30:01-08:00","id":1273689,"title":"","content":"Finesse is there to give you, the player, more say in how the Working manifests. As you say, &quot;Cleansed is cleansed,&quot; and a Finesse 1 Working <i>will</i> do the basic thing you want. However, it may not do it the <i>way</i> you want, or might have unintended side effects as a result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T05:26:55-08:00","id":1273703,"title":"","content":"I was just struggling to see a way it could be twisted by the GM. Irrelevant now though, cos they just decided not to run the game any more <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T08:26:40-08:00","id":1273724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>realitycheque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1273703#post1273703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just struggling to see a way it could be twisted by the GM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Offhand, here's some ways I could think up to make cleansing a shadowland more interesting:<ul><li>The region is now supported by the sorcerer's life (this will pass on to the sorcerer's heir, if they ever have one). Injuries to the sorcerer's body will cause &quot;wounds&quot; in the land: plants dying in an area, canyons opening up for a major cut, etc.</li> <li>The area is now so infused with life that it spontaneously generates elementals of appropriate types from natural phenomena, at a much higher rate than usual.</li> <li>The sun's light is attracted to the region, making it extremely bright during the day (not painfully so, but still quite bright), and even during the night, the air is suffused with a glow that illuminates everything, like the last moments of sunset. Your Night Caste might object.</li> <li>Children born in the area have mutations: sun-related (glowing skin, hot to the touch, ability to inflict a little extra damage on creatures of darkness), life-related ones (faster healing, resistance to disease, etc.), or some other appropriate type.</li> <li>Fixing the shadowland imposes rigid order on the area's essence, meaning that all &quot;natural&quot; processes become very scheduled - seasons <i>always</i> change at precisely the same time every year, animals mate and give birth all in one huge rush, farmers must plant exactly the same crops all together, etc. This doesn't affect the behavior of anyone with free will, but it can still be inconvenient!</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T19:06:13-08:00","id":1274293,"title":"","content":"What level should there be to be able to conjure any type of equipment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T19:57:45-08:00","id":1274298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1274293#post1274293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What level should there be to be able to conjure any type of equipment?</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically a Green Lantern Ring?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T20:03:51-08:00","id":1274299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1274298#post1274298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically a Green Lantern Ring?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda. Or shirou's projection. Only they don't... really disappear. <br /> <br /> Need a gun? Got it. Radios? Got it. Knives? Lockpicking tools? Rifle? Ok. Need a ship? One is conjured.<br /> <br /> Need an artifact? No.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of having the artifacts disappear after a scene. Except for food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T21:49:29-08:00","id":1274303,"title":"","content":"N/A. Not as a sorcerous working, not as an artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T23:06:53-08:00","id":1274310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1274303#post1274303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">N/A. Not as a sorcerous working, not as an artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a size limit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T23:12:33-08:00","id":1274311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1274303#post1274303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">N/A. Not as a sorcerous working, not as an artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a size limit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T23:34:57-08:00","id":1274313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1274310#post1274310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a size limit?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It would have to have <i>many</i> limits, because otherwise it obviates <i>entire stretches of the game</i>. <br /> <br /> A player whose character has this Working as-presented never needs to negotiate with a merchant for a precious technique scroll for his martial arts-focused Lunar mate (or steal it), because he can just fabricate a perfect copy of the scroll into existence. <br /> <br /> He never has to roll Survival to find food in the wilderness, because he can will into existence a sizzling-hot platter of his mother's recipe for Lookshy-style curry rice - any time he feels like it. <br /> <br /> He never needs to roll Bureaucracy to study the ebb and flow of the city's finances to find black-market dealers, because anything he could buy from them, he could create <i>ex nihilo</i>. Shit, he never needs to find a fence, either - he can just create a talent of silver for the hell of it. <br /> <br /> The dead will never threaten him, because he can just blink cakes of salt or rows of sprouted grain into existence. Fair Folk will not bother him, because he can conjure iron with his mind. <br /> <br /> He never has to roll Craft, ever.<br /> <br /> Trying to run a game with a player with this Working, is like trying to keep a video game challenging when the player has access to all the console commands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-14-2018, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T23:42:16-08:00","id":1274317,"title":"","content":"<b>At bare minimum</b>, I'd require that it cost a point of Willpower <i>per Resources dot</i> you'd need to be able to purchase it outright, and I wouldn't let it make magic or artifacts, living things, or anything more massive than a person. <br /> <br /> I'd also require a roll if it needed to be made to certain specifications - Larceny or Craft, for instance, to make a key that fits a specific lock, Bureaucracy for convincing paperwork, Linguistics to have something in someone else's handwriting/style, Medicine for getting the dosage right on a serum to treat someone, Martial Arts in the given style for the technique scroll mentioned earlier, et cetera.<br /> <br /> Probably also just a general &quot;no shenanigans&quot; clause.<br /> <br /> If all that was in there, then maybe, <i>maybe</i>, Celestial 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-14-2018, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T00:00:57-08:00","id":1274510,"title":"","content":"Oh god finally. A computer. <br /> <br /> That... wasn't what I meant. Do you remember glorious solar saber and glorious solar plate? That, except that there's no artifact crafting. No, you can't make stuff out of thin air.... but you can craft yourself a good sword when you're surprised in your bed. You can craft a laptop with a internet connection or a satellite phone when you're dropped into the wilderness from a falling airship. <br /> <br /> That's... kinda it. Like... if there's info, its info you can find in a local library. If you want a book on how to mechanical clocks work, you can get it. Books on how to defeat the Yozis? On that new martial art? No. <br /> <br /> The part about survival, craft, and fair folk are a thing, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T05:03:52-08:00","id":1274544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1274510#post1274510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you can't make stuff out of thin air.... but you can craft yourself a good sword when you're surprised in your bed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, unless you happen to have an ingot of iron by your bedside, ready to be forged, how is your scenario <i>not</i> &quot;[making] stuff out of thin air?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1274510#post1274510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part about survival, craft, and fair folk are a thing, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, even without the capacity to wish for artifacts or conjure something that possesses knowledge you don't have, this power is straight-up <i>better</i> than Magpie\u2019s Nest Resourcefulness, the Lunar Charm we were given a preview of in July.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-15-2018, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T12:17:35-08:00","id":1279018,"title":"","content":"An idea. Willpower is precious in 3e, right?<br /> <br /> Why not being able to mass summon demons, and spend extra willpower to do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T15:14:16-08:00","id":1279055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1279018#post1279018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idea. Willpower is precious in 3e, right?<br /> <br /> Why not being able to mass summon demons, and spend extra willpower to do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Willpower is precious but gained in my experience easily. Having a mass summons that requires devoting nightly willpower over a month, culminating in the ritual gate opening on a new moon could work maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T15:46:01-08:00","id":1279066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1279055#post1279055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower is precious but gained in my experience easily. Having a mass summons that requires devoting nightly willpower over a month, culminating in the ritual gate opening on a new moon could work maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Goddamnit. I think my vision of sorcery is much different from yours","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T16:58:42-08:00","id":1279076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1279066#post1279066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goddamnit. I think my vision of sorcery is much different from yours</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your vision of the entire Exalted setting, much less Sorcery, is very much different from ours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T03:56:53-08:00","id":1279157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1279066#post1279066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Goddamnit. I think my vision of sorcery is much different from yours</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if we are talking about a working instead of a spell, it would need to be more an object or place then a 'spell'. The problem with a spell is that Exalted tries to avoid making spells redundant--and a mass summon spell would make the other summon spells redundant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T22:50:57-08:00","id":1280832,"title":"","content":"After several years of careful cultivation by the mighty sorcerer, a small tree finally grows. Once during each month, the tree bears a single fruit; whoever eats the fruit becomes one year physically younger.<br /> <br /> It's not quite the peaches of immortality, but it'll do.<br /> <br /> (I was thinking Solar Ambition 3, but I'm actually not sure if the effects are too little or too much. It doesn't sound nearly as impressive as making modifications to the entire cosmos, but I assume that if restoring someone to the prime of youth is Solar Ambition 1, something that continually spits out age-reducing fruits without requiring another working is even better than that.<br /> <br /> As far as immortality having a catch: someone could steal the fruit or even the tree, and there are probably <i>millions</i> of people in Creation who would commit any number of murders to get this thing in their possession.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T05:56:44-08:00","id":1280884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1280832#post1280832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After several years of careful cultivation by the mighty sorcerer, a small tree finally grows. Once during each month, the tree bears a single fruit; whoever eats the fruit becomes one year physically younger.<br /> <br /> It's not quite the peaches of immortality, but it'll do.<br /> <br /> (I was thinking Solar Ambition 3, but I'm actually not sure if the effects are too little or too much. It doesn't sound nearly as impressive as making modifications to the entire cosmos, but I assume that if restoring someone to the prime of youth is Solar Ambition 1, something that continually spits out age-reducing fruits without requiring another working is even better than that.<br /> <br /> As far as immortality having a catch: someone could steal the fruit or even the tree, and there are probably <i>millions</i> of people in Creation who would commit any number of murders to get this thing in their possession.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. Could work either as artifice (craft with gardening specialty) or working. I would say solar 2. Solar 1 is restoring a person to its prime, this let you sell, spread out and repeat to a smaller extent but more in the long run. Consider questions such as; does the fruit spoil? Can you eat yourself into non-existance? Is it addictive? What if you split the fruit? What happens to bugs who have a nibble, if they do at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":15748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","user":"Carrot Crusader","date":". 01-15-2019, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T07:34:43-08:00","id":1280899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1280832#post1280832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After several years of careful cultivation by the mighty sorcerer, a small tree finally grows. Once during each month, the tree bears a single fruit; whoever eats the fruit becomes one year physically younger.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I was thinking Solar Ambition 3, but I'm actually not sure if the effects are too little or too much. It doesn't sound nearly as impressive as making modifications to the entire cosmos, but I assume that if restoring someone to the prime of youth is Solar Ambition 1, something that continually spits out age-reducing fruits without requiring another working is even better than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd peg it as Solar 1. Yes, it can spread out the youth a bit more than just restoring one person, but it also takes much longer to restore any one person, and as you noted yourself, it's much more vulnerable to theft. If you want to ensure it's Solar 1, maybe put a cap on the number of fruits a person can eat in a given time, either a hard cap (&quot;no more than three fruits in a year&quot;), or a softer one (&quot;Each fruit eaten in a year after the first requires a (Stamina + Resistance) roll, with failure creating a permanent flaw&quot;).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T16:25:19-08:00","id":1281003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1280884#post1280884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. Could work either as artifice (craft with gardening specialty) or working. I would say solar 2. Solar 1 is restoring a person to its prime, this let you sell, spread out and repeat to a smaller extent but more in the long run. Consider questions such as; does the fruit spoil? Can you eat yourself into non-existance? Is it addictive? What if you split the fruit? What happens to bugs who have a nibble, if they do at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say:<br /> - The fruit spoils eventually, but it lasts a good while -- certainly long enough to transport and sell the fruits, if you've a mind to. (Of course, given that standard age-staving cordial costs Resources 5 in 3e, something that actually makes you <i>younger</i> would be hard to put a price tag on. Probably the kind of thing you trade for favors instead of money.) After two Calibrations have passed, the fruit has an uncertain effect when eaten -- the eater only gets (d10)*10% younger. After the third Calibration, the fruit is spoiled. A skilled winemaker could turn a sufficient quantity of spoiled fruits into a unique and remarkable beverage, but it won't make you any younger.<br /> - I was originally thinking that it wouldn't push someone below the prime of youth, since these are meant to be a discount version of the peaches of immortality. I'd prefer to stick with this interpretation, mainly because the idea of someone eating youth-fruit until they ended up too young to survive is really pointlessly gruesome.<br /> - It's not addictive. It doesn't really need to be. People would be desperate to get some of these fruits even before they'd ever tasted one.<br /> - Splitting the fruit probably works fine. Eat half the fruit, you get half a year younger.<br /> - I'm really not sure about the bugs. I guess if a bug nibbles 1% of a fruit, it gets a few days younger. Whoever eats the fruit probably won't notice that they only got 99% of a year younger. Practically speaking, I would expect a sorcerer who spends this much time on agriculture to have his garden protected from common pests <i>somehow</i>, but you never know.<br /> <br /> If that would be merely Solar 1, do you think Solar Ambition 3 would be enough for a tree that grows an actual peach of immortality (or something functionally indistinguishable) once per year? I was thinking this was too much because Gnomon's Eternity-Reaping Renewal only produces one per decade; on the other hand, it's a lot easier for Gnomon's wielder to keep his staff safe than it is to protect a tree that can't easily be moved. (I wonder if the gods would be offended if some asshole sorcerer managed to reproduce their precious peaches.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T20:50:05-08:00","id":1283642,"title":"","content":"How about a plant that gives out fruits, that can, with a medicine roll, transform into organs. Eyes, kidneys, livers, blood, skin... you can't create limbs from it, though, and it doesn't give you any bonuses for surgery. Just a cool way to give out supplies for your hospital. <br /> <br /> Or appease beastmen. Or sacrifice hearts to the unconquered sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T01:13:40-08:00","id":1293255,"title":"","content":"An engine, a gold and silver wheel meant to imitate the passage of the sun and moon across the sky. As long as they move, it moves.<br /> <br /> Its purpose is to act as a source of motive power. It can be hooked up to a wheel to power a mill or a factory... Or hooked up to a cart to power a locomotive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T08:56:45-08:00","id":1293298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1293255#post1293255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An engine, a gold and silver wheel meant to imitate the passage of the sun and moon across the sky. As long as they move, it moves.<br /> <br /> Its purpose is to act as a source of motive power. It can be hooked up to a wheel to power a mill or a factory... Or hooked up to a cart to power a locomotive.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds more like an artifact than a sorcerous working. But if you're doing it as a working, I'd say Celestial, Ambition 1?<br /> <br /> I feel it should be Celestial because it is clearly supernatural (per the guidelines in the book), but while it's exceptionally useful from a mortal perspective, it's not really that <i>powerful</i> as sorcery goes. Although I might be underestimating the creative uses a player would get up to with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T18:17:27-08:00","id":1293392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1293298#post1293298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds more like an artifact than a sorcerous working. But if you're doing it as a working, I'd say Celestial, Ambition 1?<br /> <br /> I feel it should be Celestial because it is clearly supernatural (per the guidelines in the book), but while it's exceptionally useful from a mortal perspective, it's not really that <i>powerful</i> as sorcery goes. Although I might be underestimating the creative uses a player would get up to with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry then. <br /> <br /> I was more thinking of that time line where alchemical stayed when autobot left. <br /> <br /> It ended up with then having trains. <br /> <br /> So I was thinking about how useful something like a train or engine would be like. Powering a locomotive to boost trade (no need for canals), powering a wheel for milling or for factories (no need for rivers) or to act as a pump. <br /> <br /> Ambition 1 (Goal Number 5): Create or bind magical <br /> entities capable of performing mundane, household chores, <br /> but not much else, in service to a person, organization, or <br /> structure. <br /> <br /> Is it that much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T16:34:46-08:00","id":1294921,"title":"","content":"The mountain-tugging stallion (Celestial circle, Ambition 2)<br /> <br /> A bizarre looking horse, with a mane of shining silver and hooves that screech out lightning as it runs, whether on air, water, or stone. Average-sized but with a presence like that of lightning, the stallion was made by a lunar sorcerer for his dignitaries and ambassadors, as they complained of how their trips to other nations took a long time through hazardous conditions. <br /> <br /> Essence: 5, Essence pool: 80<br /> <br /> Attributes: Stamina 7, Strength 7, Appearance 3, Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> Abilities: Athletics 6 (+3 in a straight line), Awareness 3, Dodge 5, Integrity 2 (+3 to serve my master), Resistance 4, Survival 4<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> <b>Home in any place</b>: The stallion gains no damage from extreme environmental conditions. Note that this applies only to things like hail, rainstorms, or blizzards. The Stallion will die if struck by an avalanche, or hit by lava<br /> <br /> <b>Dragging them along for a ride</b>: The Stallion can carry people upon its back, or drag a carriage behind it. The structure and construction of the carriage is irrelevant, as long as there is some physical connection like a piece of rope or reigns. <br /> <br /> <b>Fast as hell:</b> The horse's travel speed is 100 miles per hour. Same as stormwind rider<br /> <br /> Charms: <br /> <b>Anyplace, anytime (10m)</b><br /> The horse gets no difficulty from terrain or even the lack of it. It can travel upon water, snow, forest, or air, the same as solid stone. This charm lasts for <br /> <br /> <b>Reinforcement </b>(15m)<br /> The horse creates fortified spiritual armor about itself, and its passengers. Add 10 soak to bashing and lethal, and 5 hardness for bashing and lethal to both the horse and whatever is attached to it. If the carriage the horse pulls is open-aired, the armour manifests as shimmering transparent fields. <br /> <br /> <b>Landscape travel</b> (10m)<br /> The horse doubles movement speed for a scene, whether to escape pursuit or to capture a fleeing prisoner.<br /> <br /> A/N: This is probably terrible. A construct meant to carry moderately large amounts of cargo, a small entourage of dignitaries, or a circle of exalted across Creation without slow travel, harassment by bandits, or having to get your own sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T17:58:02-08:00","id":1294935,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea. I had been considering ideas for a sorcerously-created super horse myself, so this is interesting to see. Perhaps I'll write one up a bit later.<br /> <br /> The Stallion really needs actual combat traits to be properly evaluated; even if it's not supposed to be able to fight by itself at all, it certainly needs a dice pool for combat movement and a speed bonus (and soak, Evasion, health levels etc.). The Landscape Travel charm should probably have an alternate function for how it works in combat or tests of speed, too.<br /> <br /> What does the &quot;Dragging Them Along for a Ride&quot; merit actually do? What can the Stallion drag that a normal horse couldn't?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm a little torn. I don't think the Mountain-Tugging Stallion is quite on par with a Second Circle demon, but its speed (200 mph with Landscape Travel!) and +10 soak bonus for itself and its passengers are downright amazing benefits. Honestly, this guy would be wasted on lugging a carriage around when he could be carrying an Exalted horseman into battle.<br /> <br /> I guess I'd agree with Celestial Ambition 2 if I had to make a decision, but if I were GMing for you I'd probably suggest downgrading that soak bonus, or coming up with an alternative mechanic for the Stallion to protect its passengers. (Maybe it can reflexively Defend Other for its passengers or something?)<br /> <br /> I think allowing sorcerously-created minions that can effectively buff the PCs themselves, like with this soak bonus, could get out of hand quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T18:57:22-08:00","id":1294948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1294935#post1294935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the idea. I had been considering ideas for a sorcerously-created super horse myself, so this is interesting to see. Perhaps I'll write one up a bit later.<br /> <br /> The Stallion really needs actual combat traits to be properly evaluated; even if it's not supposed to be able to fight by itself at all, it certainly needs a dice pool for combat movement and a speed bonus (and soak, Evasion, health levels etc.). The Landscape Travel charm should probably have an alternate function for how it works in combat or tests of speed, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so sorry. But the Stallion... is kinda like the Stalwart servitor. No fighting. Though if you want to write one, you do it. I got no idea what to do. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What does the &quot;Dragging Them Along for a Ride&quot; merit actually do? What can the Stallion drag that a normal horse couldn't?</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>You ever seen those flying carriages, those flying chariots, and those people on flying horses? Ever wondered how they did that? <br /> <br /> I mean, the horse is the magical thingy. Not the carriage. By all means and physics, the carriage should be hanging down from the horse's shoulders, the inhabitants hanging on for dear life as their ride nearly tips over. And when the horse goes at high speed... why doesn't the reigns snap apart or break? <br /> <br /> That's what the merit is for. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Anyway, I'm a little torn. I don't think the Mountain-Tugging Stallion is quite on par with a Second Circle demon, but its speed (200 mph with Landscape Travel!) and +10 soak bonus for itself and its passengers are downright amazing benefits. Honestly, this guy would be wasted on lugging a carriage around when he could be carrying an Exalted horseman into battle.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>To be frank, most of the stuff I think up is kinda in between first and second circle. As stated before, this is for mortals to arrive in style. The speed is lifted straight from stormwind rider, and the +10 bonus is because I realized that this would be pretty damned uncool if it allowed itself and its passengers to be slaughtered by the a dragonblooded with an archery excellency or a few hawkmen mercenaries. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'd probably suggest downgrading that soak bonus, or coming up with an alternative mechanic for the Stallion to protect its passengers. (Maybe it can reflexively Defend Other for its passengers or something?)</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Ok, man. Maybe. Because... I'm not sure how to write it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I think allowing sorcerously-created minions that can effectively buff the PCs themselves, like with this soak bonus, could get out of hand quickly</span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> Goddamn it. I had an idea. An oracle, a seer, and a manipulator. Good at plots, scheming, manipulation, and building networks. Its schtick is that it can do things like grant wishes and power. Doing things like granting background merits, resource dots, ability and attributes dots, adding things like exalted healing or enhanced skin, or even thaumaturgy merit. The idea is that when it 'blesses' you, it also implants suggestions, hypnotic commands, and small intimacies or principles. <br /> <br /> Say, for example, a politician comes to her, and asks. &quot;I wish for a blessing for my oratory, so that I may win over my compatriots and get elected to high seat.&quot; And she will grant him a bonus. 2 extra dots for social or persuasion. Lets him win. And in exchange, he gets an intimacy or principle of &quot;I will obey the oracle who helped me obtain my position.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or a farmboy coming up to her, begging to be a hero. She grants him skill with the sword, command, and the exalted healing merit. In exchange, he has literally zero defenses to any commands that she gives. And then he leads a mercenary company, because that's what happens when you get war 3 and Melee 4. A good source of violence and knee breakers. <br /> <br /> Little boosts. Little enhancements. Little webs of influence, spreading from the oracle. </span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T16:25:37-08:00","id":1295412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1294948#post1294948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm so sorry. But the Stallion... is kinda like the Stalwart servitor. No fighting. Though if you want to write one, you do it. I got no idea what to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, fair enough. Even if the Stallion itself can't fight at all, though, it probably should have traits like soak and health levels for when someone attacks it, and a dice pool for movement. It would still be extraordinarily helpful to someone who wants to ride into battle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1294948#post1294948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You ever seen those flying carriages, those flying chariots, and those people on flying horses? Ever wondered how they did that?<br /> <br /> I mean, the horse is the magical thingy. Not the carriage. By all means and physics, the carriage should be hanging down from the horse's shoulders, the inhabitants hanging on for dear life as their ride nearly tips over. And when the horse goes at high speed... why doesn't the reigns snap apart or break?<br /> <br /> That's what the merit is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. That's pretty cool, then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1294948#post1294948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be frank, most of the stuff I think up is kinda in between first and second circle. As stated before, this is for mortals to arrive in style. The speed is lifted straight from stormwind rider, and the +10 bonus is because I realized that this would be pretty damned uncool if it allowed itself and its passengers to be slaughtered by the a dragonblooded with an archery excellency or a few hawkmen mercenaries.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, man. Maybe. Because... I'm not sure how to write it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure either. Maybe instead of a scenelong buff, a thing where the horse spends 5 motes per attack to somehow defend its passengers? Maybe it can reflexively Defend Other (even if it doesn't seem physically plausible for the Stallion to interpose itself against the attack) or something, or it can just spend 5m per attack to add a large soak/hardness bonus?<br /> <br /> I dunno, I just think +10 soak for everyone could be excessive. Riding the horse would be better than having Diamond-Body Prana, and everyone gets the boost at once.<br /> <br /> Sorry if I'm sounding overly negative. I'm not really an expert on game balance either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1294948#post1294948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goddamn it. I had an idea. An oracle, a seer, and a manipulator. Good at plots, scheming, manipulation, and building networks. Its schtick is that it can do things like grant wishes and power. Doing things like granting background merits, resource dots, ability and attributes dots, adding things like exalted healing or enhanced skin, or even thaumaturgy merit. The idea is that when it 'blesses' you, it also implants suggestions, hypnotic commands, and small intimacies or principles.<br /> <br /> Say, for example, a politician comes to her, and asks. &quot;I wish for a blessing for my oratory, so that I may win over my compatriots and get elected to high seat.&quot; And she will grant him a bonus. 2 extra dots for social or persuasion. Lets him win. And in exchange, he gets an intimacy or principle of &quot;I will obey the oracle who helped me obtain my position.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or a farmboy coming up to her, begging to be a hero. She grants him skill with the sword, command, and the exalted healing merit. In exchange, he has literally zero defenses to any commands that she gives. And then he leads a mercenary company, because that's what happens when you get war 3 and Melee 4. A good source of violence and knee breakers.<br /> <br /> Little boosts. Little enhancements. Little webs of influence, spreading from the oracle. [/FONT]<br /> [/FONT]<br /> [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a fun idea. (I'm guessing you were fond of Malefactors in 2e?) I was thinking it would be hard to balance, but if it doesn't make people any more powerful than &quot;talented mortal with a few unusual merits,&quot; that's not unreasonable.<br /> <br /> It sounds like something a Second Circle demon (i.e. a being created by an Ambition 3 Celestial working) could do. Or perhaps, you might cut out the middleman and have a sorcerer simply develop a spell that works this way: it grants someone (insert benefits here) in exchange for them swearing an oath.<br /> <br /> Honestly, a spell that gives a mortal some buffs in exchange for their oath is probably less powerful than Demon of the First Circle (although if you're trying to spread influence throughout mortal society, having your agents be humans is probably rather important).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T17:31:46-08:00","id":1295417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1295412#post1295412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is a fun idea. (I'm guessing you were fond of Malefactors in 2e?) I was thinking it would be hard to balance, but if it doesn't make people any more powerful than &amp;quot;talented mortal with a few unusual merits,&amp;quot; that's not unreasonable.<br /> <br /> It sounds like something a Second Circle demon (i.e. a being created by an Ambition 3 Celestial working) could do. Or perhaps, you might cut out the middleman and have a sorcerer simply develop a spell that works this way: it grants someone (insert benefits here) in exchange for them swearing an oath.<br /> <br /> Honestly, a spell that gives a mortal some buffs in exchange for their oath is probably less powerful than Demon of the First Circle (although if you're trying to spread influence throughout mortal society, having your agents be humans is probably rather important).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Verdant emptiness endowment, and all that shit? I want to squeeze them down. Put them into... Say, 2 or 3 charms. Add in a few more. Give her the equivalent of sidereal astrology and charm that can enhance extended rolls. Want to build an army for your kingdom, but you're nervous cause it'll take years? Don't worry. It'll take only 3 months. Just sign on the dotted line. <br /> <br /> Add in telepathic connection to anyone she has blessed. Thing is, I want to turn the demon whose functionally useless in close combat and upfront battle.... And is hilariously, heinously awful when given time and a chance to work behind the scenes. The power to shift kingdoms, break empires, lead mortal peasants to victory over godblooded and fae and ghosts... And no one realizes. They just think its just people rolling natural 20s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T17:34:35-08:00","id":1295418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1295412#post1295412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, fair enough. Even if the Stallion itself can't fight at all, though, it probably should have traits like soak and health levels for when someone attacks it, and a dice pool for movement. It would still be extraordinarily helpful to someone who wants to ride into battle.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, okay. That's pretty cool, then.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not really sure either. Maybe instead of a scenelong buff, a thing where the horse spends 5 motes per attack to somehow defend its passengers? Maybe it can reflexively Defend Other (even if it doesn't seem physically plausible for the Stallion to interpose itself against the attack) or something, or it can just spend 5m per attack to add a large soak/hardness bonus?<br /> <br /> I dunno, I just think +10 soak for everyone could be excessive. Riding the horse would be better than having Diamond-Body Prana, and everyone gets the boost at once.<br /> <br /> Sorry if I'm sounding overly negative. I'm not really an expert on game balance either.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But the stallion is on the level of Oct avian. Second circle demon. <br /> <br /> Ya know... Guy who eats solar for breakfast?<br /> <br /> Maybe I should make it work both ways. A 10 penalty for attacking... For both sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T04:27:21-07:00","id":1295533,"title":"","content":"Hey, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11237_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11237\" data-vbnamecard=\"11237\">Jefepato</a> <br /> <br /> <b>The Granter of Wishes. The Giver of Might, The Deadly Bargainer. The Holy Grail. </b><br /> <br /> Appearance: One mode is that of a woman with silver hair and red eyes, skin pale as snow. Another is that of a maiden, clad in holy vestments, hair the colour of the sun, holding a cup of quintessence<br /> <br /> Attributes: Intelligence 7, Wits 7, Perception 6, Appearance 8, Manipulation 6, Charisma 7, Stamina 2, Dexterity 2, Strength 1<br /> <br /> Abilities: Combat 2, War 4, Lore 8, Bureaucracy 7, Athletics 3, Craft 2 (+3 to symbol of office), Dodge 2 (+3 to armed foes), Integrity 6 (+3 further the plans of the master), Investigation 3 (+3 to those who adore me), Medicine 2, Socialize 7, Presence 7, Performance 4 (+2 to instilling love for me), Occult 4 (+2 to understanding supernatural politics)<br /> <br /> Essence 7, Willpower 9 <br /> <br /> <b>Passive charms: </b><br /> <br /> <b>Beautiful Idol</b><br /> With a thought, the Bargainer can instill a major intimacy of love, loyalty, or any positive intimacy towards her in anyone. Roll Appearance and Socialize against their resolve. Upon success, an intimacy is formed. This intimacy may only be eroded by supernatural actions backed by essence, and not by mundane means<br /> <br /> <b>Connection to the pawns</b><br /> Anyone that holds a positive intimacy towards the Bargainer, is a valid target for this charm. With a reflexive action, she can look through their minds, look through their senses, and rifle through their memories. She can tell the faces of whom just walked past the guards who were loyal to her, or she can look into the memory of a man who she blessed to see the current going-ons in an enemy city. And not just that, but she can contact with them. Instilling flashes of insight, visions, or dreams. <br /> <br /> <b>Blessed presence</b><br /> Within her presence, all things look better. More beautiful. More healthier. And this is true. Anyone within medium range of the Bargainer, closes wounds, overcomes poison and disease, and heals faster<br /> <br /> <b>Obey your queen</b><br /> Anyone blessed by the Bargainer, or holds a positive intimacy towards her, has a -3 penalty on contesting any social influence originating from her. Whether it is a letter commanding him to throw himself against a fair folk army, or a word telling him to leave his family and march across the Southern Deserts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Active charms:</b><br /> <br /> Single Target: <br /> <br /> Enhancing the natural form<br /> Gazing upon a single target, the woman transforms him. She gains points, to be distributed amongst his attributes and abilities. She may distribute these as she sees fit. This pushes him into experience debt<br /> <br /> Transforming the social scene<br /> Upon a single target, the bargainer alters his pattern within the loom of fate itself. The pattern spiders chitter in anger, but they do not realize the deception and decide to correct the mistake as soon as possible. Points to be distributed amongst background, including Contacts, Influence, Resources, Allies, Command, and Followers<br /> <br /> Increasing essential stature<br /> The bargainer pumps essence into a mortal's form, making him greater than ever. This allows her to grant him merits, or remove deficiencies. <br /> <br /> Mission from the goddess<br /> The Grail grants a single mission to an person. This can range from 'set up a shop in nexus' to 'lead an army against the beastmen'. Regardless, as long as the action can be justified as completing the mission, the difficulty of the roll is reduced by 2<br /> <br /> Large-scale: <br /> <br /> Urgh, scratch it. <br /> <br /> Where on earth is the bureaucracy section? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T11:39:57-07:00","id":1295595,"title":"","content":"I like it. It's powerful, but I don't think it's any more powerful than Octavian overall.<br /> <br /> Her Charms should probably have Essence costs. I would say &quot;Beautiful Idol&quot; should cost Essence as well -- being able to create a Major intimacy all in one shot is a powerful effect. (Dragon-Blooded can do that once per story at the absolute apex of their Presence charm tree -- Solars don't have any way to do that at all, although perhaps they should.)<br /> <br /> I think &quot;Connections to the Pawns&quot; is a little excessive. I like the idea of her being able to communicate with her pawns at any distance, but total mind-reading is probably too much. Her ability to influence things at a distance should be limited by the agents she actually has in place -- she shouldn't be able to do all of their thinking for them.<br /> <br /> &quot;Obey Your Queen&quot; seems kind of redundant -- does she really need the extra -3 when she can casually give people Major Ties to herself, and has superhuman social dice pools besides?<br /> <br /> As for the actual wish-granting effects: my suggestion would be to keep it simple. How about this: her blessing can give the target up to (her Essence), i.e. 7 dots in improved Attributes, and one Attribute dot can be traded for two dots in Abilities and/or Merits. This could turn someone mediocre into someone fairly impressive in their field. (Someone who gains a bunch of innate Merits is probably going to be assumed to be God-Blooded by most casual observers.)<br /> <br /> Do her beneficiaries lose the benefit of their wishes if they turn against her, or are the upgrades permanent?<br /> <br /> For large-scale effects: the 3e rules for leadership and projects are really vague. Maybe her blessing can grant a leader double 8s on rolls aimed at overcoming the failure conditions of a major project?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T16:58:08-07:00","id":1295690,"title":"","content":"Gah. Sorry. I wrote that badly.<br /> <br /> Remember sleeping beauty? <br /> <br /> 'all who see her will love her'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T08:49:51-07:00","id":1296148,"title":"","content":"I got an idea. Sorcerous working. Probably Celestial. A working that alters the way you interact with the world. Makes you both immaterial.. and not. Mundane weapon strikes you? Bounces right off, or slides through, cause you're a spirit and you're not solid enough to hit. Bolt of energy that's primed for killing spirits? Dissipates harmlessly, because you've got a solid body, and that attack can only hurt spirits, ghosts, demons, or gods. But not ordinary mortals. <br /> <br /> You're both material and immaterial, whatever favours you the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T09:08:58-07:00","id":1296154,"title":"","content":"I'd worry about what that would do to the health of the game, but I don't think it's really impossible with the guidelines given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T09:16:30-07:00","id":1296158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1296148#post1296148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got an idea. Sorcerous working. Probably Celestial. A working that alters the way you interact with the world. Makes you both immaterial.. and not. Mundane weapon strikes you? Bounces right off, or slides through, cause you're a spirit and you're not solid enough to hit. Bolt of energy that's primed for killing spirits? Dissipates harmlessly, because you've got a solid body, and that attack can only hurt spirits, ghosts, demons, or gods. But not ordinary mortals.<br /> <br /> You're both material and immaterial, whatever favours you the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>So essentially infinite soak and infinite hardness? <br /> <br /> Yeah... no... not even at Solar level. <br /> <br /> It's worth mentioning that the only thing that even came close to this was the Yozi in 2E as of Return of the Scarlet Empress where they could choose to be material or immaterial based on whatever was most favorable, but stuff that could hit both still hit them. Even infernals couldn't pick up that charm until essence 10 iirc. and i think they needed to take the I AM (Yozi) charm first, so they literally weren't human enough for their exaltation to stick around at that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T09:22:57-07:00","id":1296161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1296148#post1296148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got an idea. Sorcerous working. Probably Celestial. A working that alters the way you interact with the world. Makes you both immaterial.. and not. Mundane weapon strikes you? Bounces right off, or slides through, cause you're a spirit and you're not solid enough to hit. Bolt of energy that's primed for killing spirits? Dissipates harmlessly, because you've got a solid body, and that attack can only hurt spirits, ghosts, demons, or gods. But not ordinary mortals. <br /> <br /> You're both material and immaterial, whatever favours you the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Others have raised issues but more importantly: type 2 doesn\u2019t to my knowledge exist. All charms I recall are \u201cenhance my normal stabs to hit ghosts\u201d. Are there \u201cspirit only\u201d attacks? I know bindings and exorcisms but attacks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T09:28:29-07:00","id":1296163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1296161#post1296161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Others have raised issues but more importantly: type 2 doesn\u2019t to my knowledge exist. All charms I recall are \u201cenhance my normal stabs to hit ghosts\u201d. Are there \u201cspirit only\u201d attacks? I know bindings and exorcisms but attacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I was more thinking about 'wards against demons and spirits'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T09:29:30-07:00","id":1296164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1296158#post1296158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So essentially infinite soak and infinite hardness?<br /> <br /> Yeah... no... not even at Solar level.<br /> <br /> It's worth mentioning that the only thing that even came close to this was the Yozi in 2E as of Return of the Scarlet Empress where they could choose to be material or immaterial based on whatever was most favorable, but stuff that could hit both still hit them. Even infernals couldn't pick up that charm until essence 10 iirc. and i think they needed to take the I AM (Yozi) charm first, so they literally weren't human enough for their exaltation to stick around at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Sure thing then. If you empower your attacks to hit spirits, then you can hit him. Its just that mundane attacks not backed by spirit cutting charms would just go through or bounce off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T19:00:16-07:00","id":1296555,"title":"","content":"Idea.<br /> <br /> The elevating flame<br /> <br /> A flickering, green white flame bound to a plate that releases harmless heat. The elevating fire cannot harm living creatures. Sometimes, it is used as a danger less, cheap source of heat. That is not its main function.<br /> <br /> The elevating flame burns away at the essence of imperfection, impurity, and deficiency present in all things.<br /> <br /> All inanimate objects that pass through the fire are first repaired from any damage, whether by accident or age, then enhanced to near impossible levels. Peasant clothing becomes imperial raiment. Useless quartz is transformed into gemstones the size of a fist. Base metals are transformed into solid silver. Rusted swords are transformed into gleaming steel. The transformation is decided by the creator of the item and the person putting it into the fire. Both for the items function and what is considered to be precious a sword is a sword. And always will be so. But depending on the person using it, it is transformed into a ceremonial piece covered in gemstones and embossed with gold, or a cold piece of steel capable of cutting through armour plating.<br /> <br /> The Elevating Flame cannot alter living creatures, or otherwise harm them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T23:58:48-07:00","id":1296923,"title":"","content":"An idea. A sorcerous working linked to a fire or earth demense. It outpours massive amounts of lava, that cool and solidify into solid steel. Used as a cheap source of raw materials for projects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T21:26:13-07:00","id":1297145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1296555#post1296555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idea.<br /> <br /> The elevating flame<br /> <br /> A flickering, green white flame bound to a plate that releases harmless heat. The elevating fire cannot harm living creatures. Sometimes, it is used as a danger less, cheap source of heat. That is not its main function.<br /> <br /> The elevating flame burns away at the essence of imperfection, impurity, and deficiency present in all things.<br /> <br /> All inanimate objects that pass through the fire are first repaired from any damage, whether by accident or age, then enhanced to near impossible levels. Peasant clothing becomes imperial raiment. Useless quartz is transformed into gemstones the size of a fist. Base metals are transformed into solid silver. Rusted swords are transformed into gleaming steel. The transformation is decided by the creator of the item and the person putting it into the fire. Both for the items function and what is considered to be precious a sword is a sword. And always will be so. But depending on the person using it, it is transformed into a ceremonial piece covered in gemstones and embossed with gold, or a cold piece of steel capable of cutting through armour plating.<br /> <br /> The Elevating Flame cannot alter living creatures, or otherwise harm them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a cool idea, but...it not only turns garbage into infinite wealth, but also upgrades the function of items in whatever way the person who created or who's using it would find precious? And it even does all the craftsmanship for you? (Making a ceremonial sword covered in gemstones would be quite a project, even if gold and gems were readily available.)<br /> <br /> I don't think I'd allow a single working to do all of this stuff. Even assuming it can't create or modify artifacts, it's infinite resources (of many kinds) with no effort. And just imagine the creative ways in which players would abuse it.<br /> <br /> The lava-steel thing is pretty reasonable, though. I'd probably call that Celestial Ambition 3. Infinite steel is a hell of a resource, but valuable as it is, it doesn't really feel quite big enough to be a Solar working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T21:55:00-07:00","id":1297153,"title":"","content":"Celestial ambition 3? I'll put it as... Well, ambition 2. With the caveat that it produces enough steel for an entire civilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T22:39:16-07:00","id":1297159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1297145#post1297145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a cool idea, but...it not only turns garbage into infinite wealth, but also upgrades the function of items in whatever way the person who created or who's using it would find precious? And it even does all the craftsmanship for you? (Making a ceremonial sword covered in gemstones would be quite a project, even if gold and gems were readily available.)<br /> <br /> I don't think I'd allow a single working to do all of this stuff. Even assuming it can't create or modify artifacts, it's infinite resources (of many kinds) with no effort. And just imagine the creative ways in which players would abuse it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah. <br /> <br /> ..... maybe its just me, but infinite resources kinda felt 'meh' to me. I mean, there's already a mercury ant which can transmute gold and silver, and you can hire earth elementals to dig up gold and jewellery. Someone already homebrewed demons that produce gemstones and act as living iron smelters. <br /> <br /> Maybe its 2 workings? <br /> <br /> One is a working that makes any thing that goes through it 'better'. Rusty swords goes in, pristine steel comes out. Chipped pot goes in, fine china comes out. <br /> <br /> Another is a working that transmutes materials. Pour in rock, and out comes gemstones and silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T23:45:43-07:00","id":1297169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1297159#post1297159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... maybe its just me, but infinite resources kinda felt 'meh' to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It shouldn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1297159#post1297159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there's already a mercury ant which can transmute gold and silver, and you can hire earth elementals to dig up gold and jewellery.</div> </div> </div> </div>These have their limits; the mercury ant is limited by its mote pool, the materials you give it, and the demands of its quicksilver queen; the other earth elementals by having to actually find and go get the metals you ask for, assuming there even is any that no existing elementals have claimed. Neither is spinning infinite money out of nowhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T00:30:02-07:00","id":1297176,"title":"","content":"Well, in that case, I propose a working that binds a certain back ground to you, that takes dedicated effort by supernatural means to deprive you of it. <br /> <br /> Like... you will always have resources five. No matter what. Things just go well for you, and you get rich. Stuck in North, with only your clothes on your back? In a week or so, you're eating meat beside a roaring fire, sleeping on furs. In 3 weeks, you're being fed meat from the South, with several serving girls right beside you on the king sized mattress made from the coat of whatever. <br /> <br /> You cannot be deprived of resources. Not permanently. But the only way for you to be stuck in a position you can't buy, bribe, gift, or otherwise your way out is to punt you into a deserted island. <br /> <br /> Same for, say, Allies or Contacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T05:55:46-07:00","id":1297220,"title":"","content":"Sorcerous working: ?<br /> <br /> Ambition: ?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Great Laborer of Lagadoom</b></span><br /> <br /> The town of Lagadoom once found an immense bounty. Metallic ore, in great quantity and purity. An immense find, enough to make a profit and wealth that would make a merchant prince envious. There was, of course, one problem. Transport. The town of Lagadoom, and its surrounding area, was filled with mountains. Worst of all, there was a distinct lack of trees, coal, or fuel. Lagadoom could barely process any of the ores themselves. And thus the ores and refined metals in Lagadoom stood there, useless, with the merchants only picking up the rare and easy to carry gemstones.<br /> <br /> Less than 20 miles away was a city with working refineries, one that could easily process the ore and transform it into finished goods to sell to the trade network it was connected to. Lagadoom could be transformed from sleepy mining town into a massive mining hub. If only they could transport the ores off these damnable mountains. <br /> <br /> And transport was developed by a sorcerer, native to the town, granted power by a wandering elemental of flame. Deciding to devote himself to the betterment of his home city, he called in favours from dozens of spirits, took dangerous quests to obtain rare materials such as red jade and orichalcum, and even once stole blood from a volcano god, all to complete his project. The days turned from weeks to months to seasons to years. After 2 decades of work, the Great Labourer was born. <br /> <br /> Shaped like a massive carriage, covered in red jade that glowed with the sigils symbolizing hard work, labour, non-stop diligence, and tireless perseverence, the Labourer is an automaton that frightens and awes any who look upon it. Steam and smoke hiss from a grill in its mouth, while behind it, trail the numerous carriages and containers that it uses to transport the goods and services up the mountain. With its help, the town of Lagadoom has transformed into small, sleepy town into a thriving city of tens of thousands, all with the prosperity of the mines. <br /> <br /> The sorcerer's name is lost to time, though. His corpse missing, gone to somewhere unknown. But if one were to somehow find the hatchway to the cabin of the Labourer, one would find the sorcerer's mummified corpse within, his hands clenching the steering wheel, his name etched upon the dashboard.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Strength 15, Stamina N/A, Dexterity 10, Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Perception 4<br /> <b>Abilities</b>: Athletics 8 (unsteady ground +3), Resistance 4 (+3 to dangerous environment)<br /> <br /> Merits: <br /> <br /> Steady movement: The Labourer's cargo is always in safety. No matter whether in the midst of an earthquake or moving upside down, it will always chug along, with no disruption inside. Not a drop of water will be spilled, and a pyramid of cards will not collapse. No disruption to the cargo under ordinary circumstances, save for direct attack or destruction of the labourer<br /> <br /> Anywhere goes: The Labourer can go anywhere. This is literal. It can drive over water as if dry land, move across sheer cliffs as if it was on flat ground, and ride on the tops of buildings and treetops as if it was on a flat terrain. Ignore all penalties due to terrain. <br /> <br /> Optimized procedure: The cargo must be kept well. This is a fact. Meat will not spoil. Passengers will be fed and watered. Pottery and fine China will not shatter. Ice will not melt. Anything stored in the laborer's cars and transported, will not decay or otherwise be damaged. <br /> <br /> <b>Charms: </b><br /> <br /> <b>Creation of transport (10m)</b><br /> The Laborer can transport any amount of things... as long as it has the power to do so. Spending 10m allows it to produce one passenger car, one railroad car, or anything needed for transport. <br /> <br /> <b>Host of spirits: </b><br /> Produces golems composed out of clockworks and steam to load and unload cargo, or to cook and serve food to passengers, or fight off intruders<br /> <br /> <b>Travelling the air (2m)</b><br /> Upon meeting a gap where it does not wish to cross, whether because it is a bottomless chasm or to move above a hoard of zombies, the Laborer can produce a ghostly road from beneath its wheels, that lasts long enough for the cars behind it to travel over. Every activation of this charm allows it to travel 100 meters<br /> <br /> <b>Shapechange</b><br /> The Laborer shifts and shrinks and changes beyond what should be physically possible. It can make 45 degree turns, although such a thing should snap its passenger cars in half, and it can squeeze through gaps half a meter wide. <br /> <br /> <b>Complications: </b><br /> <br /> The sorcerer was of the terrestrial circle, and so despite his attempts, some part of his working had unintended consequences. It is these consequences that there is a furnace within the Laborer, and the first car is always full of coal. The furnace powers the laborer. Were the flame were to go out, then it would slowly grind to a shuddering halt. Were anything hotter than glowing coal to be shovelled within it, then it would gain motive power and move again. The greater the fire, the hotter. Red-hot coals would make it move at normal speed. A flame akin to that of a campfire would double its normal speed. A bonfire capable of making the foremen sweat and and is burning white, make it go thrice as fast. And a great blaze capable of melting a steel sword stuck into it quadraples the Laborer's speed. <br /> <br /> Note: Not sure whether this is high terrestrial, or low celestial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T08:16:27-07:00","id":1298147,"title":"","content":"I just realized something. You can grant merits through sorcery. Unusual Hide, Mighty Thews... <br /> <br /> Can you also grant story merits, like ally, or Resources?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T12:14:41-07:00","id":1298175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1298147#post1298147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized something. You can grant merits through sorcery. Unusual Hide, Mighty Thews... <br /> <br /> Can you also grant story merits, like ally, or Resources?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you can make the battle groups command would give you, or the creature ally would give you (or use sorcery to enchant someone into being your ally) so yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T13:10:37-07:00","id":1298182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1298175#post1298175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, you can make the battle groups command would give you, or the creature ally would give you (or use sorcery to enchant someone into being your ally) so yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant give someone resources 5.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's a miscommunication here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T13:18:04-07:00","id":1298183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1298182#post1298182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant give someone resources 5.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's a miscommunication here</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just grabbing story merits. Can you make the wealth of a small nation with a working? Yeah probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T13:23:46-07:00","id":1298184,"title":"","content":"But Sorcerous Workings don\u00b4t grant merits. They grant something, that is represented as a merit.<br /> <br /> They give you a skin of flexible marble, also known as Unusual Hide 4 or 5. They turn your hands in shadowy, giant claws when the power word is pronounced, that is,Claws 3 with the Subtetly upgrade.<br /> <br /> As such, they can\u00b4t give you Resources 5. They can give you an inexhaustible fountain of liquid gold, which will allow you to live as a king (represented as... Resources 5, maybe). Or an army made of silent, self-repairing paper-soldiers (Command, with some Might). But never the raw Merit, because the raw Merit doesn\u00b4t exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T13:25:05-07:00","id":1298185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1298184#post1298184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Sorcerous Workings don\u00b4t grant merits. They grant something, that is represented as a merit.<br /> <br /> They give you a skin of flexible marble, also known as Unusual Hide 4 or 5. They turn your hands in shadowy, giant claws when the power word is pronounced, that is,Claws 3 with the Subtetly upgrade.<br /> <br /> As such, they can\u00b4t give you Resources 5. They can give you an inexhaustible fountain of liquid gold, which will allow you to live as a king (represented as... Resources 5, maybe). Or an army made of silent, self-repairing paper-soldiers (Command, with some Might). But never the raw Merit, because the raw Merit doesn\u00b4t exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also this, yes. I was being laconic, but the result of a working can be a story merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T13:36:27-07:00","id":1298188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1298184#post1298184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Sorcerous Workings don\u00b4t grant merits. They grant something, that is represented as a merit.<br /> <br /> They give you a skin of flexible marble, also known as Unusual Hide 4 or 5. They turn your hands in shadowy, giant claws when the power word is pronounced, that is,Claws 3 with the Subtetly upgrade.<br /> <br /> As such, they can\u00b4t give you Resources 5. They can give you an inexhaustible fountain of liquid gold, which will allow you to live as a king (represented as... Resources 5, maybe). Or an army made of silent, self-repairing paper-soldiers (Command, with some Might). But never the raw Merit, because the raw Merit doesn\u00b4t exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a blessing of good fortune, where you succeed in any venture you go in. Any business thrives. You meet business partners by chance. You make lucrative deals with ease and strange chance. You trip over bars of gold in the street. Jade falls out of the sky. You open a silver mine in your garden. <br /> <br /> Think of it like bestowal of accursed fortune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T15:31:45-07:00","id":1298202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1298188#post1298188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about a blessing of good fortune, where you succeed in any venture you go in. Any business thrives. You meet business partners by chance. You make lucrative deals with ease and strange chance. You trip over bars of gold in the street. Jade falls out of the sky. You open a silver mine in your garden. <br /> <br /> Think of it like bestowal of accursed fortune.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't think of any objective reason you couldn't do this, but it feels really generic. &quot;Normal money-making methods always work well for you&quot; doesn't feel nearly as sorcerous as &quot;your breath can turn corncobs into silver&quot; or something weird like that.<br /> <br /> For perfectly normal business stuff, sorcery probably shouldn't be as effective as Bureaucracy Charms in any case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T19:53:49-07:00","id":1298259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1298202#post1298202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't think of any objective reason you couldn't do this, but it feels really generic. &amp;quot;Normal money-making methods always work well for you&amp;quot; doesn't feel nearly as sorcerous as &amp;quot;your breath can turn corncobs into silver&amp;quot; or something weird like that.<br /> <br /> For perfectly normal business stuff, sorcery probably shouldn't be as effective as Bureaucracy Charms in any case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more thinking of blessed with money. Like FSN's golden rule<br /> <br /> I mean, maybe you can change that to &quot;breathe turns plants into valuable raw material&quot;, since money changes definition for many people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T21:19:01-07:00","id":1298267,"title":"","content":"Celestial 2: Hiding from the eyes of heaven<br /> <br /> Made by a savant that had become paranoid after several attempted assasinations. Especially one which nearly killed him, were it not for a sacrifice for one of his friends. Towards the end of his life, he became convinced that someone was watching him through scrying. And he decided to do something about it. <br /> <br /> At baseline level, the one with this power becomes immune to scrying and other esoteric and weird ways of attacking and viewing. Attempts to attack him via sympathetic magic or dreams fail. Remote viewing shows a blur. Attempting to divine his fate through the stars show nonsense. Upon interacting with Fate and Sidereals, the sorcerer slots seamlessly with the loom... at first glance. Only in close inspection does the sidereal realize that something is wrong. <br /> <br /> With the expenditure of one willpower, the sorcerer can activate one of these following effects:<ul><li>Extend this effect to (Occult X 2) beings</li> <li>Ward a room with this effect</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T21:57:03-07:00","id":1298269,"title":"","content":"That sounds less like a working, and more like a series of workings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T23:14:07-07:00","id":1298274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1298269#post1298269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds less like a working, and more like a series of workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you referring to the willpower thing, or is it the various effects i described?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T23:28:52-07:00","id":1298275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1298274#post1298274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you referring to the willpower thing, or is it the various effects i described?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of them. <br /> <br /> Being flat-out immune to just being viewed remotely through means such as scrying sounds like an acceptable supernatural power to grant through a working, but this is effectively <i>many</i> immunities, <i>combined</i> with the ability to bestow these immunities on others or on areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T21:14:11-07:00","id":1298841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1298275#post1298275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both of them.<br /> <br /> Being flat-out immune to just being viewed remotely through means such as scrying sounds like an acceptable supernatural power to grant through a working, but this is effectively <i>many</i> immunities, <i>combined</i> with the ability to bestow these immunities on others or on areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah. Ok then. <br /> <br /> So question. Lets say you're immune to being viewed remotely. Can you install a caveat that says 'can shut off this power selectively with one willpower'? Or is that another working?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T21:42:56-07:00","id":1298845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1298841#post1298841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woah. Ok then. <br /> <br /> So question. Lets say you're immune to being viewed remotely. Can you install a caveat that says 'can shut off this power selectively with one willpower'? Or is that another working?</div> </div> </div> </div>If your Storyteller okays it and you have a high enough Finesse, yes. Otherwise it might require a second Working to acquire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T16:29:50-07:00","id":1299073,"title":"","content":"After weeks of genealogical research and editing, the sorcerer blesses his mortal followers (a group that would, if they formed a battle group, possess a Magnitude no greater than the sorcerer's Essence) in a grand ceremony, formally adopting them in the eyes of Heaven. Alternatively, the sorcerer may incorporate a willing spirit or other supernatural being into the ritual, allowing their ally to adopt the mortals instead. (If the sorcerer himself is mortal, the inclusion of a different parent is essential for the ritual to have any substantial effect.)<br /> <br /> In any case, the mortals become, essentially, &quot;God-Blooded&quot; of the sort that they would have been had the sorcerer (or other adoptive parent) been one of their actual parents. They can be expected to gain a small number of Merits and/or Charms appropriate to both their new &quot;parent's&quot; nature and their own abilities or inclinations, making them above-average as God-Blooded go (even if the adoptive parent isn't powerful enough to normally sire such potent God-Blooded).<br /> <br /> If the sorcerer is Dragon-Blooded...I guess the mortals become elemental God-Blooded or something? I didn't really think that part through.<br /> <br /> Here's an example of an elite soldier adopted by a Solar sorcerer. I admittedly wrote this up in a bit of a hurry -- I would have liked to come up with something more interesting for the Charms.<br /> <br /> Sun-Blessed Soldier<br /> <br /> <b>Essence:</b> 2; <b>Willpower:</b> 6; <b>Join Battle:</b> 10 dice<br /> Personal Motes: 20<br /> <b>Health Levels:</b> -0/-1x3/-2x3/-4/Incap.<br /> <b>Actions:</b> Read Intentions: 6 dice; Senses: 9 dice; Threaten: 8 dice<br /> Appearance 3, Resolve 4, Guile 2<br /> <br /> <b>Combat</b><br /> Attack (Slashing sword): 12 dice (Damage 13, minimum 2)<br /> Attack (Self bow): 11 dice at short range (Damage 10)<br /> Combat Movement: 7 dice<br /> Evasion 3, Parry 5<br /> Soak/Hardness: 10/0 (heavy armor and augmented toughness)<br /> <br /> <i>Merits:</i><br /> <br /> <b>Filial Piety:</b> As long as the sun-blessed soldier maintains a positive Tie to the sorcerer who &quot;adopted&quot; him, that Tie cannot be changed or eliminated by non-magical means.<br /> <br /> <b>Radiant Martial Splendor:</b> A battle group composed of sun-blessed soldiers has Might 1, and adds their Essence (normally 2) in dice on all rout checks.<br /> <br /> <i>Charms:</i><br /> <br /> <b>Brilliant Flashing Blade</b> (3m or 5m; Supplemental; Instant; Uniform; Essence 1): For three motes, the sun-blessed soldier adds two dice to a physical attack roll with any weapon, or +1 Evasion or Parry against a single attack. If attacking or being attacked by a creature of darkness, the soldier may instead add four dice or +2 Defense for five motes.<br /> <br /> <b>Luminous Veteran's Toughness</b> (5m; Reflexive; Instant; Uniform; Essence 1): After being struck with a withering or decisive attack, the sun-blessed soldier may reduce the raw damage of the attack by two.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking this would be an Ambition 3 Celestial working? A large battle group of these soldiers wouldn't be any match for a combat-focused Second Circle demon, but if you have a variety of followers, they might have a fair number of interesting (albeit minor) abilities between them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T16:45:59-07:00","id":1299076,"title":"","content":"To start with, they'd start at essence 1, like any other empowered being. The solar started at essence 1, a working should not grant ess 2 right of the bat <br /> <br /> I'd also link the ambition of this to the size you're talking about. Just basing it on essence isn't enough.<br /> <br /> Given that you can empower an individual up to second circle demon level at Celestial 3, I think it's at least reasonable to empower a group of mortals to a lesser extent. The trick is pinning down how many is reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T17:16:36-07:00","id":1299080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1299076#post1299076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To start with, they'd start at essence 1, like any other empowered being. The solar started at essence 1, a working should not grant ess 2 right of the bat<br /> <br /> I'd also link the ambition of this to the size you're talking about. Just basing it on essence isn't enough.<br /> <br /> Given that you can empower an individual up to second circle demon level at Celestial 3, I think it's at least reasonable to empower a group of mortals to a lesser extent. The trick is pinning down how many is reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good call on the Essence thing. I think my brain is still stuck halfway in 2e. Also, I typed Magnitude when I meant Size. &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> And yeah, it probably makes sense to vary the number of people affected by Ambition. The tricky part is that there just aren't that many steps on the scale. The book does suggest that giving someone a supernatural power is Celestial Ambition 2, but it seems weird to have no intermediate steps in between &quot;minor supernatural power&quot; and &quot;Second Circle demon.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe something like this?<br /> Celestial Ambition 1: one or two people<br /> Celestial Ambition 2: a few dozen people (Size 2 group)<br /> Celestial Ambition 3: several hundred people (Size 4 group)<br /> Solar Ambition 1: up to a thousand people (Size 5 group), although personally I'd go for a smaller number of stronger minions if I could cast Solar workings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T18:14:05-07:00","id":1299088,"title":"","content":"I could also see a solar working on the level of &quot;enchant this spring to grant power to all who survive drinking from it&quot; <br /> <br /> The other thing is that the finesse of the project makes a big difference in result. Finesse 1 you might end up with a group that's empowered, but only ahem the sun is at full zenith or a solar exalt is at iconic anima level nearby or similar. The lower the finesse, the more caveats to the power or restrictions on its usefulness in general. <br /> <br /> Perhaps this burns out the mortal's life force, or each time they use the power they gain a harmless but noticeable blemish or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T18:53:37-07:00","id":1299095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1299080#post1299080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good call on the Essence thing. I think my brain is still stuck halfway in 2e. Also, I typed Magnitude when I meant Size. &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> And yeah, it probably makes sense to vary the number of people affected by Ambition. The tricky part is that there just aren't that many steps on the scale. The book does suggest that giving someone a supernatural power is Celestial Ambition 2, but it seems weird to have no intermediate steps in between &quot;minor supernatural power&quot; and &quot;Second Circle demon.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe something like this?<br /> Celestial Ambition 1: one or two people<br /> Celestial Ambition 2: a few dozen people (Size 2 group)<br /> Celestial Ambition 3: several hundred people (Size 4 group)<br /> Solar Ambition 1: up to a thousand people (Size 5 group), although personally I'd go for a smaller number of stronger minions if I could cast Solar workings</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. <br /> <br /> Like.... A question. You make a first circle demon level construct. Celestial 1 or terrestrial 3, depending on how you roll. <br /> <br /> Thats several supernatural powers right there. Stats. Abilities. Dematerialize. Several small charms.<br /> <br /> Like... Let's say I make a construct that can connect for someone's mind, serving as a prosthetic eye. It's like a eye with bat wings attached. <br /> <br /> It's got several charms for sensory. Like being able to do a medical diagnosis at a glance instead of having to take, like, an hour. Or able to anaylze substances without having to touch them. Or see the ties and binds in others peoples hearts. Their 'intimacies'.<br /> <br /> What celestial ambition is this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T19:12:05-07:00","id":1299100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1299088#post1299088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could also see a solar working on the level of &quot;enchant this spring to grant power to all who survive drinking from it&quot;<br /> <br /> The other thing is that the finesse of the project makes a big difference in result. Finesse 1 you might end up with a group that's empowered, but only ahem the sun is at full zenith or a solar exalt is at iconic anima level nearby or similar. The lower the finesse, the more caveats to the power or restrictions on its usefulness in general.<br /> <br /> Perhaps this burns out the mortal's life force, or each time they use the power they gain a harmless but noticeable blemish or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think low-Finesse workings are supposed to be less powerful or less useful. The player just gets less control over the details. In this example, if it's a Finesse 1 working then the Storyteller writes the subjects' new Charms without direct input from the player, but they're just as powerful (in theory) as they would be if the player had written them for a Finesse 5 working.<br /> <br /> Stuff like &quot;this only works at high noon&quot; or &quot;the mortal's life force burns out&quot; should really only be happening if the sorcerer rolled botches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T19:19:35-07:00","id":1299101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1299095#post1299095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. <br /> <br /> Like.... A question. You make a first circle demon level construct. Celestial 1 or terrestrial 3, depending on how you roll. </div> </div> </div> </div>No. You are incorrect. <br /> <br /> It is Celestial 1 AT MINIMUM. Because a 1st circle demon is by definition a supernatural being which you explicitly cannot create at the terrestrial level. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thats several supernatural powers right there. Stats. Abilities. Dematerialize. Several small charms.<br /> <br /> Like... Let's say I make a construct that can connect for someone's mind, serving as a prosthetic eye. It's like a eye with bat wings attached. <br /> <br /> It's got several charms for sensory. Like being able to do a medical diagnosis at a glance instead of having to take, like, an hour. Or able to anaylze substances without having to touch them. Or see the ties and binds in others peoples hearts. Their 'intimacies'.<br /> <br /> What celestial ambition is this? </div> </div> </div>This isn't even a working. This is an artifact. You've described an artifact. With evocations. Probably artifact 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T19:23:44-07:00","id":1299103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1299100#post1299100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think low-Finesse workings are supposed to be less powerful or less useful. The player just gets less control over the details. In this example, if it's a Finesse 1 working then the Storyteller writes the subjects' new Charms without direct input from the player, but they're just as powerful (in theory) as they would be if the player had written them for a Finesse 5 working.<br /> <br /> Stuff like &quot;this only works at high noon&quot; or &quot;the mortal's life force burns out&quot; should really only be happening if the sorcerer rolled botches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that may have been to restrictive. Perhaps something like &quot;each recipient gets a talisman that contains their power.&quot; is the same drug, but if it's stolen them they lose access to it. Things like that that complicates it's use but don't really reduce it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T02:02:01-07:00","id":1305662,"title":"","content":"Terrestrial 1 or 2<br /> <br /> Blessed self moving tools. <br /> <br /> Tools made from the best mundane materials and craftsmanship, further enhanced by a working that gives the life, movement, and motive power on their own. Examples include axes that cut down trees and stumps with greater strength than any mortal, lathes and grinders far more precise and fast than any mortal powered version. Self stirring cauldrons, spades, and other things serve to increase the rate of work of anybody using such tools, as long as the tools are appropriate. <br /> <br /> Sorry if this is a repeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T09:19:57-07:00","id":1305736,"title":"","content":"The Sighing Maiden (Celestial 3)<br /> <br /> The Sighing Maiden was created during the Shogunate to serve as the companion of the daughter of the Daimyo of Fallen Leaves. She was modeled after the 2nd Circle Demon Mara, meaning that she is a Celestial-level practitioner of supernatural martial arts and a Celestial-level sorceress (she also possesses a number of spiritual and elemental charms). While the Daimyo of Fallen Leaves died over 1,000 years ago, the Sighing Maiden still watches over her descendants, and will act as a mentor for any of her Dragon-Blooded descendants.<br /> <br /> In order to facilitate the protection of the descendants of the Daimyo of Fallen Leaves, the Sighing Maiden has created nine sisters of equal power to her, around one century, and each of them have created their own sisters. In total, fifty-five Sighing Maidens now exist, each with a different human appearance that allows them to blend in with human populations, though they are all based off the original model. Fifty of them mentor and protect the 500 surviving descendants of the Daimyo of Fallen Leaves while five of them act as messengers between the communities protected by the fifty other sisters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T10:39:51-07:00","id":1305758,"title":"","content":"Hmm. It seems a bit iffy for a sorcerer to be able to reliably create other sorcerers that in turn create other sorcerers, Von Neumann style. Like Exaltation itself, the <i>capacity</i> to wield sorcery in 3e is supposed to be something numinous and ill-understood, even by masters of the occult; they can recognize it when they see it, but replicating it is another matter.<br /> <br /> \u200bPersonally, I'd have them end up different from one another in other ways beyond just how their human form works, as an attempt sometimes develops a curious wrinkle, or the exigencies of the situation causing them to consciously make different decisions in the next maiden's creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-18-2019, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T12:53:57-07:00","id":1308762,"title":"","content":"Celestial 2<br /> <br /> Great Stone pillars placed beside the main gate. All who wish to enter the city must walk through them first. <br /> <br /> As they walk through, the pillars grant understanding of a language, that lasts for a month, and is indefinite as long as the recipient stays within the city itself. <br /> <br /> The pillars were made to facilitate trade, enabling fast and easy communication and deal making, with the City itself taking a cut from any deal.<br /> <br /> Another great use of the pillars, is the current influx of refugees. Most would have issues assimilating, lack of communication, strange habits and foreign mannerisms separating them. But with a common lingua franca, it is far easier for them to interact with the ordinary residents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T16:40:29-07:00","id":1308823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1308762#post1308762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another great use of the pillars, is the current influx of refugees. Most would have issues assimilating, lack of communication, strange habits and foreign mannerisms separating them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is nowhere near the problem some make it out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T16:45:49-07:00","id":1308824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1308823#post1308823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is nowhere near the problem some make it out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, its just a thing. <br /> <br /> To be honest, the problem is different culture, not having jobs, living in different areas, etc...<br /> <br /> But I digress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T17:45:47-07:00","id":1309336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1308824#post1308824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, the problem is different culture, not having jobs, living in different areas, etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, though, none of these are the problems that the pundits and other talking heads are making them out to be. The differences that immigrants bring to the table generally end up improving the place overall.<br /> <br /> (Not counting colonialism, et cetera., naturally, as that's a whole other kettle of fish.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-01-2019, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T20:03:04-07:00","id":1309364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1309336#post1309336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, though, none of these are the problems that the pundits and other talking heads are making them out to be. The differences that immigrants bring to the table generally end up improving the place overall.<br /> <br /> (Not counting colonialism, et cetera., naturally, as that's a whole other kettle of fish.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, then ignore that then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T06:20:57-07:00","id":1310030,"title":"","content":"A statue stands in the Underworld. A person who is hungry may give a point of Willpower to the statue, and in a short burst of varicolored light, food will appear in sufficient quantity to sate them for a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T10:44:08-07:00","id":1310063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1308823#post1308823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is nowhere near the problem some make it out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not as dangerous for the locals as right-wing pundits make it out to be (and I think that &quot;refusal to integrate&quot; is often an over-blown excuses to hide disdain for a different colour of skin, which you can tell by seeing how very integrated immigrants are treated) but I teach English to refugees, and many of them feel really isolated because they don't speak good English or understand our customs, so they find it really difficult to make friends, not to mention get a job. Anti-immigrant xenophobes tend to say &quot;they refuse to get jobs!&quot; which is rubbish, because many of them are desperate to get jobs just to get out of the house and meet people (or the government bans them from getting a job), but they find it difficult to get hired because employers prefer to hire people with good English. Not to mention getting a <i>good</i> job, which requires much better English than stacking shelves or driving a taxi. I've taught several Iranians and a Palestinian with medical degrees from their own country, who need to pass the English exam required to be a doctor here. And that exam is<i> hard</i>. Learning English (or any language) is not at all easy (unless your own language is really similar, of course, but you still need to do a lot of work; though that's work that people in the past often did put in instead of learning science or maths).<br /> <br /> Similarly, when I lived in China, my lack of Chinese obviously made it impossible for me to do most jobs, or make friends with most people. All my friends were people who happened to be good at English.<br /> <br /> If my students could just walk past a magic pillar and learn English like that (and understand our humour!)... that'd change their lives. (And put me out of a job, but oh well.)<br /> <br /> Of course, on the other hand... Creation seems to be (it's never entirely clear or consistent, so I'm sure several people can easily jump in and give three contradictory arguments against this) a place where most people across an entire continent speak mutually intelligible dialects. If the eastern An-Tengian mountainous city of Shining Trees is a popular place for merchants from across the great desert of the south, who come hundreds of miles to exchange their goods for those from the Cinder Coast, and then one year a flood of refugees come fleeing the destruction of Gem... well, they all speak Firetongue anyway, so there's hardly a need for magical translation.<br /> <br /> I suppose it might be useful in a huge port city like Wu Jian or Chiaroscoro.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As they walk through, the pillars grant understanding of a language, that lasts for a month, and is indefinite as long as the recipient stays within the city itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Celestial, but I'm not sure what Ambition. I'd probably go for 2 or 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A person who is hungry may give a point of Willpower to the statue, and in a short burst of varicolored light, food will appear in sufficient quantity to sate them for a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Food for ghosts, or real food?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T13:11:43-07:00","id":1310094,"title":"","content":"It's &quot;real&quot; in the sense that it doesn't trap you in the Underworld or only nourish ghosts or whatever. The Solar who created it wanted people to worship the person the statue was made in the image of. However, the food also dissolves after a day, and if you eat it for more than a week you stop recovering Willpower from sleep until you spend a like amount of time eating food that wasn't transmuted from your Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T13:17:33-07:00","id":1310097,"title":"","content":"Idea.<br /> <br /> Light. Or more accurately, sunlight. A lunar held dominion over a city that was under continuous attacks by ghosts and other monsters. <br /> <br /> They attacked at night, so they were driven off by sunrise... But it sapped morale, killed people, fucked up infrastructure, and other shit. <br /> <br /> So he made a celestial working over the city. No matter the time. The weather. The season. The city and the surrounding area will be covered in sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T14:25:34-07:00","id":1310106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1310030#post1310030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A statue stands in the Underworld. A person who is hungry may give a point of Willpower to the statue, and in a short burst of varicolored light, food will appear in sufficient quantity to sate them for a day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, this is a &quot;miracle of supernatural power&quot;, which is Celestial Circle. However, that feels like it might be a little too weak for Celestial Circle in general, particularly with the limit you also mentioned (not being able to recover Willpower from sleeping after eating it for too long). <br /> <br /> So, another question - can it feed someone else? Say I, Solar Anne, feel secure in my ability to recover the WP through some other method, and my circle is<i> really hungry</i>. Can I pay 4 WP and produce enough food for each of my other four circlemates? Or my followers? Or some larger group, if I have a way of recovering WP quickly? Or does the food only work for the person who paid the WP?<br /> <br /> If it works for anyone as long as someone has WP to burn, I'd call it Celestial Ambition 1. On the other hand, if it's limited to only feeding the person who paid the WP, I think that pulls it down in power enough that I'd call it Terrestrial 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T18:42:37-07:00","id":1310167,"title":"","content":"Someone else can eat the food, but the Willpower will only be converted to food if the person spending the Willpower is hungry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T20:12:23-07:00","id":1310181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1310167#post1310167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone else can eat the food, but the Willpower will only be converted to food if the person spending the Willpower is hungry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd still peg that at Celestial 1, yeah. It's a little too easy to produce food in large-scale quantities for me to be comfortable calling it Terrestrial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T22:01:48-07:00","id":1317970,"title":"","content":"Sorcerous workings can add merits to humans. <br /> <br /> I presume this applies to weapons as well. Probably easier, since it isn't stuff like giving someone superhuman strength or durability. <br /> <br /> Terrestrial 1 allows things like one-handed claymores and other things. Or silent heavy armour. Terrestrial 2 gets you things like rocket launchers that you can hide in your pants or jacket, like you conceal a hold-out pistol. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, I'm totally wrong, and this requires a celestial working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T23:26:29-07:00","id":1317985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1317970#post1317970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerous workings can add merits to humans.<br /> <br /> I presume this applies to weapons as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there aren't any rules for giving objects Merits, but I could see modifying equipment to gain Tags.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1317970#post1317970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably easier, since it isn't stuff like giving someone superhuman strength or durability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you're trying to imbue it with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1317970#post1317970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terrestrial 1 allows things like one-handed claymores and other things. Or silent heavy armour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, in both of these cases you're still effectively granting the <i>wielder</i> a supernatural power (albeit one minor enough that I'd probably let it squeak by at Terrestrial 3, especially if there were some interesting drawbacks attached).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1317970#post1317970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terrestrial 2 gets you things like rocket launchers that you can hide in your pants or jacket, like you conceal a hold-out pistol.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Exalted Modern shard, perhaps; either way, this definitely feels more in-keeping with Celestial 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T08:21:22-07:00","id":1318060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1317970#post1317970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerous workings can add merits to humans.<br /> <br /> I presume this applies to weapons as well. Probably easier, since it isn't stuff like giving someone superhuman strength or durability.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial 1 allows things like one-handed claymores and other things. Or silent heavy armour. Terrestrial 2 gets you things like rocket launchers that you can hide in your pants or jacket, like you conceal a hold-out pistol.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I'm totally wrong, and this requires a celestial working.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dislike three things about this concept: <br /> <br /> First it completely bypasses the craft system to imbue objects with supernatural powers and second, there's already a way to do things like this: Special Materials (Exalted page 590). Things like making armor out of feather steel gives it the silent tag. Third, the higher level stuff are things that straight up artifacts can do. You should never be able to just slap an enchantment on something the size of a rocket launcher so you can hide it in your pants. That's a three dot artifact at the very least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T08:33:21-07:00","id":1318062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1318060#post1318060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike three things about this concept: <br /> <br /> First it completely bypasses the craft system to imbue objects with supernatural powers and second, there's already a way to do things like this: Special Materials (Exalted page 590). Things like making armor out of feather steel gives it the silent tag. Third, the higher level stuff are things that straight up artifacts can do. You should never be able to just slap an enchantment on something the size of a rocket launcher so you can hide it in your pants. That's a three dot artifact at the very least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Probably right. <br /> <br /> Probably needless too. What with the benediction of water","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T14:48:58-07:00","id":1318127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1271964#post1271964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Graaaggghh!!!<br /> <br /> Have I ever mentioned how I really hate 3e's crafting system?<br /> <br /> How about this? An automated factory. Meant to build anything and everything a city needs. Meant for sieges and support a desert town.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I absolutely LOVE the crafting system in 3E. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T15:07:25-07:00","id":1318134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1318127#post1318127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I absolutely LOVE the crafting system in 3E. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I\u2019ve made a lot more characters in this system with