c=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T14:58:09-07:00","id":1318759,"title":"","content":"Thing is we are not just talking about securing the dreamscape but detecting them preventing escape physically dragging them out of it transporting them across creation and holding them captive. I personally thought it would be a solar working.<br /> Alternative would be trapping their mind in the dreamcatcher so their body just withers away and dies eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","user":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","date":". 06-15-2019, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T18:19:02-07:00","id":1318771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1318759#post1318759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is we are not just talking about securing the dreamscape but detecting them preventing escape physically dragging them out of it transporting them across creation and holding them captive. I personally thought it would be a solar working.<br /> Alternative would be trapping their mind in the dreamcatcher so their body just withers away and dies eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem is that would be a boring way to die.<br /> The rules try to put some effort to making it hard for exalts and similarly powerful beings to die without a dramatic death, so the list of sorcerous workings doesn't have any examples of that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T02:21:54-07:00","id":1318820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1318756#post1318756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No offence , and I do appreciate the replies, but have any of you actually read the specific effect I wanted because what you are describing is not what I\u2019m making.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what you explained your opponent may as well be just using the Terrestrial Spell : &quot;Silent Words of Dreams and Nightmares&quot;, so without further details it's hard to have an idea. But I don't think protecting your dreams and setting a trap in it should be higher than Celestial 3 in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T02:42:02-07:00","id":1318822,"title":"","content":"How much defence does he get against the trap? A roll? Spend wp?<br /> <br /> And there probably is a difference between if he's sending you nightmares, or actually coming into the dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T05:05:37-07:00","id":1319033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1318822#post1318822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much defence does he get against the trap? A roll? Spend wp?<br /> <br /> And there probably is a difference between if he's sending you nightmares, or actually coming into the dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that he doesn\u2019t give me any way way of defending against him invading my dream or leaving I don\u2019t think he should get any chance of resisting either otherwise it defeats the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T06:44:53-07:00","id":1319038,"title":"","content":"That's going to be much higher then.<br /> What does he do in the dreams? Just talk to you, or do damage, inflict social influence, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T10:16:53-07:00","id":1319076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1319038#post1319038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's going to be much higher then.<br /> What does he do in the dreams? Just talk to you, or do damage, inflict social influence, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was trying to teach my character a moral lesson. In a spirit of the ghost of Christmas future etc. And I couldn\u2019t do anything to stop him lecturing me or had a choice to leave or wake up. Safe to say he made an enemy for life. I won\u2019t stop till I hunted him down and put him down like a moralising dog that he is. Putting down Shitbreath is now on the list of my major intimacies. My dreams should be my characters safe space not a lectern for some moralising prick. And there are no charms I could use to defend myself while sleeping so dreamcatcher is my last and only hope to stop this dick coming back next Christmas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","user":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","date":". 06-17-2019, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T11:07:40-07:00","id":1319085,"title":"","content":"I don't think there is really a defense written against the spell &quot;Silent Words of Dreams and Nightmares&quot; so you would have to prepare a Working of Terrestrial 3 to stop it, and certainly Celestial 2-3 to trap your dream so you can do some reverse counter attack while he is invading your dream","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T11:43:26-07:00","id":1319096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1319085#post1319085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there is really a defense written against the spell &quot;Silent Words of Dreams and Nightmares&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure there is; if it's not the sorcerer's control spell, he's <b>got </b>to get his hands on something of yours (and since casting the spell burns it up, he's got to keep on getting stuff of yours). Every time you shave, burn the hair; every time you buy new clothes, burn the old ones. You catch anyone with their hands on your stuff, <i>burn <b>them</b></i><b>.</b><br /> <br /> If you continue to have this difficulty but nothing of yours is going missing, then it's probably his control spell... which means he's one of the people around you in your day-to-day life. See if you can get him to slip up and reveal himself.<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, you end up looking like a paranoid dingus, but <i>it's not paranoia when they really <b>are</b> out to get you</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-17-2019, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T13:54:16-07:00","id":1319117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1319076#post1319076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He was trying to teach my character a moral lesson. In a spirit of the ghost of Christmas future etc. And I couldn\u2019t do anything to stop him lecturing me or had a choice to leave or wake up. Safe to say he made an enemy for life. I won\u2019t stop till I hunted him down and put him down like a moralising dog that he is. Putting down Shitbreath is now on the list of my major intimacies. My dreams should be my characters safe space not a lectern for some moralising prick. And there are no charms I could use to defend myself while sleeping so dreamcatcher is my last and only hope to stop this dick coming back next Christmas.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he\u2019s there, in your head, and you make a trap that catches him and pulls him out (or stops him from getting in) Celestial 3. If hes somewhere else and projecting Solar 1. I will say this sounds more like a ST problem then a working one\u2014I assumed this was a weird joke ask at first because Shitbreath is an awful name and the scenario sounded very strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T14:19:34-07:00","id":1319122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1319085#post1319085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there is really a defense written against the spell &quot;Silent Words of Dreams and Nightmares&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> There are actually Lunar Charms (<i>Nightmare Beast Soul</i> and <i>Midnight Guardian Territory</i>) that specifically defend against it, as well as any other dream-affecting magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T18:59:19-07:00","id":1319172,"title":"","content":"Your St sounds terrible.<br /> <br /> Ask him more questions like how it's done. Is it actual astral travel or a spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T05:55:18-07:00","id":1319261,"title":"","content":"The character wasn't called Shitbreath, that's just what Beast calls him.<br /> It was a comedy session like 2 years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T06:07:24-07:00","id":1319263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1319261#post1319261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character wasn't called Shitbreath, that's just what Beast calls him.<br /> It was a comedy session like 2 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah okay. Guess I'll do one.<br /> <br /> If I'm a sorcerer with the Thautmurgy Exorcism (2 dot version), what level of working would modify it to:<br /> 1) Let me direct what object the demon is exorcised into?<br /> 2) bind said trapped demons to me with a Major intimacy?<br /> <br /> (I haven't checked Solar and DB Occult charms if they can pull off this effect without as much effort). <br /> My guess is Celestial 2, but any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T06:23:56-07:00","id":1319264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1319261#post1319261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character wasn't called Shitbreath, that's just what Beast calls him.<br /> It was a comedy session like 2 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like last Christmas and scarred me for life , maybe it was comedy for the ST but my character was deeply traumatised. Which is why he got the major intimacy against it and I don\u2019t want him coming back this Christmas which is why I need to make the working to defend myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T09:17:15-07:00","id":1319303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1319263#post1319263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah okay. Guess I'll do one.<br /> <br /> If I'm a sorcerer with the Thautmurgy Exorcism (2 dot version), what level of working would modify it to:<br /> 1) Let me direct what object the demon is exorcised into?<br /> 2) bind said trapped demons to me with a Major intimacy?<br /> <br /> (I haven't checked Solar and DB Occult charms if they can pull off this effect without as much effort).<br /> My guess is Celestial 2, but any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it does let you direct what object the demon is exorcised into. It just lists alternatives you could choose to put it into.<br /> <br /> In terms of splat charms, most Dragonblood charms just let you expel a possessing demon and not put it anywhere particular, but the Earth charm Anathema-Sealing Term lets you seal a spirit you incapicatated in a cave, pillar, statue, under a mountain, etc.<br /> <br /> Burning Exorcism Technique (a Solar charm) lets you absorb a possessing spirit, and Soul Projection lets you put it into people.<br /> <br /> Lunars have charms that let you exorcise a possessing spirit and put it into an animal, or into an amulet you carry (which then lets you use its Eclipse-okay charms).<br /> <br /> But these Solar and Lunar charms only work on possessing spirits like Fulope and Nemissaries. Not a rock-solid blood ape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T09:24:09-07:00","id":1319305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1319303#post1319303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure it does let you direct what object the demon is exorcised into. It just lists alternatives you could choose to put it into.<br /> <br /> In terms of splat charms, most Dragonblood charms just let you expel a possessing demon and not put it anywhere particular, but the Earth charm Anathema-Sealing Term lets you seal a spirit you incapicatated in a cave, pillar, statue, under a mountain, etc.<br /> <br /> Burning Exorcism Technique (a Solar charm) lets you absorb a possessing spirit, and Soul Projection lets you put it into people.<br /> <br /> Lunars have charms that let you exorcise a possessing spirit and put it into an animal, or into an amulet you carry (which then lets you use its Eclipse-okay charms).<br /> <br /> But these Solar and Lunar charms only work on possessing spirits like Fulope and Nemissaries. Not a rock-solid blood ape.</div> </div> </div> </div>It mentions being able to free them if you can find the object\u2014which I took to mean a random object nearby. Any thoughts on the intimacy buff? I\u2019m thinking of storing enemy demons in a brass vessel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T11:35:24-07:00","id":1319330,"title":"","content":"So I have a few questions :<br /> <br /> 1) What's the difficulty of regrowing lost limbs, or in general to Flaws you may find yourself with after a crippling injury ? Because one of my players had a crippling injury of his arm, and it seems like a mutation to me (so Terrestrial 2) to have more arm with a mutation, and what was a cool wound he got in a terrific fight become 4 exp in 1 week, which I found kinda boring. I realized something might be off when I realised the Solar Charm to do the equivalent is Essence 3, which made me wonder if someone had a better insight on the question.<br /> <br /> 2) The theme of my campaign was the Grand Beasts, ancient creatures made by the Solar of this civilisation to watch upon their land. One theme is the relation of the descendant of those people with the Beasts, and the relation of the reborn Solars with those beasts. In particular, this begged the question : What's the difficulty for conceiving this kind of being ? I don't expect a single uniform answer, because all the Beasts are not equals (&quot;All Great Beasts are equal but some or more equals than others&quot; might be a good proverb for the people of these lands I guess <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). Let's take an example : There is the Great Owl of the Forest, something that might be close to a Giant Wood Elemental, Legendary Size, capable of summoning armies of Wood Elemental to protect the giant forest he protects, travelling extremely fast accross it. I feel like this Owl would totally outmatch Octavian, the Living Tower, supposed to be the baseline combattant of second circle power of sorcerous workings (I guess). Plus the owl has many other qualities and interesting powers, further separating him from Octavian. Still I don't think this Owl should be compared to Third Circle Demons (since I only read the Splats books of Ex3 I sort of imagine these Demons being cosmic powerful, not just huge ass hp with summoning power of armies). What would that be ? Is it possible to create this Owl with sorcery ? What about the Giant Spider of Earth, the first new Grand Beast made by the players to help their people live in the chain of mountains they settled in, able to forage deep into the earth and reconfigure the tunnels that were left by their ancestors to find hidden secrets of the past and make the life of invaders more difficult ? I put it Celestial 3, because I wanted my players being able to do it (they talked of it for a long time, and it was an interesting idea to have them muster the power to finalize it), but I'm not sure it was in line with the rules as intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T12:05:12-07:00","id":1319334,"title":"","content":"1) Well, I'd argue that it depends at least partly on the how of it. Adding an extra arm through a mutation would indeed be Terrestrial 2, but absent Finesse 5, as an ST I'd be inclined to make it different based on the circumstances of its origin. If Hogane loses an arm and Seamstress of Dissolution makes him a replacement from pieces she took off a shark-god, it'd function like an arm, but cosmetically it'd be very different, Terrestrial 2. If Gasp of the Drowning gets his legs torn off and has new ones forged out of steel and binds ghosts to animate them, they'd function like legs, but he'll be substantially heavier; if he also wants some sort of powers related to the ghosts inhabiting his legs, Celestial 2, otherwise, Terrestrial 2. If a vodonik comes to Admiral Misu with his arm ripped off, and Admiral Misu has his allies in the fae courts turn the severed limb into a tree that bears limb-fruits that the vodonik can have grafted back on, I'd also put that in Celestial range since now the vodonik can come back for a new arm every month if he wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T12:12:37-07:00","id":1319337,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think what I missed was a bit of the &quot;How you do your arm-regrowing stuff ?&quot;. I was actually so not prepared by his plan I lost my ability as an ST to make a cool situation of everything, thanks for your reply. Why do you think the equivalent Charm for Solar is so high in Essence though ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T12:18:16-07:00","id":1319339,"title":"","content":"Like the long time it takes, I assume it's because in this edition you can avoid death by taking a crippling injury.<br /> <br /> So if you could heal crippling injuries easily, being beaten to death would be something you could easily avoid, which'd make the fights lack danger.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T12:22:48-07:00","id":1319340,"title":"","content":"Yeah but I believe having it be mostly a Terrestrial 2 Working defeat this purpose","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T13:22:12-07:00","id":1319347,"title":"","content":"Being pretty obviously the guy who keeps going to sorcerers for limb replacements is something of a consequence in its own right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T13:28:33-07:00","id":1319349,"title":"","content":"I think you can only do the crippling injury &quot;trick&quot; once per story anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T14:11:19-07:00","id":1319357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1319340#post1319340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but I believe having it be mostly a Terrestrial 2 Working defeat this purpose</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say that, no matter what version the Terrestrial 2 version takes, it will <i>always</i> be a mutation - that is, it will be obviously unnatural in some way. Healing a crippling injury perfectly, in a way that isn't obvious that you've been warped by sorcery, would be Celestial 1, minimum. That puts it in line, essence-wise, with Wholeness-Restoring Meditation, the Solar Medicine charm that heals crippling injuries. Note also that every sorcerous working requires XP to be used, and a working requires, absolute bare minimum, a week of work from the sorcerer as well, whereas the charm requires only 4 hours of work (though the interval for the charm is longer, so it might take longer overall). I think all these factors make regenerating parts through sorcery reasonably balanced with Solar Medicine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T15:33:07-07:00","id":1319368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1319349#post1319349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you can only do the crippling injury &amp;quot;trick&amp;quot; once per story anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but it's still an obvious and significant character-defining feature, not simply &quot;1/story, don't die.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T19:50:25-07:00","id":1319394,"title":"","content":"Considering that regrowing limbs and healing other crippling injuries is specifically what solar medicine does I dnt think it should be done with a sorcerous working considering even with supernal medicine and lots of successes it usually takes months to regrow lost limbs. Unless you want to replace an arm with a tentacle or something then by all means magic away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T20:45:05-07:00","id":1319398,"title":"","content":"Regrowing a limb was the last Sorcerous Working done in my campaign :P<br /> <br /> It was stablished from the start that the arm couldn\u00b4t be a &quot;normal&quot; arm, and the player ended with a shadowy arm which strenght was as real as the sorcerer\u00b4s will: as he lost Willpower, the arm would become more transparent, and if he had 0 WP the arm would completely disappear and be unusable until he regained at least one WP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T19:20:47-07:00","id":1324107,"title":"","content":"Talking about limbs... Anyone read elfen lied? Invisible arm, that can tear apart and cut.<br /> <br /> Celestial 2, or 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T19:40:18-07:00","id":1324114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1324107#post1324107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone read elfen lied?</div> </div> </div> </div>Watched an episode of the anime, decided it wasn\u2019t for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1324107#post1324107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial 2, or 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial 2 minimum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T05:57:58-07:00","id":1324195,"title":"","content":"Yeah. <br /> <br /> Medium to long range. Multiple arms. No penalties on using them separately. There appears to be a form of clairvoyance where it doesn't matter that they're moving right behind her. <br /> <br /> Exceptionally strong, capable of crushing human skulls, breaking through stone and steel, and basically wrecking the shit out of anything that's not reinforced. <br /> <br /> Able to handle objects with surprising gentleness. Capable of being sharp enough to cut through human bodies with ease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T06:50:39-07:00","id":1324204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1324195#post1324195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Medium to long range.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say medium at most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1324195#post1324195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No penalties on using them separately.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you say that? We don't see their dice pools. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1324195#post1324195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exceptionally strong, capable of crushing human skulls, breaking through stone and steel, and basically wrecking the shit out of anything that's not reinforced.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that's nothing that can't be done with a good Athletics and the Brawl Charm Fists of Iron Technique.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1324195#post1324195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Capable of being sharp enough to cut through human bodies with ease.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just means it does lethal damage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T07:05:00-07:00","id":1324209,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure she killed the hell out of multiple opponents. Without slowing down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T14:32:50-07:00","id":1324272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1324209#post1324209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly sure she killed the hell out of multiple opponents. Without slowing down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like she might have been fighting a battle group.<br /> <br /> (I\u2019ll also point out that, again, we don\u2019t see her dice pools. Just because she doesn\u2019t visibly slow down doesn\u2019t mean she\u2019s not exerting effort.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T20:31:44-07:00","id":1324345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1324272#post1324272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like she might have been fighting a battle group.<br /> <br /> (I\u2019ll also point out that, again, we don\u2019t see her dice pools. Just because she doesn\u2019t visibly slow down doesn\u2019t mean she\u2019s not exerting effort.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. Maybe so. She <b>was </b>particularly strong. <br /> <br /> I've been reading Iris Zero. Or more importantly, its a manga. Read it on your own time, but its basically a story were children starting from a certain year all have a certain power. Or more importantly, a perception power. Ranging from seeing who loves who, when someone is lying, or things like 'is this person suited to this job?'. <br /> <br /> Low level perception power, from perceiving people's abilites and attributes to a bargain basement Judge's ear technique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T09:21:51-07:00","id":1325271,"title":"","content":"A werewolf alternate form. For an agent that's meant to sow chaos behind enemy lines.<br /> <br /> Adds 4 dots to any ability. Gives natural weapons, both ranged and melee. Sharpened senses, like night vision. And enhanced durability and healing.<br /> <br /> What's it for? Terrestrial 3 or celestial 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T09:43:35-07:00","id":1325279,"title":"","content":"Permanently transforming your shape into that of a wolfman sounds like Terrestrial 3, though adding healing powers on top of that would bring it up to Celestial.<br /> <br /> \u200bGaining the power to transform at will between your regular shape and a wolfman shape, definitely Celestial 2.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Also, &quot;adds 4 dots to any ability?&quot; How does being in a wolfman shape make you better at Bureaucracy?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:18:48-07:00","id":1325291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325279#post1325279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Permanently transforming your shape into that of a wolfman sounds like Terrestrial 3, though adding healing powers on top of that would bring it up to Celestial.<br /> <br /> \u200bGaining the power to transform at will between your regular shape and a wolfman shape, definitely Celestial 2.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Also, &amp;quot;adds 4 dots to any ability?&amp;quot; How does being in a wolfman shape make you better at Bureaucracy?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry was thinking of the garou warform ability. It adds 4 dots to your physical stats. And gives you absurd regeneration and durability. <br /> <br /> That was worded badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:33:47-07:00","id":1325301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325291#post1325291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It adds 4 dots to your physical stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how easily the dice math gets wonky when you push past a certain threshold, I'd either cap the boost at 5 or have those count as Charm dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325291#post1325291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And gives you absurd regeneration and durability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pairing regeneration <i>and</i> durability with the numerous physical boosts I'd say we've passed the &quot;granting a supernatural power&quot; threshold and moved into &quot;with supernatural powers comparable to a Second Circle Demon.&quot; Definitely Celestial 3.<br /> <br /> \u200bAssuming, of course, that an ST would allow it at all; at this point, you're basically asking to <i>play </i>a Lunar without having to <i>be </i>a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-17-2019, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T11:23:00-07:00","id":1325318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325301#post1325301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how easily the dice math gets wonky when you push past a certain threshold, I'd either cap the boost at 5 or have those count as Charm dice.<br /> <br /> Pairing regeneration <i>and</i> durability with the numerous physical boosts I'd say we've passed the &quot;granting a supernatural power&quot; threshold and moved into &quot;with supernatural powers comparable to a Second Circle Demon.&quot; Definitely Celestial 3.<br /> <br /> \u200bAssuming, of course, that an ST would allow it at all; at this point, you're basically asking to <i>play </i>a Lunar without having to <i>be </i>a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless your just making beastmen or it\u2019s a curse where you turn someone into a werewolf over which you have no control where you hunt people and eat them at night as a werewolf and then wake up in morning covered in blood, it very much sounds like you should be playing a lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T11:28:01-07:00","id":1325319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325318#post1325318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless your just making beastmen or it\u2019s a curse where you turn someone into a werewolf over which you have no control where you hunt people and eat them at night as a werewolf and then wake up in morning covered in blood, it very much sounds like you should be playing a lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not the one asking about it, that's <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T11:46:58-07:00","id":1325328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325319#post1325319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not the one asking about it, that's <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes I quoted the wrong person , no hard feelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T11:59:47-07:00","id":1325337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325328#post1325328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah yes I quoted the wrong person , no hard feelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, no hard feelings.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T20:39:05-07:00","id":1325477,"title":"","content":"How about this: <br /> <br /> <b>Enhanced Adrenal Glands</b><br /> With a single willpower cost and an instantaneous transformation, the character's implanted artificial organs begin pumping out a cocktail of combat enhancers and adrenal boosters, driving the character's body beyond the limits of humanity<br /> <br /> *Grants Exalted healing and durability<br /> *Grants 4 extra dice to Dexterity and Strength rolls<br /> *Adds 3 extra dice to Stamina rolls<br /> *reduces 2 of all wound penalties<br /> <br /> The adrenal glands have a cooldown time of 1 day, and the enhancements last for a single scene. <br /> <br /> Celestial 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T22:17:42-07:00","id":1325497,"title":"","content":"Adrenaline isn\u2019t really something that factors into healing. In fact, you\u2019re generally <i>more</i> likely to damage your muscles during a fight-or-flight reaction.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Celestial 2 is fine, though once again I\u2019d count them as Charm dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T23:12:43-07:00","id":1325502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325497#post1325497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adrenaline isn\u2019t really something that factors into healing. In fact, you\u2019re generally <i>more</i> likely to damage your muscles during a fight-or-flight reaction.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Celestial 2 is fine, though once again I\u2019d count them as Charm dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. <br /> <br /> Adrenal glands... Maybe combat drug dispenser?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T04:06:41-07:00","id":1325536,"title":"","content":"If we're just riffing of Mr. Banks then don't forget the <i>Coolblue</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T04:09:06-07:00","id":1325538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325536#post1325536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're just riffing of Mr. Banks then don't forget the <i>Coolblue</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry man. I missed that reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T04:22:10-07:00","id":1325542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325538#post1325538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry man. I missed that reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. Every human citizen of The Culture is genetically enhanced with glands that give them concious control over their bodily functions like increasing adrenaline at will. They can also gland combat drugs and narcotics, the most iconic being <i>Coolblue</i> which is basically Sci-Fi THC. I'm a big Culture fan.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> <i>We'll be hearing about those famous glands next...</i> Thought Horza bitterly.<br /> <br /> &quot;And those glands!&quot; Kraiklyn carried on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-18-2019, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T04:54:55-07:00","id":1325552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325542#post1325542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry. Every human citizen of The Culture is genetically enhanced with glands that give them concious control over their bodily functions like increasing adrenaline at will. They can also gland combat drugs and narcotics, the most iconic being <i>Coolblue</i> which is basically Sci-Fi THC. I'm a big Culture fan.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> <i>We'll be hearing about those famous glands next...</i> Thought Horza bitterly.<br /> <br /> &quot;And those glands!&quot; Kraiklyn carried on</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Ok. <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing of Riches and Power</b><br /> <br /> The knots of fate around a person has been twisted, warped, their very presence in the Loom disrupted. A quality has been bound to their very existence. Monks and those sensitive to the supernatural may sense this if they are astute and perceptive enough. Sidereals know immediately upon seeing him. Others, require the ability to see spirits and enchantments before they know of the mortal with such a blessing. <br /> <br /> The blessing is simple. Where a sorcerer may grant a person great healing, increased strength, hardy flesh, or wings, a sorcerer has instead granted the person in question riches, wealth, and power. The person's very presence twists luck around him, granting him luck that should be given to those in legend. He comes across riches and buried treasure. Chance meetings with others turn into friendships and alliances with those in the seats of power. A route he takes through a dimly lit woodpath grants him the chance to make friends with an Ifrit Lord. A walk along the beach lets him find a fish, its stomach filled with gold coins. A journey through the slums lets him crash into a girl, who is the princess in disguise searching for her hidden lover. Whether from Chiaroscuro to the Imperial City, the person so blessed often rises to the top of mortal society. <br /> <br /> In mechanical terms, the character is bound to have Resources 4+, Allies 4+, and Influence 5*. He gains one dot over the course of a week, until it reaches either 4 or 5. Moving from his present location loses him allies and influence, unless he keeps up constant correspondence or brings his treasures with him.**<br /> <br /> *Each one is a terrestrial 3 working. <br /> ** This depends greatly on the gap in relationship, as well as the character's social prowess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T04:58:32-07:00","id":1325554,"title":"","content":"In what way is it \u201clucky\u201d to accidentally crash into a girl who is already in a relationship?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:02:54-07:00","id":1325556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325554#post1325554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what way is it \u201clucky\u201d to accidentally crash into a girl who is already in a relationship?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because now you're her friend, and accidentally help legitimise her relationship with the hidden lover. They both thank you. Now the king decides to not only give him recognition, but also lets him be part of the royal family (i.e. royalty) after shenanigans occur. <br /> <br /> So now you have a queen that likes you because you helped secure a happy marriage for her, and a king that realizes that without you, he'll be stuck as a vagrant in the slums. <br /> <br /> Or maybe its different now. I mean, I got the 'crashing into girl' part from Chrono trigger. Its just as likely the princess runs out to explore and have fun, and you crash into her. And then she gets kidnapped by thugs, and you gotta rescue her. <br /> <br /> Which reminds me. I should add that it helps you get into situations and gives you mild bonuses, but there's a good chance that it also kills you, what with the thugs potentially deciding to kill you for trying to slow them down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T07:14:36-07:00","id":1325602,"title":"","content":"So how is this discernable from just having an ST who is fond of making strange coincidences and occurrences take place?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T07:25:55-07:00","id":1325604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325602#post1325602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how is this discernable from just having an ST who is fond of making strange coincidences and occurrences take place?</div> </div> </div> </div>... I'm too tired to talk about this. It's meant to be an equivalent of verdant emptiness endowment. Don't like it? You can just ignore it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T22:15:12-07:00","id":1325875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325602#post1325602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how is this discernable from just having an ST who is fond of making strange coincidences and occurrences take place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did a JRPG trope kill your parents? relax mate. I really like the idea of a riches and luck producing sorcery.<br /> <br /> EDIT: somehow the culture drug list didn't get sent.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Most Culture individuals opt to have drug glands that allow for hormonal levels and other chemical secretions to be consciously monitored, released and controlled. These allow owners to secrete on command any of a wide selection of synthetic drugs, from the merely relaxing to the mind-altering: &quot;Snap&quot; is described in Use of Weapons and The Player of Games as &quot;The Culture's favourite breakfast drug&quot;. &quot;Sharp Blue&quot; is described as a utility drug, as opposed to a sensory enhancer or a sexual stimulant, that helps in problem solving. &quot;Quicken&quot;, mentioned in Excession, speeds up the user's neural processes so that time seems to slow down, allowing them to think and have mental conversation (for example with artificial intelligences) in far less time than it appears to take to the outside observer. &quot;Sperk&quot;, as described in Matter, is a mood- and energy-enhancing drug, while other such self-produced drugs include &quot;Calm&quot;, &quot;Gain&quot;, &quot;Charge&quot;, &quot;Recall&quot;, &quot;Diffuse&quot;, &quot;Somnabsolute&quot;, &quot;Softnow&quot;, &quot;Focal&quot;, &quot;Edge&quot;, &quot;Drill&quot;, &quot;Gung&quot;, &quot;Winnow&quot; and &quot;Crystal Fugue State&quot;. The glanded substances have no permanent side-effects and are non-habit-forming.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T22:47:07-07:00","id":1325883,"title":"","content":"Hmm....<br /> <br /> How about sorcerous workings to merge it with plants and organs, as a form of hellish biotech? Drugs to enhance healing. Drugs to boost wits or intelligence. Drugs to reduce wound penalties or grant clear thinking and movement despite being drugged or drunk...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T23:34:04-07:00","id":1325893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325875#post1325875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the idea of a riches and luck producing sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luck is great, but as someone who actually has to ST for people, I generally find stories work better when there\u2019s some coherence to things. <br /> <br /> Mind, occasionally I myself will throw in a Random Princess From Nowhere, as I <i>do</i> understand that improvisation is healthy, but having it mandated to me by one of the players leaves something of a bad taste in my mouth, and I\u2019m having trouble working out a way for the power to work that I feel would leave everybody satisfied.<br /> <br /> Please don\u2019t assume I\u2019m out to shit on people\u2019s ideas just because I question them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T03:46:55-07:00","id":1325925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325893#post1325893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luck is great, but as someone who actually has to ST for people, I generally find stories work better when there\u2019s some coherence to things.<br /> <br /> Mind, occasionally I myself will throw in a Random Princess From Nowhere, as I <i>do</i> understand that improvisation is healthy, but having it mandated to me by one of the players leaves something of a bad taste in my mouth, and I\u2019m having trouble working out a way for the power to work that I feel would leave everybody satisfied.<br /> <br /> Please don\u2019t assume I\u2019m out to shit on people\u2019s ideas just because I question them.</div> </div> </div> </div>but, you <i>did</i> shit on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> 's idea. &quot;In what way is [Sorcerous Working that gives strange luck] different then a ST just throwing a bunch of rando shit in?&quot; does not a healthy question make. Domino from Deadpool 2 had the &quot;extreme luck&quot; superpower, is that the same as saying &quot;she doesnt have a power the director just wanted to shoehorn her in so here's a bunch of rando stuff&quot;? Does Logan's power of healing not exist when the Director can just say &quot;yeah you survived that bullet&quot;? It's a bad comparison you made, and the wording in it leads me only to bad faith interpretations. <br /> <br /> I'm also someone who &quot;actually has to ST for people&quot; and your concern about &quot;stories work better when there\u2019s some coherence to things&quot; is a wildly off base remark, because the Working <i>literally provides a coherent reason for random things to happen. </i>That's <b>literally</b> the power in question. A sorcerer takes a mortal's thread off the Loom and does some magic shenanigans to it and <i>voila!</i> it runs into other amazing events seemingly randomly. Because it's powered by <b>literal magic</b>. <br /> <br /> If you can't reconcile a Working that twists people's fate and luck into whatever kind of game that you run, that's a you problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T05:16:24-07:00","id":1325942,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve had luck talismans and the line show up in my games. They work by doing things like turning your 1s into 10s when you roll a botch. \u201cThe woman you bumped into turns out to be a princess\u201d feels more like ST fiat, and I\u2019m not sure how to mechanize it, is what I\u2019m saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T05:21:37-07:00","id":1325944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325942#post1325942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve had luck talismans and the line show up in my games. They work by doing things like turning your 1s into 10s when you roll a botch. \u201cThe woman you bumped into turns out to be a princess\u201d feels more like ST fiat, and I\u2019m not sure how to mechanize it, is what I\u2019m saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems a might strong for a luck talisman.<br /> <br /> But hey, it worked for Aladdin. So why not your players? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T08:38:45-07:00","id":1326000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1325925#post1325925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but, you <i>did</i> shit on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> 's idea. &quot;In what way is [Sorcerous Working that gives strange luck] different then a ST just throwing a bunch of rando shit in?&quot; does not a healthy question make. Domino from Deadpool 2 had the &quot;extreme luck&quot; superpower, is that the same as saying &quot;she doesnt have a power the director just wanted to shoehorn her in so here's a bunch of rando stuff&quot;? Does Logan's power of healing not exist when the Director can just say &quot;yeah you survived that bullet&quot;? It's a bad comparison you made, and the wording in it leads me only to bad faith interpretations.<br /> <br /> I'm also someone who &quot;actually has to ST for people&quot; and your concern about &quot;stories work better when there\u2019s some coherence to things&quot; is a wildly off base remark, because the Working <i>literally provides a coherent reason for random things to happen. </i>That's <b>literally</b> the power in question. A sorcerer takes a mortal's thread off the Loom and does some magic shenanigans to it and <i>voila!</i> it runs into other amazing events seemingly randomly. Because it's powered by <b>literal magic</b>.<br /> <br /> If you can't reconcile a Working that twists people's fate and luck into whatever kind of game that you run, that's a you problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8830_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8830\" data-vbnamecard=\"8830\">Sorcerous Overlord</a> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> why the fuck is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> allowed to act like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T16:57:49-07:00","id":1326129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbc