" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve had luck talismans and the line show up in my games. They work by doing things like turning your 1s into 10s when you roll a botch. \u201cThe woman you bumped into turns out to be a princess\u201d feels more like ST fiat, and I\u2019m not sure how to mechanize it, is what I\u2019m saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a healthy and valid way to express your concern over a Working. As ST, I would just find a reason why my regular plothooks would cross paths with the Worked Over One and prewrite some interesting shenanigans to pull out of the metaphorical hat. <br /> <br /> &quot;Turning around the corner, a women trying and failing to cover her aristocratic clothes and jewels with rough cloth barges right into you and trips. She is being chased by 3 cruel looking thugs.&quot;<br /> <i>Ok, I go to step inbetween them and put my hand on my swordhilt</i><br /> Ok, they see you defending the girl and bark out at you in Flametongue. He pulls out his sword and ... (check notes) a loud clamor appears off to your right. sensing trouble, you duck as the Sultan's Menagerie barrels down the road. A hungry looking blue tiger lands on the lead bandit and starts eating his face. the remaining two bandits draw their swords and....&quot; tadaaaaa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T17:02:28-07:00","id":1326131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1326129#post1326129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't make a storm in a peachtea cup mate, we're just at &quot;forumn banter&quot; level here. Alucard might have worded his disagreement better but it;s nothing worth calling mum out to the playground.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is not the first time he has done this. I&quot;m just about done with this shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T18:55:35-07:00","id":1326146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1326131#post1326131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not the first time he has done this. I&amp;quot;m just about done with this shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>He...disagreed with your idea. Calm down man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T18:57:10-07:00","id":1326147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalzky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1326146#post1326146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He...disagreed with your idea. Calm down man.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many ways to disagree. <br /> <br /> This was not one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T19:54:52-07:00","id":1326160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1326147#post1326147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are many ways to disagree.<br /> <br /> This was not one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely was and wasn't even overly impolite in the grand scheme of internet discussions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T18:24:56-07:00","id":1326845,"title":"","content":"So I'm work-shopping a working my underworld obsessed Lunar may make at some point; I was interested in seeing some opinions on if it is a Celestial or Solar circle working.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Byrgan Flame</span><br /> <br /> A Byrgan Flame is a crackling blue-green bonfire of pyre-flame nested in a vast brazier of soulsteel and red jade. It is pyre-flame subverted by the purifying essence of creation-fire. It radiates a comforting warmth and at its center burns a core of bright red. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While within medium range of the Byrgan Flame, ghosts no longer hear the whispers of the Neverborn. Ghosts with derangements derived from the Labyrinth or similar suppress them as long as they remain within the flame\u2019s protective light.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Creatures like Nephwracks, who are too tainted by the neverborn to ever truly heal, are incapable of entering the protective radius of a Byrgan Flame. Deathlords are able to withstand the light, though the intensity of the fire imposes a -2 penalty to all actions they take while near it. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ghosts or necromancers may bond with a Byrgan Flame by tossing something of deep personal value into it. This may be an object or something more abstract, like a memory. For as long as they remain so bonded to the flame, they suppress a single intimacy they possess that resonates with their sacrifice. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those bonded to the fire find it no longer burns them, and they may take a piece of the flame out of the brazier with their bare hands. It continues to burn so long as they remain within a mile of the central brazier; the power of the Byrgan Flame burns out from short range of that piece of the fire. A piece of the Byrgan Flame like this will not burn anything around it, and those bonded to it may leave it in any container they might store liquid in. They are not uncommonly seen hanging from bottles in some vistas of the underworld. These small fires are difficult to extinguish, but can be easily recovered from the central brazier. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every year, at calibration, every piece of the Brygan flame taken from the brazier goes out.The Byrgan flame must be stoked with the willing sacrifice of a single ghost, or dozens of living animals. Additionally, every ghost or necromancer bonded with the Byrgan flame must erode the intimacy they have suppressed to bond with it. If this erodes the intimacy away completely, they must make a new sacrifice and suppress another intimacy. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once the fire has been fed, those bonded with it may take a new piece of flame for their personal use.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Should the fire not be fed, then it will go out for an entire year. At the next calibration, ten ghosts must be fed to the brazier to ignite it once more. </span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T18:54:04-07:00","id":1326851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1326845#post1326845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm work-shopping a working my underworld obsessed Lunar may make at some point; I was interested in seeing some opinions on if it is a Celestial or Solar circle working.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a cool effect! A couple of things: First, what does a suppressed Intimacy do? Is it basically just gone? Second, if Deathlords can enter the area, but don't like it, I'd suggest saying that that counts as a minor Intimacy of dislike for them. <br /> <br /> As to its level, I'd peg it at Solar 1. I'd say the ability to put down anti-spectre fires anywhere within a mile of the central flame would match the example of &quot;Ward an entire city against invasion with supernatural traps, barriers, or concealment&quot;. I suppose, given that only affects Neverborn-touched beings, one could argue that it's less powerful, but I feel that the ability to purge the Whispers from others bumps it back up again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T18:57:21-07:00","id":1326852,"title":"","content":"Sounds more like an artifact to me; that said, if pressed I'd probably peg it at Celestial 3. EDIT: Scratch that, Kelly's right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-22-2019, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T19:06:58-07:00","id":1326854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1326852#post1326852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds more like an artifact to me;</div> </div> </div> </div>It does kind of skirt the line between working and artifact, but I think that given its (apparently) stationary nature, working makes a bit more sense. If the brazier was movable, though, I'd definitely lean more towards artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T19:22:26-07:00","id":1326857,"title":"","content":"Hmm. That makes sense. The brazer was not intended as being an important fixture of the working- it'd probably be a sorcerous means since I'm in a game with a twilight crafter. I should have emphasized that better.<br /> <br /> Also! I forgot that suppressed isn't a big templating thing, so I'll need to write it out: the intimacy can't be used in social influence or to resist social influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T09:00:47-07:00","id":1330388,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I had in mind for a character concept a No Moon Lunar that had taken over the life of a young Dragon Blooded Dynast but kept her alive and locked in a cell somewhere. I was thinking of a sorcerous working on the cell that would slowly sap the will of anyone that stays in it for more than say a day, essentially hollowing them out. Which circle and level of ambition would you say it is?</span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","name":"Plastic Doll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T10:04:09-07:00","id":1330398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Plastic Doll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1330388#post1330388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking of a sorcerous working on the cell that would slowly sap the will of anyone that stays in it for more than say a day, essentially hollowing them out. Which circle and level of ambition would you say it is?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's just draining temporary Willpower and perhaps preventing Willpower regeneration through sleep, I think you could justify Terrestrial 2. Note that that wouldn't really &quot;hollow them out&quot;, though. They'd be less likely to succeed, since they don't have WP to burn, and they'll be less resistant to attempts to persuade them, since they can't go into decision points, but neither of those effects makes them non-persons or anything. If you wanted a more severe effect, perhaps something along the lines of being dream-eaten by a raksha, I'd obviously go with a higher level. I think an effect capable of doing what I've just described would probably be Celestial 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T13:30:03-07:00","id":1330434,"title":"","content":"It's a dragonblooded being drained. What's the power level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T13:40:48-07:00","id":1330438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1330434#post1330434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a dragonblooded being drained. What's the power level?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Willpower isn't intrinsically harder to drain than mortal Willpower, absent the Deeb buying Integrity Charms, which we haven't been told is the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-16T23:08:50-07:00","id":1331306,"title":"","content":"The sorcerer attempts a working to give his subject a new (albeit subtle) special ability: immunity to a certain type of disease. Let's say it's cancer: cancer can no longer develop, grow, or spread in the subject's body at all. (This effect doesn't actually remove any existing tumors, if any -- you'd need actual medical treatment for that, I think -- but they aren't likely to be dangerous anymore.)<br /> <br /> Or perhaps it's another broad category of disease. Something other than the Great Contagion, anyway -- cholera, plague, whatever. (I'm assuming the Great Contagion is <i>much</i> harder to ward someone against, although it's probably within a Solar sorcerer's power to at least partially protect someone if he really wants to put the effort in. I'm open to suggestions on that as well.)<br /> <br /> How tough a working is this? Might it be Celestial Ambition 2 (because you're granting the subject a supernatural power, even if it's not a flashy one)? Or perhaps Terrestrial Ambition 2 (you might consider it essentially just a mutation -- effective immunity to one specific category of disease isn't <i>obviously</i> magical in any way, nor terribly impressive compared to existing merits in the book)?<br /> <br /> (I have mixed feelings on the idea of sorcerous workings doing medical stuff at all, but I can't think of a reason to disallow it if the sorcerer's player really wants to spend the XP on this.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-16T23:53:55-07:00","id":1331313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1331306#post1331306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sorcerer attempts a working to give his subject a new (albeit subtle) special ability: immunity to a certain type of disease. Let's say it's cancer: cancer can no longer develop, grow, or spread in the subject's body at all. (This effect doesn't actually remove any existing tumors, if any -- you'd need actual medical treatment for that, I think -- but they aren't likely to be dangerous anymore.)<br /> <br /> How tough a working is this? Might it be Celestial Ambition 2 (because you're granting the subject a supernatural power, even if it's not a flashy one)? Or perhaps Terrestrial Ambition 2 (you might consider it essentially just a mutation -- effective immunity to one specific category of disease isn't <i>obviously</i> magical in any way, nor terribly impressive compared to existing merits in the book)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd call immunity to a <i>specific</i> non-magical disease Terrestrial 2 - it seems pretty reasonable as a mutation, given that people are immune to specific diseases in real life too. A whole category of diseases, I'd actually rate at Terrestrial 3 instead. However, I actually wouldn't treat cancer as a whole category, just a single disease, despite in reality it being a whole swathe of diseases. That's because, narratively, cancer does tend to be treated as a single disease. A character doesn't really get &quot;bone cancer&quot; or &quot;thyroid cancer&quot; or whatever, they just get &quot;cancer&quot;, in fiction. Plus, it kind of feels like a dick ST move to say &quot;Okay, you're immune to colon cancer. Too bad <i>you</i> got stomach cancer instead!&quot; I'd probably make the broader category something like &quot;disease based on malfunctioning body&quot;, and lump in at least autoimmune diseases as well, for the Terrestrial 3 version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'm assuming the Great Contagion is <i>much</i> harder to ward someone against, although it's probably within a Solar sorcerer's power to at least partially protect someone if he really wants to put the effort in. I'm open to suggestions on that as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd peg any supernatural disease as requiring a supernatural power to be immune to, and thus Celestial 2. The Great Contagion I'd specifically make Solar 1, though, since it's supposed to be the ultimate badass disease, and putting it that high means that very, very few Terrestrial-tier sorcerers would have had a chance to make themselves immune.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T04:54:31-07:00","id":1331324,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1533_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1533\" data-vbnamecard=\"1533\">Kelly Pedersen</a> is very in-line with my thinking on this; being immune to a specific disease type feels like a reasonable mutation, and thus Terrestrial 2 (though they might still be a carrier).<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, I'm still not a fan of no-sells, so I'd probably have the Celestial 2 version feel a tad more, well, supernatural. Like instead of just being flatly immune to diseases, you have a barrier around you that causes infectious material to burst into flame; if a disease manages to get through, you can't die from it (like an Exalt) and each time you fail a roll against the disease you get an increasing bonus on your next resistance roll as white fire surges through your veins, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-17-2019, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T10:08:02-07:00","id":1331349,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I think that sounds very reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1331324#post1331324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThat said, I'm still not a fan of no-sells, so I'd probably have the Celestial 2 version feel a tad more, well, supernatural. Like instead of just being flatly immune to diseases, you have a barrier around you that causes infectious material to burst into flame; if a disease manages to get through, you can't die from it (like an Exalt) and each time you fail a roll against the disease you get an increasing bonus on your next resistance roll as white fire surges through your veins, or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>TBH I was already thinking that simple immunity was kind of boring and also that making the effect weirder would go a long way towards reducing the &quot;using sorcery to do Medicine&quot; problem here. But it was getting late and I was in a hurry to get my question posted in a coherent form. &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the subject being bonded with some kind of minor fire elemental that embodies purity. If a disease gets through the flaming defense, the disease starts burning up inside the body; the subject might end up with an unpleasant fever for a few days, but that cancer probably isn't long for this world.<br /> <br /> ...A related question might be: could one reasonably develop a <i>Medicine</i> Charm that preemptively gives someone resistance or immunity to a future disease? It makes a lot of sense (of course a Solar physician could develop a cancer vaccine!), but I'm not sure what form the mechanics would take. (In particular, I'm wondering if it could be done without committing Essence to each patient.) I guess that's a question for a different thread though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T11:31:48-07:00","id":1331366,"title":"","content":"Definitely agree that a working to provide immunity, even one to a mundane disease, is better described with cool and weird effects, rather than just &quot;you don't get sick&quot;. For cancer immunity, I kind of like the idea that every so often, the sorcerer hacks up a tiny lump of flesh, the incipient tumor, that animates as a tiny homunculous under their control, and &quot;lives&quot; for a few days. After a particularly nasty dose of carcinogens (direct exposure to Ligier's light, for instance), this could produce several homunculi of notable size, or possibly they'd merge together to make one of human infant size.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-24T12:11:45-07:00","id":1332459,"title":"","content":"Any fool knows better than to attack a sorcerer within his own prepared grounds, right?<br /> <br /> With the help of a friendly local spirit, the sorcerer blesses his home and its immediate surroundings (i.e. he's still protected outside on his front lawn or whatever) so that he draws strength and fortune from his territory. Should the sorcerer encounter danger while at home, his soak is increased by (sorcerer's Essence) and he gains a +1 Defense bonus. The Defense increase counts as a bonus from Charms.<br /> <br /> What circle/Ambition would you give an effect like this? My initial thought was that a sorcerous working really shouldn't be handing anyone a persistent <i>non-Charm</i> Defense boost (could have serious effects on combat balance), but this might be kinda weak for a benefit the sorcerer gains <i>only</i> at home. (A sorcerer who ends up never getting into a serious fight outside his own home is either not doing anything interesting, some kind of tactical genius who probably deserves his home field advantage, or fighting a purely defensive action in which he needs all the help he can get.)<br /> <br /> One way to make this a lot nastier might be to make the working's benefits apply to all the sorcerer's summoned or created entities as well. I'd probably make that version Solar Ambition 1. (By Solar working standards, it's not all that impressive sounding, but if the buff can apply to as many Second Circle demons as you can pack into your manse it could really get out of hand.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-24T12:23:19-07:00","id":1332462,"title":"","content":"Too weak. Make it a +2 for the defensive value.<br /> <br /> Have you ever heard of the styles system, created by Aleph? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_5CqA9T0dTMW7xvhRCz3uzOoHW-YKUD_kE-GeMNsJvE/pub#h.7vahbk9kf8bm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_5CqA9T0dTMW7xvhRCz3uzOoHW-YKUD_kE-GeMNsJvE/pub#h.7vahbk9kf8bm\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_5CqA9T0dTMW7xvhRCz3uzOoHW-YKUD_kE-GeMNsJvE/pub#h.7vahbk9kf8bm\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_5CqA9T0dTMW7xvhRCz3uzOoHW-YKUD_kE-GeMNsJvE/pub#h.7vahbk9kf8bm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T00:50:58-07:00","id":1332618,"title":"","content":"The Elseroad<br /> <br /> The sorcerer creates a road through Elsewhere, accessible from anywhere in Creation by using a specific mantra and sequence of mudras, and leading anywhere in Creation, possibly with an Intelligence + Occult roll to reach a specific destination.<br /> <br /> A traveler wishing to use the Elseroad stands before a gate, doorway, or other portal; performs the mudras while reciting the mantra; and steps through. She finds herself on a smooth road paved with hexagonal flagstones (think the Giant's Causeway) extending as far as she can see in both directions. The terrain to either side (if there is any) is completely obscured by dense fog. Focusing her thoughts on a particular destination, she sets off along the road. Eventually, she reaches a glowing portal to one side of the road and, stepping through it, finds herself emerging from a gate or doorway at her destination.<br /> <br /> Stepping off the Elseroad without a portal may deposit the traveler anywhere in Creation... or outside of it...<br /> <br /> Would this be a Celestial, Ambition 3 working, or a Solar, Ambition 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T01:07:50-07:00","id":1332621,"title":"","content":"Considering that it exists across all of Creation, that sounds like Solar 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T05:18:01-07:00","id":1332638,"title":"","content":"Yup have to agree with Solar 3, that spell rewrites the fundamental laws of Creation as a whole, basically creating a new type of Occult power on Creation which didn't exist before. Giving non-sorcerers the power to cross realms of existence from anywhere in Creation also points to high Ambition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T12:31:21-07:00","id":1332693,"title":"","content":"What sort of difficulty working would it be to have the stone statues come alive to defend your castle from invaders say like 500 assorted archers warriors and monsters ? I\u2019m not very clear on war rules so not sure how they would work. I could make a celestial working god/ 2nd circle equivalent who could lead them but other than that I\u2019m kinda fishing. My twilight enjoys sculpting his circle in their castle so I was wondering if he could turn a hobby to something more productive.<br /> I don\u2019t suppose there is any way for th circles dawn to train statues is there ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","user":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","date":". 08-26-2019, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T12:38:42-07:00","id":1332695,"title":"","content":"Celestial 2 or 3. Training? Hmm... I would allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T13:19:36-07:00","id":1332712,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of unknown variables for that working, I'd say it could be anywhere between celestial 2 and solar 2 depending on how strong the statues are as combatants and what will be the process to activate/deactivate them and to order them around.<br /> <br /> I'd say the statues can be trained so long as you shape them to be capable of learning OR your Dawn knows the Lore Charm First Knowledge's Grace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T19:55:58-07:00","id":1332768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1332693#post1332693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of difficulty working would it be to have the stone statues come alive to defend your castle from invaders say like 500 assorted archers warriors and monsters ?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bLike <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25285_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25285\" data-vbnamecard=\"25285\">Epitome</a> says, there's really too many variables here to pin this down precisely. I'll go over some of the options at various Ambition levels.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial 3: The lowest level you can expect. At the Terrestrial level, you could <i>individually</i> animate and grant sapience to the statues. Their stats won't be incredibly high, at best equivalent to ordinary mortals, with a few supernatural merits like Claws and Unusual Hide to represent being made of stone. I wouldn't give them either notable combat skills or inherent loyalty to you at this level - both of those could be taught/instilled in them, but that would be separate from the working.<br /> <br /> Celestial 1: This would be as per Terrestrial 3 (i.e., individually-created individuals), but I'd allow you to do <i>one</i> of the following additionally per working: either give them superior traits (roughly equivalent to the Battle-Ready Troops QC, Exalted Core pp. 496-497), <i>or</i> give them an automatic intimacy of loyalty to you. <br /> At this level, you could also animate all the statues at once, but only as a non-sapient defense. They'd be limited in where they could go, remaining more or less in the area of the fortress, and being incapable of acting on very complex orders. Also, you'd have to command them in groups, not as individuals. I'd probably say that 20% of the statues at once would be the smallest group you could effectively command. So if you had 100 statues, you could tell 20 of them to &quot;attack that target&quot;, and they'd do it, but you couldn't put on any conditionals or subsequent commands - you or a designated authority would have to tell them to do each thing in order.<br /> <br /> Celestial 2: At this level, I'd let you animate individual statues with <i>both </i>good stats and an intimacy of loyal to you as a single working.<br /> Once a statue was individually animated, Celestial 2 would also let you give it more potent supernatural powers, as a separate working.<br /> I'd also let you create a collective defensive system, as per Celestial 1, that had more complex and useful behavior. It still wouldn't be self-aware, but you could give individual statues orders, rather than whole groups, and those orders could be a bit more complex (instead of just &quot;shoot at that target&quot;, it could include things like &quot;wait until the target gets within 10 yards of you, then open fire, and once they stop moving, switch to the next nearest target&quot;).<br /> <br /> Celestial 3: At Ambition 3 Celestial, individually-animated statues can be <i>very</i> potent - equivalent to 2nd-Circle demons - and they'll come with inherent loyalty to you to boot.<br /> This level would also allow you to animate a whole batch of Terrestrial 3-equivalent statues (that is, self-aware, with roughly mortal stats, no inherent loyalty) at once.<br /> As a defense system, the statues would be able to accept extremely complex commands and make their own decisions, effectively, though they wouldn't be self-aware, and wouldn't be capable of truly original or creative strategies, or going outside their assigned roles. You could also add supernatural abilities to them, like the archers being able to shoot lightning bolts or the swordsmen being capable of hitting incorporeal creatures.<br /> <br /> Solar 1: At this point, you can do a collective animation of what I described for the Celestial 1 level, creating a whole bunch of self-aware statues with either exceptional traits or inherent loyalty.<br /> As a defense system, it doesn't really get much stronger than Celestial 3, but the area they can cover gets larger - a city or similar sized region instead of just a single fortress.<br /> <br /> Solar 2: Here's where you can mass-produce self-aware, elite stats, inherent loyalty individuals, and throw in a supernatural power or two for each of them as well. <br /> As a collective defense, the statues should be capable of everything at Celestial 3, with the scope of Solar 1, and add additional potent supernatural abilities, like the ability to multiply when attacked, nigh-invulnerability, or similarly potent powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t suppose there is any way for th circles dawn to train statues is there ?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're self-aware, I'd allow them to be trained, though if they're sufficiently good, they might not benefit from it very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T09:32:42-07:00","id":1332824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1332768#post1332768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bLike <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25285_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25285\" data-vbnamecard=\"25285\">Epitome</a> says, there's really too many variables here to pin this down precisely. I'll go over some of the options at various Ambition levels.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial 3: The lowest level you can expect. At the Terrestrial level, you could <i>individually</i> animate and grant sapience to the statues. Their stats won't be incredibly high, at best equivalent to ordinary mortals, with a few supernatural merits like Claws and Unusual Hide to represent being made of stone. I wouldn't give them either notable combat skills or inherent loyalty to you at this level - both of those could be taught/instilled in them, but that would be separate from the working.<br /> <br /> Celestial 1: This would be as per Terrestrial 3 (i.e., individually-created individuals), but I'd allow you to do <i>one</i> of the following additionally per working: either give them superior traits (roughly equivalent to the Battle-Ready Troops QC, Exalted Core pp. 496-497), <i>or</i> give them an automatic intimacy of loyalty to you. <br /> At this level, you could also animate all the statues at once, but only as a non-sapient defense. They'd be limited in where they could go, remaining more or less in the area of the fortress, and being incapable of acting on very complex orders. Also, you'd have to command them in groups, not as individuals. I'd probably say that 20% of the statues at once would be the smallest group you could effectively command. So if you had 100 statues, you could tell 20 of them to &quot;attack that target&quot;, and they'd do it, but you couldn't put on any conditionals or subsequent commands - you or a designated authority would have to tell them to do each thing in order.<br /> <br /> Celestial 2: At this level, I'd let you animate individual statues with <i>both </i>good stats and an intimacy of loyal to you as a single working.<br /> Once a statue was individually animated, Celestial 2 would also let you give it more potent supernatural powers, as a separate working.<br /> I'd also let you create a collective defensive system, as per Celestial 1, that had more complex and useful behavior. It still wouldn't be self-aware, but you could give individual statues orders, rather than whole groups, and those orders could be a bit more complex (instead of just &quot;shoot at that target&quot;, it could include things like &quot;wait until the target gets within 10 yards of you, then open fire, and once they stop moving, switch to the next nearest target&quot;).<br /> <br /> Celestial 3: At Ambition 3 Celestial, individually-animated statues can be <i>very</i> potent - equivalent to 2nd-Circle demons - and they'll come with inherent loyalty to you to boot.<br /> This level would also allow you to animate a whole batch of Terrestrial 3-equivalent statues (that is, self-aware, with roughly mortal stats, no inherent loyalty) at once.<br /> As a defense system, the statues would be able to accept extremely complex commands and make their own decisions, effectively, though they wouldn't be self-aware, and wouldn't be capable of truly original or creative strategies, or going outside their assigned roles. You could also add supernatural abilities to them, like the archers being able to shoot lightning bolts or the swordsmen being capable of hitting incorporeal creatures.<br /> <br /> Solar 1: At this point, you can do a collective animation of what I described for the Celestial 1 level, creating a whole bunch of self-aware statues with either exceptional traits or inherent loyalty.<br /> As a defense system, it doesn't really get much stronger than Celestial 3, but the area they can cover gets larger - a city or similar sized region instead of just a single fortress.<br /> <br /> Solar 2: Here's where you can mass-produce self-aware, elite stats, inherent loyalty individuals, and throw in a supernatural power or two for each of them as well. <br /> As a collective defense, the statues should be capable of everything at Celestial 3, with the scope of Solar 1, and add additional potent supernatural abilities, like the ability to multiply when attacked, nigh-invulnerability, or similarly potent powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If they're self-aware, I'd allow them to be trained, though if they're sufficiently good, they might not benefit from it very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm thanks that\u2019s very helpful, I want to animate a whole bunch of them at once and maybe have them act as a few battle groups it kinda sounds like what I\u2019m looking for is solar 1 or 2. And I would want either our dawn command them when we are home or my 2nd circle equivalent when we are away. How difficult would it be to do for celestial level sorceror ? And is there any way of lowering the difficulty ? My main issue isn\u2019t the roll difficulty but time involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","user":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","date":". 08-27-2019, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T12:06:27-07:00","id":1332858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1332824#post1332824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How difficult would it be to do for celestial level sorceror ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's doable, but will definitely be more difficult. The basic difficulty of the rolls will be (2 + Finesse), instead of just (Finesse), and the time required for each roll will be 3 months, rather than just a week. If you have (Intelligence + Occult) at 10, meaning you can throw 20 dice at each roll, on average you'll get 7 successes for each interval, if you go for Finesse 1. So a Solar 1 working will require, on average, 6 intervals (it requires 40 successes), while a Solar 2 one will require 8 intervals. So, either 18 months or 24 months.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And is there any way of lowering the difficulty ? My main issue isn\u2019t the roll difficulty but time involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only canonical way of reducing the difficulty is by accepting a lower Finesse, meaning that your ST will get to determine more of the details of what the working involves exactly. Note that this shouldn't ever make the working useless - if you ask for the working to be &quot;a bunch of animated statues with self-awareness, who are loyal to me&quot;, that's what you'll get. But the ST will put in complications or weirdness on that. <br /> <br /> For time reduction, I'd be okay with a custom Occult charm, along these lines:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Flashing Wonder Technique</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014; <b>Mins: </b>Occult 5, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> The Copper Spider's mastery over the esoteric secrets of sorcery is so great that she can transform the world in a fraction of the time. This charm improves the speed at which she can perform sorcerous workings. Workings of a level she has mastered (meaning those she has the appropriate Sorcery charm for) have an interval of only three days, while those one circle below that have an interval of only a single day, while two circles lower have an interval of a single hour. Workings of a circle higher than the Solar has mastered, meanwhile, have an interval of one month if they are one circle higher than her mastery, and 6 months if they are two circles higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T16:39:48-07:00","id":1332915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1332858#post1332858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's doable, but will definitely be more difficult. The basic difficulty of the rolls will be (2 + Finesse), instead of just (Finesse), and the time required for each roll will be 3 months, rather than just a week. If you have (Intelligence + Occult) at 10, meaning you can throw 20 dice at each roll, on average you'll get 7 successes for each interval, if you go for Finesse 1. So a Solar 1 working will require, on average, 6 intervals (it requires 40 successes), while a Solar 2 one will require 8 intervals. So, either 18 months or 24 months.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The only canonical way of reducing the difficulty is by accepting a lower Finesse, meaning that your ST will get to determine more of the details of what the working involves exactly. Note that this shouldn't ever make the working useless - if you ask for the working to be &quot;a bunch of animated statues with self-awareness, who are loyal to me&quot;, that's what you'll get. But the ST will put in complications or weirdness on that. <br /> <br /> For time reduction, I'd be okay with a custom Occult charm, along these lines:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Flashing Wonder Technique</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014; <b>Mins: </b>Occult 5, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> The Copper Spider's mastery over the esoteric secrets of sorcery is so great that she can transform the world in a fraction of the time. This charm improves the speed at which she can perform sorcerous workings. Workings of a level she has mastered (meaning those she has the appropriate Sorcery charm for) have an interval of only three days, while those one circle below that have an interval of only a single day, while two circles lower have an interval of a single hour. Workings of a circle higher than the Solar has mastered, meanwhile, have an interval of one month if they are one circle higher than her mastery, and 6 months if they are two circles higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quality stuff there I\u2019ll speak to the ST about it although it sounds like the Dawn caste doesn\u2019t like the idea so I might just clone him 500 times instead see how he likes that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T17:25:01-07:00","id":1332918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1332858#post1332858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For time reduction, I'd be okay with a custom Occult charm, along these lines:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Flashing Wonder Technique</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014; <b>Mins: </b>Occult 5, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> The Copper Spider's mastery over the esoteric secrets of sorcery is so great that she can transform the world in a fraction of the time. This charm improves the speed at which she can perform sorcerous workings. Workings of a level she has mastered (meaning those she has the appropriate Sorcery charm for) have an interval of only three days, while those one circle below that have an interval of only a single day, while two circles lower have an interval of a single hour. Workings of a circle higher than the Solar has mastered, meanwhile, have an interval of one month if they are one circle higher than her mastery, and 6 months if they are two circles higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't much like this, tbh. Mainly because of how weirdly it interacts with taking extra time and its balance concerns.<br /> <br /> normal: 1 week interval<br /> can be extended to:<br /> one month<br /> three months<br /> one year<br /> <br /> if one circle above: three months<br /> extends to<br /> one year<br /> three years<br /> five years<br /> <br /> if two circles above: one year<br /> extends to<br /> three years<br /> five years<br /> ten years<br /> <br /> So logically if you're simply dropping everything by one step with your charm, this would mean that you'd go from one year to <b>three months</b> for going two circles above as the base interval.<br /> <br /> I <i>also </i>don't like this effect because it basically adds in extra means for free, and makes solar sorcerers able to slap down overlapping sorcerous workings in rapid fire. Do you really want a solar sorcerer to be able to lay down literally 168 sorcerous workings for every <i><b>one </b></i>a terrestrial can drop down (the first one could be not needing sleep for a week!)? Assuming similar difficulties and dice pools, which means that the solar could probably drop <i>even more</i> comparatively. All of this for a single purchase at Essence 1? I mean, Solar sorcerers are good but I don't think they should be this good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T20:07:11-07:00","id":1332926,"title":"","content":"Wow. Charms that affect sorcerous workings? Are those kosher? I'm fairly sure that the book said there were issues with doing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T21:17:14-07:00","id":1332931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1332918#post1332918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>also </i>don't like this effect because it basically adds in extra means for free,</div> </div> </div> </div>To address this, I would say that using the effect is optional, but if you do use it, you can't take extra time as a means. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and makes solar sorcerers able to slap down overlapping sorcerous workings in rapid fire. Do you really want a solar sorcerer to be able to lay down literally 168 sorcerous workings for every <i><b>one </b></i>a terrestrial can drop down</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also a good point. I think I'd limit the &quot;two circles of mastery higher&quot; effect to only Terrestrial 1 workings, not any higher than that. So a Solar-Circle sorcerer could drop 168 as many minor blessings as a Terrestrial-Circle sorcerer could, but anything higher than that would take a full day. I think the fact that each such low-level working will still cost 1 XP will be sufficient balance at that point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T21:25:26-07:00","id":1332933,"title":"","content":"Frankly speaking, wasn't there a problem in 2e of, say, people continuously pumping out artifacts? Wouldn't doing something like this make sorcerous workings devalue? Don't get me wrong, I like making the setting magical as a whole. But something that would warp and alter sorcerous workings should be somewhere in Essence 4-5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T21:35:54-07:00","id":1332934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1332768#post1332768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial 3: At Ambition 3 Celestial, individually-animated statues can be <i>very</i> potent - equivalent to 2nd-Circle demons - and they'll come with inherent loyalty to you to boot.<br /> This level would also allow you to animate a whole batch of Terrestrial 3-equivalent statues (that is, self-aware, with roughly mortal stats, no inherent loyalty) at once.<br /> As a defense system, the statues would be able to accept extremely complex commands and make their own decisions, effectively, though they wouldn't be self-aware, and wouldn't be capable of truly original or creative strategies, or going outside their assigned roles. You could also add supernatural abilities to them, like the archers being able to shoot lightning bolts or the swordsmen being capable of hitting incorporeal creatures.<br /> <br /> Solar 1: At this point, you can do a collective animation of what I described for the Celestial 1 level, creating a whole bunch of self-aware statues with either exceptional traits or inherent loyalty.<br /> As a defense system, it doesn't really get much stronger than Celestial 3, but the area they can cover gets larger - a city or similar sized region instead of just a single fortress.<br /> <br /> Solar 2: Here's where you can mass-produce self-aware, elite stats, inherent loyalty individuals, and throw in a supernatural power or two for each of them as well.<br /> As a collective defense, the statues should be capable of everything at Celestial 3, with the scope of Solar 1, and add additional potent supernatural abilities, like the ability to multiply when attacked, nigh-invulnerability, or similarly potent powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If they're self-aware, I'd allow them to be trained, though if they're sufficiently good, they might not benefit from it very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're kinda lowballing the appropriate power level for mass-produced statues at the higher levels. Whipping up a bunch of untrained mortals with no loyalty to you who happen to have Unusual Hide just isn't all that impressive compared to other stuff you can do at that level.<br /> <br /> For Celestial 3, I'd probably allow a group of loyal statues on par with elite soldiers (with Unusual Hide 5 and Claws). I'm not sure <i>how big</i> a group you should get at that point, but honestly, it would need to be a fair-sized group to be remotely worth choosing when the alternative could throw down with a Second Circle demon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1332926#post1332926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. Charms that affect sorcerous workings? Are those kosher? I'm fairly sure that the book said there were issues with doing this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall the book saying anything like that.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't reduce the intervals that far, but I don't think there's any reason why it shouldn't be possible to perform workings faster than usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T21:12:25-07:00","id":1338389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0326.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://keychain.patternspider.net/images/rss.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0326.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Keychain of Creation - Updates Monday and Friday </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0326.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0326.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Making a name unutterable: Solar 3, &quot;Make subtle alterations to the metaphysics of the entire cosmos?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T21:57:18-07:00","id":1338395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338389#post1338389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making a name unutterable: Solar 3, &quot;Make subtle alterations to the metaphysics of the entire cosmos?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds within the scope of what\u2019s allowed, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T22:34:12-07:00","id":1338400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338389#post1338389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0326.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0326.html</a><br /> <br /> Making a name unutterable: Solar 3, &quot;Make subtle alterations to the metaphysics of the entire cosmos?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's <i>such</i> a small effect (the name can clearly be <i>remembered</i>, spelled out, and otherwise referenced) that I'd be willing to put it at Solar 2, instead of 3. In 2e, there was a Sidereal charm, Name Pilfering Practice, that did much more than that (it stole someone's name so that <i>only</i> the Sidereal, in the entire world, could remember it), and that was available at Essence 2. I see no reason to assume Sidereals won't get something like that again in Ex 3rd ed, so I'm pretty okay with making it require a bit less than the peak of sorcery to pull off otherwise. Definitely not lower than Solar Circle, though - even for weak effects, Solar Circle is a must, I think, for anything that affects the entire universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T11:33:00-07:00","id":1338658,"title":"","content":"What level of working would it be to either coat with, or wholesale turn/replace one's bones into/with a Magical Material?<br /> Celestial 2 for just coating and 3 or Solar 1 for complete change?<br /> What kind of side effects would you suggest if done at Finesse 3 or 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8011-imadaman","name":"imadaman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8011_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T11:40:14-07:00","id":1338661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>imadaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338658#post1338658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What level of working would it be to either coat with, or wholesale turn/replace one's bones into/with a Magical Material?</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds more like the means (lowercase-\u201cm\u201d) than the end. What are you wanting starmetal bones to accomplish?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T12:09:46-07:00","id":1338663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338661#post1338661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds more like the means (lowercase-\u201cm\u201d) than the end. What are you wanting starmetal bones to accomplish?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good observation and a question.<br /> I did not think this through and feel rather silly.<br /> <br /> The first thing that comes to mind is using White Jade to give protection from the Wyld, perhaps in inscriptions about stability or something in the ribs.<br /> Another thought is inscribing sorcerous texts/rituals/prayers with Orichalcum into the bones to enhance sorcery in some way.<br /> Or inscribing koans about rote learning in the skull with Blue Jade to get Eidetic Memory.<br /> <br /> But you are right, I didn't think this through and those are just some ideas. Blergh. I'll try and think on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8011-imadaman","name":"imadaman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8011_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T12:11:30-07:00","id":1338664,"title":"","content":"The first two sound like Celestial 2; the last sounds like Celestial 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T12:19:26-07:00","id":1338667,"title":"","content":"Right, thanks. I'll try and actually think things through next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8011-imadaman","name":"imadaman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8011_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T12:26:26-07:00","id":1338668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>imadaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338667#post1338667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, thanks. I'll try and actually think things through next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong, it's a cool idea - for instance, back in 2e, one of my characters underwent the equivalent of a sorcerous working (we used the Artifact rules) to get orichalcum bonded to his bones to make himself immune to amputation, broken bones, and other crippling effects (and incidentally making his unarmed damage go up slightly).<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for downsides, depending on how much metal we're talking about, the weight alone might play a factor in their ability to swim; it might also increase the time it takes for them to recover from blood loss (as your bones are responsible for the creation of new blood cells).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-30-2019, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T12:56:19-07:00","id":1338676,"title":"","content":"We are working on a Working in game to create a novel plant species but the players don't know if it is Terrestrial 1 or Celestial 1 because we stacked so many additional features onto it.<br /> <br /> We used Kudzu as a base. We blended it with Moly (from the Odyssey) to give it some minor anti-enchantment properties, had the thorns become cold iron to make life difficult for fey, then used a demesne-dwelling species to allow the result to grow rapidly in demesnes but not elsewhere to prevent it from spreading everywhere.<br /> <br /> The players all agree that one of those crosses would be Terrestrial 1. We aren't certain about the final product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T13:08:11-07:00","id":1338679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338676#post1338676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We used Kudzu as a base. We blended it with Moly (from the Odyssey) to give it some minor anti-enchantment properties, had the thorns become cold iron to make life difficult for fey, then used a demesne-dwelling species to allow the result to grow rapidly in demesnes but not elsewhere to prevent it from spreading everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd definitely peg doing all of that at once at Celestial 1. You could do them sequentially with lower-level workings, but I wouldn't allow them as Terrestrial 1. It takes Terrestrial 3 to create &quot;a completely new but mundane form of life&quot;, or to &quot;breed a specimen of an existing species with a minor supernatural power that augments its strongest traits&quot;. I'd say that creating the iron thorns plant would qualify as the first, and making it grow supernaturally quickly in a demesne would be the second. I suppose if you had a plant that, when consumed, was able to make people more alert or mentally more resilient, I could see upgrading that to actual anti-enchantment magic would fall into &quot;a minor supernatural power that augments its strongest trait&quot;. But, anyway, you'd need, I'd say, three Terrestrial 3 workings in order to upgrade the plant like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T06:49:14-07:00","id":1338777,"title":"","content":"So let me get this straight. Celestial 2. Lets you chuck mutations into an ecosystem. So basically, grant mutations en masse. <br /> <br /> Let's say I create a fountain of legend. Drinking from this fountain will grant you the power to heal and resist disease like an exalt. Permanently. And I set it out there. <br /> <br /> Is it Celestial 2, Celestial 3, or Solar 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:03:28-07:00","id":1338778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338777#post1338777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let me get this straight. Celestial 2. Lets you chuck mutations into an ecosystem. So basically, grant mutations en masse. <br /> <br /> Let's say I create a fountain of legend. Drinking from this fountain will grant you the power to heal and resist disease like an exalt. Permanently. And I set it out there. <br /> <br /> Is it Celestial 2, Celestial 3, or Solar 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial 3. 2 is giving supernatural abilities to 1 person, and exalted healing seems like a supernatural ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:11:34-07:00","id":1338780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338778#post1338778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Celestial 3. 2 is giving supernatural abilities to 1 person, and exalted healing seems like a supernatural ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, I'm not quite sure myself, not having read the merits section for awhile. But isn't exalted healing literally a normal-ish merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:14:17-07:00","id":1338781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338780#post1338780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I'm not quite sure myself, not having read the merits section for awhile. But isn't exalted healing literally a normal-ish merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's under Supernatural Merits, page 165 CRB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8011-imadaman","name":"imadaman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8011_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:19:31-07:00","id":1338784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>imadaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338781#post1338781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's under Supernatural Merits, page 165 CRB.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine then. Celestial 3, or Solar 1. <br /> <br /> Here's the thing. Let's say that I, an enterprising Lunar/ Solar/ Dragonblooded. Decide to do this. Finesse 5. Over a century's worth of time. With priceless reagents and numerous willpower and stunts. <br /> <br /> Its done. It. Is. Done. One fountain that, whosoever drinks it, heals like an exalt, and resists disease like one. It's permanent, and it works perfectly well with no side-effects. The fountain's light enough such that a team of a dozen men can lift it, and its composed out of the magical materials, making it ultra-hard. <br /> <br /> So... what now? So let's say that anyone from the kingdom can drink from it. Do we have an entire city-state/ nation with people that can heal of anything short of amputation and near-immunity to all diseases? Do we literally have a place that, if you get access to it, you can heal from almost any wound and any disease?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:19:43-07:00","id":1338785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338780#post1338780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I'm not quite sure myself, not having read the merits section for awhile. But isn't exalted healing literally a normal-ish merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sort of a grey area. Exalted Healing is under &quot;Supernatural Merits&quot;, but so are wings or gills, which could quality as &quot;normal&quot; mutations by a Sorcerous Working's standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:23:16-07:00","id":1338787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338785#post1338785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's sort of a grey area. Exalted Healing is under &quot;Supernatural Merits&quot;, but so are wings or gills, which could quality as &quot;normal&quot; mutations by a Sorcerous Working's standards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, seriously? You can fly/ breathe under water. That's pretty much as supernatural as 'slightly more thorough and faster healing'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:30:21-07:00","id":1338788,"title":"","content":"So supernatural that birds and fish can do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:31:02-07:00","id":1338789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338787#post1338787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, seriously? You can fly/ breathe under water. That's pretty much as supernatural as 'slightly more thorough and faster healing'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having gills and an adapted respiration system is not supernatural. At least not in Exalted: you are just a weird human with gills and strange lungs.<br /> <br /> Flying is probably more supernatural unless you have a serious body restructuring: our body shape and mass is not precisely adapted to flying, and flying is HARD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:33:32-07:00","id":1338790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338784#post1338784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... what now? So let's say that anyone from the kingdom can drink from it. Do we have an entire city-state/ nation with people that can heal of anything short of amputation and near-immunity to all diseases? Do we literally have a place that, if you get access to it, you can heal from almost any wound and any disease?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. Creating a fountain of healing should have a huge impact on the world, which is part of why the first instinct is to rate it Celestial 3/Solar 1 even though Celestial 2 might be enough. Let the wars for the Fountain begin!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:44:54-07:00","id":1338794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338787#post1338787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, seriously? You can fly/ breathe under water. That's pretty much as supernatural as 'slightly more thorough and faster healing'.</div> </div> </div> </div>And being able to ignore dieseases with a good enough roll and not die of bleeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:57:39-07:00","id":1338796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338790#post1338790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much. Creating a fountain of healing should have a huge impact on the world, which is part of why the first instinct is to rate it Celestial 3/Solar 1 even though Celestial 2 might be enough. Let the wars for the Fountain begin!</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally. So basically, you now create the McGuffin for lower level adventures? I can see a dragonblooded dragging his heroic mortal friends to the fountain to heal him of a crippling injury. Or someone walking there, to heal himself of leprosy/ curse/ broken leg. Or, say, someone tasked with stealing the fountain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T08:03:19-07:00","id":1338799,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded have Exalted healing. What do the Fountain do? Does it grant Exalted Healing, or does it heal any injury? They are different things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T08:07:44-07:00","id":1338800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338796#post1338796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally. So basically, you now create the McGuffin for lower level adventures? I can see a dragonblooded dragging his heroic mortal friends to the fountain to heal him of a crippling injury. Or someone walking there, to heal himself of leprosy/ curse/ broken leg. Or, say, someone tasked with stealing the fountain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything an E3+ Celestial Exalt does is basically &quot;No, <b>I</b> make the story now&quot;. There's a definite shift in tone as an Exalt grows past plucky adventuring and into the realm of legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T08:08:31-07:00","id":1338801,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't expect it be able to completely restore a mortal's crippling injuries acquired long before the Merit was gained. After all, Cynis Tagnaka, the Dragon-Blooded who was castrated right before his Exaltation in <i>Aspect Book: Earth</i> didn't mystically regenerate his testicles just because he received Pasiap's blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-01-2019, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T08:27:31-07:00","id":1338803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338801#post1338801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't expect it be able to completely restore a mortal's crippling injuries acquired long before the Merit was gained. After all, Cynis Tagnaka, the Dragon-Blooded who was castrated right before his Exaltation in <i>Aspect Book: Earth</i> didn't mystically regenerate his testicles just because he received Pasiap's blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. But if a man had his arms crushed or tendons cut, I say that the fountain can regenerate it. Just no regeneration from amputation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T08:28:10-07:00","id":1338804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338799#post1338799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded have Exalted healing. What do the Fountain do? Does it grant Exalted Healing, or does it heal any injury? They are different things</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroic mortal friends. The fountain is for the friend. Not the dragon blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T21:44:23-07:00","id":1338933,"title":"","content":"A sorcerer, the child of a simple farming family, has spent weeks upon end repeatedly tilling and plowing one acre of farmland; on the four corners of this plot of land, the sorcerer has placed the statues of four divinities: the Sextes Jylis, Pasiap, Venus, and the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> The enchanted plot of land is <i>absurdly</i> fertile. If seeds are planted and watered before the sun goes down one day, the crops will be ready to harvest as the sun rises the next morning. Plants with a longer life-cycle may take proportionately longer; if apple seeds are planted, it may take a week or two before the trees are bearing fruit, but once the trees are grown they will grow a fresh crop of apples each morning. Crop rotation is not necessary, and while fertilizer and perhaps some bees certainly wouldn't hurt anything, the plants will grow just fine with only water.<br /> <br /> Little does the sorcerer know that a local Guild factor has already heard about the miraculous field, and will stop at nothing to acquire the land (and possibly convince the sorcerer to make more) for a new opium plantation.<br /> <br /> (I'm actually thinking this could be Solar Ambition 1? It might not be game-breaking in mechanical terms, but it would be kind of a big deal -- <i>everyone</i> needs crops grown.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T21:49:11-07:00","id":1338936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338933#post1338933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sorcerer, the child of a simple farming family, has spent weeks upon end repeatedly tilling and plowing one acre of farmland; on the four corners of this plot of land, the sorcerer has placed the statues of four divinities: the Sextes Jylis, Pasiap, Venus, and the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> The enchanted plot of land is <i>absurdly</i> fertile. If seeds are planted and watered before the sun goes down one day, the crops will be ready to harvest as the sun rises the next morning. Plants with a longer life-cycle may take proportionately longer; if apple seeds are planted, it may take a week or two before the trees are bearing fruit, but once the trees are grown they will grow a fresh crop of apples each morning. Crop rotation is not necessary, and while fertilizer and perhaps some bees certainly wouldn't hurt anything, the plants will grow just fine with only water.<br /> <br /> Little does the sorcerer know that a local Guild factor has already heard about the miraculous field, and will stop at nothing to acquire the land (and possibly convince the sorcerer to make more) for a new opium plantation.<br /> <br /> (I'm actually thinking this could be Solar Ambition 1? It might not be game-breaking in mechanical terms, but it would be kind of a big deal -- <i>everyone</i> needs crops grown.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Urm, no. Celestial 2 or 3. Or maybe 1. Remember, Terrestrial circle is anything a terrestrial circle sorcerer can do. Making golems, summoning fire, or hell, making an entire field grow in a minute. The only catch here is that it works continuously all the while, while a terrestrial circle sorcerer works only once a year per plot of land. <br /> <br /> So yeah, Celestial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T23:17:29-07:00","id":1338949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338933#post1338933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The enchanted plot of land is <i>absurdly</i> fertile. If seeds are planted and watered before the sun goes down one day, the crops will be ready to harvest as the sun rises the next morning. Plants with a longer life-cycle may take proportionately longer; if apple seeds are planted, it may take a week or two before the trees are bearing fruit, but once the trees are grown they will grow a fresh crop of apples each morning. Crop rotation is not necessary, and while fertilizer and perhaps some bees certainly wouldn't hurt anything, the plants will grow just fine with only water.<br /> <br /> (I'm actually thinking this could be Solar Ambition 1? It might not be game-breaking in mechanical terms, but it would be kind of a big deal -- <i>everyone</i> needs crops grown.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If the field is only an acre, I <i>might</i> be okay with as low as Celestial 2. Celestial 2 can affect the weather of a town sized region on a long-term basis, giving an extra month of growing season every year. I haven't worked out the math, but I suspect that that extra month of growing season over hundreds or even thousands of acres would probably about equal the productivity of one super-fast acre. However, I would definitely require the field be fertilized periodically at that level. If it was magically made permanently fertile, with no need to replenish any nutrients besides water, I think that bumps it up to Celestial 3, to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T23:21:57-07:00","id":1338952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338949#post1338949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the field is only an acre, I <i>might</i> be okay with as low as Celestial 2. Celestial 2 can affect the weather of a town sized region on a long-term basis, giving an extra month of growing season every year. I haven't worked out the math, but I suspect that that extra month of growing season over hundreds or even thousands of acres would probably about equal the productivity of one super-fast acre. However, I would definitely require the field be fertilized periodically at that level. If it was magically made permanently fertile, with no need to replenish any nutrients besides water, I think that bumps it up to Celestial 3, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>But towns are a lot bigger than an acre....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T23:29:49-07:00","id":1338954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338952#post1338952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But towns are a lot bigger than an acre....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that\u2019s what their argument is. The stated effect is much more potent than the example effect from the book, but the area it\u2019s affecting is much smaller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T23:40:00-07:00","id":1338956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338954#post1338954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that\u2019s what their argument is. The stated effect is much more potent than the example effect from the book, but the area it\u2019s affecting is much smaller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Apologies then. Granted, I don't have 3e right in front of me, but isn't Celestial the one that says 'Egregrious and blatant alterations of the laws of physics'?<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11237_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11237\" data-vbnamecard=\"11237\">Jefepato</a> <br /> \u200b<br /> Anyway, on the growing of plants.... does it bypass seasons and surroundings? I bet that if you tweak it a bit, you can make a pretty penny selling rare flowers and herbs that you can't find anywhere else. Does your sorcerer have access to wood elementals and Summoning the Stalwart Servitor? If so, then maybe you can stunt a thing, mass growing peach trees, and then moving them somewhere else to start up an orchard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T08:17:00-07:00","id":1338995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338956#post1338956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, I don't have 3e right in front of me, but isn't Celestial the one that says 'Egregrious and blatant alterations of the laws of physics'?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not those exact words, but yeah, localized changes to the laws of nature are acceptable within the Sapphire Circle - <i>hence why Celestial 2 was recommended</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T04:06:46-07:00","id":1339329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1338956#post1338956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, on the growing of plants.... does it bypass seasons and surroundings? I bet that if you tweak it a bit, you can make a pretty penny selling rare flowers and herbs that you can't find anywhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>My general thought was that pretty much any plant will grow at any time there, unless it gets so cold that the ground is actually frozen or something.<br /> <br /> There are probably any number of ways to make money off something like this. I was originally thinking &quot;the Guild would want this for their cash crops, which are obviously drugs,&quot; but I guess if some plants are rare or it's hard to find the right conditions in which to grow them, they might be a more valuable use for the super-field than poppies. (Seven bounties paste is made of expensive plants, right?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T04:40:27-07:00","id":1339333,"title":"","content":"There's always some expensive plant that can only be found in the far off reaches of the elemental poles..<br /> <br /> Or your sorcerers front yard. <br /> <br /> How old is he, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T11:28:45-07:00","id":1339418,"title":"","content":"Absurdly fertile doesn't mean everything will grow here. Some plants and especially rare and magical plants often have a requirement beyond fertile ground. In fact for some magical plants that might kill them! Rare flowers that grow only in death touched soils, mystical trees that feed on wyld energy, fruits picked from the elemental poles. They all likely need something that a simple magically fertile land can't offer. I can see it being a Solar level project if it can nurtish these plants as well, and a high solar level if it can make things &quot;That bloom once a century&quot; make daily crops too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T20:44:52-07:00","id":1341771,"title":"","content":"I just remembered something. Someone once posted a jade millstone that could grind stone into flour. What's the level? Celestial 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T22:00:08-07:00","id":1341786,"title":"","content":"Terrestrial 3 sounds like it. &quot;Bless a region to enhance its natural properties, causing a field to always deliver a bountiful harvest or a freshwater river to always run clean.&quot; To me, a millstone that turns stone into flour is equivalent to a field of, say, wheat always delivering great harvests (grinding stone makes up for the process of making flour), so it's not really higher than T3 imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T22:36:01-07:00","id":1341793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1341786#post1341786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terrestrial 3 sounds like it. &quot;Bless a region to enhance its natural properties, causing a field to always deliver a bountiful harvest or a freshwater river to always run clean.&quot; To me, a millstone that turns stone into flour is equivalent to a field of, say, wheat always delivering great harvests (grinding stone makes up for the process of making flour), so it's not really higher than T3 imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. But its constant, not set by the seasons or time, and pretty darned reliable. Me, I'll put it as... Celestial 1. Depending on the rate of production. Giant millstone capable of making a literal waterfall of flour? Celestial. Small one that can be moved by hand and probably feeds a village? Terrestrial 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T10:28:08-07:00","id":1341896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1341793#post1341793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. But its constant, not set by the seasons or time, and pretty darned reliable. Me, I'll put it as... Celestial 1. Depending on the rate of production. Giant millstone capable of making a literal waterfall of flour? Celestial. Small one that can be moved by hand and probably feeds a village? Terrestrial 3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Harvests enhanced by Terrestrial Workings don't really need to rely on the seasons (See: that one Working that allows people to gather sunlight for the seasons that lack it), and you still need rock to grind; eventually, you run out of it if you go overboard, unless you have a very gracious Earth DB stunting rock into being. And also, it only ever makes flour, whereas a field can make whatever you sow in it. Terrestrial Workings are things you think a Dragon-Blooded sorcerer should be able to do without an extreme amount of effort, and that's where I'd peg something like a flour-conjuring millstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T11:08:37-07:00","id":1341901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1341771#post1341771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just remembered something. Someone once posted a jade millstone that could grind stone into flour. What's the level? Celestial 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mercury Ants (as previously discussed IIT) can turn lead into gold - we pegged that as a squarely Terrestrial feat as you can just make Mercury Ants at this level with Summon Elemental. And we pegged classic alchemy as turning one natural substance into another as Terrestrial.<br /> <br /> So... stone into flour isn't that much of a stretch over lead into gold.<br /> <br /> I'd say Terrestrial 3. But you're looking at a high Finesse if you specifically want a millstone that grinds rock into flour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-03-2019, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T20:25:34-07:00","id":1342002,"title":"","content":"The jade millstone sounds more like an artifact than a sorcerous working, but if we're making it a working than I'd say Celestial 1.<br /> <br /> I don't think a millstone that grinds stone into flour is necessarily more <i>useful</i> than e.g. a field that always grows an excellent crop of wheat, but it's <i>more supernatural</i> than the field -- an outright miracle of transmutation. It seems different to me in pretty much exactly the way that the book describes the difference between Celestial and Terrestrial workings.<br /> <br /> You might have a point about the mercury ants, though. Are those still around in 3e?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1341901#post1341901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you're looking at a high Finesse if you specifically want a millstone that grinds rock into flour.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're always looking at a high Finesse if you want a working exactly how you're envisioning it, of course. The question might then be, what's the <i>basic goal</i> of this working? You always get the basic goal even at Finesse 1, after all.<br /> <br /> If our sorcerer's player proclaims &quot;I want this mill to always be able to produce plenty of flour&quot; as he rolls at Finesse 1, he might have been hoping the new millstone would just multiply the wheat it grinds, or maybe all the nearby fields would grow extra wheat or something. Now the villagers have to keep lugging stones into the mill and everyone is annoyed at him.<br /> <br /> (Or something like that. It's hard to think of good ways low Finesse might manifest when you've <i>started</i> with a specific idea of how the working should work out.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T03:28:12-07:00","id":1342050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1342002#post1342002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Celestial 1.<br /> <br /> I don't think a millstone that grinds stone into flour is necessarily more <i>useful</i> than e.g. a field that always grows an excellent crop of wheat, but it's <i>more supernatural</i> than the field -- an outright miracle of transmutation. It seems different to me in pretty much exactly the way that the book describes the difference between Celestial and Terrestrial workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Celesrial 1 is fine. But it's not making magical flour. Nor is it magically making flour from nothing.<br /> <br /> It's turning one natural substance into another natural (if refined) substance. Transformation of the mundane is squarely Terrestrial in my eyes. This specific exanple is probably the extreme upper boarder for me -- lead and gold are at least chemically similiar.<br /> <br /> But people IRL make faux food out of mud and sand. Pasaip's Grace existed in 1E as bread baked with sand (it did kill the mortals who tried to eat it). A working to render the inedible edible doesn't seem like it should tax a Terrestrial sorcerer so much as a Celestial 1 working would.<br /> <br /> Milling flour out of moonlight is certainly not Terrestrial. Rocks? Eh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-18-2019, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T23:37:07-07:00","id":1342285,"title":"","content":"Thank you.<br /> <br /> So I saw something on sufficient velocity. Someone made a pretty cool SORCEROUS initiation based on Dark Souls.<br /> <br /> If you were to make a SORCEROUS working that initiated people unfailingly into sorcery, would it be celestial 3 or solar 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T23:56:49-07:00","id":1342289,"title":"","content":"N/A. \u201cUnfailingly\u201d isn\u2019t something that happens when the material you\u2019re working with is <i>people</i>. Some people will just never be able to sew a dress. Or write a symphony. Or forge a horseshoe. Or walk a tightrope. Or speak in front of crowds. Or escape handcuffs. <br /> <br /> And those things are all vastly less difficult and inherently transformative as sorcery is.<br /> <br /> Some people just are not cut out for certain endeavors, and more than a few won\u2019t want to try.<br /> <br /> Also, not sure why you\u2019re putting \u201csorcerous\u201d in all-caps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-19-2019, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T00:00:56-07:00","id":1342290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1342289#post1342289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">N/A. \u201cUnfailingly\u201d isn\u2019t something that happens when your material is people. Some people will just never learn how to sew a dress. Or write a symphony. Or make a horseshoe. Or walk a tightrope. Or escape handcuffs.<br /> <br /> And those things are all vastly less difficult and inherently transformative than sorcery is.<br /> <br /> Also, not sure why the all-caps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frickin' auto corrupt. But anyway, yes. I'm not too sure about the 'unfailing' part, but well, its a sorcerous initiation that's reasonably reliable, such that people actually search for and use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T00:09:54-07:00","id":1342291,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s more reasonable, but I\u2019d still not peg that below Solar 3 and I\u2019d still want it more fleshed out than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T00:36:25-07:00","id":1342295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1342291#post1342291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s more reasonable, but I\u2019d still not peg that below Solar 3 and I\u2019d still want it more fleshed out than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give me 10 minutes, and I'll grab it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T00:55:23-07:00","id":1342300,"title":"","content":"Solar 3.<br /> <br /> The metaphysical law of Creation states that people <i>can</i> learn sorcery. Subtly changing that law to say people can learn sorcery <i>infalliably</i>, is a Solar 3 feat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T03:02:56-07:00","id":1342315,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t feel that\u2019s a subtle change. It\u2019s closer to say the rule as regards sorcery is that people <i>can\u2019t</i> grasp its secrets without first undergoing some intrinsic transformation, internal or external, that marks you forever after as a sorcerer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-19-2019, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T14:44:16-07:00","id":1342411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1342315#post1342315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t feel that\u2019s a subtle change. It\u2019s closer to say the rule as regards sorcery is that people <i>can\u2019t</i> grasp its secrets without first undergoing some intrinsic transformation, internal or external, that marks you forever after as a sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this Working provides a reliable way of undergoing that transformation. When multiple other options already exist. Subtly changing the metaphysical laws of Creation. Solar 3.<br /> <br /> I get your point that a truly infallible method is beyond Solar 3. But if we look at the current initiations (wield a unique artifact, be permanently scarred by nightmares, make a deal with a soul eating demon), I feel like the unpalatablity of an initiation that always works probably balances itself -- sacrifice the thing you care about more than any other, after study, finding a teacher, going on a journey etc. probably is ok as an infailable initiation. (Especially as people generally aren't self-aware enough to realize what is most valuable to them.) Or a reliable, repeatable initiation which isn't guaranteed to work but has a good chance (pluck out your eye and hang from a tree) is also balanced at Solar 3.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't peg it below Solar 3, and I wouldn't allow the initiation to be something like &quot;anyone who says 'SHAZAM' is now a sorcerer&quot;, but I think the general idea is in scope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-20-2019, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T15:08:22-07:00","id":1342416,"title":"","content":"Might have been asked but Flying Fortress\u2014celestial 2 or 3? Making a moving building is 2, but flight seems a bit bigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T15:56:51-07:00","id":1342419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1342416#post1342416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might have been asked but Flying Fortress\u2014celestial 2 or 3? Making a moving building is 2, but flight seems a bit bigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda feel like &quot;moving building&quot; is Celestial 3. Deciding <i>how</i> it moves is Finesse -- and any kind of sustained flight is going to be Finesse 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-20-2019, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T17:26:25-07:00","id":1342438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1342416#post1342416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might have been asked but Flying Fortress\u2014celestial 2 or 3? Making a moving building is 2, but flight seems a bit bigger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, &quot;Enchant the architecture of an entire structure to grant it limited mobility...&quot; is Celestial 3, not 2. To make a structure actually fly would be, in my opinion, Solar 1. Solar 2, note, can cause a city-sized region to &quot;rise up and float&quot;, so as long as your fortress is notably smaller than a city, I think making it fly is reasonable at Solar 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T18:12:17-07:00","id":1342442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1342411#post1342411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When multiple other options already exist.<br /> <br /> [snip]<br /> <br /> But if we look at the current initations [sic] (wield a unique artifact, be permanently scarred by nightmares, make a deal with a soul eating demon)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple options exist that <i>still require you to have the right stuff</i>. Mara doesn't grant sorcery to just anyone - it's those with darksome destinies that catch her eye. Nor is every person who shuffles into the Wyld able to command occult forces thereafter. And it shouldn't be likely that if Stephen Strange were to hand his Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes to a random Lunar to hold for a minute, the Lunar ends up knowing how to summon demons.<br /> <br /> \u200bMaking a new avenue for sorcery <i>is itself</i> making a change to the laws of Creation, and thus Solar 3. Making one that anyone who seeks it out, gets it, is not what I'd call a subtle change. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T21:29:37-07:00","id":1342461,"title":"","content":"I think, as a Solar 3 working, I'd allow a reasonably broad swathe of people to be given the potential to be initiated into sorcery. Initiating them all simultaneously would be a separate Solar 3 working. By &quot;reasonably broad&quot;, I mean something like &quot;all the people in a given queendom&quot; or &quot;everyone who speaks a certain dialect of Airtongue&quot; or something like that. Something that would take approximately 10 or more workings to cover 90% of Creation, and there'd always be the possibility of missing a few people. I think that giving almost everyone sorcerous potential is something that could be accomplished if you're willing to really work at it, mostly because I like the characterization of Salinea from 2e, and think that her ultimate goal, of giving everyone sorcery, should be something theoretically achievable, but very, very difficult, explaining why she never completed it, but also why it wasn't a complete fools errand to think she could do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T01:32:22-07:00","id":1342489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1342295#post1342295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give me 10 minutes, and I'll grab it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been more than twenty-four hours. Have you got it yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T03:13:23-07:00","id":1342493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1342489#post1342489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been more than twenty-four hours. Have you got it yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-922#post-5950436\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-922#post-5950436\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-922#post-5950436\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-922#post-5950436 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> That just makes it weirder! Usually threads derail because of arguments. Not because The Worst Thing comes up and everyone rushes to re-affirm their hatred. Eric is. Dean doesn't seem to be. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T22:22:16-07:00","id":1343347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1342493#post1342493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-922#post-5950436\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.sufficientvelocity.co...2#post-5950436</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T13:22:38-07:00","id":1344486,"title":"","content":"I want to bind a circle together, such as that whenever any of the 5 go iconic, the other 4 sense it in their soul even no matter how far away they are within the same realm of existence. What level would that be?<br /> <br /> Also if I make a smaller version of this, where a single person can bind themselves to 1 other to sense whenever the target goes iconic within extreme range, what would that lower the working to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 10-29-2019, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T14:21:47-07:00","id":1344502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1344486#post1344486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to bind a circle together, such as that whenever any of the 5 go iconic, the other 4 sense it in their soul even no matter how far away they are within the same realm of existence. What level would that be?<br /> <br /> Also if I make a smaller version of this, where a single person can bind themselves to 1 other to sense whenever the target goes iconic within extreme range, what would that lower the working to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Celestial 2 for the latter, Celestial 3 for the former; you're still ultimately granting someone a supernatural power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T22:09:35-07:00","id":1344580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1344502#post1344502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Celestial 2 for the latter, Celestial 3 for the former; you're still ultimately granting someone a supernatural power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed, although I'd suggest bumping up the powers provided by both versions, particularly the second one - detecting when a circlemate goes iconic is actually pretty easy if they're &quot;only&quot; at extreme range, since the iconic display can be seen for miles by default.<br /> <br /> For the &quot;detect when one circlemate goes iconic&quot; one, I'd include the ability to both get a vision of what they're seeing at that moment, and the choice to teleport to where they are at that time as well (I'd give the person detecting enough time to assess the situation briefly before choosing whether or not to teleport, but if they decided not to, they couldn't change their minds later). <br /> <br /> For the bigger one, that binds the whole Circle together, I'd keep the &quot;see through your eyes&quot; idea, but I wouldn't allow teleportation, unless the target was pretty close (a few miles, at most). But some other sort of benefit would still be in order, I think. I'd be tempted to say that circlemates might be able to voluntarily &quot;eat&quot; the anima flare of their colleagues, basically doing the flare instead of the original person. That still puts them at risk, and, of course, the other person wouldn't have the anima to burn on charms or other effects that require expending anima levels, so I think that's balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T05:57:20-07:00","id":1344642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1344580#post1344580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Agreed, although I'd suggest bumping up the powers provided by both versions, particularly the second one - detecting when a circlemate goes iconic is actually pretty easy if they're &quot;only&quot; at extreme range, since the iconic display can be seen for miles by default.<br /> <br /> For the &quot;detect when one circlemate goes iconic&quot; one, I'd include the ability to both get a vision of what they're seeing at that moment, and the choice to teleport to where they are at that time as well (I'd give the person detecting enough time to assess the situation briefly before choosing whether or not to teleport, but if they decided not to, they couldn't change their minds later).<br /> <br /> For the bigger one, that binds the whole Circle together, I'd keep the &quot;see through your eyes&quot; idea, but I wouldn't allow teleportation, unless the target was pretty close (a few miles, at most). But some other sort of benefit would still be in order, I think. I'd be tempted to say that circlemates might be able to voluntarily &quot;eat&quot; the anima flare of their colleagues, basically doing the flare instead of the original person. That still puts them at risk, and, of course, the other person wouldn't have the anima to burn on charms or other effects that require expending anima levels, so I think that's balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like these ideas. The reason why I went with Extreme range is that the Exalt in question is blind, so for them this is still extremely useful. For that same reason, she wouldn't be able to benefit from shared vision, and teleporting or eating flares might be especially dangerous for her... But! Those might be great effects for her Circlemates to keep her safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T18:33:49-07:00","id":1345496,"title":"","content":"An idea for a thought experiment I had.<br /> <br /> THE WITCH'S CAULDRON<br /> <br /> An unassuming pot the size of a man, made of black iron. It is surprisingly light and easy to use, with a handle for a ladle and such. <br /> <br /> The cauldron is a granter of mutations. <br /> <br /> Upon being filled with water and out over a fire, the cauldron begins to boil and bubble. Placing in of specific herbs and alchemical ingredients can alter the composition of the cauldron content, granting different mutations. When boiling the pot will never run out, always having enough fluid to transform anyone who drinks the liquid. This works even when tipped over and the liquid spills out. As long as the fire burns, the fluid flowing from the cauldron is infinite and works to transform whatever touches it. More than one enterprising sorcerer has used to to transform an entire river or pour it into an aqueduct to transform a city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T18:54:50-07:00","id":1345497,"title":"","content":"Sounds more like a high-end artifact to me. That said, since its capacity to mutate is near-infinite and can work on a scale that affects huge geographic areas, if you <i>did</i> represent it with a Working, it'd pretty much <i>have</i> to be Solar.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T19:19:25-07:00","id":1345503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345497#post1345497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds more like a high-end artifact to me. That said, since its capacity to mutate is near-infinite and can work on a scale that affects huge geographic areas, if you <i>did</i> represent it with a Working, it'd pretty much <i>have</i> to be Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it celestial to affect an entire Ecosystem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T19:56:36-07:00","id":1345510,"title":"","content":"Affecting an entire city is Solar. The capacity to affect many cities, by situating an entire river into it, might even push it beyond that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T20:03:03-07:00","id":1345511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345510#post1345510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Affecting an entire city is Solar. The capacity to affect many cities, by situating an entire river into it, might even push it beyond that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.... You're right. Probably so. Maybe I'll just say 'it can only affect a city'. The image I had was for an enterprising lunar to take the cauldron, and tip it over, the infinite waters spilling across the dry ground in a short lived river, and the beneficiaries of the mutations drinking from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T19:50:53-08:00","id":1345689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345510#post1345510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Affecting an entire city is Solar. The capacity to affect many cities, by situating an entire river into it, might even push it beyond that.</div> </div> </div> </div>May I ask, why do you say this? I am fairly sure that Celestial-scale workings are capable of encompassing an entire city or region.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T21:08:24-08:00","id":1345700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345689#post1345689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May I ask, why do you say this? I am fairly sure that Celestial-scale workings are capable of encompassing an entire city or region.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Workings are capable of affecting an ecosystem once. This cauldron appears to be reusable and even usable by mortals. It's effectively an artifact that lets mortals produce a Celestial Working instantly whenever they please, therefore its scope goes beyond the Celestial level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T21:11:51-08:00","id":1345701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345700#post1345700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Celestial Workings are capable of affecting an ecosystem once. This cauldron appears to be reusable and even usable by mortals. It's effectively an artifact that lets mortals produce a Celestial Working instantly whenever they please, therefore its scope goes beyond the Celestial level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. So you're saying that its the reusability that's the issue. Not the scale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T21:23:32-08:00","id":1345705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345701#post1345701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. So you're saying that its the reusability that's the issue. Not the scale?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah basically. After all the basic effect is explicitly part of what's allowed in a Celestial Working :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambition 2 Celestial Working</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spread mutations throughout the mundane flora and fauna of an entire ecosystem.</div> </div> </div> </div>One might argue that mutating mortals is technically a greater effect than affecting mundane plants and animals, but that would be more of a decision for individual ST's to make, not a hard rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T22:01:40-08:00","id":1345706,"title":"","content":"Well, ok then. Here's another: <br /> <br /> Excellence Enforced (Celestial 3)<br /> <br /> A supernatural power that can only be used once a day. Upon spending a dot of willpower, the tattoos, infused with orichalcum dust and white jade, glow faintly with a golden sheen (this is cosmetic, and can be ignored). At the scene where the willpower payment is made, the recipient of the sorcerous working is considered to have 23 dice for any action he carries out, ranging from cooking, to knitting, to making a speech, or planning urban construction. This dice is considered to be charm dice, and cannot be added with excellencies, etc. <br /> <br /> The sorcerous working was created by a solar, who tired of being one of the few with supernatural excellence. Seeking supernatural and worthy lieutenants, she granted this working to one of her viziers, letting him run the state while she retired to focus on her own discoveries of the sapphire circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T01:15:36-08:00","id":1345727,"title":"","content":"Um, pretty much no one can benefit from 23 Charm dice on a roll. That goes over every dice cap in Ex3.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso pretty sure you mean spend a point of Willpower, not a dot of Willpower; if you're spending a dot of Willpower every time you want to max out your dice pool, then that's probably where the bulk of your XP is going to be headed towards.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso also, sometimes a huge dice pool by itself isn't going to make an action actually possible; you still won't be crossing four range bands in a single bound by dint of having twenty-one dice, nor will you be crafting artifacts, understanding a language you've never encountered, or stealing a ruby in a glass case just by gesturing at it.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Side note, I know you said it's just cosmetic, but the notion of glowing as part of the process of becoming better at hiding is pretty humorous to me.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-04-2019, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T01:29:50-08:00","id":1345728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345727#post1345727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, pretty much no one can benefit from 23 Charm dice on a roll. That goes over every dice cap in Ex3.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso pretty sure you mean spend a point of Willpower, not a dot of Willpower; if you're spending a dot of Willpower every time you want to max out your dice pool, then that's probably where the bulk of your XP is going to be headed towards.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso also, sometimes a huge dice pool by itself isn't going to make an action actually possible; you still won't be crossing four range bands in a single bound by dint of having twenty-one dice, nor will you be crafting artifacts, understanding a language you've never encountered, or stealing a ruby in a glass case just by gesturing at it.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Side note, I know you said it's just cosmetic, but the notion of glowing as part of the process of becoming better at hiding is pretty humorous to me.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thrice damn it. More 2e and 3e confusion. <br /> <br /> Basically, what I'm saying is that the user reaches the limit of what a solar with full training to mortal limit can use, along with an Excellency use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T01:45:46-08:00","id":1345730,"title":"","content":"Even so, being able to roll once as though you could apply a full Solar Excellency isn't all that amazing. Rolling fourteen successes on a Perception + Investigation roll won't give you more clues than getting five would have, if the difficulty was only three; nor does having a huge pile of dice <i>available </i>for a hypothetical Linguistics roll actually make you <i>literate</i>. And even for the rolls where net successes make a difference, reducing your Willpower rating from 8 to 7 until you can train it back up is a pretty abysmal cost for it.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's a reason the Excellency is still at the bottom rung of the ladder when it comes to Charms.<br /> <br /> Celestial 2, but \u200bI wouldn't permit this at my table, because &quot;I want tattooed servants capable of amazing feats&quot; translating to &quot;Once per day they can burn <i>a dot </i>of Willpower to just roll some more dice&quot; would be a pretty lackluster use of a sorcerer's time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-04-2019, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T02:15:45-08:00","id":1345735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345730#post1345730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even so, being able to roll once as though you could apply a full Solar Excellency isn't all that amazing. Rolling fourteen successes on a Perception + Investigation roll won't give you more clues than getting five would have, if the difficulty was only three; nor does having a huge pile of dice <i>available </i>for a hypothetical Linguistics roll actually make you <i>literate</i>. And even for the rolls where net successes make a difference, reducing your Willpower rating from 8 to 7 until you can train it back up is a pretty abysmal cost for it.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's a reason the Excellency is still at the bottom rung of the ladder when it comes to Charms.<br /> <br /> Celestial 2, but \u200bI wouldn't permit this at my table, because &amp;quot;I want tattooed servants capable of amazing feats&amp;quot; translating to &amp;quot;Once per day they can burn <i>a dot </i>of Willpower to just roll some more dice&amp;quot; would be a pretty lackluster use of a sorcerer's time.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in terms of enhancing power, what would be a good benchmark for a celestial 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T02:38:32-08:00","id":1345738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345735#post1345735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in terms of enhancing power, what would be a good benchmark for a celestial 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Enhancing stealth by turning invisible. Enhancing larceny via telekinesis. Enhancing social action through hypnotic suggestion. Enhancing feats of strength by your potence increasing while in contact with the earth. Enhancing tests of speed by reducing the forces acting on your body. Enhancing survival by melding into the earth itself for shelter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T02:43:37-08:00","id":1345740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345738#post1345738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enhancing stealth by turning invisible. Enhancing larceny via telekinesis. Enhancing social action through hypnotic suggestion. Enhancing feats of strength by your potence increasing while in contact with the earth. Enhancing tests of speed by reducing the forces acting on your body. Enhancing survival by melding into the earth itself for shelter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant in a general 'I am broadly capable in any mundane thing, despite having zero training'. You know, trading potency for sheer broadness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T02:54:17-08:00","id":1345741,"title":"","content":"B&amp;WT has a Celestial spell for making mortals awesome. I'd peg that as a Celestial 3 Working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T02:56:54-08:00","id":1345743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345741#post1345741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B&amp;WT has a Celestial spell for making mortals awesome. I'd peg that as a Celestial 3 Working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't everyone not like that spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T03:03:54-08:00","id":1345744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345740#post1345740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant in a general 'I am broadly capable in any mundane thing, despite having zero training'.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Broadly capable&quot; is not &quot;twenty-plus dice.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, if I were to fluff such a power, it'd involve having a repertoire of expert ghosts trapped in soulsteel or perhaps yasal crystal surgical pins at various points in your body, allowing you to channel their skill (and perhaps occasionally their Arcanoi). Instead of burning a dot of Willpower off your sheet, the downside would be a vulnerability to wards and other things that affect ghosts, and the possibility that the ghosts might have to be placated from time to time in order to continue to call on their skills.<br /> <br /> There's your Celestial 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-04-2019, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T04:06:06-08:00","id":1345750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345744#post1345744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Broadly capable&amp;quot; is not &amp;quot;twenty-plus dice.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, if I were to fluff such a power, it'd involve having a repertoire of expert ghosts trapped in soulsteel or perhaps yasal crystal surgical pins at various points in your body, allowing you to channel their skill (and perhaps occasionally their Arcanoi). Instead of burning a dot of Willpower off your sheet, the downside would be a vulnerability to wards and other things that affect ghosts, and the possibility that the ghosts might have to be placated from time to time in order to continue to call on their skills.<br /> <br /> There's your Celestial 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you poor dumb elf. Don't you get it? Be a vampire, or a ghost, or an immortal with a paint-by-numbers portrait in the rec room. Hell, even a brain-in-a-jar, in a pinch. Anything to avoid the Big Fire Below. So what this tells me is you're channeling the &quot;raw unlimited energies&quot; of two chumps who didn't have the balls to stay in the game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T04:06:52-08:00","id":1345751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345744#post1345744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat said, if I were to fluff such a power, it'd involve having a repertoire of expert ghosts trapped in soulsteel or perhaps yasal crystal surgical pins at various points in your body, allowing you to channel their skill (and perhaps occasionally their Arcanoi). Instead of burning a dot of Willpower off your sheet, the downside would be a vulnerability to wards and other things that affect ghosts, and the possibility that the ghosts might have to be placated from time to time in order to continue to call on their skills.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, this idea is awesome, I have to remember to use it, either in Exalted or in other game :O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T04:52:58-08:00","id":1345754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345750#post1345750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, if you\u2019re going to be like that about it, gods or elementals work just fine. I just figure ghosts tend to have skillsets more useful to humans, given that they once wore a human form, and thus might not experience difficulty in trying to do surgery without a dozen arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T08:21:22-08:00","id":1345770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1345754#post1345754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, if you\u2019re going to be like that about it, gods or elementals work just fine. I just figure ghosts tend to have skillsets more useful to humans, given that they once wore a human form, and thus might not experience difficulty in trying to do surgery without a dozen arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, ghosts are cool. But that just screamed &quot;Soul Splice&quot; to me. (Which did not end well, as the quote implied.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T11:44:12-08:00","id":1346528,"title":"","content":"In celebration of my newfound understanding of exalted 3e, what would a 'double 7s on all rolls involving sorcery' count as? Celestial 1 or celestial 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T12:10:48-08:00","id":1346533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1346528#post1346528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In celebration of my newfound understanding of exalted 3e, what would a 'double 7s on all rolls involving sorcery' count as? Celestial 1 or celestial 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Breezing past the first question (what is the in universe explanation for this sudden power in sorcery), free doubling all successes is at the least going to depend on the type of sorcerer, and is probably going to be Solar of some sort\u2014I wouldn\u2019t want it in the easy range of most Lunar and Sidereal sorcereres. Solar of some sort, if at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T12:14:14-08:00","id":1346535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1346533#post1346533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Breezing past the first question (what is the in universe explanation for this sudden power in sorcery), free doubling all successes is at the least going to depend on the type of sorcerer, and is probably going to be Solar of some sort\u2014I wouldn\u2019t want it in the easy range of most Lunar and Sidereal sorcereres. Solar of some sort, if at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>A sorcerous working. Celestial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T12:25:14-08:00","id":1346539,"title":"","content":"Permanent double 7s is plainly game-breaking without some sort of condition for use or drawback. You need to figure out what it is exactly that would empower the character in such a way and to figure out complications that arise from that. And then depending on the complications you might be able to lower the working below Solar 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T14:00:06-08:00","id":1346567,"title":"","content":"No, no, Double 7s is not a thing that exists in-universe; it\u2019s a game mechanic.<br /> <br /> Getting Double 7s on a certain kind of roll would be how a player and ST <i>decides</i> a given sorcerous working manifests. A player might, for example, design a working that lightens his mortal sorcerer character\u2019s body whenever he\u2019s in the air. The ST decides the effect is best manifested by giving him Double 7s on Dexterity+Athletics-based jumping rolls. In this instance it\u2019s not overwhelmingly powerful, as there\u2019s no number of successes you can achieve that lets you cross more than a range band with a jump; a Solar with Monkey Leap Technique can do everything this mortal can, without rolling.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think an ST would grant permanent Double 7s on all sorcery rolls, because that\u2019s much more potent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T14:44:52-08:00","id":1346580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1346567#post1346567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, no, Double 7s is not a thing that exists in-universe; it\u2019s a game mechanic.<br /> <br /> Getting Double 7s on a certain kind of roll would be how a player and ST <i>decides</i> a given sorcerous working manifests. A player might, for example, design a working that lightens his mortal sorcerer character\u2019s body whenever he\u2019s in the air. The ST decides the effect is best manifested by giving him Double 7s on Dexterity+Athletics-based jumping rolls. In this instance it\u2019s not overwhelmingly powerful, as there\u2019s no number of successes you can achieve that lets you cross more than a range band with a jump; a Solar with Monkey Leap Technique can do everything this mortal can, without rolling.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think an ST would grant permanent Double 7s on all sorcery rolls, because that\u2019s much more potent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly this.<br /> Sorcerous Workings shouldn't be built Effect -&gt; Narrative.<br /> Because of the Finesse system and Botches, they <i>have</i> to be built Intent -&gt; Narrative -&gt; Effect.<br /> I want to feed this village during this drought -&gt; Rocks left overnight on the roof of this shrine to the Herald of Dawn hatch into full-grown roosters at dawn -&gt; Feeds a Size 4 of people with a Size 2 group's work<br /> I want to be proof against sneak attacks -&gt; Every gemstone on my outfit functions as an eye -&gt; Wearing sufficient jewelry makes hiding from me at Close require cover, darkness, or a really good stunt<br /> I want to feed this village during this drought -&gt; The people of the village can now eat rocks -&gt; Self explanatory<br /> I want to be better at sorcery -&gt; My ears now directly hear the sorcerous wisdom encoded into natural patterns -&gt; New shaping ritual based around stunts and natural features<br /> I want to feed this village during this drought -&gt; People here transform instead of dying when they starve -&gt; Anyone who starves here becomes a [statblock goes here]<br /> I want deadly claws -&gt; I grow deadly claws -&gt; Claws merit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T15:29:52-08:00","id":1346593,"title":"","content":"Double 7 on sorcery is not a sorcerous working, and honestly it probably isn't even in the range of Solar Charms before E3 or so. Even then the Charm would need some sort of condition or drawback, possibly both. Other Celestials maaaay get something similar like Sidereals getting Target Number reduction through different Charms or Lunars rerolling 1s with Penumbra Witch Mastery, but either less powerful than Double 7s or something you only get by combining several effects bought separately, would be my guess. <br /> <br /> A Working to make your sorcery better could grant you a new shaping ritual, a non-Charm success on shape sorcery rolls and Working rolls when a specific condition is met, a Sorcery-based Merit from a different shaping ritual as the ones you have, or a Charm or set of Charms on the level of a God-Blooded (so less powerful or broad than Dragon-Blooded Charms) that directly interact with sorcery. That kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T23:08:56-08:00","id":1347172,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Fine then. Narrative first?<br /> <br /> Building up of power. The sorcerer blasts... Again, again, and again, each new attack faster and more dangerous than the other. If the sorcerer fights long enough, his blasts can tear down entire fortresses. <br /> <br /> A sorceorus working that works only in battle, that adds a bonus success for each successful cast sorcery roll. Constantly building up and getting more and more powerful. The counter will reset itself the moment the tide of battle turns against him, he gets injured, or he makes a botch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T23:45:54-08:00","id":1347179,"title":"","content":"How can he botch when he gets any number of bonus successes? <br /> <br /> Also, what is <i>making</i> the sorcerer\u2019s repeated blasts more powerful?<i> That\u2019s</i> what we mean by \u201cnarrative.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T01:35:37-08:00","id":1347193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347172#post1347172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... Fine then. Narrative first?<br /> <br /> Building up of power. The sorcerer blasts... Again, again, and again, each new attack faster and more dangerous than the other. If the sorcerer fights long enough, his blasts can tear down entire fortresses.<br /> <br /> A sorceorus working that works only in battle, that adds a bonus success for each successful cast sorcery roll. Constantly building up and getting more and more powerful. The counter will reset itself the moment the tide of battle turns against him, he gets injured, or he makes a botch.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds a lot more like a charm than a working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T01:57:19-08:00","id":1347196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347193#post1347193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds a lot more like a charm than a working.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the difference? <br /> <br /> How do you tell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T02:16:04-08:00","id":1347197,"title":"","content":"This is just the sorcerer being better at sorcery. More skilled, more powerful.<br /> <br /> Whereas a working would be something like creating a giant crystal that blesses the land, giving someone two extra arms, creating a lava-monster, cursing a city with increased aging, etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T02:32:52-08:00","id":1347199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347197#post1347197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is just the sorcerer being better at sorcery. More skilled, more powerful.<br /> <br /> Whereas a working would be something like creating a giant crystal that blesses the land, giving someone two extra arms, creating a lava-monster, cursing a city with increased aging, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about... Storing spells? <br /> <br /> Like, there's a bunch of floating crystals about a sorcerer, and he can pre prepare spells in them with a casting roll. Whether it is Obsidian butterflies, skin of Bronze, or whatever. Unleashing these spheres of crystal take a single reflexive action, unleashing them.<br /> <br /> Is that not charm like enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T02:45:43-08:00","id":1347203,"title":"","content":"That sounds a lot more like a Working.<br /> <br /> I think casting a whole spell reflexively is OP (IIRC e5 Lunars can get a charm to make a reflexive casting roll if they win Join Battle), but the idea of the crystals is fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T03:02:54-08:00","id":1347204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347203#post1347203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds a lot more like a Working.<br /> <br /> I think casting a whole spell reflexively is OP (IIRC e5 Lunars can get a charm to make a reflexive casting roll if they win Join Battle), but the idea of the crystals is fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about... You 'attune' it to specific spells, and at tuning it basically gets you a discount in the motes needed to throw it out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T03:13:21-08:00","id":1347205,"title":"","content":"That could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T03:18:21-08:00","id":1347206,"title":"","content":"Ok then...<br /> <br /> How about this? There was a moment in fsn that stuck out to me. The mage, caster, moved her cloak covered arm... And revealed was saber, bound by magic. <br /> <br /> How about a sorcerous working that grants you a pocket dimension you can bring things into and outside. The size of a warehouse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T08:07:14-08:00","id":1347242,"title":"","content":"Sounds like an Artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T08:15:18-08:00","id":1347243,"title":"","content":"You'd have to define what that pocket dimension is. If it's tied to an object then it's more of an Artifact like JohnDoe says.<br /> <br /> I could see a sorcerous mutation that gives you a sort of sac that leads Elsewhere. Or a spirit sanctum which has its entrance bound to your person, with a spirit inside and everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T17:22:26-08:00","id":1347349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347243#post1347243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd have to define what that pocket dimension is. If it's tied to an object then it's more of an Artifact like JohnDoe says.<br /> <br /> I could see a sorcerous mutation that gives you a sort of sac that leads Elsewhere. Or a spirit sanctum which has its entrance bound to your person, with a spirit inside and everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>A sac the size of a warehouse? Ok.....<br /> <br /> I guess minor or major supernatural power. Celestial 2/3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T19:18:42-08:00","id":1347381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347349#post1347349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A sac the size of a warehouse? Ok.....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn\u00b4t need to be a sac the size of a warehouse. Things that are a lot bigger in the inside that the outside would suggest are common in fiction, from the TARDIS of Doctor Who to the Bag of Holding of D&amp;D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T19:59:07-08:00","id":1347384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347349#post1347349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A sac the size of a warehouse? Ok.....<br /> <br /> I guess minor or major supernatural power. Celestial 2/3</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the contents are Elsewhere\u2122, the physical dimensions of the sac can be as small as you want, so long as it opens wide enough for your stuff to go through.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T22:35:39-08:00","id":1347408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347384#post1347384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since the contents are Elsewhere\u2122, the physical dimensions of the sac can be as small as you want, so long as it opens wide enough for your stuff to go through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. A shadowy dimension. A pocket on your belly. Or a satchel which can hold anything. <br /> <br /> But should the size of the internal pocket affect the rating of the working? After all, it's one thing to be able to store a bunch of weapons and explosives. It's another to store enough to outfit an army.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T06:40:39-08:00","id":1347460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347408#post1347408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course. A shadowy dimension. A pocket on your belly. Or a satchel which can hold anything.<br /> <br /> But should the size of the internal pocket affect the rating of the working? After all, it's one thing to be able to store a bunch of weapons and explosives. It's another to store enough to outfit an army.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it probably should, although I'm at a bit of a loss to determine what volume corresponds to what rating.<br /> <br /> Personally I think I'd just say that the sac/dimension/etc. has an Evocation with an effect much like Many-Pockets Meditation :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Many-Pockets Meditation</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Stackable<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00000A\">The Lunar is never caught unprepared. She banishes Elsewhere an item light enough to hold in her hands or wear. Artifacts can only be banished if she\u2019s attuned to them. Ending this Charm recalls the banished item, though the Lunar must still take any actions required to ready it, such as donning armor (</span><span style=\"color:#00000A\">Exalted</span><span style=\"color:#00000A\">, p. 591). She can banish multiple items with multiple uses of this Charm.<br /> <br /> An Essence 3 repurchase lets the Lunar pay a three-mote surcharge to banish an object too large to hold, as long as it could be lifted by a feat of strength with a difficulty no higher than 10 (</span><span style=\"color:#00000A\">Exalted</span><span style=\"color:#00000A\">, p. 231). This requires her to spend five minutes concentrating or devising an ingenious hiding place for it, and she can\u2019t banish large objects that aren\u2019t hers.</span> </div> </div> </div>I figure it would be Celestial 2, with the effect being closer to 100% as strong as Many-Pockets Meditation the higher your Finesse.<br /> <br /> Or you know, just find your Lunar mate and have them act as your personal Warehouse. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 11-10-2019, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T06:59:19-08:00","id":1347463,"title":"","content":"Wow. Does that mean the lunar can carry out that scene where they constantly pull out a giant pile of weapons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T07:09:01-08:00","id":1347467,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. Upon buying this Charm, a Lunar can transport up to 59 weapons with it, and when they buy the E3 repurchase they can carry 16 pianos. All of which will continue to increase with Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T08:31:52-08:00","id":1347476,"title":"","content":"So, I have no idea where this fits because this is not (only) Sorcery, but I couldn't find any other place to do it so I'll do it here.<br /> <br /> One of my former players wanted to have the following :<ul><li>A moving mountain<ul><li>The hidden was hidden from the outside, a bit like Wakkanda in the Marvel movies for illustration</li> <li>It was big enough to hold his city, a First Age ruin, and his 10 000 warrior people</li> <li>The mountain was quite slow. You couldn't &quot;raid&quot; quickly and by surprise any other place</li> </ul></li> <li>Inside the mountain, he wanted to have more godlike powers linked to a crown he crafted that could control the mountain<ul><li>For example, define the weather at will</li> <li>Every of his citizen would swear allegiance to his crown, and while he wore it he could feel traitors inside the city</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> There were numerous other things, but I think this is enough so stress my point : It was kind of hard to balance everything from the Craft/sorcery standpoint. My answers were the following : The moving mountain was a Solar working, and the crown was a N/A artefact. Suffice to say, in retrospect I was totally not prepared for his demands and I think I balanced everything pretty poorly.<br /> <br /> So, what do you think would be the best to handle this kind of demands ? In particular, what best fall into the &quot;Working&quot; part, and what best falls into the &quot;Crafting&quot; parts ? Because sometimes I'm wondering if something is a working, or if it is a First Age artifice, which means it should be multiple workings and a Craft project ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T08:49:26-08:00","id":1347478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347476#post1347476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A moving mountain<br /> The hidden was hidden from the outside, a bit like Wakkanda in the Marvel movies for illustration</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually sounds like two different Workings on the same place; one to move the mountain, and the other to hide the city on it.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for the crown allowing control of the weather, I'd say that one possibility is to simply have a number of elementals bound to the crown and forced to carry out the wearer's will with regard to the weather the mountain experiences.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347476#post1347476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every of his citizen would swear allegiance to his crown, and while he wore it he could feel traitors inside the city...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just curious - what's the process for deciding what is a &quot;traitor?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347476#post1347476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what do you think would be the best to handle this kind of demands ? In particular, what best fall into the &quot;Working&quot; part, and what best falls into the &quot;Crafting&quot; parts?</div> </div> </div> </div>The line is intentionally left a little fuzzy, because players are going to be creative, but taking a thing that already exists and making it fly are pretty solidly in the former camp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T09:01:45-08:00","id":1347480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347478#post1347478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This actually sounds like two different Workings on the same place; one to move the mountain, and the other to hide the city on it.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for the crown allowing control of the weather, I'd say that one possibility is to simply have a number of elementals bound to the crown and forced to carry out the wearer's will with regard to the weather the mountain experiences.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just curious - what's the process for deciding what is a &quot;traitor?&quot;<br /> <br /> The line is intentionally left a little fuzzy, because players are going to be creative, but taking a thing that already exists and making it fly are pretty solidly in the former camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that makes sense to ask for multiple workings I guess. I may have asked for two workings at first, but as the line of extravagant things he wanted to do were 1) growing and 2) limited to &quot;inside the mountain&quot;, I thought this was too much to ask for Solar workings everytime. Maybe in retrospect this wasn't a good idea, and every new power should indeed ask for the right price (ie, pex and investment).<br /> <br /> I guess for the traitor thing I was acting in good faith, a bit like when Bureaucracy Charms allows you to sense treason.<br /> <br /> Yeah that makes sense, when something exists and you wanna change it it ususally should be a working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T09:06:23-08:00","id":1347481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347476#post1347476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have no idea where this fits because this is not (only) Sorcery, but I couldn't find any other place to do it so I'll do it here.<br /> <br /> One of my former players wanted to have the following :<br /> <br /> A moving mountain<br /> <br /> [snip]<br /> <br /> So, what do you think would be the best to handle this kind of demands ?</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is something the character started the game with, I would actually use the Manse merit to model the whole &quot;moving city&quot;. Definitely a greater manse, if not NA, though as long as the powers you've described were all confined to the inside of the area, I think they could be defined as the top end of greater. <br /> <br /> But as to what sort of working this would be...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular, what best fall into the &quot;Working&quot; part, and what best falls into the &quot;Crafting&quot; parts ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this can all be covered by a working. It's fine for a working to involve an object as a focus or control device of some sort, without making that object an artifact. Where it starts crossing over from &quot;working&quot; to &quot;artifact&quot; is when the powers of the working basically follow the item around, and feel more like they're coming from the object, rather than it being merely the way the user is channeling other power. So in this case, where all the effects are confined to the mountain and the defined area within it, it's sufficient, in my opinion, to call the crown simply a focus for the working. <br /> <br /> If you're wondering what level to put all this at, I'd say that making the mountain move would be Solar 2, and so would giving it the mountain disguise. Controlling the weather and detecting traitors in the whole city both sound like Solar 1 workings to me. If the sorcerer wants to combine all of these effects into a single working, that would definitely be Solar 3.<br /> <br /> If a player <i>does</i> have Craft as well as sorcery, and <i>wants </i>to integrate an artifact into this kind of thing, there's a couple of ways I'd handle that. First, an Artifact that's intimately tied to the working, and only really functions to affect it and enhance it, would count as a Means while performing the working. I'd be inclined to say that it gives Means equal to its dot rating as an Artifact, minus 1. So a simple 2-dot Artifact would give one extra roll, while a 5-dot artifact would give 4 rolls. An NA artifact would count as 10 dots for this purpose, giving 9 extra rolls. Second, when evaluating the power of the working, I'd reduce my estimate of the power if some or all of the effects weren't inherently on all the time, but rather were evocations of the artifact that had to be learned. <br /> <br /> So in your crown-and-mountain example, if the crown were crafted as an Artifact 3, it would provide the workings with 2 extra rolls, and if the weather-control disloyalty-detection powers were evocations that had to be learned, I'd be willing to bump those workings down to Celestial 2, or possibly just fold them into one or the other of the bigger Solar 2 workings. However, I'd definitely specify that the crown would be inherently linked to the whole business - taking it out of the area of the working would either mean the place stopped dead, or possibly would start to move erratically, and I'd make the illusion disguise element go unreliable too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T09:41:12-08:00","id":1347487,"title":"","content":"Eh, I\u2019d go with one or two Means, like the examples out of the books. Nine is far too many. If the results of the rolls are insufficient to complete the working, well, you keep the Artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T09:51:58-08:00","id":1347488,"title":"","content":"Thanks Kelly Pedersen. Like TheCountAlucard, I think 9 means is a lot, but I get the idea. Using an artefact as a mean is a fine idea actually, I didn't think of it like this.<br /> <br /> Also, yes my player wanted to integrate Craft into the sorcery, because he was a Craft Supernal. That's where it's becoming complicated, usually : Arguing he can craft almost anything (he could), it becomes complicated to separate what is a Solar working or what is a N/A Artefact when the character can produce both &quot;quite&quot; easily, hence my questioning. But I think in retrospect, I should have considered the crown some sort of mean, in particular due to how he used it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T13:45:43-08:00","id":1347755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347487#post1347487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I\u2019d go with one or two Means, like the examples out of the books. Nine is far too many. If the results of the rolls are insufficient to complete the working, well, you keep the Artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347488#post1347488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Kelly Pedersen. Like TheCountAlucard, I think 9 means is a lot, but I get the idea. Using an artefact as a mean is a fine idea actually, I didn't think of it like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it, I agree, 9 means is way too many. I'd go higher than 2, because I think the effort of custom-building an artifact for this kind of thing should be rewarded (it's notable, I think, that the &quot;Exotic Components&quot; examples are all stuff you've found or otherwise acquired in the process of other adventures). Thinking about it a bit more, I'd say that &quot;Dedicated Artifice&quot; could be its own category of Means, one that stacks with Exotic Components and Sorcerous Infrastructure. A 2-, 3-, or 4-dot artifact would provide 1 means, a 5-dot would give 2, and an NA artifact would give 3. I wouldn't allow the artifact to be otherwise used even if the working failed, though. In order to use an artifact as a means like this, it would have to be designed from the ground up to channel sorcerous energies, and it would be useless without a working to act on. I <i>would</i> allow an artifact built for a working that failed to be repurposed for a different working, though, as long as the goal of the new working was reasonably similar.<br /> <br /> I'd still keep the benefits I mentioned above, with the artifact's power <i>also</i> enhancing what the working could do, and allowing a bit more potency for a given working Ambition, but with that power gated behind evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T14:33:35-08:00","id":1347766,"title":"","content":"Yeah that makes sense. If you create your artifact for nothing but to channel your Sorcerous Working, it should have a higher reward. The only &quot;problem&quot; is from a balance perspective where the list of existing means seems to be written in a way that makes Solar 3 Workings with good finesse difficult but achievable by assembling lots of conditions, and adding additional means break this balance I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T15:07:09-08:00","id":1347774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347206#post1347206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok then...<br /> <br /> How about this? There was a moment in fsn that stuck out to me. The mage, caster, moved her cloak covered arm... And revealed was saber, bound by magic.<br /> <br /> How about a sorcerous working that grants you a pocket dimension you can bring things into and outside. The size of a warehouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds just like &quot;Elsewhere&quot; to me... Melee and Resistance charms let you put weapons and armor in Elsewhere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T15:20:27-08:00","id":1347776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347774#post1347774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds just like &amp;quot;Elsewhere&amp;quot; to me... Melee and Resistance charms let you put weapons and armor in Elsewhere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. But more general.<br /> <br /> I mean, resistance and melee charms don't let you put a picnic basket into a pocket dimension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T15:38:39-08:00","id":1347779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347776#post1347776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. But more general.<br /> <br /> I mean, resistance and melee charms don't let you put a picnic basket into a pocket dimension.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but there is a Lunar Charm that does (Many Pockets Meditation) provided above. That does not mean you could not use a Working to get to the same place, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T16:27:02-08:00","id":1347786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347776#post1347776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, resistance and melee charms don't let you put a picnic basket into a pocket dimension.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the picnic basket would count for Summoning the Loyal Steel if you whacked someone upside the head with it, first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T16:36:49-08:00","id":1347789,"title":"","content":"Heh... that is funny, and probably very true <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T16:49:14-08:00","id":1347793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347789#post1347789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh... that is funny, and probably very true <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a thread for 'most absurd improvised weaponry'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T08:05:57-08:00","id":1348261,"title":"","content":"You know, I've been thinking.<br /> <br /> You bless a field to never fail<br /> <br /> You bless a scarecrow such that any field it is planted on will never fail. <br /> <br /> You bless a spring to flow eternally, in the midst of a desert. <br /> <br /> You bless a statue of a toad, to spring water from its mouth eternally, that can be moved around. <br /> <br /> What's the difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T08:15:12-08:00","id":1348263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1348261#post1348261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I've been thinking.<br /> <br /> You bless a field to never fail<br /> <br /> You bless a scarecrow such that any field it is planted on will never fail. <br /> <br /> You bless a spring to flow eternally, in the midst of a desert. <br /> <br /> You bless a statue of a toad, to spring water from its mouth eternally, that can be moved around. <br /> <br /> What's the difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>2 and 4 can be moved, allowing the blessing to be transferred<br /> 3 and 4 still require work to make a farm and cultivate the land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T08:22:51-08:00","id":1348267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1347793#post1347793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there a thread for 'most absurd improvised weaponry'?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a matter of a fact, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1326263-what-is-the-best-most-ridiculous-improvised-weapon-you-ve-ever-used\">someone did make one</a> a while back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T10:59:57-08:00","id":1349623,"title":"","content":"Do you think it would be in the purview of Workings to bless an area to grow/form one of the Magical Materials?<br /> It'd probably be in Solars, and the forming would likely be rather slow. I would see it warping the area in some way towards the MM that was growing too, like Green Jade having more flora and fauna, Black Jade maybe forming marshes, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8011-imadaman","name":"imadaman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8011_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T11:02:47-08:00","id":1349624,"title":"","content":"I'd say yes in theory; after all, Ahlat was able to bribe the Jade goddesses to plant jade under Harborhead.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T12:21:26-08:00","id":1349647,"title":"","content":"I'd actually be willing to allow limited production of magical materials at Celestial. Specifically, a small source of one of the MMs feels to me like it's about balanced at Celestial 2, comparable to the &quot;enchant the fortifications of a place&quot; level. I could see, for example, a small fountain in a Wyld pocket whose droplets sometimes came out as pure moonsilver. At that level, though, I'd definitely limit the production level. I'd say enough MM for a 2-dot artifact in a year, a decade for a 3-dot artifact, a century for a 4-dot, and a millennium for a 5-dot or NA artifact. Higher levels could produce more, though I'd definitely never go <i>too</i> high - there really needs to be a reason why Creation isn't already dotted with such workings producing a steady stream of the magical materials. <br /> <br /> I think, at Solar level ambition, I'd rather have workings involve producing a fair bit of MM as a one-off thing, a non-renewable resource. A Solar 1 working could transform random rocks in a hundred-mile radius into jade, for example, while a Solar 2 working might be able to transform all the marble in a quarry into white jade, a specific redwood tree into green jade, and so forth. Those supplies would be big, but ultimately finite, meaning there wouldn't be so much MM-producing infrastructure hanging around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T01:20:38-08:00","id":1349807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1349647#post1349647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, at Solar level ambition, I'd rather have workings involve producing a fair bit of MM as a one-off thing, a non-renewable resource. A Solar 1 working could transform random rocks in a hundred-mile radius into jade, for example, while a Solar 2 working might be able to transform all the marble in a quarry into white jade, a specific redwood tree into green jade, and so forth. Those supplies would be big, but ultimately finite, meaning there wouldn't be so much MM-producing infrastructure hanging around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, as noted in the Codifying Leadership topic, there are NO clear rules (to my knowledge) on how to handle &quot;finite ressources&quot; in Exalted. I'm not saying this is a problem, but specifically for Workings that would produce &quot;a lot but not that much&quot; of Magical Materials it makes things a bit complicated to have a good insight about. What can I do with all the White Jade in a quarry that was transformed from marble ? It seems quite vague to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":"that made my sentence say the opposite of what I meant 11-20-2019, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T08:30:44-08:00","id":1349861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1349807#post1349807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, as noted in the Codifying Leadership topic, there are clear rules (to my knowledge) on how to handle &quot;finite ressources&quot; in Exalted. I'm not saying this is a problem, but specifically for Workings that would produce &quot;a lot but not that much&quot; of Magical Materials it makes things a bit complicated to have a good insight about. What can I do with all the White Jade in a quarry that was transformed from marble ? It seems quite vague to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I think I'd handle something like this in my own games is to give the resource a Value stat. Then, every time something was extracted from it, I'd roll (Value + Value) as a die pool, against a difficulty equal to the dot level of whatever Merit was being supported - the Artifact level being produced, in the case of the magical materials. If the roll fails, the resource is still produced, but the Value of the source drops by 1 (to a minimum of 1). On a botch, the dot level the source is capable of supporting permanently drops by 1. So, using my above examples, I'd peg the working to change all the rocks in a region as Value 2, while the &quot;convert a whole quarry of marble to jade&quot; one would be Value 3. Then, when someone ordered enough white jade from the quarry to make an Artifact 5 daiklaive, I'd roll 6 dice against difficulty 5. If it succeeded, there'd still be plenty of jade in the quarry, and the Value doesn't decrease. If, on the other, more likely hand, it failed, you'd still get the jade, but now the quarry has Value 2. <br /> <br /> If a more abstract and variable system doesn't appeal, you could always just say that the working produces a certain number of dots worth of stuff. For these examples, I'd put the quarry at 15 dots worth of artifacts, and the &quot;turn all the rocks into jade&quot; one at 10 dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T08:57:08-08:00","id":1349864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1349861#post1349861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way I think I'd handle something like this in my own games is to give the resource a Value stat. Then, every time something was extracted from it, I'd roll (Value + Value) as a die pool, against a difficulty equal to the dot level of whatever Merit was being supported - the Artifact level being produced, in the case of the magical materials. If the roll fails, the resource is still produced, but the Value of the source drops by 1 (to a minimum of 1). On a botch, the dot level the source is capable of supporting permanently drops by 1. So, using my above examples, I'd peg the working to change all the rocks in a region as Value 2, while the &quot;convert a whole quarry of marble to jade&quot; one would be Value 3. Then, when someone ordered enough white jade from the quarry to make an Artifact 5 daiklaive, I'd roll 6 dice against difficulty 5. If it succeeded, there'd still be plenty of jade in the quarry, and the Value doesn't decrease. If, on the other, more likely hand, it failed, you'd still get the jade, but now the quarry has Value 2.<br /> <br /> If a more abstract and variable system doesn't appeal, you could always just say that the working produces a certain number of dots worth of stuff. For these examples, I'd put the quarry at 15 dots worth of artifacts, and the &quot;turn all the rocks into jade&quot; one at 10 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah I actually like your second solution it's kinda straightforward but allows bur easier management.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T09:08:36-08:00","id":1350022,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for a bodyguard spirit specially created to protect a sorcerer while he casts 'gather sorcerous motes'. A giant, purplish humanoid in heavy armour plating with 4 arms, floating in the air and prepared to defend its master. I'm planning for it to have these merits: <br /> <br /> Iron Hands<br /> The hands of the bodyguard need many weaponry, depending on the situation. This enable the bodyguard to have access to any form of weaponry that can be held in mortal hands. This ranges from poison gas, flamepieces, arrows, spears, or ballistae. The bodyguard is presumed to be fully trained in the usage of these weapons when calculating damage. <br /> <br /> Defensive presence<br /> Passively, the bodyguard shields his charge. As long as the bodyguard is considered to be active in any form at all, the sorcerer is considered to be under heavy/ full cover, shielding him from all ranged missiles. However, as long as this merit applies, the sorcerer may not move faster than walking speed. <br /> <br /> Bodyguard's unbreakable body<br /> The bodyguard has a body of spirit and ectoplasm, meaning it is not of the mortal coil. The bodyguard is immune to mundane poisons and sickness attacks, and does not receive wound penalties. It dissipates when it dies, but reforms a week later. <br /> <br /> Excellent Shield Prana<br /> The sorcerer spends a point of willpower, and for the rest of the day, the bodyguard double 8s whenever carrying out its duties as a shield and guardian. Whether it is defending against an attack, detecting poison, or killing someone firing upon his master.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T09:55:10-08:00","id":1350029,"title":"","content":"Sounds like creating a minion of a power level consistent with a Second Circle Demon... oh, wait, double 8s on all rolls for things it was already going to be doing anyway, at no cost to itself and requiring only one WP from you, for an entire day? Never mind, this guy stands head and shoulders above Octavian.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, how trained you are in a weapon isn't part of damage calculation (completely ignoring the question of what Ability you'd even use to wield poison gas).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T10:03:28-08:00","id":1350030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1350029#post1350029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like creating a minion of a power level consistent with a Second Circle Demon... oh, wait, double 8s on all rolls for things it was already going to be doing anyway, at no cost to itself and requiring only one WP from you, for an entire day? Never mind, this guy stands head and shoulders above Octavian.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, how trained you are in a weapon isn't part of damage calculation (completely ignoring the question of what Ability you'd even use to wield poison gas).</div> </div> </div> </div>so 3rd circle, or 2nd circle? How about 'it can only counter attack things that are attacking you'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T10:14:30-08:00","id":1350037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1350022#post1350022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea for a bodyguard spirit specially created to protect a sorcerer while he casts 'gather sorcerous motes'. A giant, purplish humanoid in heavy armour plating with 4 arms, floating in the air and prepared to defend its master. I'm planning for it to have these merits:<br /> <br /> Iron Hands<br /> The hands of the bodyguard need many weaponry, depending on the situation. This enable the bodyguard to have access to any form of weaponry that can be held in mortal hands. This ranges from poison gas, flamepieces, arrows, spears, or ballistae. The bodyguard is presumed to be fully trained in the usage of these weapons when calculating damage.<br /> <br /> Defensive presence<br /> Passively, the bodyguard shields his charge. As long as the bodyguard is considered to be active in any form at all, the sorcerer is considered to be under heavy/ full cover, shielding him from all ranged missiles. However, as long as this merit applies, the sorcerer may not move faster than walking speed.<br /> <br /> Bodyguard's unbreakable body<br /> The bodyguard has a body of spirit and ectoplasm, meaning it is not of the mortal coil. The bodyguard is immune to mundane poisons and sickness attacks, and does not receive wound penalties. It dissipates when it dies, but reforms a week later.<br /> <br /> Excellent Shield Prana<br /> The sorcerer spends a point of willpower, and for the rest of the day, the bodyguard double 8s whenever carrying out its duties as a shield and guardian. Whether it is defending against an attack, detecting poison, or killing someone firing upon his master.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to figure out the level of the working without knowing the spirit's general combat power, but judging from the merits, I'd say this falls in &quot;Create a loyal minion with supernatural powers comparable to a Second Circle demon or notable god.&quot; which is Celestial 3.<br /> <br /> Some comments on specific merits :<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Hands</b> - Why Ballistae? it's not a defensive weapon, it's not a weapon you wield in your hands, and it's much stronger than the rest of the arsenal.<br /> <br /> <b>Defensive presence</b> - since this is meant for combat, what is the combat effect of only moving at walking speed? Is all terrain difficult terrain? Also how is the bodyguard activated/deactivated?<br /> <br /> <b>Excellent Shield Prana</b> - the duration is so long vs the cost that this is basically a Permanent effect. I'd say either just make it permanent and remove the wp cost, or balance it by adding a mote commitment or reducing the duration to e.g. One Scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T10:19:33-08:00","id":1350043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1350037#post1350037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's hard to figure out the level of the working without knowing the spirit's general combat power, but judging from the merits, I'd say this falls in &quot;Create a loyal minion with supernatural powers comparable to a Second Circle demon or notable god.&quot; which is Celestial 3.<br /> <br /> Some comments on specific merits :<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Hands</b> - Why Ballistae? it's not a defensive weapon, it's not a weapon you wield in your hands, and it's much stronger than the rest of the arsenal.<br /> <br /> <b>Defensive presence</b> - since this is meant for combat, what is the combat effect of only moving at walking speed? Is all terrain difficult terrain? Also how is the bodyguard activated/deactivated?<br /> <br /> <b>Excellent Shield Prana</b> - the duration is so long vs the cost that this is basically a Permanent effect. I'd say either just make it permanent and remove the wp cost, or balance it by adding a mote commitment or reducing the duration to e.g. One Scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ballistae? I mean that as an expression of 'Yes, this guy is huge and strong. Strong enough that he can hold a shield, sword, and ballistae in his hands to kill anyone who comes near him. Strong enough he can use seige weaponry'. <br /> <br /> Combat? Its more like... is Defensive presence overpowered? <br /> <br /> Excellent shield prana... I wanted double 8s. Permanent appears to be too overpowered. How about a willpower cost, it lasts for 1 day, and it can only be used once a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T10:21:56-08:00","id":1350045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1350030#post1350030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so 3rd circle, or 2nd circle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per what Epitome says, it's hard to be sure without more of an idea of how good it is at things, but if its dice pools resemble Octavian's, its basically-free practically-always-on double 8s to all rolls (or at least, all the rolls that are going to matter) would prove comparable in effect to, but vastly more economical than the Quarter Prince's pseudo-Excellency, Infernal Might Unleashed.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, I wouldn't put it on the level of a Third Circle from that alone.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Octavian has fourteen dice with which to attack with his magic staff, Equitable Resolution, and can add three successes with Infernal Might Unleashed (or five successes if he spends a Willpower for a success), at two motes per added success. Let's assume your bodyguard's dice pool is the same.<br /> <br /> I just rolled fourteen dice. I got 1, 5, 6, 5, 7, 10, 1, 10, 8, 9, 9, 1, 1, 7. For Octavian, that would be nine successes. With the one auto from the Willpower and the five extra from Infernal Might Unleashed, that's fifteen successes.<br /> <br /> Rolling the same number of dice for your bodyguard, I got 3, 8, 8, 9, 7, 6, 10, 6, 3, 1, 10, 7, 5, 9, or fourteen successes, <i>without having to spend a Willpower or anything from his mote pool</i>. If he spends a Willpower, he matches Octavian exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-21-2019, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T10:37:35-08:00","id":1350048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1350043#post1350043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Combat? Its more like... is Defensive presence overpowered?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have trouble parsing this, I'm not sure what you're saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1350043#post1350043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Excellent shield prana... I wanted double 8s. Permanent appears to be too overpowered. How about a willpower cost, it lasts for 1 day, and it can only be used once a week.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say 3wp once a week. Or as an alternative, remove the cost but at the end of the day the spirit disappears for a week as though it had been slain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T11:55:30-08:00","id":1350867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1350048#post1350048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have trouble parsing this, I'm not sure what you're saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Defensive shield. Full cover to matter what. Doesn't that make you immune to ranged attacks? Or at least so I read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T12:34:35-08:00","id":1350881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1350867#post1350867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combat? Its more like... is Defensive presence overpowered?<br /> <br /> Defensive shield. Full cover to matter what. Doesn't that make you immune to ranged attacks? Or at least so I read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Yeah it does make you immune. I don't think it's overpowered in itself no.<br /> <br /> But part of the merit's balance is that it limits the character's movement speed, so I'm wondering what the exact effect is when the character is in combat.<br /> <br /> Movement in combat is measured in range bands, so &quot;walking speed&quot; isn't enough information. Would it take 2 turns to move 1 range band or something similar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T12:57:21-08:00","id":1350892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1350881#post1350881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh! Yeah it does make you immune. I don't think it's overpowered in itself no.<br /> <br /> But part of the merit's balance is that it limits the character's movement speed, so I'm wondering what the exact effect is when the character is in combat.<br /> <br /> Movement in combat is measured in range bands, so &amp;quot;walking speed&amp;quot; isn't enough information. Would it take 2 turns to move 1 range band or something similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't quite see that part, so.... You know that leisurely pace? Yeah, that. I guess 1 range band a turn? <br /> <br /> What's the normal movement speed anyway? Are there 'dash' and 'movement' separation? I didn't quite get that part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T14:04:20-08:00","id":1350906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1350892#post1350892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't quite see that part, so.... You know that leisurely pace? Yeah, that. I guess 1 range band a turn?<br /> <br /> What's the normal movement speed anyway? Are there 'dash' and 'movement' separation? I didn't quite get that part.</div> </div> </div> </div>The normal speed is 1 range band per turn (a few seconds of sprinting), so a good penalty for walking speed could be moving only 1/2 range band.<br /> <br /> There is no dash mechanic, only special actions to catch up to an enemy (Rush) or to escape from them (Disengage). Arguably those 2 actions would both be unavailable while walking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T20:49:32-08:00","id":1350963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1350906#post1350906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The normal speed is 1 range band per turn (a few seconds of sprinting), so a good penalty for walking speed could be moving only 1/2 range band.<br /> <br /> There is no dash mechanic, only special actions to catch up to an enemy (Rush) or to escape from them (Disengage). Arguably those 2 actions would both be unavailable while walking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... Yes. No rush actions. The thought here is bascially:<br /> <br /> &quot;Here I am, standing in the open, gathering power. While you pound away at me with your ballista, bullets, arrows, grenades, and missiles, I gather power. So charge at me now, and die under the fists of my servant, or get out do the way.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T20:56:35-08:00","id":1350964,"title":"","content":"SPRING OF THE ETERNAL MOTHER<br /> <br /> Celestial 1/ 2<br /> <br /> A spring created by a lunar after her people was devastated by a plague much like the black death. The spring forms from a vase held by a statue of the goddess of fertility and motherhood. <br /> <br /> As long as a mother drinks the water before childbirth, she gains the following benefits:<br /> <br /> No birth complications. No childbed fever. No breech birth. No birth defects. No prematures. <br /> Strengthened children. Children have increased resistance to disease and damage, equal to adults, up until the age of 13<br /> Birth is painless and lasts for an hour<br /> Post partum recovery lasts for 8 hours. <br /> If the water is taken early enough, pregnancy lasts for 6 months instead of 9.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T11:20:52-08:00","id":1351325,"title":"","content":"THE WALKING FORTRESS<br /> Celestial 2<br /> <br /> Extending out to medium range to protect the beneficiary and his allies, an invisible Sphere of energy surrounds the sorcerer, spinning and turning. He and all within medium range are considered to be beneath full cover. In melee combat, the sorcerer alone is considered to be in artifact heavy armour. This does not stack.<br /> <br /> BELL OF TRUTH<br /> Celestial 1<br /> <br /> A simple bell with a button on top, this small piece of equipment rings whenever a lie is audibly produced in its presence. Whether from recordings or by scrying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T05:08:37-08:00","id":1351453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1350964#post1350964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SPRING OF THE ETERNAL MOTHER<br /> <br /> Celestial 1/ 2<br /> <br /> A spring created by a lunar after her people was devastated by a plague much like the black death. The spring forms from a vase held by a statue of the goddess of fertility and motherhood. <br /> <br /> As long as a mother drinks the water before childbirth, she gains the following benefits:<br /> <br /> No birth complications. No childbed fever. No breech birth. No birth defects. No prematures. <br /> Strengthened children. Children have increased resistance to disease and damage, equal to adults, up until the age of 13<br /> Birth is painless and lasts for an hour<br /> Post partum recovery lasts for 8 hours. <br /> If the water is taken early enough, pregnancy lasts for 6 months instead of 9.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything apart from cutting the term to 6 months is a solid Celestial 1.<br /> <br /> What's the intent behind cutting the term? I can't parse that, but it's definitely well above Celestial 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T05:15:18-08:00","id":1351454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1351325#post1351325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THE WALKING FORTRESS<br /> Celestial 2<br /> <br /> Extending out to medium range to protect the beneficiary and his allies, an invisible Sphere of energy surrounds the sorcerer, spinning and turning. He and all within medium range are considered to be beneath full cover. In melee combat, the sorcerer alone is considered to be in artifact heavy armour. This does not stack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is appropriate for a working. Looking at the examples, I feel like this is WAAAY above having a hypnotic gaze, and slightly above returning someone to the prime of youth. Solar 2: Remake a magical being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BELL OF TRUTH<br /> Celestial 1<br /> <br /> A simple bell with a button on top, this small piece of equipment rings whenever a lie is audibly produced in its presence. Whether from recordings or by scrying. </div> </div> </div>Celestial 1 is fine. I'd consider Terrestrial 3, but Celestial 1 is probably right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T06:09:57-08:00","id":1351459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1351453#post1351453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything apart from cutting the term to 6 months is a solid Celestial 1.<br /> <br /> What's the intent behind cutting the term? I can't parse that, but it's definitely well above Celestial 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember how pregnancy lasts 9 months? <br /> <br /> Now it's shorter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T06:10:29-08:00","id":1351460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1351454#post1351454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this is appropriate for a working. Looking at the examples, I feel like this is WAAAY above having a hypnotic gaze, and slightly above returning someone to the prime of youth. Solar 2: Remake a magical being.<br /> <br /> <br /> Celestial 1 is fine. I'd consider Terrestrial 3, but Celestial 1 is probably right.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes it solar instead of celestial? Was it the armour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T06:26:17-08:00","id":1351462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1351325#post1351325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THE WALKING FORTRESS<br /> Celestial 2<br /> <br /> Extending out to medium range to protect the beneficiary and his allies, an invisible Sphere of energy surrounds the sorcerer, spinning and turning. He and all within medium range are considered to be beneath full cover. In melee combat, the sorcerer alone is considered to be in artifact heavy armour. This does not stack.<br /> <br /> BELL OF TRUTH<br /> Celestial 1<br /> <br /> A simple bell with a button on top, this small piece of equipment rings whenever a lie is audibly produced in its presence. Whether from recordings or by scrying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Walking Fortress seems like a circle spell more than a working of any kind. Maybe Celestial but not a built in power of any kind. Bell of Truth could be a minor artifact if it only rings when other people lie. <br /> <br /> For the spring of mom's, I'd require the childbirth reduction to have both parents drink from it before copulation in a ritual for that part to take effect and call it Celestial 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T07:04:46-08:00","id":1351469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1351462#post1351462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the spring of mom's, I'd require the childbirth reduction to have both parents drink from it before copulation in a ritual for that part to take effect and call it Celestial 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. Why? Medicine for ensuring a safe and good pregnancy has been around for ages in both history and myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T09:26:40-08:00","id":1351493,"title":"","content":"safe but not fast. having kids in 1/3 less time than normal is a powerful magical ability that dragonblooded would kill to create. Even more so if it is a quick sip from a spring for 1 parent. What happens if animals drink from it? Adding in a ritual component helps removes these issues. Just my thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T09:47:14-08:00","id":1351496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1351493#post1351493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">safe but not fast. having kids in 1/3 less time than normal is a powerful magical ability that dragonblooded would kill to create. Even more so if it is a quick sip from a spring for 1 parent. What happens if animals drink from it? Adding in a ritual component helps removes these issues. Just my thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>*raises eyebrow*<br /> <br /> Huh? <br /> <br /> No it isn't. Not compared to other things. Hell, you can't even use it to breathe fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T12:14:20-08:00","id":1351521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1351459#post1351459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember how pregnancy lasts 9 months? <br /> <br /> Now it's shorter.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why?<br /> <br /> I get &quot;what&quot;. &quot;How&quot; is &quot;magic&quot;. Why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T12:26:19-08:00","id":1351524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1351460#post1351460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What makes it solar instead of celestial? Was it the armour?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's the armor.<br /> <br /> Celestial Spell: Incompatable Body Arsenal<br /> <br /> Provides artifact armor for Essence hours and can be Disrupted.<br /> <br /> Your working: Artifact armor, permanently, with full cover for all your allies, permanently, which can't be disrupted, with no mote commitment.<br /> <br /> I'd be disinclined to allow it as a working, period. But the step up between this and Incomparable Body Arsenal is about the same as IBA and Invulnerable Skin of Bronze.<br /> <br /> Put a time limitation on it and it might serve as a Celestial spell. Put a usage limitation (like it only activates whilst you're taking Shape Sorcery actions) and it might do for a Celestial Working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T19:34:32-08:00","id":1351572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1351524#post1351524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's the armor.<br /> <br /> Celestial Spell: Incompatable Body Arsenal<br /> <br /> Provides artifact armor for Essence hours and can be Disrupted.<br /> <br /> Your working: Artifact armor, permanently, with full cover for all your allies, permanently, which can't be disrupted, with no mote commitment.<br /> <br /> I'd be disinclined to allow it as a working, period. But the step up between this and Incomparable Body Arsenal is about the same as IBA and Invulnerable Skin of Bronze.<br /> <br /> Put a time limitation on it and it might serve as a Celestial spell. Put a usage limitation (like it only activates whilst you're taking Shape Sorcery actions) and it might do for a Celestial Working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scene length body armour activated reflexively? What about simply a permanent &quot;Incomparable Body arsenal'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T10:59:01-08:00","id":1352034,"title":"","content":"Creation of Natural Resource (Celestial 1)<br /> <br /> The sorcerer takes an example of the resource he wishes, implants it within the earth, and buries with it a horn of plenty, meanwhile speaking the invocations of autochthon and of the gods of prosperity. The earth erupts and transforms, the inner earth giving up whatever they need. This creates a natural source of the resources that was buried, ranging from an oil field, to a vein of iron, to a diamond mine.<br /> <br /> Upgrading this to Celestial 2, will render the resource inexhaustible. Oil wells refill themselves. Veins of metal grow back after mining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 12-01-2019, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T17:31:09-08:00","id":1352080,"title":"","content":"Creation of Natural Resource seems like a Celestial circle spell, most likely keyword: Ritual. Something like &quot;Produces (Essence) Resource value of the copied material per week for 1 year. If unmined the material will grow into easy to mine veins in the earth, or near surface pools of easy to reach liquids. If this is your control spell extend the duration to indefinite if you commit 1 WP when casting. Such wells or mines also produce twice as much material per week.&quot; Yes this would allow production of unlimited silver coin or gold, or vast salt mines or really anything. You can always recast. The Celestial 2 version seems more like a good working. Making a single ever restoring mundane resource seems right on at Celestial 2 and cost slightly more than learning the celestial circle spell but have the upside of no waiting and unlimited value even if it might be ever decreasing if you keep selling it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T10:28:37-08:00","id":1352180,"title":"","content":"Cynis Ganan, an Earth Aspect DB whose control spell is Invulnerable Skin of Bronze, wants to perform a Working to make himself tougher.<br /> <br /> I, the player, think that a cool way of doing this would be to suffuse his aspect markings with Essence, giving him a stony mantle. Mechanically, this might be achieved as a mutation: Unusual Hide, to grant &quot;a body of living stone&quot;. As he's already an Earth Aspect Dragon-Blooded, what I want is to attach the Subtlety mutation to the Working so that it's not immediately obvious that he's anything but a normal Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Can this be done as a single Terrestrial Working, Ambition 2, &quot;Grant mutation<b>s</b> to oneself&quot; (emphasis added)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T11:30:08-08:00","id":1352186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352180#post1352180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cynis Ganan, an Earth Aspect DB whose control spell is Invulnerable Skin of Bronze, wants to perform a Working to make himself tougher.<br /> <br /> I, the player, think that a cool way of doing this would be to suffuse his aspect markings with Essence, giving him a stony mantle. Mechanically, this might be achieved as a mutation: Unusual Hide, to grant &quot;a body of living stone&quot;. As he's already an Earth Aspect Dragon-Blooded, what I want is to attach the Subtlety mutation to the Working so that it's not immediately obvious that he's anything but a normal Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Can this be done as a single Terrestrial Working, Ambition 2, &quot;Grant mutation<b>s</b> to oneself&quot; (emphasis added)?</div> </div> </div> </div>My ruling would depend on how you're meaning &quot;not immediately obvious&quot;. The Subtlety merit specifies that it makes the attached merit &quot;non-obvious to observers <i>when not in use</i>&quot; (emphasis mine). So, what counts as &quot;in use&quot; for armor? I'd argue that if the armor is capable of protecting you, it's &quot;in use&quot;. Therefore, Subtlety combined with Unusual Hide would mean you could <i>produce</i> armor quickly, but that would take an action. If you want its benefit to apply against attacks you didn't have time to prep for, you'd have to have it visible. In combat, I'd rule that it takes a Draw/Ready Weapon action to &quot;don&quot;, essentially. <br /> <br /> If you want the Unusual Hide to be constantly there, but only <i>visible</i> once it stops an attack, I'd probably let you slide with a Terrestrial 3 working, on the grounds that this is effectively &quot;a minor supernatural power that augments [your] strongest traits&quot;. I don't think just the equivalent of a mutation is powerful enough to count for the full-blown &quot;Grant a supernatural power&quot; of Celestial 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T11:35:41-08:00","id":1352188,"title":"","content":"I think I would limit a single Ambition 2 working to 5 dots of mutations, which may cover one or multiple mutations. So a single working could only give you Unusual Hide 3 with Subtlety, not Unusual Hide 4 or 5. For 6-10 dots of mutations I'd ask for Ambition 3 instead.<br /> <br /> That said it's mostly a matter of principle, 1 or 2 extra dots of mutation certainly isn't gonna break the game if it's allowed or anything.<br /> <br /> Edit : alternatively, it could be done at Ambition 2 with Finesse<br /> Finesse 1 : you get Unusual Hide 3, Subtlety (the general idea of what you asked for, but not stone)<br /> Finesse 3 : You get Unusual Hide 4, Subtlety (body of living stone, but not as strong as it could be)<br /> Finesse 5 : You get Unusual Hide 5, Subtlety (exactly what you asked for)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 12-02-2019, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T11:49:33-08:00","id":1352190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352186#post1352186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My ruling would depend on how you're meaning &amp;quot;not immediately obvious&amp;quot;. The Subtlety merit specifies that it makes the attached merit &amp;quot;non-obvious to observers <i>when not in use</i>&amp;quot; (emphasis mine). So, what counts as &amp;quot;in use&amp;quot; for armor? I'd argue that if the armor is capable of protecting you, it's &amp;quot;in use&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>See I was thinking it looks like rocky, earthen skin, always. But he's a Dragon-Blooded so who cares? But when you punch him, you can immediately tell he's basically made of rock. Hit him with a sword and you don't cut him, so much as chip off chunks of rock.<br /> <br /> But I see your point of view and value your input.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352188#post1352188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I would limit a single Ambition 2 working to 5 dots of mutations, which may cover one or multiple mutations. So a single working could only give you Unusual Hide 3 with Subtlety, not Unusual Hide 4 or 5. For 6-10 dots of mutations I'd ask for Ambition 3 instead.<br /> <br /> That said it's mostly a matter of principle, 1 or 2 extra dots of mutation certainly isn't gonna break the game if it's allowed or anything.<br /> <br /> Edit : alternatively, it could be done at Ambition 2 with Finesse<br /> Finesse 1 : you get Unusual Hide 3, Subtlety (the general idea of what you asked for, but not stone)<br /> Finesse 3 : You get Unusual Hide 4, Subtlety (body of living stone, but not as strong as it could be)<br /> Finesse 5 : You get Unusual Hide 5, Subtlety (exactly what you asked for)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was working on Finesse 5, but I wasn't sure if I'm being too &quot;game-y&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T12:36:09-08:00","id":1352200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352190#post1352190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See I was thinking it looks like rocky, earthen skin, always. But he's a Dragon-Blooded so who cares? But when you punch him, you can immediately tell he's basically made of rock. Hit him with a sword and you don't cut him, so much as chip off chunks of rock.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that's beyond the intent of Subtlety, yeah. If you can be ambushed and still have the mutation's benefit, I don't think Subtlety as written covers it. I <i>could</i> see a different interpretation of Subtlety, where it conceals the mutation from casual inspection, but any degree of scrutiny would pick it out. So, someone who was just casually walking by might think &quot;oh, a Dragonblood with unusually prominent aspect markings&quot;, but any serious attacker who took a moment to roll (Perception + Investigate) would probably think &quot;no, those are <i>way</i> too strong to be just aspect markings. He's gotta have some kind of armor&quot;. <br /> <br /> But as you've described it, I'd rule Terrestrial 3, for the reasons I previously explained.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352188#post1352188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I would limit a single Ambition 2 working to 5 dots of mutations, which may cover one or multiple mutations. So a single working could only give you Unusual Hide 3 with Subtlety, not Unusual Hide 4 or 5. For 6-10 dots of mutations I'd ask for Ambition 3 instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than a strict dot limit on mutations, I think I'd prefer to have Terrestrial 2 only grant a single themed &quot;package&quot; of mutations at once. So if you wanted to make a manticore (here defined as a creature with a tiger's body, scorpion tail, bat wings, and a human face with an unnaturally beautiful piping voice), I'd have you start with a tiger, and then do three Terrestrial 2 workings, one to add Wings, one to add the 4-dot version of Claws/Fangs/Hooves/Horns, Deadly Weaponry (from Lunars), and Venomous, representing the scorpion tail, and finally one to add the human face and voice. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit : alternatively, it could be done at Ambition 2 with Finesse<br /> Finesse 1 : you get Unusual Hide 3, Subtlety (the general idea of what you asked for, but not stone)<br /> Finesse 3 : You get Unusual Hide 4, Subtlety (body of living stone, but not as strong as it could be)<br /> Finesse 5 : You get Unusual Hide 5, Subtlety (exactly what you asked for)</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, I think adding power with Finesse is a bad idea. If a working is balanced at a given Ambition, it's balanced no matter what Finesse you use, and if it's not, it should be a higher Ambition, not a higher Finesse. Low Finesse workings should have narratively interesting complications involved, but the real difference between Finesse 1 and Finesse 5 is not that Finesse 5 has no complications, it's that the complications are chosen entirely by the player at Finesse 5, and entirely by the ST at Finesse 1. For something like this, where I feel the base effect (Unusual Hide + Subtlety) is balanced at Terrestrial 2 (as long as Subtlety is being interpreted as in the book), I wouldn't have many complications at all. Low Finesse would probably mean somewhat unusual conditions for the process of performing the working, instead. <br /> <br /> If you think that Unusual Hide 5 + Subtlety isn't balanced on its own at Terrestrial 2, I'd suggest instead telling the player that they can have it, but it needs to come with some kind of drawback or flaw. Finesse 1 would then mean that you, the ST, gets to pick the flaw, whereas Finesse 5 would mean they get to pick it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T22:49:41-08:00","id":1352282,"title":"","content":"A thing I've been wondering.<br /> <br /> A high speed maneuverable vehicle. One moving as fast as Stormwind Rider or Azure Chariot. Large enough to hold an apocethary office or something and several beds. Like a medivac, without the healing laser.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial, or celestial? Because apparently creating a millstone that creates grain out of sand is terrestrial. And that really confuses me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T00:14:47-08:00","id":1352289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352282#post1352282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing I've been wondering.<br /> <br /> A high speed maneuverable vehicle. One moving as fast as Stormwind Rider or Azure Chariot. Large enough to hold an apocethary office or something and several beds. Like a medivac, without the healing laser.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial, or celestial? Because apparently creating a millstone that creates grain out of sand is terrestrial. And that really confuses me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this is more of an Artifact than a Working.<br /> <br /> Cloud Trapeze is a Celestial Spell that makes a vehicle approximately this size. But it's much slower than what you want. But it can fly.<br /> <br /> A building with limited mobility is Celestial 3. A flying city is Solar 2. A fast moving doctor's office with beds, I put at Solar 1.<br /> <br /> And if you want to argue that you're not enchanting a building but making a vehicle, then I point you at the rules for making magical things (Superior Craft projects, page 241).<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> As an aside, Jefepato said Celestial 1 for grinding sand into flour, Alistair said Terrestrial 3. I said it was pretty much on the boarder and either could be appropriate (admittedly, I'd lean towards &quot;this is something a mortal sorcerer should be able to do&quot;). But we all thought that idea was better as an Artifact.<br /> <br /> A Working is a magical spell which does something.<br /> An Artifact is a magical item which does something.<br /> <br /> I strongly believe that this is the distinction which is causing your confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-03-2019, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T00:23:33-08:00","id":1352292,"title":"","content":"Fast moving doctors office?<br /> <br /> See. This is the thing. I wanted a vehicle the size of roughly.... Twenty meters by ten meters. Capable of lifting a ton and moving 200 miles per hour. <br /> <br /> Is that really solar 1?<br /> <br /> Edit: but Nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T00:38:34-08:00","id":1352293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352292#post1352292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fast moving doctors office?<br /> <br /> See. This is the thing. I wanted a vehicle the size of roughly.... Twenty meters by ten meters. Capable of lifting a ton and moving 200 miles per hour. <br /> <br /> Is that really solar 1?<br /> <br /> Edit: but Nevermind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered just casting Cloud Trapeze? Indefinite duration. Carry tons of cargo. Lay out all your beds and stuff and whip cloud stuff around them. It only goes at ~30mph, but it's Indefinite duration and flys.<br /> <br /> You want something roughly the size of six school buses strapped side by side which travel at 200mph?<br /> <br /> That really sounds like a moving building more than a vehicle to me.<br /> <br /> Did you want it to fly? Because it's not going to fit on a road.<br /> <br /> As previously discussed, I'm not an authority. My opinion is just my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T00:44:51-08:00","id":1352295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352292#post1352292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See. This is the thing. I wanted a vehicle the size of roughly.... Twenty meters by ten meters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's huge for a vehicle. That's only <i>slightly</i> smaller than the average American household.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352292#post1352292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Capable of lifting a ton and moving 200 miles per hour.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's twice as fast as a Stormwind Rider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352292#post1352292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that really solar 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like John was closer in suggesting it be a work of artifice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352292#post1352292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: but Nevermind.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <i>okay</i> if we give push-back on an idea, that doesn't mean it's necessarily a bad idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T01:00:56-08:00","id":1352302,"title":"","content":"I think Acc was using &quot;medivac&quot; to mean Cargo Lifter -- like a C-17 Globemaster III, which is twice the size, carries ten times the cargo and travels three times the speed of what he wants. (Or like, you know, the StarCraft unit.)<br /> <br /> (&quot;So I said, 'if you've got a ship that can carry a tank, why not put guns on the ship and use it instead?'&quot;)<br /> <br /> So if the question is &quot;what Working to I need to summon a modern day $200000000 cargo plane&quot;, then I'm sticking with Solar 1.<br /> <br /> It should be absolutely possible to do this. Wyld Shaping. Sorcery. Buying a Boeing factory. All valid ways of doing it. I'd build it as an Artifact. But, again, I stress that my opinion is just my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T06:35:50-08:00","id":1352349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352186#post1352186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My ruling would depend on how you're meaning &amp;quot;not immediately obvious&amp;quot;. The Subtlety merit specifies that it makes the attached merit &amp;quot;non-obvious to observers <i>when not in use</i>&amp;quot; (emphasis mine). So, what counts as &amp;quot;in use&amp;quot; for armor? I'd argue that if the armor is capable of protecting you, it's &amp;quot;in use&amp;quot;. Therefore, Subtlety combined with Unusual Hide would mean you could <i>produce</i> armor quickly, but that would take an action. If you want its benefit to apply against attacks you didn't have time to prep for, you'd have to have it visible. In combat, I'd rule that it takes a Draw/Ready Weapon action to &amp;quot;don&amp;quot;, essentially. <br /> <br /> If you want the Unusual Hide to be constantly there, but only <i>visible</i> once it stops an attack, I'd probably let you slide with a Terrestrial 3 working, on the grounds that this is effectively &amp;quot;a minor supernatural power that augments [your] strongest traits&amp;quot;. I don't think just the equivalent of a mutation is powerful enough to count for the full-blown &amp;quot;Grant a supernatural power&amp;quot; of Celestial 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I really like the idea of &quot;sweating&quot; out a rocky armor. But I think I've got a refinement of the idea.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial 3 - a minor supernatural power that augments [your] strongest trait<br /> <br /> How about having the Bonfire Earth Anima power kick in at Glowing (and Burning)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T21:48:08-08:00","id":1352518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352282#post1352282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing I've been wondering.<br /> <br /> A high speed maneuverable vehicle. One moving as fast as Stormwind Rider or Azure Chariot. Large enough to hold an apocethary office or something and several beds. Like a medivac, without the healing laser.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial, or celestial? Because apparently creating a millstone that creates grain out of sand is terrestrial. And that really confuses me.</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have said, a vehicle sounds more like an artifact than a working.<br /> <br /> That said, if you wanted something like a spirit whose main functions are 1) carrying your office and 2) traveling very fast, I might argue that Celestial 3 is suitable. I could see a Second Circle demon doing that if those were its main areas of expertise.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be good for much else, though. Moving a <i>lot</i> of stuff <i>very fast</i> is a very useful trick in the Age of Sorrows, and one that few people can duplicate, so your spirit would be very much a specialist.<br /> <br /> (All that said, I understand why people often come up with working ideas that make more sense as artifacts. I've often been guilty of the same myself. The working rules are way less of a pain than the artifact crafting rules, and definitely require less Charm investment...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T12:58:31-08:00","id":1352860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352293#post1352293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you considered just casting Cloud Trapeze? Indefinite duration. Carry tons of cargo. Lay out all your beds and stuff and whip cloud stuff around them. It only goes at ~30mph, but it's Indefinite duration and flys.<br /> <br /> <br /> As previously discussed, I'm not an authority. My opinion is just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really indefinite duration since, if i remember correctly, it requires concentration..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 12-05-2019, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T13:20:26-08:00","id":1352864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352860#post1352860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not really indefinite duration since, if i remember correctly, it requires concentration..</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The sorcerer must remain aboard the trapeze to direct its course, though she need not constantly <br /> focus on piloting it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T15:27:13-08:00","id":1352880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352864#post1352864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;The sorcerer must remain aboard the trapeze to direct its course, though she need not constantly<br /> focus on piloting it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Need not <i><b>Constantly </b></i>focus does not mean <i><b>Never </b></i>focus... <br /> <br /> Additionally, is this spell updated to 3rd Edition, maybe in the Lunar's Book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T16:42:00-08:00","id":1352894,"title":"","content":"Celestial 2/3<br /> <br /> The garden of learning. <br /> <br /> A garden the size of a small park, filled with flowers and a unique species of butterfly and bird. No other living creature lives within the garden. A thousand blossoms exist within the garden, all with a unique shape and scent. <br /> <br /> The garden is a teacher, a source of knowledge for any known subject in Creation. A sorcerer may discover the secrets of a spell in the movement patterns of the butterflies as they flit past. A warrior may devise a new style as he observes the petals fall to the ground. The scent of the flowers may bring visions of places to explore, and the taste of its fruits may inspire musicians to greater heights.<br /> <br /> The garden itself is considered to be a tutor in all known subjects, and halves the time needed to learn any subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 12-05-2019, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T17:20:57-08:00","id":1352902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352894#post1352894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial 2/3<br /> <br /> The garden of learning.<br /> <br /> A garden the size of a small park, filled with flowers and a unique species of butterfly and bird. No other living creature lives within the garden. A thousand blossoms exist within the garden, all with a unique shape and scent.<br /> <br /> The garden is a teacher, a source of knowledge for any known subject in Creation. A sage may discover the secrets of sorcery in the movement patterns of the butterflies as they flit past. A warrior may devise a new style as he observes the petals fall to the ground. The scent of the flowers may bring visions of places to explore, and the taste of its fruits may inspire musicians to greater heights.<br /> <br /> The garden itself is considered to be a tutor in all known subjects, and halves the time needed to learn any subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kinda torn here. While it's not that powerful in game-mechanical terms (I don't consider training time all that big a deal anyway), it essentially makes libraries obsolete. For that matter, schools and tutors would only serve any purpose for kids who won't learn without adults keeping them on task.<br /> <br /> I'd say Celestial 3. I can't justify going any higher without it doing more to directly affect the game, but the effect on the society around it would be <i>huge</i>. I'm probably not even thinking of half the ways it would change things.<br /> <br /> ...How many Means does it count for, if you hang around in the garden while you do your next sorcerous working?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T17:38:15-08:00","id":1352908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352902#post1352902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...How many Means does it count for, if you hang around in the garden while you do your next sorcerous working?</div> </div> </div> </div>One? Surely not more than an actual laboratory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:00:58-08:00","id":1352913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352902#post1352902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm kinda torn here. While it's not that powerful in game-mechanical terms (I don't consider training time all that big a deal anyway), it essentially makes libraries obsolete. For that matter, schools and tutors would only serve any purpose for kids who won't learn without adults keeping them on task.<br /> <br /> I'd say Celestial 3. I can't justify going any higher without it doing more to directly affect the game, but the effect on the society around it would be <i>huge</i>. I'm probably not even thinking of half the ways it would change things.<br /> <br /> ...How many Means does it count for, if you hang around in the garden while you do your next sorcerous working?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude. Celestial 2 let's you make a spring that gives anyone who drinks from it exalted level healing. Celestial 2 let's you rearrange the weather of a region. Permanently. Celestial 3 lets you create something like octavian. <br /> <br /> Yes, it makes libraries obsolete. That's what celestial level magic is supposed to be able to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:04:56-08:00","id":1352915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352913#post1352913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude. Celestial 2 let's you make a spring that gives anyone who drinks from it exalted level healing. Celestial 2 let's you rearrange the weather of a region. Permanently. Celestial 3 lets you create something like octavian.<br /> <br /> Yes, it makes libraries obsolete. That's what celestial level magic is supposed to be able to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also trains sorcerers, which is a lot bigger deal than giving people Exalted Healing. <br /> If it does so but only for those chosen few, C3. Training sorcerers is a <i>big deal</i>. <br /> If it lets anyone become a sorcerer, N/A.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:06:48-08:00","id":1352917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352915#post1352915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also trains sorcerers, which is a lot bigger deal than giving people Exalted Healing. <br /> If it does so but only for those chosen few, C3. Training sorcerers is a <i>big deal</i>. <br /> If it lets anyone become a sorcerer, N/A.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerers? It can train occult and intelligence, yes. But sorcerers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:11:04-08:00","id":1352918,"title":"","content":"You were the one who said it could let \u201ca sage discover the secrets of sorcery.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:12:18-08:00","id":1352919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352918#post1352918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You were the one who said it could let \u201ca sage discover the secrets of sorcery.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine. Changing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:16:37-08:00","id":1352923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352917#post1352917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorcerers? It can train occult and intelligence, yes. But sorcerers?</div> </div> </div> </div>You said &quot;A sage may discover the secrets of sorcery in the movement patterns of the butterflies as they flit past.&quot;. It <i>explicitly</i> trains sorcerers. <br /> If it were strictly for Ability and Attribute training, then it'd be T2. But not if it trains sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:18:44-08:00","id":1352925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352923#post1352923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You said &amp;quot;A sage may discover the secrets of sorcery in the movement patterns of the butterflies as they flit past.&amp;quot;. It <i>explicitly</i> trains sorcerers. <br /> If it were strictly for Ability and Attribute training, then it'd be T2. But not if it trains sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop. <br /> <br /> A garden that trains your attributes and abilities is considered terrestrial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:32:45-08:00","id":1352929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352925#post1352925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stop.<br /> <br /> A garden that trains your attributes and abilities is considered terrestrial?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's how I'd call it. It seems like a cross between T1's &quot;Create or bind magical entities capable of performing mundane, household chores, but not much else, in service to a person, organization, or structure. &quot; and T2's &quot;Instill a plant, animal, or object with human-level intelligence.&quot;.<br /> It doesn't give out dots, it doesn't give out XP, it doesn't help with charms or sorcery or anything supernatural. All it really does is reduce training times for the really boring stuff. And that's pretty trivial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:35:50-08:00","id":1352930,"title":"","content":"Huh. Reduce training times and act as a tutor. En masse. That's low?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:55:50-08:00","id":1352935,"title":"","content":"I disagree that it\u2019d bump it all the way down to <i>Terrestrial</i>, but it\u2019s definitely lower if it can\u2019t speed up how quickly you can develop magical traits like sorcery or Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T19:13:50-08:00","id":1352936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352935#post1352935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree that it\u2019d bump it all the way down to <i>Terrestrial</i>, but it\u2019s definitely lower if it can\u2019t speed up how quickly you can develop magical traits like sorcery or Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Just... Any dot. Any subject. It's basically a perfect university. In the form of a garden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T19:29:12-08:00","id":1352937,"title":"","content":"Any subject? Including Lore topics?<br /> <br /> The history of Chiaroscuro?<br /> Incunabulum of Nexus?<br /> The nature of Underworld Essence?<br /> Bird species native to Whitewall?<br /> Art history?<br /> Imperial City genealogy?<br /> <br /> What topics will a character with three dots of Lore possess if he\u2019s educated in your garden?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T19:31:50-08:00","id":1352938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352937#post1352937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any subject? Including Lore topics?<br /> <br /> The history of Chiaroscuro?<br /> Incunabulum of Nexus?<br /> The nature of Underworld Essence?<br /> Bird species native to Whitewall?<br /> Art history?<br /> Imperial City genealogy?<br /> <br /> What topics will a character with three dots of Lore possess if he\u2019s educated in your garden?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it something hidden on purpose? <br /> <br /> No? <br /> <br /> Then you can learn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T22:06:14-08:00","id":1352949,"title":"","content":"Just curious. Have you read about Lore topics in third edition?<br /> <br /> Basically, when you build a character with Lore dots in 3E, you decide what their background is, and they can only make Lore rolls related to subjects reasonably related to that background. A character who studied philosophy in Chiaroscuro won\u2019t know anything about the First Age or how to read a Realm Dynast\u2019s family tree; likewise, an herbalist in Great Forks won\u2019t know about the null hypothesis or the melting temperature of aluminum.<br /> <br /> Do you see why saying, \u201cYour Lore background can be, \u2018everything that\u2019s not actively kept a secret,\u2019\u201d might not jibe with that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-06-2019, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T01:43:26-08:00","id":1352968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352949#post1352949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious. Have you read about Lore topics in third edition?<br /> <br /> Basically, when you build a character with Lore dots in 3E, you decide what their background is, and they can only make Lore rolls related to subjects reasonably related to that background. A character who studied philosophy in Chiaroscuro won\u2019t know anything about the First Age or how to read a Realm Dynast\u2019s family tree; likewise, an herbalist in Great Forks won\u2019t know about the null hypothesis or the melting temperature of aluminum.<br /> <br /> Do you see why saying, \u201cYour Lore background can be, \u2018everything that\u2019s not actively kept a secret,\u2019\u201d might not jibe with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... Yes? <br /> <br /> They can learn all that. Yes, the background doesn't make sense. Do they want to learn it? They can.<br /> <br /> They can't do shit like learn the locations of secret military bases, but they can learn realm history as if they were sitting within a Blessed Isle classroom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T01:52:28-08:00","id":1352970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352968#post1352968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um... Yes?<br /> <br /> They can learn all that. Yes, the background doesn't make sense. Do they want to learn it? They can.<br /> <br /> They can't do shit like learn the locations of secret military bases, but they can learn realm history as if they were sitting within a Blessed Isle classroom.</div> </div> </div> </div>My objection is that <i>can</i> learn and <i>did</i> learn are very different things. I went to a major agriculture university! That means I know lots of stuff about plants and animals and growing food, right? Wrong, because that wasn't my major. I <i>could</i> have learned agri stuff, but I <i>didn't</i> learn agri stuff. <br /> <br /> The garden <i>can</i> teach a bunch of things. But as I read the working it doesn't teach <i>everything at once</i>. If it does teach everything at once, then the working needs to be reassessed again. <br /> <br /> And this is why I always start conversations about workings with <b>intent</b>. Because &quot;garden that teaches people&quot; sounds like a means to an end rather than an end in and of itself. And without knowing that desired end, all we can really do is blindly guess what the actual effect of the working is. <br /> Trying to shave a month off your Solar XP spending? Trying to make an entire backwater village into professional scribes? Eh, no biggie. <br /> Trying to have a legion of scholar-bodyguards who know everything taught in any school anywhere? Pretty big deal even if you're providing the people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T07:54:28-08:00","id":1353020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352949#post1352949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious. Have you read about Lore topics in third edition?<br /> <br /> Basically, when you build a character with Lore dots in 3E, you decide what their background is, and they can only make Lore rolls related to subjects reasonably related to that background. A character who studied philosophy in Chiaroscuro won\u2019t know anything about the First Age or how to read a Realm Dynast\u2019s family tree; likewise, an herbalist in Great Forks won\u2019t know about the null hypothesis or the melting temperature of aluminum.<br /> <br /> Do you see why saying, \u201cYour Lore background can be, \u2018everything that\u2019s not actively kept a secret,\u2019\u201d might not jibe with that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say that that is easily solved, though... For the topics of learning that would fall under Lore, you just use the garden to learn a new specialty... there is in fact a Charm that already allows that. You are not learning everything at once, but a mortal can learn a new specialty and at a far more rapid rate in the Garden (after 1 weeks study time rather than 2). Seems not too horrible.<br /> <br /> I actually kind of like the premise...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T08:15:21-08:00","id":1353022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353020#post1353020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would say that that is easily solved, though... For the topics of learning that would fall under Lore, you just use the garden to learn a new specialty... there is in fact a Charm that already allows that. You are not learning everything at once, but a mortal can learn a new specialty and at a far more rapid rate in the Garden (after 1 weeks study time rather than 2). Seems not too horrible.<br /> <br /> I actually kind of like the premise...</div> </div> </div> </div>The premise is good I think it must be made clear that someone who studied there has a specific field of knowledge. I also think that a place that contains all knowledge available to mankind should be higher than terrestrial but I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T08:58:47-08:00","id":1353027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353022#post1353022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The premise is good I think it must be made clear that someone who studied there has a specific field of knowledge. I also think that a place that contains all knowledge available to mankind should be higher than terrestrial but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if would-be learners are limited to learning topics one at a time (even at an accelerated pace), and there's a reasonable limit on how many people can learn from it at a time, the initial assessment wasn't far from the mark - Celestial 2-3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-06-2019, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T12:06:30-08:00","id":1353080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1352880#post1352880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Need not <i><b>Constantly </b></i>focus does not mean <i><b>Never </b></i>focus... <br /> <br /> Additionally, is this spell updated to 3rd Edition, maybe in the Lunar's Book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quoting the Luna KS manuscript.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T14:50:18-08:00","id":1353155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353080#post1353080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quoting the Luna KS manuscript.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ahhh... Good to know. I do not have any access to that document as of yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T18:31:59-08:00","id":1353195,"title":"","content":"When you think about learning from insects and birds and flowers, I doubt most people would be able to study for extended periods or many subjects. While there isn't a mechanical limit (And based on Finesse maybe one would appear) I figure a normal person could study one or maybe two subjects before needing a break and a chance to test if what the butterflies told them was true. Players are limited by Exp, which basically means they too must go out and put that knowledge to use after learning it. Really cool idea Accelerator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T19:07:23-08:00","id":1353207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353195#post1353195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you think about learning from insects and birds and flowers, I doubt most people would be able to study for extended periods or many subjects. While there isn't a mechanical limit (And based on Finesse maybe one would appear) I figure a normal person could study one or maybe two subjects before needing a break and a chance to test if what the butterflies told them was true. Players are limited by Exp, which basically means they too must go out and put that knowledge to use after learning it. Really cool idea Accelerator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. <br /> <br /> So anyway, the first age! I think there's potential for this.<br /> <br /> I think we should, like, think about making things that aren't magitech. Or at least, obliviate it. We aren't getting stuff like air conditioners in the south. But we do get mass sorcerous workings that alter the weather in a large region, so that in this part of the desert its surprisingly cool and comfortable. Or instead of things like hydroponics gardens or stuff that lets people live in places that are impossible for normal plant life, we get things like trees that create nuts (for a staple crop) that feed on deep underground reservoirs and consume heat as readily as normal plants eat light. Maybe we don't get the equivalent of essence lights... but you can make a tree whose leaves that, when ground into powder and placed into glass vials, would give off suitable light for a month before needing to be replaced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T19:39:04-08:00","id":1353220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353207#post1353207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we should, like, think about making things that aren't magitech.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s what I\u2019ve been doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353207#post1353207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we do get mass sorcerous workings that alter the weather in a large region, so that in this part of the desert its surprisingly cool and comfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. As a reminder, though, not all deserts are going to be hot, and not all hot places are going to be deserts, even in the South of Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353207#post1353207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe we don't get the equivalent of essence lights... but you can make a tree whose leaves that, when ground into powder and placed into glass vials, would give off suitable light for a month before needing to be replaced.</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of my old games, a manse in a town had warped the trees growing around it so their fruits would glow faintly, and if the fruits were eaten, resulted in a temporary numbness in the eater\u2019s mouth.<br /> <br /> Naturally, our characters informed the Guild that there was a potential breakthrough to be had in the field of dentistry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T22:59:56-08:00","id":1353257,"title":"","content":"A thing I've been wondering. Obviously you can make a millstone that turns sand into grain. Or light into grain. Or just pop it out of thin air.<br /> <br /> Does anyone wonder what this would do to a city state or a village? I mean, majority of human existence is predicated on food. Until recently, 90% of humanity were farmers, eking out a living on the hard soil.<br /> <br /> So now you have something that pumps out food like no tomorrow. Doesn't even have the associated problems, like drought, plant disease, or locust attacks.<br /> <br /> How would this even be dealt with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T23:42:44-08:00","id":1353262,"title":"","content":"One millstone can only produce so much flour at a time; it\u2019s not going to replace an entire city\u2019s need for farmers.<br /> <br /> Also, I don\u2019t see anything to indicate that the flour would be immune to locusts or weevils after it\u2019s been produced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T00:26:43-08:00","id":1353272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353262#post1353262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One millstone can only produce so much flour at a time; it\u2019s not going to replace an entire city\u2019s need for farmers.<br /> <br /> Also, I don\u2019t see anything to indicate that the flour would be immune to locusts or weevils after it\u2019s been produced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno. How much do you think is needed, when pouring in sand and dirt, day in, day out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T02:54:48-08:00","id":1353295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353272#post1353272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno. How much do you think is needed, when pouring in sand and dirt, day in, day out?</div> </div> </div> </div>So who is digging the dirt day in, day out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T03:09:22-08:00","id":1353297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353295#post1353295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So who is digging the dirt day in, day out?</div> </div> </div> </div>The peasants. <br /> <br /> Or maybe several dedicated elementals and Stalwart Servitor with a digging spade?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T03:10:24-08:00","id":1353298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353272#post1353272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno. How much do you think is needed, when pouring in sand and dirt, day in, day out?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, cursory Google searches informed me that sizable enough millstones could turn hundreds of pounds of grain into flour in an hour. You could supplement the diets of a community of thousands with a dole of dirt-bread, sure. But people can\u2019t live off of just bread. Other crops are still going to have to be produced. <br /> <br /> (Also, it does mean, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> indicated, you\u2019ve shifted from farming to mining. Hardly makes them safer.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just saw your next post. If you\u2019re just going to enslave spirits to do the manual anyway, why not just have the elementals grow the crops?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-07-2019, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T03:16:17-08:00","id":1353300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353298#post1353298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, it does mean, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> indicated, you\u2019ve shifted from farming to mining. Hardly makes them safer.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that could be a great way for a mining town to get rid of waste and pull double duty on labor.<br /> <br /> Also crops of &quot;dirt&quot; don't fail in a drought or what-have-you.<br /> <br /> But in essence, you shift the peasants from working in the field to working in the pit.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353297#post1353297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe several dedicated elementals and Stalwart Servitor with a digging spade?</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a look at a modern village IRL where most of the labor is done by tractors and combine-harvesters. Look at the professions and quality of life. Something like that I imagine.<br /> <br /> But, also, just get the elementals to grow the rice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T03:24:01-08:00","id":1353302,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't get it. Doesn't rice take at least several months, with possibility of failure due to drought and disease and pests, and takes back braking work and specialized tools and ground to work?<br /> <br /> Being able to produce without any thought to plant growth rate or agriculture much better?<br /> <br /> Besides. What's this about mining? The dangers of mining come from tunnel collapse and fire. That's for getting seams of metal. You can just start on a neighbouring hill or just dig it out of the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T11:48:36-08:00","id":1353593,"title":"","content":"So, here's a classic idea.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer makes a floating island of cloud-stuff. The cloud is large, solid, and sturdy enough to build a castle or mansion on (because this is in fact what the sorcerer intends), and floats around at up to 20 mph as long as the sorcerer is either on board or within line-of-sight to direct it.<br /> <br /> There's no hugely significant reason for this, the sorcerer just thinks it would be awesome and impressive to live in a castle on a cloud. The actual building he wants isn't part of the working -- the sorcerer is going to have to get workers and materials to build it the normal way (probably using Cloud Trapeze to bring them up there).<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Celestial 3? It's fairly grandiose and might have considerable tactical value, but I don't think it operates on the same scale as Solar Circle workings tend to. (Making a city-sized region fly is Solar 2, but a city is a lot bigger than a single large building.)<br /> <br /> Alternative option: the cloud-island has the properties of a demense (presumably Air-aspected), allowing the sorcerer to build a <i>manse</i> on the damned thing. I'm thinking Solar 2, because having a flying manse is kinda crazy (and creating a new demense might actually count as altering the major metaphysical properties of a city-sized region)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T11:52:19-08:00","id":1353595,"title":"","content":"How much to say create a method of sorcerous initiation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:26:37-08:00","id":1353617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353593#post1353593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sorcerer makes a floating island of cloud-stuff. <br /> [snip]<br /> I'm thinking Celestial 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's where I'd peg it - I think it's reasonably equivalent to &quot;Enchant the architecture of an entire structure to grant it limited mobility&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternative option: the cloud-island has the properties of a demense (presumably Air-aspected), allowing the sorcerer to build a <i>manse</i> on the damned thing. I'm thinking Solar 2, because having a flying manse is kinda crazy (and creating a new demense might actually count as altering the major metaphysical properties of a city-sized region)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd put &quot;just create a demesne out of nowhere&quot; as Solar, but I'd put a standard demesne at Solar 1, a greater at Solar 2, and an NA demesne at Solar 3. Just to have some distinction between them. The benefits of doing that through a working as opposed to geomancy would be a) it's probably faster with a working, at least if you've got Solar Circle Sorcery, and b) using geomancy will require changes to the landscape at large, which observers will notice, whereas the working-created one will just be there and much easier to keep secret.<br /> <br /> I think that the default working, however, would produce a demesne of an aspect chosen by the ST. If the sorcerer wanted to specify aspect as well, that would require taking on some complications and conditions on the working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:27:42-08:00","id":1353618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353595#post1353595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much to say create a method of sorcerous initiation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there some reason you would need a working for this? There are any number of methods by which one might attain sorcerous enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Or are you thinking of something like the Salinan Working? (I have no idea whether the Salinan Working is still a thing in 3e, come to think of it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:34:43-08:00","id":1353621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353618#post1353618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or are you thinking of something like the Salinan Working? (I have no idea whether the Salinan Working is still a thing in 3e, come to think of it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been mentioned by the devs, but it's functionally closer to what it was in 1e, &quot;we tasked a number of spirits across Creation to teach sorcery to those who would seek it, and encoded the secrets of spells into nature itself,&quot; as opposed to 2e's &quot;we stamped sorcery itself into the shinma such that even sufficiently enlightened mortals might learn grasp the Emerald Circle.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T23:39:22-08:00","id":1353715,"title":"","content":"Didn't we already have this conversation?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1342442#post1342442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bMaking a new avenue for sorcery <i>is itself</i> making a change to the laws of Creation, and thus Solar 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-09-2019, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T01:36:49-08:00","id":1353733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1353715#post1353715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't we already have this conversation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, this thread\u2019s been around for more than seventy pages; I don\u2019t expect folks to jump in having read it in its entirety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T14:16:22-08:00","id":1355054,"title":"","content":"There's a picnic blanket in Doraemon, that can let you conjure up any kind of food, high quality food. But mundane.<br /> <br /> What rating should it be as a sorcerous working?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://doraemon.fandom.com/wiki/Gourmet_Table_Cloth\" target=\"_blank\">https://doraemon.fandom.com/wiki/Gourmet_Table_Cloth</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 12-15-2019, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T14:47:22-08:00","id":1355058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1355054#post1355054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a picnic blanket in Doraemon, that can let you conjure up any kind of food, high quality food. But mundane.<br /> <br /> What rating should it be as a sorcerous working?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://doraemon.fandom.com/wiki/Gourmet_Table_Cloth\" target=\"_blank\">https://doraemon.fandom.com/wiki/Gourmet_Table_Cloth</a></div> </div> </div> </div>It should be an artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T14:52:02-08:00","id":1355059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1355054#post1355054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a picnic blanket in Doraemon, that can let you conjure up any kind of food, high quality food. But mundane.<br /> <br /> What rating should it be as a sorcerous working?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://doraemon.fandom.com/wiki/Gourmet_Table_Cloth\" target=\"_blank\">https://doraemon.fandom.com/wiki/Gourmet_Table_Cloth</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The blanket really sounds more like an artifact than a sorcerous working.<br /> <br /> That said, I think a sorcerous working to give oneself (or someone else) the ability to conjure up mundane food on command would be at least Celestial Ambition 2? Merely creating mundane food doesn't sound like a tremendous power, of course, but being able to create food ex nihilo anywhere you are is clearly a miracle of outright supernatural power. It might even be higher than that, if there isn't some reasonable limit to how often you can do it. (Having an endless supply of food without requiring <i>any</i> inputs is kind of a big deal. People would go to war for that.)<br /> <br /> If you wanted something a little weirder, perhaps the sorcerer could create a garden where the trees, shrubs, and vines grow food that's ready to eat. (Meaning, a bush will literally grow pork buns, a tree will be laden with roasted chicken legs, the pitcher plants are full of fine wine or soup, etc.) A gardener trained in geomancy can make subtle adjustments in order to control what menu the garden will produce the next day.<br /> <br /> Although if you were going to grant yourself the ability, you might just make it a spell instead. I think in 1e/2e, there was a Terrestrial Circle spell for conjuring food (Food from the Aerial Table, I think?), although it was fairly bland and eating only magic food indefinitely was a bad idea. Considering what Ivory Orchid Pavilion can do (bringing forth endless food as part of the mansion), a Celestial Circle spell focused entirely on whipping up a feast would probably create a spread fit for a king.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T15:45:16-08:00","id":1355073,"title":"","content":"&quot;Your mother can\u2019t produce food out of thin air, no one can. Food is the first of the five Principal Exceptions to Gamp\u2019s Law of Elemental Transfiguration... It\u2019s impossible to make good food out of nothing! You can Summon it if you know where it is, you can transform it, you can increase the quantity if you\u2019ve already got some...&quot;<br /> <br /> This is definitely an artifact. Even the source material is an artifact -- it's a gadget not a spell.<br /> <br /> But it's probably not a millions miles off turning blood into scorpions. Celestial 2.<br /> <br /> Have you considered something like a cauldron that makes <a href=\"https://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0080.html\" target=\"_blank\">stone soup</a>? Because that you could probably get down to Terrestrial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T16:33:10-08:00","id":1355081,"title":"","content":"Basically, get a cauldron, boil, and rocks and pebbles mysteriously turn into turnips and potatoes and carrots and meat chunks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T20:56:23-08:00","id":1355116,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the ability to make soup out of water and a stone...I could see that as a thaumaturgical ritual. It's quite specific and not really very powerful.<br /> <br /> Stone Soup (2 dots): The mystic places a stone (any perfectly normal rock will do) into a cooking pot or cauldron full of water, heats it and spends a point of Willpower. Over the course of the next twenty minutes of simmering, the water transforms into a nutritious soup, usually of a type the mystic remembers fondly from their childhood. The finished soup is indistinguishable from a soup made with normal, mundane ingredients. Rumor holds that the first thaumaturge to develop this ritual was a con artist trying and failing to cheat some suspicious villagers out of ingredients for his supper; he was more surprised than anyone else when his lie turned out to be true and also delicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T17:30:48-08:00","id":1355297,"title":"","content":"Celestial 3<br /> <br /> CREATOR OF EFFICACIOUS SUBORDINATES<br /> <br /> A great tower that stretches up into the sky. When someone within the ciry limits turns towards it and directs a prayer wishing for help, a spirit manifests right by his side. The spirit has a total of 18 dots of abilities and attributes they can distribute, as well as up to 3 spirit charms they can use themed around whatever purpose they are called for. The spirits function much like demons in obedience and time, with an intimacy of love and loyalty to the one that called them into existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T18:06:57-08:00","id":1355305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1355297#post1355297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial 3<br /> <br /> CREATOR OF EFFICACIOUS SUBORDINATES<br /> <br /> A great tower that stretches up into the sky. When someone within the ciry limits turns towards it and directs a prayer wishing for help, a spirit manifests right by his side. The spirit has a total of 18 dots of abilities and attributes they can distribute, as well as up to 3 spirit charms they can use themed around whatever purpose they are called for. The spirits function much like demons in obedience and time, with an intimacy of love and loyalty to the one that called them into existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would probably avoid statting them through Ability/Attribute spread and more just say &quot;They have X dice on their primary function, X-2 dice on secondary but related functions, and 4 dice elsewhere, as well as three Charms directly related to their function besides the usual Spirit Charms (Materialize, Hurry Home, Measure The Wind)&quot;. I'd probably try to make it interesting or put some drawback on it so that it doesn't become strictly better than demon summoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T19:44:15-08:00","id":1355322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1355305#post1355305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would probably avoid statting them through Ability/Attribute spread and more just say &quot;They have X dice on their primary function, X-2 dice on secondary but related functions, and 4 dice elsewhere, as well as three Charms directly related to their function besides the usual Spirit Charms (Materialize, Hurry Home, Measure The Wind)&quot;. I'd probably try to make it interesting or put some drawback on it so that it doesn't become strictly better than demon summoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's wrong with making it better than demon summoning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T19:59:45-08:00","id":1355327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1355322#post1355322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's wrong with making it better than demon summoning?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Working should not make a Spell, Charm or Evocation obsolete? Workings are good when it comes to diversity of effects, not so good when it comes to a reliable, powerful effect compared to spells. Notice how summoning Working examples all mention *unbound* demons and never a bound one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T20:06:29-08:00","id":1355328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1355327#post1355327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Working should not make a Spell, Charm or Evocation obsolete? Workings are good when it comes to diversity of effects, not so good when it comes to a reliable, powerful effect compared to spells. Notice how summoning Working examples all mention *unbound* demons and never a bound one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... how about this, then? They last only half a year. And you can never have more than 10 at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T17:16:26-08:00","id":1356726,"title":"","content":"So drawing up a spring is terrestrial. Creating vast natural resources is Celestial. <br /> <br /> Let's say that you're an island, like Haiti. You're pelted by hurricanes and waves. You're small. You don't have much resoures. You want to: <br /> <br /> 1. Make a working to turn all horrible weather into 'normal weather'. <br /> <br /> 2. You want more land. Basically, a land reclamation project. Like the one singapore does. <br /> <br /> What's the ambition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T17:31:10-08:00","id":1356727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1356726#post1356726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Make a working to turn all horrible weather into 'normal weather'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Altering the weather of a town-sized region to give it an extra season for growing crops is an example of Celestial 2. Turning a desert into a lush tropical paradise is Solar 1. Depending on the size of the island, I'd say Celestial 3 sounds about right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1356726#post1356726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. You want more land. Basically, a land reclamation project. Like the one singapore does.<br /> <br /> What's the ambition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Paying to import rocks and dirt from another region would not be a sorcerous working. If you're cutting out all the middlemen with demonic or elemental magic, though, I'd probably put that at Celestial 2-3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T17:52:11-08:00","id":1356730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1356727#post1356727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Altering the weather of a town-sized region to give it an extra season for growing crops is an example of Celestial 2. Turning a desert into a lush tropical paradise is Solar 1. Depending on the size of the island, I'd say Celestial 3 sounds about right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Here's the thing. <br /> <br /> Let's say you put a working that transforms hurricanes into harsh storms. Like the terrestrial spell that can quiet deadly weather into 'harsh, but not horrible'. Isn't it basically an always on terrestrial spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T18:00:23-08:00","id":1356731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1356730#post1356730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Here's the thing.<br /> <br /> Let's say you put a working that transforms hurricanes into harsh storms. Like the terrestrial spell that can quiet deadly weather into 'harsh, but not horrible'. Isn't it basically an always on terrestrial spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a massive difference between doing a working which lasts forever then going to do something else and dedicating your entire life to casting a spell every time a bad storm rolls around. <br /> That's also not how levels of working and spell function. There's no interconnection. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T18:02:35-08:00","id":1356732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1356730#post1356730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say you put a working that transforms hurricanes into harsh storms. Like the terrestrial spell that can quiet deadly weather into 'harsh, but not horrible'. Isn't it basically an always on terrestrial spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>How is an always-on supernatural power <i>not</i> Celestial? We've already established that just because something exists as a Terrestrial spell, doesn't mean it's suitable as a Terrestrial Working.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T20:16:22-08:00","id":1356743,"title":"","content":"I have to disagree with The Count on this one. An always on Terrestrial working for a spell seems Terrestrial 3. You are weakening storms, and storms would destroy property but be less damaging to people except maybe at finesse 5. A working seems like the right way to bless area. The reverse of enhancing a natural aspect, you are weakening it. The hurricanes would still destroy stuff, but less stuff. Context matters a lot on workings, as does intent. If you want to actual fix the weather so storms aren't constant and the rain isn't as harsh, Celestial 2, you are not blessing the area with better weather (weakening the storms) but improving the weather (shorter storm seasons or only soft rains.) Solar 1 would allow you to rewrite the weather to be soft rains and loving lapping waves, mostly sunny with 99% growing seasons. Or you can do a something like Banning clouds from passing over an area. (Perhaps creating cloudless hurricanes? Maybe just prevent hurricanes in the area. Depends on Finesse) as Celestial 1, but this would greatly reduce inland water and have other effects. You could then make ever full fresh water wells with Celestial 1, and another Celestial 1 to make an idol that protects the shores from both waves and warns of incoming unknown ships, keeping people safe regardless. <br /> <br /> Creating land again, context and amount. Want a small chunk of land to build a house on? Terrestrial 1. On par with a new well or flattening a hill. Celestial 2-3 for major and profitable expansions. mutate shoreline trees to convert sand into soil, mutate coastal creatures to add sand to the shoreline as they die. Firmly Celestial 2. Creating a new animal that spawns in hills, and pushes dirt out to sea before beginning its life (Some kind of mole like early stage, to a aquatic secondary stage and the dirt moving something like it makes a dirt and rock shell that it loses as it reaches the seas edge, returns to lay eggs after some time, and dies to provide food for the young before they build armor and start the long journey again.) is only Terrestrial 3 but it takes a lot longer to let nature work in such a fashion. After some generations you could even do a second Terrestrial working to enhance your now mundane natural species to make a supernaturally large shell so it moves more dirt faster. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T21:22:07-08:00","id":1356749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1356743#post1356743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are weakening storms, and storms would destroy property but be less damaging to people except maybe at finesse 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>He didn't say they'd still be destructive - he said &quot;normal weather.&quot; I also don't know the spell he's referring to off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1356743#post1356743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Context matters a lot on workings, as does intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1356743#post1356743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to actual fix the weather so storms aren't constant and the rain isn't as harsh, Celestial 2, you are not blessing the area with better weather (weakening the storms) but improving the weather (shorter storm seasons or only soft rains.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial 2 was reworking the weather in a <i>town-sized</i> area; he was talking about doing it for a place like <i>Haiti</i>. Hence why I suggested Celestial 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T06:58:31-08:00","id":1356924,"title":"","content":"Terrestrial Circle Workings: Workings of the Terrestrial Circle are generally rooted in transforming, enhancing, or <b>weakening pre-existing elements of the natural world, </b>rather than directly invoking supernatural forces. <br /> <br /> An Emerald Circle working <b>might enchant all the fields of a village</b>, but only with a minor blessing\u2014something that would still be a marvel to the inhabitants of the village, but augments the natural properties of that area or <b>protects it against a mundane threat</b> or nuisance, rather than completely overwriting the nature of that region through magic.<br /> <br /> Ambition 1 (Goal Number 5): Ward a town or neighborhood-sized region against a particular type of mundane nuisance, such as forest fires, crop-eating pests, or rabid animals.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Protecting an entire, Hati sized island, is probably Celestial 3.<br /> <br /> Protecting each <i>settlement</i> on that island individually is <i>firmly</i> Terrestrial 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T19:00:28-08:00","id":1356970,"title":"","content":"A sorcerer spends some time enchanting his home, a well-built brick building with iron-shod doors, to improve its security. His working has the following effects:<br /> - The walls (and floors, and ceilings, and doors) are all magically reinforced and stronger; a feat of demolition would require a Strength one &quot;step&quot; higher on the chart (corebook p. 231), and +5 difficulty. Thus, the doors require Strength 7+ and 14 successes to break down, and the walls (and floors, and ceilings) require Strength 10+ and 15 successes. <br /> - The building's structure is solid against immaterial beings, and just as tough for a dematerialized god (for example) to break through as it would be if the god were materialized.<br /> - The locks on the doors and windows are proof against any mundane intrusion. An interloper capable of challenging sorcerous locks, such as a Solar using Lock-Opening Touch (corebook p. 317), faces a difficulty of (the sorcerer's Intelligence+Essence).<br /> - As long as the building remains locked, it resists any attempt to teleport from the outside in via effects such as Travel Without Distance (corebook p. 480), unless the teleporter (or a willing person they're bringing along) is carrying a key to the building. Anyone attempting to gain entrance in this manner must roll a suitable dice pool (Wits+Occult is appropriate for a sorcerer) against the same difficulty as the doors' locks. This defense ceases to apply if doors are unlocked such that a mundane path exists from the teleporter's origin point to their destination without passing through any currently-locked doors.<br /> - The sorcerer has a basic awareness of any breaches. If one of the walls is seriously damaged, or one of the locks undone without the proper key being used, the sorcerer becomes aware of it as long as he is in the same realm of existence. This effect doesn't provide any information about the intruder(s) themselves, only which wall(s) or door(s) they've broken.<br /> - The enchantment persists as long as the building hasn't been totally destroyed. If one of the walls has been knocked down and needs to be replaced, the magical enhancement goes into effect again as soon as a new wall is built, without the sorcerer having to put any additional work into repairing the magic. (On the other hand, if the entire building is ruined via an effect such as Starfall Eschaton Hammer (Arms of the Chosen p. 147), the working is ended and the sorcerer gets his XP back.)<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Celestial 2 or 3. Per the book, warding a structure with magical barriers is Celestial 1 and enchanting fortifications to strengthen them is Celestial 2, but I may have gone a bit further with this list of effects. On one hand, I don't think this is anywhere near as fantastic as e.g. making a building fly or giving it the ability to rearrange its internal structure, but I think I may have pushed the effect from Celestial 2 to Celestial 3 when I started including things like resistance to teleportation and an instant warning if something gets damaged?<br /> <br /> If doing this to a good-sized residence is indeed Celestial 2, I'm guessing that doing it for a modest-sized fortress would be Celestial 3.<br /> <br /> Augmenting the defenses of one's own home is probably <i>very</i> common among sorcerers capable of performing Celestial workings reliably, so I'm interested in other ideas people have for sorcerous home defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T19:58:17-08:00","id":1356973,"title":"","content":"I'd call that C2F5 for a single structure of any (mundanely reasonable) size since most of it is just &quot;walls and doors that <i>work</i>, dammit&quot;. If you want to ward every part of The Lap or your mountain-fortress that's a different story. <br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't allow unpickable locks. Stiff penalty or difficulty, but not &quot;Have this charm or lose&quot;, since that's a terrible game mechanic. Probably scale it off the intruder's Occult, I'd aim to make it nigh-impossible without Occult but within the reach of a DB with Occult. <br /> Likewise, I'd have there be some sort of roll to avoid detection <i>if</i> the intruder had Occult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T20:58:12-08:00","id":1356979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1356973#post1356973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I wouldn't allow unpickable locks. Stiff penalty or difficulty, but not &quot;Have this charm or lose&quot;, since that's a terrible game mechanic. Probably scale it off the intruder's Occult, I'd aim to make it nigh-impossible without Occult but within the reach of a DB with Occult.<br /> Likewise, I'd have there be some sort of roll to avoid detection <i>if</i> the intruder had Occult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think you're right about the locks. I was misreading Lock-Opening Touch and thought it was implying that sorcerous locks <i>can't</i> be picked without a Charm, but it really doesn't say that at all. I'm not sure whether (Intelligence+Essence) is the right difficulty, though. Maybe just make it 5+(sorcerer's Essence)? That seems like a decent number.<br /> <br /> What about this option: the intruder can either roll Dexterity+Larceny normally against the lock (and warn the sorcerer about the break-in), or roll Dexterity+(lower of Larceny or Occult) at +2 difficulty to open the lock without the sorcerer knowing. Or would it be better to have the Occult roll to bypass the &quot;security system&quot; be separate? I guess it's cool if you could have a team work together to break into the sorcerer's warded sanctum. (Also that offers the option of someone disabling the security on a wall and then breaking through the damn wall unnoticed.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T02:41:47-08:00","id":1357177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1356979#post1356979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure whether (Intelligence+Essence) is the right difficulty, though. Maybe just make it 5+(sorcerer's Essence)? That seems like a decent number.</div> </div> </div> </div>That should work fine. That said, I'm a stickler for Craft/Working separation so in my game I'd leave the difficulty alone and make the guy get/make good locks if he wants good locks. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1356979#post1356979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about this option: the intruder can either roll Dexterity+Larceny normally against the lock (and warn the sorcerer about the break-in), or roll Dexterity+(lower of Larceny or Occult) at +2 difficulty to open the lock without the sorcerer knowing. Or would it be better to have the Occult roll to bypass the &quot;security system&quot; be separate? I guess it's cool if you could have a team work together to break into the sorcerer's warded sanctum. (Also that offers the option of someone disabling the security on a wall and then breaking through the damn wall unnoticed.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of using lower of Larceny or Occult for the lockpicking. That offers a nice challenge hike (and limits Excellencies) for people who don't have the skills needed to deal with magic but doesn't hinder those who do. <br /> I <i>really</i> like the idea of moving the avoiding detection check over to a separate roll so a buddy can join in. The difficulty for that, should it scale off the Working-maker's Intelligence (since it's a Working) or their Perception (since it's detection)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T08:45:00-08:00","id":1357204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1357177#post1357177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difficulty for that, should it scale off the Working-maker's Intelligence (since it's a Working) or their Perception (since it's detection)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just make it 5.<br /> <br /> Anyone who cares is going to get a 5 in the relevant stat, and save yourself the ST head-ache of trying to remember the Intelligence score of every character who's performed this Working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T12:53:38-08:00","id":1357238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1357204#post1357204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just make it 5.<br /> <br /> Anyone who cares is going to get a 5 in the relevant stat, and save yourself the ST head-ache of trying to remember the Intelligence score of every character who's performed this Working.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree if it was Intelligence, but does <i>every</i> sorcerer also have 5 Perception? That's not been the case in my game. <br /> And how many C2 capable sorcerers is your circle breaking into the houses of that you're expecting problems keeping track of them all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T19:35:15-08:00","id":1357291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1357177#post1357177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That should work fine. That said, I'm a stickler for Craft/Working separation so in my game I'd leave the difficulty alone and make the guy get/make good locks if he wants good locks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I think it's fair for a working to make your locks more difficult to pick. (Given how Lock-Opening Touch is written, &quot;sorcerous locks&quot; are definitely a thing.) You would need to have good-quality locks in the first place, though!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1357177#post1357177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of using lower of Larceny or Occult for the lockpicking. That offers a nice challenge hike (and limits Excellencies) for people who don't have the skills needed to deal with magic but doesn't hinder those who do.<br /> I <i>really</i> like the idea of moving the avoiding detection check over to a separate roll so a buddy can join in. The difficulty for that, should it scale off the Working-maker's Intelligence (since it's a Working) or their Perception (since it's detection)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to set the difficulties of both picking the locks (Dexterity+Larceny) and avoiding detection (Wits+Occult probably?) at (5+sorcerer's Essence).<br /> <br /> In retrospect I'm not convinced it's a good idea to set difficulties based on the working-maker's Attributes or Abilities (unless the working <i>is</i> an ability being granted to the working-maker personally, perhaps). If a sorcerer with relatively modest traits manages to complete the working, he shouldn't be stuck with a pathetically weak result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T19:58:32-08:00","id":1357292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1357291#post1357291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In retrospect I'm not convinced it's a good idea to set difficulties based on the working-maker's Attributes or Abilities (unless the working <i>is</i> an ability being granted to the working-maker personally, perhaps). If a sorcerer with relatively modest traits manages to complete the working, he shouldn't be stuck with a pathetically weak result.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T14:13:52-08:00","id":1358247,"title":"","content":"I talked about this idea a while back, but I've finally gotten around to writing up some stats for this creature. (Please note that this is a first draft, so let me know if you think anything in it is a bad idea or if it's missing something it should really have.) This breezy beast is meant to be the result of an Ambition 3 Celestial working and broadly on par with a second circle demon; it's nowhere near as deadly head-on as Octavian, but it can <i>really</i> move.<br /> <br /> <b>Storm Horse</b><br /> <br /> The storm horse is the creation of an eccentric Marukani sorcerer, the result of crossbreeding a (very confused) prize stallion with an actual cumulonimbus cloud. The resulting creature is a magnificent warhorse, with a stormcloud-grey coat and a mane the color of blue-tinged lightning.<br /> <br /> Although it's easy to mistake for an air elemental at a glance, the storm horse is a creature of flesh and blood -- essentially of the same nature as a (very powerful) God-Blood. While hardly an academic and probably not literate, the horse is as smart as some humans and can understand spoken Riverspeak well enough. It cannot speak human tongues but is quite expressive with its body language, and a capable horseman will usually understand what it wants to convey.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence:</b> 3; <b>Willpower:</b> 8; <b>Join Battle:</b> 8 dice<br /> <b>Personal Motes:</b> 80<br /> <b>Health Levels:</b> -0x2/-1x5/-2x5/-4x3/Incap.<br /> <b>Speed Bonus:</b> +5<br /> <br /> <b>Actions:</b> Feats of Strength: 12 dice (may attempt Strength 5 feats); Senses: 8 dice; Stealth: 7 dice<br /> Resolve 4, Guile 3<br /> <br /> <b>Combat:</b><br /> Attack (Kick): 12 dice (Damage 16, minimum 2)<br /> Attack (Lightning blast): 14 dice (5m per attack, Damage 18, ignores 3 points of soak or hardness from metal armor)<br /> Combat Movement: 14 dice (see Swift-Hooved)<br /> Evasion 5, Parry 3<br /> Soak/Hardness: 12/4<br /> <br /> <i>Special Attacks</i><br /> <br /> <b>Brutal Kick:</b> Enemies smaller than human size that take 5+ damage from the storm horse\u2019s withering stomps are knocked back one range band and fall prone.<br /> <br /> <i>Merits</i><br /> <br /> <b>Swift-Hooved:</b> The storm horse applies the double 9s rule on all rolls to disengage, withdraw or rush.<br /> <br /> <b>Noble Steed:</b> The storm horse has a Defining Tie of loyalty to the sorcerer who created it, which cannot be reduced or altered by any means.<br /> <br /> <b>Like the Wind:</b> Outside of combat, the storm horse can generally gallop at half again the speed of a normal horse, and go at least twice as long without requiring rest.<br /> <br /> <i>Offensive Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Hooves of Thunder</b> (5m, 1wp or 10m, 1 wp; Supplemental; Instant; Essence 3): The impact of the storm horse's hooves unleashes a brutal thunderclap, affecting everyone within close range (for 5m, 1wp) or short range (for 10m, 1wp) other than the horse and its rider. This effect may optionally be used in conjunction with a normal kick attack, using the same attack roll for both, but dealing damage separately. The thunderclap is unblockable, and any opponent whose Defense is overcome suffers 5 dice of unsoakable withering damage; victims who suffer damage greater than or equal to their Stamina are knocked prone. Battle groups instead suffer 10 dice, and if a rout check is provoked, the +1 difficulty for a supernatural area-of-effect attack applies.<br /> <br /> <b>Crackling Fury Discharge</b> (5m; Simple; Instant; Dual; Essence 3): The storm horse unleashes a bolt of lightning from its nostrils, rolling 14 dice to attack at up to medium range without requiring an aim action. A withering attack deals a base of 18 damage and ignores up to 3 soak from metal armor (including alloys made with the five magical materials); a decisive attack converts extra successes on the attack roll into additional damage dice, and ignores up to 3 hardness from metal armor.<br /> <br /> <b>Foe-Scattering Tempest</b> (10m; Supplemental; Instant; Essence 3): The storm horse may use this Charm to supplement either a normal movement action or any sort of combat movement action, as apprpriate; regardless, the horse moves through a battle group's space without treating it as difficult terrain. Additionally, the storm horse rolls its Combat Movement pool with double 9s against the battle group's Defense; if successful, the battle group suffers 10 dice of unsoakable withering damage (as with Hooves of Thunder, above). In the alternative, this Charm may be used when an enemy or battle group attempts a grapple or engage gambit against the storm horse and/or its rider; the horse resists the control roll with its Combat Movement pool (with double 9s), and deals damage as from Hooves of Thunder if it successfully escapes.<br /> <br /> <i>Defensive Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Swift Cyclone Defense</b> (2m+ or 5m; Reflexive; Instant; Essence 2): The storm horse may increase its Parry or Evasion against an attack by spending 2 motes per +1, to a maximum of its Essence (i.e. +3). It may also spend 5 motes to negate all penalties to its Defense against one attack<br /> <br /> <b>Impact-Dispersing Exhale</b> (10m, 1wp; Reflexive; Instant; Uniform; Essence 3): The storm horse may shunt the force of an incoming attack into the air around it, halving the damage dice rolled (round up) after applying soak or hardness.<br /> <br /> <i>Mobility Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sky-Treading Style</b> (2m; Reflexive; One turn; Essence 2): The storm horse can run across the air itself, requiring no solid ground to take movement actions. The horse cannot hover or ascend straight up or down; it is generally limited to an angle no sharper than 45 degrees. This effect cannot be maintained if the storm horse is knocked down. However, if the horse falls from a height for any reason, it may reflexively spend 2 motes to perfectly negate falling damage for both itself and its rider, assuming the rider remains on its back. (This effect is not generally useful against other effects that deal the equivalent of falling damage, such as being smacked into a wall with Heaven Thunder Hammer, unless the Storyteller deems it appropriate.)<br /> <br /> <b>Inescapable Whirlwind Motion</b> (2m+; Supplemental; Instant; Essence 2): The storm horse may supplement any roll for combat movement by spending 2 motes per automatic success, up to a maxmimum of (Essence, i.e. 3) successes. This Charm may also be used to supplement any feat of demolition in which the horse bodily crashes through the object it intends to destroy, in which case the horse may attempt Strength 7+ feats, and the cost of using Impact-Dispersing Exhale to resist damage caused directly by this foolishness is reduced to 5 motes.<br /> <br /> <i>Miscellaneous Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Wind-Body Prana</b> (10m, 1wp; Simple; One scene; Essence 3): Although it is not a spirit and cannot actually dematerialize, the storm horse can transform itself physically into a gust of wind. Anything worn by the horse (such as a saddle, barding, or relatively light saddlebags) transforms along with its body, but the horse can by no means bring its rider along (unless they have some means of riding the wind itself) or carry anything else in this form. In wind form, the horse can get through any gap that isn't airtight, and can't be affected by attacks that would not harm the air itself (physical attacks are generally of no use unless capable of striking a dematerialized being, although energy attacks can be effective). Being a gust of wind does not make the horse any stealthier; the wind remains audible and tends to blow light objects around as it passes.<br /> <br /> <b>Swift Gale Approach</b> (10m; Supplemental; One day; Essence 2): Unifying its Essence with the wind itself, the storm horse can travel around 100 mph overland, and gallop all day without tiring. The horse also applies double 9s to any roll necessary to overcome obstacles or hazards that would slow it down; it may reflexively spend 5 motes to apply double 8s instead. (If the rider must also roll to resist a hazard, he also gains the benefits of double 9s or 8s as appropriate, as the horse manuevers to protect its master.) A rider with appropriate Charms of his own can achieve incredible speeds on the mighty horse's back.<br /> <br /> Author's notes:<br /> - I'm wondering if Hooves of Thunder should have some kind of limit on how much Initiative the horse can reap at once if it smacks a large group of people. Many similar area effects have one.<br /> - I'm also wondering if the horse should have slightly more offensive punch when it comes to single-target attacks. I didn't want to overdo things Charm-wise, but a really brutal stomp might be a fair addition.<br /> - If a Solar with Wind-Racing Essence Infusion takes this thing for a spin, it's going to get ridiculously fast. I don't think this is necessarily a problem, but it's possible I went a little too far.<br /> - I very nearly wrote a Charm for what happens if you hitch the storm horse to a chariot or something, but eh. I'm not sure we even have normal rules for land vehicles in this edition. It probably <i>should</i> be able to pull one through the air with Sky-Treading Style (possibly for an extra mote cost) though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11237,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","user":"Jefepato","date":". 01-01-2020, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T15:11:10-08:00","id":1358266,"title":"","content":"I'm not familiar enough with mounts to answer your questions... but is the lack of Hardness intentional?<br /> <br /> Even a token amount (1-3) would render it immune to Anima Flux.<br /> <br /> &quot;I ride my sorcerous horse into battle against the Dragons... and it's dead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T15:17:02-08:00","id":1358269,"title":"","content":"Seconding the Hardness bit; would recommend about Hardness 3-4 just to also avoid base-initiative barrages, at least those that don't have Hardness-ignoring Charms built into them. Those ones are already fine by virtue of forcing them to spend motes on damaging your steed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T15:50:59-08:00","id":1358287,"title":"","content":"It wasn't especially intentional, no (at least, I didn't deliberately plan on that being a weakness for the horse). I didn't think too hard about hardness -- I ended up giving it the same base soak as Alvuea, since she's a second-circle demon who is a fair scrapper but not really <i>focused</i> on personal combat. Of course, Alvuea has a Charm that gives her artifact armor, so she doesn't <i>need</i> innate hardness...<br /> <br /> I think giving the storm horse a hardness of 4 would be reasonable. It is supposed to be a rather hardy beast. I've made that edit above.<br /> <br /> The horse's health levels were pretty much eyeballed as well. I considered giving it a few more, but I didn't really have a guideline in mind other than &quot;a lot tougher than a normal horse, but not nearly as tough as Octavian.&quot; I admit I don't have a tremendous amount of experience with the combat system, so I wasn't sure how major an effect Impact-Dispersing Exhale would have (although it seems fairly strong to me).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, as a formatting issue: I guess I should have included the lightning attack from Crackling Fury Discharge in the section on combat traits. I wasn't sure if Charm-created attacks belonged there, but Amon Mora has his elemental bolts listed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11237,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","user":"Jefepato","date":". 01-01-2020, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T15:55:21-08:00","id":1358289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1358287#post1358287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The horse's health levels were pretty much eyeballed as well. I considered giving it a few more, but I didn't really have a guideline in mind other than &quot;a lot tougher than a normal horse, but not nearly as tough as Octavian.&quot; I admit I don't have a tremendous amount of experience with the combat system, so I wasn't sure how major an effect Impact-Dispersing Exhale would have (although it seems fairly strong to me).</div> </div> </div> </div>Halving damage dice is tremendously powerful, more than a Solar E...2? 3? Resistance Charm (Iron Kettle Body) if it also works on Decisive attacks. I'd recommend either a once per scene clause or to reevaluate its balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T16:23:10-08:00","id":1358297,"title":"","content":"That's fair. I might change that to once per scene, and/or consider a cheaper and less overwhelming soak buff/damage reducer. Also might slap an Initiative cost on it as well.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it could be retooled like this:<br /> - When hit with a withering attack, the horse can spend 1m per point to increase soak, up to +6 soak<br /> - When hit with a decisive attack, the horse can spend 3m per die to negate damage dice, up to 2 dice<br /> - Once per scene, when hit with an attack the horse can spend 10m, 1wp, 5i to halve the damage dice (rounded up) after applying soak or hardness, as described above<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about removing Wind-Body Prana as well. Although it does demonstrate the storm horse's powerful connection to the elements, it doesn't serve many actual purposes, since the horse is hardly a scout or infiltrator. I guess it could conceivably help the horse get back to the sorcerer if they get separate and trapped somehow, but it's already quite maneuverable and good at breaking things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T17:24:44-08:00","id":1358310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1358297#post1358297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fair. I might change that to once per scene, and/or consider a cheaper and less overwhelming soak buff/damage reducer. Also might slap an Initiative cost on it as well.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it could be retooled like this:<br /> - When hit with a withering attack, the horse can spend 1m per point to increase soak, up to +6 soak<br /> - When hit with a decisive attack, the horse can spend 3m per die to negate damage dice, up to 2 dice<br /> - Once per scene, when hit with an attack the horse can spend 10m, 1wp, 5i to halve the damage dice (rounded up) after applying soak or hardness, as described above<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about removing Wind-Body Prana as well. Although it does demonstrate the storm horse's powerful connection to the elements, it doesn't serve many actual purposes, since the horse is hardly a scout or infiltrator. I guess it could conceivably help the horse get back to the sorcerer if they get separate and trapped somehow, but it's already quite maneuverable and good at breaking things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flavor powers are fine for non-official stuff since you have no word-count to worry about. As for the Charm, I'd probably consider something like &quot;Pay 3m to reroll a success on a damage roll, up to 3 successes&quot;, maybe with a conditional increase to make it reach 5 sux rerolled. Maybe giving it a Charm to gain a temporary Hardness boost so it can fight off low-initiative kiting momentarily. Dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T23:14:12-08:00","id":1361219,"title":"","content":"A sorcerer eats a specially prepared cock's-egg omelette and gains the hypnotic, burning gaze of a cockatrice.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer's attacks use (Wits+Occult) to target the burning gaze and (Intelligence+Occult) for the control roll. For the purpose of withering savaging attacks, the gaze is treated as a light weapon with damage based on Intelligence instead of Strength. This ability otherwise works like that of an actual cockatrice; the sorcerer can maintain both a physical grapple and a gaze if he chooses.<br /> <br /> ...I don't know, should the withering attacks bypass armor soak somehow? The actual cockatrice stats are notably missing a withering damage value for the gaze entirely. It doesn't make sense that armor would do any good, though, since the victim burns from the inside out.<br /> <br /> Celestial 2 or 3? I'm kinda thinking 3 since, if nothing else, it allows the sorcerer to wield traits he's almost certainly good at and force his opponent to resist with a dice pool not normally applicable to physical combat. Still, unless it bypasses armor it's not fundamentally better than a physical grapple, and it has the downside of not being usable for anything <i>but</i> grappling. It'd give the sorcerer a hell of a reputation, though. (&quot;Did you hear? Sharp-Eyed Corwin killed some dude last week just by staring him down...&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T11:44:16-08:00","id":1361314,"title":"","content":"I don't have the cockatrice's stats but I'd say that a cockatrice's gaze sounds like a Celestial 2 power equivalent to turning your blood into scorpions.<br /> <br /> Dictating what dice pools you use sounds like Finesse to me.<br /> <br /> Celestial 2. Finesse 5.<br /> <br /> If you just want a cockatrice themed gaze attack, Finesse 3 (and maybe give the ST a copy of the Hundred Devils stats as a <s>bribe</s> gift). Or if you hate yourself and want to risk Midas, Finesse 1 and roll the dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T23:26:18-08:00","id":1361667,"title":"","content":"The cockatrice's stats are fully viewable in the full-size preview: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/259886/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Black-Hollow-and-Cockatrice?src=also_purchased\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...also_purchased</a><br /> <br /> Notably, they don't turn people to stone, but rather their gaze paralyzes the target and burns them from the inside out. It's functionally equivalent to a grapple (but at up to medium range and with different dice pools involved).<br /> <br /> Honestly, half the time I forget that attempting a Finesse lower than 5 is even an option. I don't think I would do a low-Finesse working unless I was playing a mortal sorcerer for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T23:35:10-08:00","id":1361670,"title":"","content":"Why not? Unforeseen wrinkles can be hella fun, provided your ST isn\u2019t a tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T23:46:53-08:00","id":1361675,"title":"","content":"I guess that by the time I get interested in a working idea, I've got a pretty specific image in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T10:00:08-08:00","id":1361755,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't stamp my foot and insist on Celestial 2. Celestial 3 is fine as a balance point if you have concerns.<br /> <br /> But Celestial 2 is for single target superpowers. And burning someone from the inside with your gaze isn't any &quot;more&quot; magical than turning your blood into scorpions in my mind. Celestial 3 is for creating entire magical beings whole-cloth, enchanting buildings and punching holes in reality. <br /> <br /> Single superpower (&quot;such as a burning gaze&quot;) is Celestial 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T20:45:35-08:00","id":1363904,"title":"","content":"Let's say you're a sorcerer who wants to solve world hunger in Creation. A few options for this:<br /> <br /> 1) Doing what <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norman_Borlaug\" target=\"_blank\">Norman Borlaug</a> did and creating an improved version of a staple crop like wheat or rice. I'm pretty sure inventing <a href=\"https://croplife.org/news/semi-dwarf-wheat-the-game-changer/\" target=\"_blank\">semi-dwarf wheat</a> is Terrestrial 2, like creating a hybrid plant species. Of course, you don't really need sorcery at all for this (obviously), but it's probably faster.<br /> <br /> 2) Creating a new version of a crop with the actual supernatural power to grow a lot faster than usual (say, five times faster), and have it breed true. Terrestrial 3 is enough to create &quot;a specimen&quot; of an existing species with a minor supernatural power, but I'm not sure if that's minor and I'm not sure if Terrestrial 3-level powers normally pass on to the specimen's offspring.<br /> <br /> 3) Creating a new subspecies of <i>animal</i> (cows, pigs, chickens, whatever) that breeds and grows a lot faster than usual (again, let's go with five times faster), while consuming the same amount of food per day. This also makes it relatively cheaper, both in food and labor, to raise your meat. I don't know, I have trouble seeing this as a Terrestrial working.<br /> <br /> Creating spirits to do the work of helping feed mortals would be another option. You'd need either a quite powerful spirit or a lot of them to make a serious dent in hunger Creation-wide, though. (Speaking of spirits, if you create fast-growing cows that become widely popular, does Ahlat get a significant boost? Or is he mad that people might no longer need to raid their neighbors in order to afford their hecatomb sacrifice?)<br /> <br /> Does anyone have other interesting ideas? There must be some more creative possibilities than this. Of course, distribution can be just as troublesome as supply, and I'm not sure how a sorcerous working (or several) could fix that on a large scale. I just had the mental image of food animals (probably chickens) that instinctively seek out and present themselves to hungry humans, but that is perhaps a little too silly.<br /> <br /> ...A Solar 3 working to alter the whole world slightly so that rulers gain personal benefits from their subjects all being fed would be an interesting concept, but it would probably just lead to people deliberately starving their enemies' subjects to weaken them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T21:17:03-08:00","id":1363906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1363904#post1363904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Doing what <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norman_Borlaug\" target=\"_blank\">Norman Borlaug</a> did and creating an improved version of a staple crop like wheat or rice. I'm pretty sure inventing <a href=\"https://croplife.org/news/semi-dwarf-wheat-the-game-changer/\" target=\"_blank\">semi-dwarf wheat</a> is Terrestrial 2, like creating a hybrid plant species. Of course, you don't really need sorcery at all for this (obviously), but it's probably faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, Terrestrial 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Creating a new version of a crop with the actual supernatural power to grow a lot faster than usual (say, five times faster), and have it breed true. Terrestrial 3 is enough to create &quot;a specimen&quot; of an existing species with a minor supernatural power, but I'm not sure if that's minor and I'm not sure if Terrestrial 3-level powers normally pass on to the specimen's offspring.<br /> <br /> 3) Creating a new subspecies of <i>animal</i> (cows, pigs, chickens, whatever) that breeds and grows a lot faster than usual (again, let's go with five times faster), while consuming the same amount of food per day. This also makes it relatively cheaper, both in food and labor, to raise your meat. I don't know, I have trouble seeing this as a Terrestrial working.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the &quot;single specimen&quot; of a creature at Terrestrial <i>is</i> significant, yes - I don't think such abilities would breed true. In any case, 5 times faster growth and breeding is more than I would classify as &quot;a minor supernatural trait&quot;. At best, I'd allow maybe double growing speed at Terrestrial 3. For something like grain, I'd probably be generous and let &quot;enough to plant a single field's worth&quot; count as &quot;a single specimen&quot;, but it still wouldn't breed true, you'd only get one crop off of that. For making minor supernatural alterations to a creature that breed true, I'll call that Celestial Ambition 1. Compare it to Celestial 2, which has &quot;Spread mutations throughout the mundane flora and fauna of an entire ecosystem.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Speaking of spirits, if you create fast-growing cows that become widely popular, does Ahlat get a significant boost? Or is he mad that people might no longer need to raid their neighbors in order to afford their hecatomb sacrifice?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, personally, I'd guess that unless you made cattle a <i>great deal</i> more productive, that people would still be raiding. There's definitely going to be a tipping point past which cattle stop being so valuable, but I think Creation, as it is, is quite a long way from that point. If you have 100 cattle now, and could have 200 cattle after this, you're going to want to <i>keep </i>those extra 100 cattle for all the milk, meat, leather, and other secondary products they produce, so it's still better to raid your neighbor for <i>her</i> 100 cattle.<br /> <br /> Actually, that brings up another issue with using animals to solve hunger - in quite a lot of cases, the limiting factor isn't &quot;how many animals can we breed&quot;, it's &quot;how many animals can we <i>support&quot;. </i>The fact that this new strain of cattle breeds and grows to adulthood twice as quickly probably doesn't mean twice as many cattle around, because the land doesn't grow enough grass to raise twice as many cattle. Odds are, you're already raising close to as many cattle as you can support already. Really, the faster breeding/growing would just mean that people can recover from losses twice as fast. Which is still useful, don't get me wrong! But it's not as totally transformative as &quot;now we have twice as much livestock&quot; might be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have other interesting ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that just produces food from inorganic material, or straight-up nothing, would be handy. Imagine a village where the recipe for stone soup actually doesn't need anything extra besides the stone to produce a good meal! Beyond producing <i>more</i> food, I'd also consider ways to produce food more efficiently, with less loss. A working that totally barred vermin from a location's granaries would save a great deal of food, for example. Stack more workings against various other sorts of loss (molds and fungus, simple dampness, etc), and you could probably get a very large increase in available food with little extra production. Or improve the efficiency of planting! Pre-modern planting was quite inefficient - lots of farmers simply scattered handfuls of seed over the ground, where a good portion of it was eaten by animals, or simply failed to get buried deeply enough to grow and never germinated. If you did a working over a village so that every grain thrown over a field found its way into a furrow and buried itself, and maybe threw on one to scare off the birds and other seed-eating animals, the farmers would be able to re-plant each year with a far smaller portion of their stored grain, in turn allowing more of it to be eaten.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, distribution can be just as troublesome as supply, and I'm not sure how a sorcerous working (or several) could fix that on a large scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I think there's definitely some potential for workings here too. Consider a working placed on a road running through decent farmland to the nearest city. Any grain poured on the road simply rolls itself to the city's granary (probably throw in another working to prevent animals from stealing the grain, though). Oxen and similar beasts of burden eat a <i>lot</i> of food, particularly when they're hauling a load, meaning that any sort of transport that eliminates the need for them makes long-distance transport of food <i>much</i> more practical. Or if you're talking about meat, think of a working that ensured that a particular road was always below freezing in temperature. If you also set up some way to freeze meat at the farms, and keep it frozen at its destination, you could have long-distance transport of meat too, even if you otherwise had to haul it with animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T00:03:50-08:00","id":1363923,"title":"","content":"Re:making food out of nothing, I had a statue in one of my games that transmuted a point of Willpower into a day\u2019s worth of food in the style of the user\u2019s mother\u2019s cooking.<br /> <br /> Naturally, it made most of the PCs pretty sad (one can\u2019t go back to her family for fear of them discovering she\u2019s a Solar; two lost their mother to the Realm), and one of them confused (as he had two dads and was conceived by a Neomah, when he used it, it produced the exotic cuisine of the Demon City).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T04:16:23-08:00","id":1363941,"title":"","content":"While I appreciate the idea, I think that trying to think &quot;locally&quot;, (ie at the size of the region you are playing in) is a better answer than &quot;Can I solve X forever everywhere&quot;. Maybe I'm wrong, but I like to think the First Age was attained after centuries of hard work on each region to make it wonderful, rather than centralized sorcerers casting spells from the center and great things spreading automatically in every direction. <br /> <br /> Also, spreading a mutation that makes humans less reliant on food and water, maybe ? Like their organism live at a 1/10th rate and consume less everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T20:04:51-08:00","id":1364088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1363941#post1363941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I appreciate the idea, I think that trying to think &quot;locally&quot;, (ie at the size of the region you are playing in) is a better answer than &quot;Can I solve X forever everywhere&quot;. Maybe I'm wrong, but I like to think the First Age was attained after centuries of hard work on each region to make it wonderful, rather than centralized sorcerers casting spells from the center and great things spreading automatically in every direction.<br /> <br /> Also, spreading a mutation that makes humans less reliant on food and water, maybe ? Like their organism live at a 1/10th rate and consume less everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true that 1) it's much easier to work locally than globally, and 2) you're going to need a lot of time and help if you expect to create a golden age.<br /> <br /> But if one man can save a billion lives IRL, surely a Solar could do even better with a sufficiently clever idea. That being said, the clever idea would almost certainly take time and the work of many people over a generation (at least) to actually spread across a world as huge as Creation, even if it started with one sorcerer's working.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of players around the table, it's unlikely that the actual game will last long enough to see the sorcerer's brilliant plan spread any further than the region they're in, anyway. And solving food concerns doesn't necessarily solve anything else -- Creation has plenty of problems that couldn't possibly be fixed with a new strain of plant life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T20:16:53-08:00","id":1364090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1364088#post1364088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creation has plenty of problems that couldn't possibly be fixed with a new strain of plant life.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Factually incorrect</i>, good sir. No problem cannot be solved with the proper new strain of plant life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T21:45:58-08:00","id":1364098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1364090#post1364090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Factually incorrect</i>, good sir. No problem cannot be solved with the proper new strain of plant life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not gonna lie, even as I typed that sentence I was really hoping someone was going to pop up with a genius plan to defeat the Deathlords by modifying the common whisk fern or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T21:57:28-08:00","id":1364100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1364098#post1364098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not gonna lie, even as I typed that sentence I was really hoping someone was going to pop up with a genius plan to defeat the Deathlords by modifying the common whisk fern or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deathlords? Too easy. Modify the common dandelion to have a massively accelerated lifecycle and undertake life-affirming ceremonies. They will carpet the world and snuff out all shadowlands, thus permanently removing the ability of some stuffy old ghosts to interfere in our horticulture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T07:22:50-08:00","id":1364156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1364100#post1364100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Deathlords? Too easy. Modify the common dandelion to have a massively accelerated lifecycle and undertake life-affirming ceremonies. They will carpet the world and snuff out all shadowlands, thus permanently removing the ability of some stuffy old ghosts to interfere in our horticulture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, is destroying shadowlands really as easy as carpeting them in plant life and doing ceremonies? I didn't think it was that easy.<br /> <br /> I guess holy dandelions might be an option, though.<br /> <br /> (Also, still need more modifications for the North and South. I don't think normal dandelions will grow in the desert or frozen tundra.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T14:22:10-08:00","id":1364226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1364156#post1364156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, is destroying shadowlands really as easy as carpeting them in plant life and doing ceremonies? I didn't think it was that easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making dandelions capable of performing life-affirming ceremonies is &quot;easy?&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b(That said, I don't know that it <i>would</i> be that easy, as ghosts interested in the shadowlands staying open could probably just, y'know, possess a mortal to take a scythe and cut them down.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T14:40:48-08:00","id":1364231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1364226#post1364226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b(That said, I don't know that it <i>would</i> be that easy, as ghosts interested in the shadowlands staying open could probably just, y'know, possess a mortal to take a scythe and cut them down.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worse than that. If the grass is life-infused enough to close Shadowlands on its own, then I'd argue that cutting it down could <u>create</u> Shadowlands as though a terrible loss of life had occured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T15:00:19-08:00","id":1364233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1364226#post1364226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making dandelions capable of performing life-affirming ceremonies is &quot;easy?&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b(That said, I don't know that it <i>would</i> be that easy, as ghosts interested in the shadowlands staying open could probably just, y'know, possess a mortal to take a scythe and cut them down.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortals can do them, how hard could it possibly be? <br /> <br /> You raise a good point regarding ghosts. Most of them are idiots but there's bound to be a few that are halfway competent. I'll make sure these dandelions have an affinity for exorcism and develop basic self defense ability in the presence of deathly energies. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1364231#post1364231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's worse than that. If the grass is life-infused enough to close Shadowlands on its own, then I'd argue that cutting it down could <u>create</u> Shadowlands as though a terrible loss of life had occured.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life naturally subdues Shadowlands. Slowly, but it does it. So I make the dandelions live <i>faster</i> so they execute that natural process <i>faster</i>. By several orders of magnitude! They don't live <i>more</i>, that's nonsense. How can something be <i>more alive</i>? <br /> Now get out of my workshop before I sic the ferns on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T19:52:15-08:00","id":1364457,"title":"","content":"Another weird idea on the topic of food: something rather like a magical vending machine.<br /> <br /> The working is anchored to a statue sitting somewhere in a Threshold city, depicting a benevolent-looking man in a chef's apron bearing a ladle. If anyone places a coin in a bowl, presents it before the statue and asks for food, the coin will be replaced immediately with a nutritious soup or stew.<br /> <br /> The statue accepts any currency with which the creating sorcerer was familiar. Thus, it accepts jade, jade scrip, silver, cowrie shells, and the fangs of a certain species of viper (one of the sorcerer's friends was a shaman from an obscure jungle tribe, which used these for some reason). The statue is not actually storing up money anywhere -- the working essentially transmutes the money into food, somehow using the insubstantial <i>value</i> of fiat currency as a catalyst to generate the requested food. (This is in accordance with the creating sorcerer's peculiar mystic tradition -- one of his shaping rituals gives him sorcerous motes for making a favorable trade, to give another example. While he was a generous man, he believed that paying for things was an inherent necessity.)<br /> <br /> The statue can create any soup or stew with which the sorcerer was familiar, as well. (If someone asks for a dish it can't provide, it delivers the closest thing it can manage.) A dish involving especially rare or expensive ingredients (such as siaka's fin soup) or that would be especially difficult to make costs extra, although the price is still a bargain, relatively speaking. A certain fish stew the sorcerer remembers fondly from his childhood is discounted.<br /> <br /> I dunno. Celestial 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T02:59:45-08:00","id":1364725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1364457#post1364457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another weird idea on the topic of food: something rather like a magical vending machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's blatantly and obviously supernatural, which leans heavy into Celestial. There's clearly more utility than the millstone that grinds stone to flour.<br /> <br /> I'd probably eyeball it at Celestial 2 -- it's not too different to having an extra growing season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T14:46:41-08:00","id":1369663,"title":"","content":"Can a sorcerous working create a demense?<br /> <br /> It seems like doing this is obviously less impressive than a lot of other stuff sorcery can do, but I'm not sure if it should be considered a bigger deal than it appears, since creating an entirely new geomantic wellspring of power suggests you may be indirectly affecting a lot more than just the actual spot you're working on.<br /> <br /> I dunno. I was vaguely thinking Celestial 3 for a normal demense and Solar 2 for a greater demense. That might be aiming a little too high though -- since demenses exist naturally in Creation, creating even a greater demense is probably not as huge a deal as making a city rise up and fly away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T15:05:06-08:00","id":1369669,"title":"","content":"C3 to make a normal demense seems about right. I'd probably say it's a second C3 working to make it a greater demense, not a different scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T01:11:35-08:00","id":1369789,"title":"","content":"I think you'd have to alter the mystic geography of a large area of land to create a demesne. Celestial 3.<br /> <br /> Raising that to greater is Solar 1.<br /> <br /> Creating a greater in a single working is Solar 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T00:42:34-08:00","id":1373159,"title":"","content":"Changing the nature and powers of a demon is Celestial 2 and the way it is written as well as the other examples for this tier makes me think they mean Second Circle demons. Do you think a terrestrial 3 working would be enough to change the appearance of a bound demon of the First Circle without altering its charms? For example to make a Blood-Ape passable as human from a distance or closer if possible? Would a spell and not a working be enough if you intend to use it quite a bit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","name":"Plastic Doll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T00:52:58-08:00","id":1373160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Plastic Doll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1373159#post1373159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing the nature and powers of a demon is Celestial 2 and the way it is written as well as the other examples for this tier makes me think they mean Second Circle demons. Do you think a terrestrial 3 working would be enough to change the appearance of a bound demon of the First Circle without altering its charms? For example to make a Blood-Ape passable as human from a distance or closer if possible? Would a spell and not a working be enough if you intend to use it quite a bit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds to me like you want to &quot;Grant mutations to oneself or a willing subject&quot; which is T2. <br /> I disagree RE 2CD and don't feel that conclusion is supported by the text. But it's a moot point if you're just trying to futz with appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T01:04:52-08:00","id":1373161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1373160#post1373160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree RE 2CD and don't feel that conclusion is supported by the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creating a creature with powers similar to a Second Circle demon is Celestial 3 so I didn't think modifying an existing and willing one would be out of the ordinary for an Ambition 2 working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","user":"Plastic Doll","date":". 03-06-2020, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","name":"Plastic Doll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T01:14:03-08:00","id":1373162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Plastic Doll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1373161#post1373161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Creating a creature with powers similar to a Second Circle demon is Celestial 3 so I didn't think modifying an existing one would be out of the ordinary for an Ambition 2 working.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean I disagree about there being ANY restrictions on circle for that example working. 1CD, 3CD, Lesser Elemental Dragon, City God, Deathlord, 'sall the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T06:19:58-08:00","id":1373186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1373162#post1373162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I mean I disagree about there being ANY restrictions on circle for that example working. 1CD, 3CD, Lesser Elemental Dragon, City God, Deathlord, 'sall the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree on both counts.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial 2 to make cosmetic alterations to a Blood Ape (with a roll to recognise the disguised demon).<br /> Celestial 2 to alter the nature of ANY willing supernatural being (but it has to stay within theme -- elementals can reflect different elements but are still elementals, demons still reflect their oversoul, deathlords are still deathlords).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-07-2020, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T07:01:25-08:00","id":1373192,"title":"","content":"Thank you both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","name":"Plastic Doll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T20:13:59-08:00","id":1373316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1373186#post1373186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agree on both counts.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial 2 to make cosmetic alterations to a Blood Ape (with a roll to recognise the disguised demon).<br /> Celestial 2 to alter the nature of ANY willing supernatural being (but it has to stay within theme -- elemntals can reflect different elements but are still elementals, demons still reflect their oversoul, deathlords are still deathlords).</div> </div> </div> </div>I might say you can do cosmetic alterations to any sort of being, or at least any sort of willing being, at the same level (probably Terrestrial 2). It doesn't matter how powerful they are if all you're doing is giving them a metaphorical paint job - you aren't touching the power at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T00:13:13-08:00","id":1373335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1373316#post1373316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might say you can do cosmetic alterations to any sort of being, or at least any sort of willing being, at the same level (probably Terrestrial 2). It doesn't matter how powerful they are if all you're doing is giving them a metaphorical paint job - you aren't touching the power at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For a paint job sure, but what was giving me pause is that the Blood-Ape is described as massive with massive claws and teeth and generally humans lack those kinds of merits. Not taking away his charms is one thing but the transformation isn't meant to be an illusion. The demon wouldn't be 8f tall anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","name":"Plastic Doll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T01:46:32-08:00","id":1373343,"title":"","content":"As I see it, a Terrestrial 2 working could make a Blood Ape passable as a large, hunched, feral looking human. Like a Garou's <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Glabro\" target=\"_blank\">Glabro</a> form: it looks human but it explicitly doesn't look normal.<br /> <br /> You're not going to convince anyone your Erymanthoi are dainty Patrician noblemen of the Realm. But 6-7' foot tall wild savages with pointy (but passibly human) teeth and nails, sounds like it should be doable.<br /> <br /> Of course, you haven't changed their nature. They're still blood apes. They still love violence. They still hate cats. They still are naturally immaterial. Anyone who knows their demons, or has a chance to study your disguised servants, is going to realise that something is screwy. Anyone who sees them up close without a heavy cloak hiding them is going to be freaked out by your strange, feral savages.<br /> <br /> Turning your blood apes into 5', 98lb, mild mannered, cat lovers who can pass for dainty patrician noblemen is not a Terrestrial working. That's Celestial 3/Solar 1 cosmic ****ery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T03:31:56-08:00","id":1373349,"title":"","content":"That's why I was aiming for celestial 2 at the beginning. The character would have no interest in changing the nature or powers of the Demon, but would want to make it unrecognizable for what it really is. Like you said a dainty patrician but one that'll still snarl and eat cats and humans. Maybe taking inspiration from the lunars' charm Moon's Hidden Face where the claws would be changed into claw bracers, the bony spikes becoming part of a cloak...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1373343#post1373343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turning your blood apes into 5', 98lb, mild mannered, cat lovers who can pass for dainty patrician noblemen is not a Terrestrial working. That's Celestial 3/Solar 1 cosmic ****ery.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems kind of expensive for a first circle demon when Celestial 3 could allow me to create a creature comparable to a 2nd circle out of whole cloth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","user":"Plastic Doll","date":". 03-07-2020, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","name":"Plastic Doll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T05:43:53-08:00","id":1373362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Plastic Doll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1373349#post1373349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I was aiming for celestial 2 at the beginning. The character would have no interest in changing the nature or powers of the Demon, but would want to make it unrecognizable for what it really is. Like you said a dainty patrician but one that'll still snarls and eat cats and humans. Maybe taking inspiration from the lunar's charm Moon's Hidden Face where the claws would be changed into claw bracers, the bony spikes becoming part of a cloak...</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Plastic Doll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1373349#post1373349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems kind of expensive for a first circle demon when Celestial 3 could allow me to create a creature comparable to a 2nd circle out of whole cloth.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a balance concern, it's a nature of magic thing.<br /> <br /> Yes, it is easier to create a new being whole cloth than it is to completely rewrite the nature of a being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T10:42:09-07:00","id":1385089,"title":"","content":"Your anima gains the properties of a Lunar Tell - it can only be noticed by non-trivial characters who succeed at a roll.<br /> <br /> Nontrivial characters can attempt a difficulty 7 (Perception + Awareness) roll to notice your anima. Characters who\u2019ve previously detected your anima get +3 dice. Magic that enhances attempts to see through disguises applies on this roll. Success lets them notice the anima. On a failure, that character can\u2019t attempt the roll until the Exalt's anima has returned to dim and then becomes active again. If the Exalt makes an overt display of supernatural power, witnesses may roll to detect her anima again with 1-3 bonus dice. The Storyteller should award higher bonuses for more egregious displays, and for onlookers who verify their suspicions with read intentions or profile character actions.<br /> <br /> This only hides your anima, not supernatural displays from Charms such as Blazing Solar Bolt or Eye of the Unconquered Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T11:32:38-07:00","id":1385096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1385089#post1385089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your anima gains the properties of a Lunar Tell - it can only be noticed by non-trivial characters who succeed at a roll.<br /> <br /> Nontrivial characters can attempt a difficulty 7 (Perception + Awareness) roll to notice your anima. Characters who\u2019ve previously detected your anima get +3 dice. Magic that enhances attempts to see through disguises applies on this roll. Success lets them notice the anima. On a failure, that character can\u2019t attempt the roll until the Exalt's anima has returned to dim and then becomes active again. If the Exalt makes an overt display of supernatural power, witnesses may roll to detect her anima again with 1-3 bonus dice. The Storyteller should award higher bonuses for more egregious displays, and for onlookers who verify their suspicions with read intentions or profile character actions.<br /> <br /> This only hides your anima, not supernatural displays from Charms such as Blazing Solar Bolt or Eye of the Unconquered Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div><s>N/A.<br /> <br /> Absolutely setting breaking.<br /> <br /> Note the Tell explicity becomes Obvious at Glowing Anima.</s><br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Kelly's ideas below are much better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-01-2020, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T12:04:22-07:00","id":1385099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1385089#post1385089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your anima gains the properties of a Lunar Tell - it can only be noticed by non-trivial characters who succeed at a roll.<br /> <br /> Nontrivial characters can attempt a difficulty 7 (Perception + Awareness) roll to notice your anima. Characters who\u2019ve previously detected your anima get +3 dice. Magic that enhances attempts to see through disguises applies on this roll. Success lets them notice the anima. On a failure, that character can\u2019t attempt the roll until the Exalt's anima has returned to dim and then becomes active again. If the Exalt makes an overt display of supernatural power, witnesses may roll to detect her anima again with 1-3 bonus dice. The Storyteller should award higher bonuses for more egregious displays, and for onlookers who verify their suspicions with read intentions or profile character actions.<br /> <br /> This only hides your anima, not supernatural displays from Charms such as Blazing Solar Bolt or Eye of the Unconquered Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow something like this at Celestial 2 (the &quot;supernatural powers&quot; category, but as JohnDoe says, as written it's pretty setting-breaking. I'd have the full difficulty 7 only apply to glowing anima, and reduce it by 3 for every anima level above that (i.e., 4 at burning, and 1 at bonfire). Also, on the general principle that every working should have some kind of weirdness/interesting narrative complications, here's some suggestions for that:<ul><li>It makes your anima harder to spot by diffusing it, spreading it out across a larger area, meaning that while people have to roll to spot it, they also have the opportunity to make that roll from much further away.</li> <li>Something messes with people's perceptions, preventing them from recognizing your anima <i>as</i> an anima. But this messes with their memories of <i>you</i> as well, a la Sidereals and Arcane Fate. Except that unlike Sidereals, there's no way to get around it with Resplendent Destinies. Building an empire becomes more difficult.</li> <li>The process weakens your anima, meaning it can't be used as effectively for charms that cost anima levels - each such level now reduces your anima by two levels. You can only fuel charms that cost 2a or 3a by spending the requisite peripheral motes to flare your anima enough as part of the charm cost (so if you were at burning anima, fueling a 2a cost would cost 10 extra motes, while if you were at bonfire, it would only cost 5m).</li> <li>Similar to the above, except it affects anima abilities - your anima powers that would normally get a discount at bonfire no longer do so.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T19:46:09-07:00","id":1406041,"title":"","content":"Hello people of the Oynx Path Forums! A Working has come up, and I'd like to hear(Read) from everyone on how difficult the attempt of the working should be.<br /> <br /> Context: Well Long ago, about 4 stories worth long ago (About 5-6 months in game) the circle has made a promise to a night caste solar that they would help restore his daughter to from being transformed into a statue by the fair folk.<br /> <br /> There is only one problem. The circles own night had taken the statue through a wyld area and the statue had the soul ripped out of it and shredded. And then since <b>somehow </b>(It was a series of bad rolls) no one actually noticed that and instead of deadly kung fu happening. The two parties agreed to help each other. (Magic Oaths helping that along)<br /> <br /> So eventually one of the circle notices and finds out what had happened to the soul in question. So now she and the other members of the circle know that they need to collect her fragmented soul from the wyld pocket, repair it, and place it back into the statue. So how difficult should this be, and what kind of finesse things should happen if it isn't attempted as a finnesse 5 working?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14713,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","user":"Chronos12","date":". 08-02-2020, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T20:36:24-07:00","id":1406048,"title":"","content":"First of all, the question is this: <br /> <br /> 1. Does this count as the little girl being dead?<br /> 2. How badly shredded is this little girl? <br /> <br /> If its all the same, this is either solar or celestial. Normally without the soul shredding I'll just peg the 'turned into a statue' as some kind of flaw that has to be removed by terrestrial mutation workings. But putting a soul back together... Yep, most definitely something on the level of Celestial. <br /> <br /> Finesse 5 working to have her soul put together perfectly intact, and another working to have her get turned back into a normal flesh and blood person. Skimping on the finesse when putting her soul back together should lead to shit like personality changes, lost memories, or outright losses of certain brain functions not too dissimilar to that of traumatic brain injuries. Finesse 3 should have her be slightly 'off'. Like someone who's speech is constantly slurring, appears to have a stroke, or aphasia. Finesse 1 should be someone in a coma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T21:29:00-07:00","id":1406053,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> That's not what Finesse is. Finesse represents how much control <i>the player</i> has over how the effects of the working manifest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T21:31:09-07:00","id":1406054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronos12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1406041#post1406041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So eventually one of the circle notices and finds out what had happened to the soul in question. So now she and the other members of the circle know that they need to collect her fragmented soul from the wyld pocket, repair it, and place it back into the statue. So how difficult should this be, and what kind of finesse things should happen if it isn't attempted as a finnesse 5 working?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, putting the soul back together I would rate as Solar 1 working. Solar is the circle necessary to transform souls, and this seems comparable to the example of &quot;Extract the soul of a willing mortal from his body and transfer it into a new vessel&quot;. However, the general rule in Exalted is that you can't unbake the bread, uncrack the egg, or otherwise completely eliminate the consequences of your actions, so no matter what, the girl's going to have some lingering effects from all this.<br /> <br /> As for Finesse, remember that Finesse 5 does <i>not </i>mean &quot;a working with no weirdness&quot;. <i>Every</i> working should have some kind of weird, uncanny thing going on. Finesse 5 just means that the player doing the working gets to <i>pick</i> the weirdness. But that should still be the same degree of weirdness as any other working of similar Circle and Ambition. For this one, some possible strangenesses could include:<ul><li>Since the girl had her soul ripped up in the Wyld, putting her back together will necessarily involve getting some Wyld-stuff on it. That means she now counts as a Fair Folk for things that care about it, and the touch of iron now burns her.</li> <li>Putting the pieces of the girl's soul back together is an imperfect process, and now her memories are kinda scrambled - she remembers having her first day of school before learning to walk, she thinks her father is her uncle, that kind of thing. Mostly, this is a derangement of some type, but occasionally, she remembers things that <i>haven't happened yet</i>, effectively flashes of precognition.</li> <li>Her soul is now permanently a bit &quot;unsettled&quot; in her body. Sometimes, while she sleeps, her higher soul drifts out, in which case it's effectively her own ghost. Other times, her <i>lower</i> soul wanders, and then it's a <i>hungry</i> ghost.</li> <li>Along the same lines as the first one, maybe her soul-bits got mixed in with a fae creature, and now she has a permanent &quot;guest&quot; in her mind, one that needs to snack on people's emotions and dreams from time to time.</li> <li>The process of binding her soul bits back together requires a physical focus, a piece of jewelry or something of personal significance to her. It works reasonably well, but if she ever loses that item, her soul might fragment again.</li> <li>The way of binding her soul into her body again involved making her body into a spirit trap, and now, low-level spirits who touch her incautiously could get sucked into her as well. Basically, she's a living yasal crystal, but can't let the spirits out again without some kind of external assistance, leaving her to deal with their incessant whining until she can get them out again.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":1533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","user":"Kelly Pedersen","date":". 08-03-2020, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T21:43:47-07:00","id":1406059,"title":"","content":"While I do thank you as well Accelerator for the reply, I do really like your reply Kelly Pederson and will be noting down your suggestion with great gusto! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T08:01:50-07:00","id":1412600,"title":"","content":"Firebloom petals (Terrestrial 3)<br /> <br /> The firebloom so named is an orange plant that glows luminously in the night, making it especially easy to find in the cold winters of the North. It is extraordinarily hardy, with native defenses against frost and coverage, able to subsist entirely on stores of energy it creates when exposed to heat and light. Additional growths on the plant allow it to capture the odd insect that comes near it, smelling the sweet nectar and wishing to bask in its warmth. <br /> <br /> The firebloom is an alteration of a native thermogenic plant. Created to be shorter, stouter, brighter, and even more durable against the cold, it's ability to produce heat has been transformed into a minor supernatural power, allowing it to produce far more heat, far more steadily, with no damage to the plant due to using up its food stores. The Firebloom keeps the temperature at 28 degrees celsius. Not anything like a fireplace or a furnace, but enough to keep someone from freezing to death in cold winter nights. Specialised alchemical drugs can make this ability surge, increasing the amount of heat produce for a short amount of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T09:00:43-07:00","id":1412606,"title":"","content":"Fiber-tree (Terrestrial 3)<br /> <br /> Trees have many uses. Plants, in general, have many uses. One of the uses is the production of cloth. But it takes effort, it often takes great fields to produce them, and worst of all, the best ones like silk require silkworms and extensive processing. The Fiber tree is meant to remedy this. A tree with fast growing roots, it can only grow to a select height. It has specialized fruits containing densely packed fibers all in one long string, not unlike that secreted by a silkworm cocoon. Peeling the 'fruit' and then dumping it into hot water makes the strand unwind, creating thread that can be spun. A single 'fruit' is the equivalent of a dozen silk worms, the thread produced has a -1 difficulty to add thaumaturgy to, serves as an ingredient for Fine clothes, and a tree produces hundreds of them at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T16:48:35-07:00","id":1412655,"title":"","content":"Self replicating food (Terrestrial 3- Celestial 2)<br /> <br /> Self replicating food has long since been a staple of this entire genre. This can take many forms, from bread that can regenerate entire loaves from leftover crumbs, to self replicating cakes, to cheese blocks that bud off new blocks. Either way, it is a historical fact that self replicating food is a staple of many legends, many stories, and many sorcerers. There's always been a fair folk or sorcerer or exalted ready to create something like that to ensure a stable food supply... if they're pragmatic minded enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T18:49:58-07:00","id":1412660,"title":"","content":"So is there any consensus on whether or not you can &quot;stack&quot; rituals, or if every change to the individual/object/area has to be done in one go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T20:12:19-07:00","id":1412669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1412660#post1412660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is there any consensus on whether or not you can &quot;stack&quot; rituals, or if every change to the individual/object/area has to be done in one go?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know about a consensus. But I would allow multiple workings to stack. The trick there is that every working would have its own weirdness, so you'd get compounding effects there. Of course, conversely, stacking workings might well be the only way to do everything you want to do in the first place, because workings <i>do</i> need to consider the &quot;how&quot;, not just the &quot;what&quot; of their mechanics. Even if it would be balanced to put 30 dots of mutations onto a single person with just a Terrestrial 2 working, you'd probably have to work <i>very</i> hard to explain to me, as the ST, what kind of magical process would actually bestow all 30.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T19:45:34-07:00","id":1413479,"title":"","content":"Snake Hair (Terrestrial 3 - Celestial 1)<br /> <br /> This is the equivalent of a hanging spell. Once a day, the sorcerer can roll Occult + Intelligence against difficulty 3. Success means that they have cast Dance of the Smoke Cobras, and her hair billows smoke, eventually coalescing to form five gigantic snakes. The sorcerer must already know the spell and be able to cast it. This working simply means that they can cast it faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T00:36:10-07:00","id":1416811,"title":"","content":"Fast-growing fish (Terrestrial 3)<br /> <br /> Fish which grow exceptionally fast, have a love for eating parasites and other small insects, and can live in the worst of conditions. They grow to maturation in a year, and can enter schools of tens of thousands. No fish can reproduce on its own. There is no method for getting its eggs out of its body. Instead, wise fishermen take the fish, gut it, and put its eggs into a specialized alchemical mixture (requires occult 1 to build), and let the eggs hatch in small specialized ponds, safe from predators. When the fish are big enough to fend off most predators, they are released back into the lake, to replenish numbers. The fish are r-strategists, each one capable of creating tens of thousands of spawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T09:01:58-07:00","id":1417002,"title":"","content":"Would a working be a valid method for trying to make an antidote for the Golden Viper's (from Arms of the Chosen) gold venom? If so, what kinda of working would it be? I'm going to be joining a game where a variety of NPCs have been turned to gold. My character is well-versed in poisons/medicine, so I'm wondering it if makes more sense to use the craft system or the working system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--Lurker Extraordinaire!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/344-darkwolff","name":"DarkWolff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T09:43:25-07:00","id":1417010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkWolff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1417002#post1417002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a working be a valid method for trying to make an antidote for the Golden Viper's (from Arms of the Chosen) gold venom?</div> </div> </div> </div>A working would definitely be one way to help victims of the Golden Viper. The trick is, I don't think it would be an <i>antidote</i>, as such. Exalted in general prefers to avoid simple solutions that just reverse what's happened - &quot;the bread stays baked&quot;, basically. And sorcery specifically is all about transforming and permanently changing things. So rather than an antidote, think in terms of transforming the victims into something else, something that might count as &quot;alive&quot; but won't be the same as before. Maybe you animate the golden statues that their bodies have turned into with their spirits. Maybe you pull their souls out and put them into something else. Maybe you transform the gold into flesh - but it's just a homogenous mass of flesh, and though their minds are still controlling it, that has consequences, like having to absorb nutrients from a paste, or not feeling any heartbeat or breathing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkWolff</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, what kinda of working would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's going to depend on exactly what you want to do, what sort of transformation you imagine. But it probably won't be lower than Celestial, whatever you do. You're effectively bringing people back to life here, and that's potent.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T10:01:45-07:00","id":1417014,"title":"","content":"Are people poisoned and turned to gold dead or transmuted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T11:42:13-07:00","id":1417028,"title":"","content":"Dead. The text talks about how the serpent absorbs the knowledge and experience of the victims <b>killed</b> this way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","user":"Plastic Doll","date":". 10-06-2020, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","name":"Plastic Doll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T12:20:57-07:00","id":1417035,"title":"","content":"The largest barrier to making an antidote for the venom via sorcerous working is that it takes, at minimum, a week to perform a sorcerous working, and most victims will be done with the poison, one way or the other, by that time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T14:12:49-07:00","id":1417049,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the help folks. I guess I forgot to mention the venom was inspired by the Golden Serpents but was effectively modified to lock the targets in a stasis. In the game, the Golden Serpent was found and inferior variants were made from it (it was a plot point from the story). I was mostly having a hard time seeing the line between an artifact and a working since I hadn't been involved in a game that made use of workings yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--Lurker Extraordinaire!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/344-darkwolff","name":"DarkWolff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T16:09:55-07:00","id":1417074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkWolff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments?p=1417049#post1417049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was mostly having a hard time seeing the line between an artifact and a working since I hadn't been involved in a game that made use of workings yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>The line can get fuzzy, it's true. In general, though, I'd say that the more of the following boxes a magical thing ticks, the closer it is to an artifact, instead of a working:<ul><li>Is it focused in an object?<ul><li>Is that object portable?</li> <li>Can the object be used by anyone who can attune to it?</li> <li>Does the process of using the object feel like using the type of tool its shaped like? That is, if its a weapon, does attacking with it involve swinging or stabbing someone with it, and is it shaped like a sword, spear, etc.?</li> </ul></li> </ul>If none of those are true, it's almost certainly a working. If just one or two of them are, it might be either a working or an artifact. If all three are, it's probably an artifact.<br /> <br /> In any case, working or artifact, I'd still say that the effect of de-golding people should be a bit more complicated than &quot;and now you're back to exactly the way you were, congratulations&quot;. The Gold Viper's poison is explicitly death, but even if this version is different, anything that's supposed to be permanent without other means should have long-term consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T07:19:05-07:00","id":1417140,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I agree there should be consequences but just wanted to know my options when the question &quot;can you fix this?&quot; comes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--Lurker Extraordinaire!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/344-darkwolff","name":"DarkWolff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T00:43:42-07:00","id":1417281,"title":"","content":"Came here after realizing people thought the calabash had healing properties<br /> <br /> Healing Gourd (Celestial 1/ Artifact 2) <br /> <br /> The healing gourd is composed out of green jade, semi-translucent, capable of holding any liquid inside. The gourd has inscriptions of vitality, health, and purity, letting it purify any liquid it contains. However its main ability is to produce a liquid, that when poured into the mouth of a patient, lets the next medicine roll carried out on him to have a -2 difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T12:10:08-07:00","id":1524537,"title":"","content":"I got a question. I remember reading here about someone mentioning a... thing? Celestial circle working for lunars. Basically, someone posited that a concept for lunars making sorcerous workings is to have a mountaintop temple where time has been warped, so that highly trained martial artists can be made in the span of a week. <br /> <br /> Anyone gave further thought to this idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T15:22:29-07:00","id":1539344,"title":"","content":"I remember asking this a long time ago, but i cannot find it but what level of working would it be too create mines that regenerate mundane ores, and what tier of working would it be too create a regenerating ja